{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"ashby:1x:b6743a34-6533-4e23-ad1a-ea98dd8dcd59","source":{"type":"ashby","board":"1x","job_id":"b6743a34-6533-4e23-ad1a-ea98dd8dcd59","source_url":"https://api.ashbyhq.com/posting-api/job-board/1x","response_hash":"deb152f77659a032a4ffd1a98bb2954aa61c4fbc68b444bd53066145b38487ad","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"1X","slug":"1x","lists":["robotics","ai-ml"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Quality Engineering Technician Polymer","canonical_url":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/1x/b6743a34-6533-4e23-ad1a-ea98dd8dcd59","apply_url":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/1x/b6743a34-6533-4e23-ad1a-ea98dd8dcd59/application","locations":[{"label":"San Carlos, CA","city":"San Carlos","region":"California","country":"United States","remote":null,"hybrid":null}],"workplace_type":"on_site","employment_type":"full_time","departments":["Manufacturing Operations"],"teams":["Quality Engineering "],"language":null,"requisition_id":null,"internal_job_id":null,"first_published_at":"2026-06-17T01:39:22.683+00:00","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":null,"description_html":null,"compensation":[{"type":"salary","summary":"$42 – $50 per hour • Offers Equity","salary_summary":null,"tiers":[{"title":null,"summary":"$42 – $50 per hour • Offers Equity","additional_information":null}]}],"custom_fields":{},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":false,"tier":"stretch","score":0,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":[],"role_matches":[],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["robotics","ai-ml"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"ashby:1x:d6f54e78-6ae0-47fd-bb2a-f93484d21a2c","source":{"type":"ashby","board":"1x","job_id":"d6f54e78-6ae0-47fd-bb2a-f93484d21a2c","source_url":"https://api.ashbyhq.com/posting-api/job-board/1x","response_hash":"1f206f9e74f4726921ece643ae0c8a5cfb9c5afb738242c0ad0d49efbfd3db8a","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"1X","slug":"1x","lists":["robotics","ai-ml"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Robot Assembly Technician","canonical_url":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/1x/d6f54e78-6ae0-47fd-bb2a-f93484d21a2c","apply_url":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/1x/d6f54e78-6ae0-47fd-bb2a-f93484d21a2c/application","locations":[{"label":"Hayward, CA","city":"Hayward","region":"California","country":"United States","remote":null,"hybrid":null}],"workplace_type":"on_site","employment_type":"full_time","departments":["Manufacturing Operations"],"teams":["Production"],"language":null,"requisition_id":null,"internal_job_id":null,"first_published_at":"2026-06-23T18:43:43.368+00:00","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Role Name: Assembly Technician\n\nDepartment: Production\n\nLocation: Hayward, CA\n\nShift: Day Shift (6:00 AM – 2:30 PM) or Swing Shift (3:00 PM – 11:30 PM)\n\n\n\n\nABOUT 1X\n\nWe're building humanoid robots that work in home - doing the chores, handling the tasks, and giving people their time back. Simple, but it's not.\n\nTo do this right, we have to solve robotics, AI, manufacturing - at the same time, at scale, in a form factor that has to be safe enough to live with your family. If you're inspired by this, you'll thrive here. We've been at this since 2014 and we're at the point where the hard problems are behind us and the hard work is in front of us.\n\nNEO is our flagship - a home robot designed to move, learn, and operate in the real world alongside real people. We're not demoing it - we're shipping it. We're excited to meet you, if this excites you.\n\nIf you've spent your career working on problems that matter and want to see them actually reach the world - this is that moment. We're scaling, we're hiring with intention, and we need people who want to build something that will genuinely change how humans spend their time - safely creating abundance for all.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE TEAM\n\nThe Manufacturing team is where NEO goes from CAD files to physical reality. Every robot that ships to a customer's home passes through our hands first, and the precision of our work directly determines whether NEO performs safely and reliably in the real world. This team is critical to 1X's mission - without us, there is no robot, no shipment, and no abundance to create.\n\n\n\n\nYOUR CHARTER\n\nTo create an abundant supply of physical labor through safe, intelligent humanoids, every single NEO must be built to a standard that earns its place in someone's home. As an Assembly Technician, you are responsible for translating engineering intent into a physical robot - building precision mechanical subassemblies that meet exacting tolerances so NEO can move, learn, and operate safely alongside real people. Your craftsmanship is the foundation that everything else - AI, software, customer trust - is built on.\n\n\n\n\nKEY OUTCOMES\n\n - Consistently meet daily and weekly production output targets without compromising on quality or safety standards\n\n - Deliver subassemblies that pass first-time inspection, minimizing rework and downstream defects\n\n - Maintain dimensional accuracy and proper torque specifications across every assembly you complete\n\n - Identify and escalate process issues, tooling problems, or recurring defects so the line gets better over time\n\n - Contribute to a clean, organized, and safe work area that meets ESD and manufacturing standards every shift\n\n\n\n\nKEY COMPETENCIES\n\n - Craftsmanship mindset - you take pride in building things correctly and care how the work turns out, not just that it's done\n\n - Strong manual dexterity and comfort with detailed, repetitive precision work on small parts\n\n - Reads engineering drawings fluently and works from written instructions without needing constant direction\n\n - Reliable and accountable - shows up on time, finishes what they start, and supports the team to hit shared goals\n\n - Quality-first instinct - would rather flag a defect than let it pass\n\n\n\n\nMINIMUM REQUIREMENTS\n\n - 2+ years of experience in mechanical assembly or manufacturing\n\n - Ability to read and follow assembly drawings, work instructions, and engineering documentation\n\n - Proficient with hand tools, power tools, and basic measuring instruments (calipers, torque wrenches, gauges)\n\n - Able to lift up to 50 lbs and perform sustained hands-on, physical work throughout a shift\n\n - Reliable, punctual, and able to work effectively in a team environment\n\n - Professional-level English proficiency (written and verbal)\n\n\n\n\nPREFERRED SKILLS\n\n - Experience assembling robotics, aerospace, medical device, or other precision mechanical products\n\n - Familiarity with ESD procedures and controlled manufacturing environments\n\n - Experience with high-mix, low-volume or early-stage production environments where processes are still being refined\n\n - Exposure to lean manufacturing or continuous improvement practices\n\n\n\n\nWHAT DOES A SUCCESSFUL 1X TEAM MEMBER LOOK LIKE\n\nTeam members at 1X who thrive here are builders. They move fast, own their work completely, and treat time like it's the one thing you can't get back - because it is. They say what they mean, finish what they start, and hold themselves to a standard before anyone has to ask. We push each other to be better, and we do it with honesty and respect.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$28.00/hr – $30.00/hr + Equity\n\n\n\n\nBENEFITS\n\n - Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage\n\n - Generous paid time off, company holidays, and parental leave\n\n - 401(k) plan with company match (100% on the first 3% of contributions, 50% on the next 2%)\n\n - Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA) and Health Savings Accounts (HSA) options\n\n - Commuter benefits (transit and parking)\n\n - Short-term and long-term disability, and life insurance\n\n - Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, financial, and personal support\n\n - Onsite snacks and catered lunches\n\n\n\n\n1X IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER\n\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, age, marital status, medical condition, genetic information, disability, military or veteran status, justice system impact, or any other characteristic protected under applicable federal, state, or local law.","description_html":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Role Name:</strong> Assembly Technician</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Department:</strong> Production</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Hayward, CA</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shift:</strong> Day Shift (6:00 AM – 2:30 PM) or Swing Shift (3:00 PM – 11:30 PM)</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About 1X</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're building humanoid robots that work in home - doing the chores, handling the tasks, and giving people their time back. Simple, but it's not.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To do this right, we have to solve robotics, AI, manufacturing - at the same time, at scale, in a form factor that has to be safe enough to live with your family. If you're inspired by this, you'll thrive here. We've been at this since 2014 and we're at the point where the hard problems are behind us and the hard work is in front of us.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">NEO is our flagship - a home robot designed to move, learn, and operate in the real world alongside real people. We're not demoing it - we're shipping it. We're excited to meet you, if this excites you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you've spent your career working on problems that matter and want to see them actually reach the world - this is that moment. We're scaling, we're hiring with intention, and we need people who want to build something that will genuinely change how humans spend their time - safely creating abundance for all.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About the Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Manufacturing team is where NEO goes from CAD files to physical reality. Every robot that ships to a customer's home passes through our hands first, and the precision of our work directly determines whether NEO performs safely and reliably in the real world. This team is critical to 1X's mission - without us, there is no robot, no shipment, and no abundance to create.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Your Charter</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To create an abundant supply of physical labor through safe, intelligent humanoids, every single NEO must be built to a standard that earns its place in someone's home. As an Assembly Technician, you are responsible for translating engineering intent into a physical robot - building precision mechanical subassemblies that meet exacting tolerances so NEO can move, learn, and operate safely alongside real people. Your craftsmanship is the foundation that everything else - AI, software, customer trust - is built on.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Key Outcomes</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Consistently meet daily and weekly production output targets without compromising on quality or safety standards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deliver subassemblies that pass first-time inspection, minimizing rework and downstream defects</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain dimensional accuracy and proper torque specifications across every assembly you complete</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and escalate process issues, tooling problems, or recurring defects so the line gets better over time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to a clean, organized, and safe work area that meets ESD and manufacturing standards every shift</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Key Competencies</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Craftsmanship mindset - you take pride in building things correctly and care how the work turns out, not just that it's done</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong manual dexterity and comfort with detailed, repetitive precision work on small parts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reads engineering drawings fluently and works from written instructions without needing constant direction</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable and accountable - shows up on time, finishes what they start, and supports the team to hit shared goals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Quality-first instinct - would rather flag a defect than let it pass</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Minimum Requirements</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in mechanical assembly or manufacturing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to read and follow assembly drawings, work instructions, and engineering documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficient with hand tools, power tools, and basic measuring instruments (calipers, torque wrenches, gauges)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Able to lift up to 50 lbs and perform sustained hands-on, physical work throughout a shift</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable, punctual, and able to work effectively in a team environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional-level English proficiency (written and verbal)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Preferred Skills</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience assembling robotics, aerospace, medical device, or other precision mechanical products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with ESD procedures and controlled manufacturing environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with high-mix, low-volume or early-stage production environments where processes are still being refined</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to lean manufacturing or continuous improvement practices</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What does a successful 1X Team Member look like</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team members at 1X who thrive here are builders. They move fast, own their work completely, and treat time like it's the one thing you can't get back - because it is. They say what they mean, finish what they start, and hold themselves to a standard before anyone has to ask. We push each other to be better, and we do it with honesty and respect.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Compensation Range</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$28.00/hr – $30.00/hr + Equity</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Benefits</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Generous paid time off, company holidays, and parental leave</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) plan with company match (100% on the first 3% of contributions, 50% on the next 2%)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA) and Health Savings Accounts (HSA) options</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Commuter benefits (transit and parking)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Short-term and long-term disability, and life insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, financial, and personal support</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Onsite snacks and catered lunches</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>1X is an Equal Opportunity Employer</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, age, marital status, medical condition, genetic information, disability, military or veteran status, justice system impact, or any other characteristic protected under applicable federal, state, or local law.</p>","compensation":[{"type":"salary","summary":"$28 – $30 per hour • Offers Equity","salary_summary":null,"tiers":[{"title":null,"summary":"$28 – $30 per hour • Offers Equity","additional_information":null}]}],"custom_fields":{},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["robotics"],"role_matches":["Robot"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["robotics","ai-ml"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"ashby:1x:20e83c98-46f4-4db9-8a9c-631ce9f527f6","source":{"type":"ashby","board":"1x","job_id":"20e83c98-46f4-4db9-8a9c-631ce9f527f6","source_url":"https://api.ashbyhq.com/posting-api/job-board/1x","response_hash":"4bd21332bb5ee63a753e7d415bfa45cfe3d160d14c8373c4a2c9c4d5c1c2a503","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"1X","slug":"1x","lists":["robotics","ai-ml"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Robot Assembly Technician, Hands","canonical_url":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/1x/20e83c98-46f4-4db9-8a9c-631ce9f527f6","apply_url":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/1x/20e83c98-46f4-4db9-8a9c-631ce9f527f6/application","locations":[{"label":"San Carlos, CA","city":"San Carlos","region":"California","country":"United States","remote":null,"hybrid":null}],"workplace_type":"on_site","employment_type":"full_time","departments":["Manufacturing Operations"],"teams":["Production"],"language":null,"requisition_id":null,"internal_job_id":null,"first_published_at":"2026-06-23T18:43:01.735+00:00","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Role Name: Assembly Technician, Hands Team\n\nDepartment: Production, Hands\n\nLocation: San Carlos\n\nShift: Day Shift (6:00 AM – 2:30 PM) or Swing Shift (3:00 PM – 11:30 PM)\n\n\n\n\nABOUT 1X\n\nWe're building humanoid robots that work in home – doing the chores, handling the tasks, and giving people their time back. Simple, but it's not.\n\nTo do this right, we have to solve robotics, AI, manufacturing – at the same time, at scale, in a form factor that has to be safe enough to live with your family. If you're inspired by this, you'll thrive here. We've been at this since 2014 and we're at the point where the hard problems are behind us and the hard work is in front of us.\n\nNEO is our flagship – a home robot designed to move, learn, and operate in the real world alongside real people. We're not demoing it – we're shipping it. We're excited to meet you, if this excites you.\n\nIf you've spent your career working on problems that matter and want to see them actually reach the world – this is that moment. We're scaling, we're hiring with intention, and we need people who want to build something that will genuinely change how humans spend their time – safely creating abundance for all.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE TEAM\n\nThe Hands team builds the most dexterous part of NEO – the hands that pick up cups, fold laundry, and turn doorknobs in real homes. Every subassembly we ship is built to micron-level precision because the difference between a robot that helps and a robot that frustrates comes down to how well its hands work. Without this team, NEO can't do its job – and 1X can't deliver on the mission.\n\n\n\n\nYOUR CHARTER\n\nBuild the precision electromechanical subassemblies that give NEO the dexterity to work alongside people. Every motor, encoder, PCB, and harness you assemble is a direct contribution to 1X's mission of creating an abundant supply of physical labor through safe, intelligent humanoids. The quality of your work decides whether the robots we ship can be trusted in someone's home.\n\n\n\n\nKEY OUTCOMES\n\n - Build hand subassemblies to spec with zero defects passed downstream – micron-level tolerances, sub-M2 fasteners, ESD-sensitive components, fine-pitch connectors\n\n - Hit shift production targets without compromising quality – own your station's output, uptime, and conformance\n\n - Catch and document defects, process deviations, and material issues at the workstation before they reach the next station\n\n - Maintain complete, accurate build logs and inspection data for every unit you touch\n\n - Drive continuous improvement on your line – surface issues, propose fixes, and partner with engineering and the opposite shift to keep the line moving\n\n\n\n\nKEY COMPETENCIES\n\n - Fine motor precision and steady hands – you can work confidently with parts smaller than M2 fasteners, hour after hour\n\n - Quality-first mindset – you'd rather flag a problem and fix it than ship it and hope\n\n - Strong drawing literacy – you read engineering specs and detailed work instructions and build to them independently\n\n - Calm under repetition – you do detailed, focused work for full shifts without losing accuracy\n\n - Clear communicator – especially across shift handoffs, with quality, and with engineering\n\n\n\n\nMINIMUM REQUIREMENTS\n\n - 3+ years in precision electromechanical assembly, micro assembly, or similar fine-component manufacturing (humanoid robotics, medical devices, aerospace actuators, consumer electronics internals, optical assemblies)\n\n - Hands-on experience assembling miniature components – small motors, gearboxes, encoders, PCBs, and fine-pitch connectors\n\n - Proficiency with precision hand tools, calibrated torque instruments at low values (~1 Nm), and dimensional inspection tools (micrometers, pin gauges, dial indicators, calipers, or similar)\n\n - Working knowledge of ESD handling procedures and controlled-environment protocols\n\n - Reliable attendance and the ability to work scheduled shifts consistently in a team environment\n\n - Professional-level English proficiency (written and verbal)\n\n\n\n\nPREFERRED SKILLS\n\n - MES or ERP experience (Odoo, SAP, or similar) for production tracking and work order management\n\n - Background in robotic, actuator, gearbox, or servo assembly\n\n - Soldering experience (through-hole or SMT rework)\n\n - Familiarity with thermal compounds or adhesives (Loctite, etc.) and comfort working near thermal processing equipment\n\n - Experience with vision inspection systems or digital measurement tools\n\n - Firmware flashing or programming of embedded components\n\n - Functional testing of PCBs, small motors, or encoders (continuity checks, run-in, performance validation)\n\n - Lean manufacturing, 5S, or continuous improvement experience\n\n\n\n\nPHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS\n\n - Able to sit or stand at a workstation for extended periods performing fine detail work\n\n - Able to lift up to 30 lbs occasionally\n\n - Sufficient vision (corrected or uncorrected) to inspect miniature components and read fine markings at close range\n\n\n\n\nWHAT DOES A SUCCESSFUL 1X TEAM MEMBER LOOK LIKE\n\nTeam members at 1X who thrive here are builders. They move fast, own their work completely, and treat time like it's the one thing you can't get back – because it is. They say what they mean, finish what they start, and hold themselves to a standard before anyone has to ask. We push each other to be better, and we do it with honesty and respect.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$28.00/hr – $36.00/hr + Equity\n\n\n\n\nBENEFITS\n\n - Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage\n\n - Generous paid time off, company holidays, and parental leave\n\n - 401(k) plan with company match (100% on the first 3% of contributions, 50% on the next 2%)\n\n - Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA) and Health Savings Accounts (HSA) options\n\n - Commuter benefits (transit and parking)\n\n - Short-term and long-term disability, and life insurance\n\n - Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, financial, and personal support\n\n - Onsite snacks and catered lunches\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER\n\n1X is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, age, marital status, medical condition, genetic information, disability, military or veteran status, justice system impact, or any other characteristic protected under applicable federal, state, or local law.","description_html":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Role Name:</strong> Assembly Technician, Hands Team</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Department:</strong> Production, Hands</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> San Carlos</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shift:</strong> Day Shift (6:00 AM – 2:30 PM) or Swing Shift (3:00 PM – 11:30 PM)</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>About 1X</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're building humanoid robots that work in home – doing the chores, handling the tasks, and giving people their time back. Simple, but it's not.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To do this right, we have to solve robotics, AI, manufacturing – at the same time, at scale, in a form factor that has to be safe enough to live with your family. If you're inspired by this, you'll thrive here. We've been at this since 2014 and we're at the point where the hard problems are behind us and the hard work is in front of us.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">NEO is our flagship – a home robot designed to move, learn, and operate in the real world alongside real people. We're not demoing it – we're shipping it. We're excited to meet you, if this excites you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you've spent your career working on problems that matter and want to see them actually reach the world – this is that moment. We're scaling, we're hiring with intention, and we need people who want to build something that will genuinely change how humans spend their time – safely creating abundance for all.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>About the Team</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Hands team builds the most dexterous part of NEO – the hands that pick up cups, fold laundry, and turn doorknobs in real homes. Every subassembly we ship is built to micron-level precision because the difference between a robot that helps and a robot that frustrates comes down to how well its hands work. Without this team, NEO can't do its job – and 1X can't deliver on the mission.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Your Charter</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the precision electromechanical subassemblies that give NEO the dexterity to work alongside people. Every motor, encoder, PCB, and harness you assemble is a direct contribution to 1X's mission of creating an abundant supply of physical labor through safe, intelligent humanoids. The quality of your work decides whether the robots we ship can be trusted in someone's home.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Key Outcomes</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build hand subassemblies to spec with zero defects passed downstream – micron-level tolerances, sub-M2 fasteners, ESD-sensitive components, fine-pitch connectors</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hit shift production targets without compromising quality – own your station's output, uptime, and conformance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Catch and document defects, process deviations, and material issues at the workstation before they reach the next station</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain complete, accurate build logs and inspection data for every unit you touch</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive continuous improvement on your line – surface issues, propose fixes, and partner with engineering and the opposite shift to keep the line moving</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Key Competencies</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fine motor precision and steady hands – you can work confidently with parts smaller than M2 fasteners, hour after hour</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Quality-first mindset – you'd rather flag a problem and fix it than ship it and hope</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong drawing literacy – you read engineering specs and detailed work instructions and build to them independently</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Calm under repetition – you do detailed, focused work for full shifts without losing accuracy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear communicator – especially across shift handoffs, with quality, and with engineering</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Minimum Requirements</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years in precision electromechanical assembly, micro assembly, or similar fine-component manufacturing (humanoid robotics, medical devices, aerospace actuators, consumer electronics internals, optical assemblies)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience assembling miniature components – small motors, gearboxes, encoders, PCBs, and fine-pitch connectors</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency with precision hand tools, calibrated torque instruments at low values (~1 Nm), and dimensional inspection tools (micrometers, pin gauges, dial indicators, calipers, or similar)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of ESD handling procedures and controlled-environment protocols</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable attendance and the ability to work scheduled shifts consistently in a team environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional-level English proficiency (written and verbal)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Preferred Skills</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">MES or ERP experience (Odoo, SAP, or similar) for production tracking and work order management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in robotic, actuator, gearbox, or servo assembly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Soldering experience (through-hole or SMT rework)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with thermal compounds or adhesives (Loctite, etc.) and comfort working near thermal processing equipment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with vision inspection systems or digital measurement tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Firmware flashing or programming of embedded components</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Functional testing of PCBs, small motors, or encoders (continuity checks, run-in, performance validation)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lean manufacturing, 5S, or continuous improvement experience</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Physical Requirements</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Able to sit or stand at a workstation for extended periods performing fine detail work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Able to lift up to 30 lbs occasionally</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Sufficient vision (corrected or uncorrected) to inspect miniature components and read fine markings at close range</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What does a successful 1X Team Member look like</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team members at 1X who thrive here are builders. They move fast, own their work completely, and treat time like it's the one thing you can't get back – because it is. They say what they mean, finish what they start, and hold themselves to a standard before anyone has to ask. We push each other to be better, and we do it with honesty and respect.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Compensation Range</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$28.00/hr – $36.00/hr + Equity</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Benefits</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Generous paid time off, company holidays, and parental leave</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) plan with company match (100% on the first 3% of contributions, 50% on the next 2%)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA) and Health Savings Accounts (HSA) options</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Commuter benefits (transit and parking)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Short-term and long-term disability, and life insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, financial, and personal support</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Onsite snacks and catered lunches</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Equal Opportunity Employer</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1X is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, age, marital status, medical condition, genetic information, disability, military or veteran status, justice system impact, or any other characteristic protected under applicable federal, state, or local law.</p>","compensation":[{"type":"salary","summary":"$28 – $36 per hour • Offers Equity","salary_summary":null,"tiers":[{"title":null,"summary":"$28 – $36 per hour • Offers Equity","additional_information":null}]}],"custom_fields":{},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["robotics"],"role_matches":["Robot"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["robotics","ai-ml"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"ashby:1x:d718036a-530c-40cd-bfed-63ce8e64dc75","source":{"type":"ashby","board":"1x","job_id":"d718036a-530c-40cd-bfed-63ce8e64dc75","source_url":"https://api.ashbyhq.com/posting-api/job-board/1x","response_hash":"efdded1daf0e76c9e165d7ed63f8b2121f509c45e03f7e439888621900804e13","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"1X","slug":"1x","lists":["robotics","ai-ml"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Robot Operations Manager PM","canonical_url":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/1x/d718036a-530c-40cd-bfed-63ce8e64dc75","apply_url":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/1x/d718036a-530c-40cd-bfed-63ce8e64dc75/application","locations":[{"label":"San Carlos, CA","city":"San Carlos","region":"California","country":"United States","remote":null,"hybrid":null}],"workplace_type":"on_site","employment_type":"full_time","departments":["Fleet Operations "],"teams":["Fleet Operations "],"language":null,"requisition_id":null,"internal_job_id":null,"first_published_at":"2026-06-17T01:38:39.873+00:00","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":null,"description_html":null,"compensation":[{"type":"salary","summary":"$145K – $175K • Offers Equity","salary_summary":"$145K - $175K","tiers":[{"title":null,"summary":"$145K – $175K • Offers Equity","additional_information":null}]}],"custom_fields":{},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":false,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"manager","term":null,"tracks":["robotics"],"role_matches":["Robot"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":["Manager"],"configured_tracks":["robotics","ai-ml"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"ashby:1x:a6e6eb67-2faf-4369-879d-9d9901e7f3ac","source":{"type":"ashby","board":"1x","job_id":"a6e6eb67-2faf-4369-879d-9d9901e7f3ac","source_url":"https://api.ashbyhq.com/posting-api/job-board/1x","response_hash":"598d89d104da742ebf43b8d63d3b4f7c809712755b5c46c814c5f9ffd5648fe2","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"1X","slug":"1x","lists":["robotics","ai-ml"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Robot Service Technician","canonical_url":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/1x/a6e6eb67-2faf-4369-879d-9d9901e7f3ac","apply_url":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/1x/a6e6eb67-2faf-4369-879d-9d9901e7f3ac/application","locations":[{"label":"San Carlos, CA","city":"San Carlos","region":"California","country":"United States","remote":null,"hybrid":null}],"workplace_type":"on_site","employment_type":"full_time","departments":["Fleet Operations "],"teams":["Fleet Operations "],"language":null,"requisition_id":null,"internal_job_id":null,"first_published_at":"2026-08-24T16:38:03.114+00:00","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Shift: Day Shift\n\n\n\n\nABOUT 1X\n\nWe’re building humanoid robots that work in home - doing the chores, handling the tasks, and giving people their time back. Simple, but it’s not.\n\n\n\nTo do this right, we have to solve robotics, AI, manufacturing - at the same time, at scale, in a form factor that has to be safe enough to live with your family. If you’re inspired by this, you’ll thrive here. We’ve been at this since 2014 and we’re at the point where the hard problems are behind us and the hard work is in front of us.\n\n\n\nNEO is our flagship - a home robot designed to move, learn, and operate in the real world alongside real people. We’re not demoing it - we’re shipping it. We’re excited to meet you, if this excites you.\n\n\n\nIf you’ve spent your career working on problems that matter and want to see them actually reach the world - this is that moment. We’re scaling, we’re hiring with intention, and we need people who want to build something that will genuinely change how humans spend their time - safely creating abundance for all.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE TEAM\n\nThe Robot Services team is responsible for maintaining and improving the health of our deployed robotic fleet. As robots operate in customer homes and real-world environments, this team diagnoses failures, performs repairs, and partners closely with Engineering to improve reliability, serviceability, and overall fleet performance.\n\n\n\n\nYOUR CHARTER\n\nAs a Robot Service Technician, you will be responsible for diagnosing, repairing, testing, and validating humanoid robots and their subsystems. Your work will directly impact fleet uptime, product reliability, and the speed at which engineering teams can learn from real-world robot performance.\n\n\n\n\nKEY OUTCOMES\n\n - Complete high-quality repairs and maintenance activities that return robots to service safely and efficiently.\n\n - Diagnose mechanical, electrical, and system-level failures while documenting root causes and corrective actions.\n\n - Execute validation and test procedures to ensure repaired robots meet operational and performance requirements.\n\n - Maintain accurate service records that support fleet reliability analysis and continuous product improvement.\n\n - Identify recurring failure trends and provide actionable feedback to Engineering and Operations teams.\n\n\n\n\nKEY COMPETENCIES\n\n - Strong electromechanical troubleshooting and repair skills.\n\n - High attention to detail and craftsmanship when working on precision assemblies.\n\n - Ability to follow structured processes while maintaining a strong sense of ownership and accountability.\n\n - Clear communicator who can document technical findings and collaborate across teams.\n\n - Comfortable working in a fast-paced environment where priorities and challenges evolve quickly.\n\n\n\n\nMINIMUM REQUIREMENTS\n\n - 2+ years of experience in robotics, manufacturing, aerospace, automotive, electronics, or another hands-on technical field.\n\n - Experience assembling, maintaining, or repairing electromechanical systems.\n\n - Ability to read and interpret technical drawings, schematics, and work instructions.\n\n - Experience using measurement and diagnostic tools such as calipers, multimeters, torque tools, or similar equipment.\n\n - Ability to work safely around electrical systems, lift components, and perform hands-on work for extended periods.\n\n\n\n\nPREFERRED SKILLS\n\n - Experience working on robotic systems, automation equipment, or complex electromechanical products.\n\n - Experience with wiring harness repair, precision soldering, crimping, or connector assembly.\n\n - Familiarity with command-line tools, hardware diagnostics, or embedded system troubleshooting.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT DOES A SUCCESSFUL 1X TEAM MEMBER LOOK LIKE\n\nTeam members at 1X who thrive here are builders. They move fast, own their work completely, and treat time like it’s the one thing you can’t get back - because it is. They say what they mean, finish what they start, and hold themselves to a standard before anyone has to ask. We push each other to be better, and we do it with honesty and respect.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$25.00 - $34.00 per hour\n\n\n\n\nBENEFITS\n\n - Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage\n\n - Generous paid time off, company holidays, and parental leave\n\n - 401(k) plan with company match (100% on the first 3% of contributions, 50% on the next 2%)\n\n - Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA) and Health Savings Accounts (HSA) options\n\n - Commuter benefits (transit and parking)\n\n - Short-term and long-term disability, and life insurance\n\n - Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, financial, and personal support\n\n - Onsite snacks and catered lunches\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER\n\n1X is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, age, marital status, medical condition, genetic information, disability, military or veteran status, justice system impact, or any other characteristic protected under applicable federal, state, or local law.","description_html":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shift: </strong>Day Shift</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>About 1X</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re building humanoid robots that work in home - doing the chores, handling the tasks, and giving people their time back. Simple, but it’s not.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To do this right, we have to solve robotics, AI, manufacturing - at the same time, at scale, in a form factor that has to be safe enough to live with your family. If you’re inspired by this, you’ll thrive here. We’ve been at this since 2014 and we’re at the point where the hard problems are behind us and the hard work is in front of us.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">NEO is our flagship - a home robot designed to move, learn, and operate in the real world alongside real people. We’re not demoing it - we’re shipping it. We’re excited to meet you, if this excites you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you’ve spent your career working on problems that matter and want to see them actually reach the world - this is that moment. We’re scaling, we’re hiring with intention, and we need people who want to build something that will genuinely change how humans spend their time - safely creating abundance for all.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>About the Team</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Robot Services team is responsible for maintaining and improving the health of our deployed robotic fleet. As robots operate in customer homes and real-world environments, this team diagnoses failures, performs repairs, and partners closely with Engineering to improve reliability, serviceability, and overall fleet performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Your Charter</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Robot Service Technician, you will be responsible for diagnosing, repairing, testing, and validating humanoid robots and their subsystems. Your work will directly impact fleet uptime, product reliability, and the speed at which engineering teams can learn from real-world robot performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Key Outcomes</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Complete high-quality repairs and maintenance activities that return robots to service safely and efficiently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Diagnose mechanical, electrical, and system-level failures while documenting root causes and corrective actions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Execute validation and test procedures to ensure repaired robots meet operational and performance requirements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate service records that support fleet reliability analysis and continuous product improvement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify recurring failure trends and provide actionable feedback to Engineering and Operations teams.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Key Competencies</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong electromechanical troubleshooting and repair skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High attention to detail and craftsmanship when working on precision assemblies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to follow structured processes while maintaining a strong sense of ownership and accountability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear communicator who can document technical findings and collaborate across teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working in a fast-paced environment where priorities and challenges evolve quickly.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Minimum Requirements</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in robotics, manufacturing, aerospace, automotive, electronics, or another hands-on technical field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience assembling, maintaining, or repairing electromechanical systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to read and interpret technical drawings, schematics, and work instructions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience using measurement and diagnostic tools such as calipers, multimeters, torque tools, or similar equipment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work safely around electrical systems, lift components, and perform hands-on work for extended periods.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Preferred Skills</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working on robotic systems, automation equipment, or complex electromechanical products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with wiring harness repair, precision soldering, crimping, or connector assembly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with command-line tools, hardware diagnostics, or embedded system troubleshooting.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What does a successful 1X Team Member look like</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team members at 1X who thrive here are builders. They move fast, own their work completely, and treat time like it’s the one thing you can’t get back - because it is. They say what they mean, finish what they start, and hold themselves to a standard before anyone has to ask. We push each other to be better, and we do it with honesty and respect.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Compensation Range</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$25.00 - $34.00 per hour</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Benefits</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Generous paid time off, company holidays, and parental leave</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) plan with company match (100% on the first 3% of contributions, 50% on the next 2%)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA) and Health Savings Accounts (HSA) options</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Commuter benefits (transit and parking)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Short-term and long-term disability, and life insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, financial, and personal support</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Onsite snacks and catered lunches</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Equal Opportunity Employer</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1X is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, age, marital status, medical condition, genetic information, disability, military or veteran status, justice system impact, or any other characteristic protected under applicable federal, state, or local law.</p>","compensation":[{"type":"salary","summary":"$25 – $43 per hour • Offers Equity","salary_summary":null,"tiers":[{"title":null,"summary":"$25 – $43 per hour • Offers Equity","additional_information":null}]}],"custom_fields":{},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-24T20:50:05.208Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["robotics"],"role_matches":["Robot"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["robotics","ai-ml"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"ashby:1x:aea0150b-5690-422a-b43a-773c706305ff","source":{"type":"ashby","board":"1x","job_id":"aea0150b-5690-422a-b43a-773c706305ff","source_url":"https://api.ashbyhq.com/posting-api/job-board/1x","response_hash":"e2ee5617e0e3d5f1ad756b32fdf608e4011dc9acdf4787feb3ba5a3b3ec21e27","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"1X","slug":"1x","lists":["robotics","ai-ml"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Robot Service Technician","canonical_url":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/1x/aea0150b-5690-422a-b43a-773c706305ff","apply_url":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/1x/aea0150b-5690-422a-b43a-773c706305ff/application","locations":[{"label":"San Carlos, CA","city":"San Carlos","region":"California","country":"United States","remote":null,"hybrid":null}],"workplace_type":"on_site","employment_type":"full_time","departments":["Fleet Operations "],"teams":["Fleet Operations "],"language":null,"requisition_id":null,"internal_job_id":null,"first_published_at":"2026-08-07T18:45:21.610+00:00","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Shift: Day Shift\n\n\n\n\nABOUT 1X\n\nWe’re building humanoid robots that work in home - doing the chores, handling the tasks, and giving people their time back. Simple, but it’s not.\n\n\n\nTo do this right, we have to solve robotics, AI, manufacturing - at the same time, at scale, in a form factor that has to be safe enough to live with your family. If you’re inspired by this, you’ll thrive here. We’ve been at this since 2014 and we’re at the point where the hard problems are behind us and the hard work is in front of us.\n\n\n\nNEO is our flagship - a home robot designed to move, learn, and operate in the real world alongside real people. We’re not demoing it - we’re shipping it. We’re excited to meet you, if this excites you.\n\n\n\nIf you’ve spent your career working on problems that matter and want to see them actually reach the world - this is that moment. We’re scaling, we’re hiring with intention, and we need people who want to build something that will genuinely change how humans spend their time - safely creating abundance for all.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE TEAM\n\nThe Robot Services team is responsible for maintaining and improving the health of our deployed robotic fleet. As robots operate in customer homes and real-world environments, this team diagnoses failures, performs repairs, and partners closely with Engineering to improve reliability, serviceability, and overall fleet performance.\n\n\n\n\nYOUR CHARTER\n\nAs a Robot Service Technician, you will be responsible for diagnosing, repairing, testing, and validating humanoid robots and their subsystems. Your work will directly impact fleet uptime, product reliability, and the speed at which engineering teams can learn from real-world robot performance.\n\n\n\n\nKEY OUTCOMES\n\n - Complete high-quality repairs and maintenance activities that return robots to service safely and efficiently.\n\n - Diagnose mechanical, electrical, and system-level failures while documenting root causes and corrective actions.\n\n - Execute validation and test procedures to ensure repaired robots meet operational and performance requirements.\n\n - Maintain accurate service records that support fleet reliability analysis and continuous product improvement.\n\n - Identify recurring failure trends and provide actionable feedback to Engineering and Operations teams.\n\n\n\n\nKEY COMPETENCIES\n\n - Strong electromechanical troubleshooting and repair skills.\n\n - High attention to detail and craftsmanship when working on precision assemblies.\n\n - Ability to follow structured processes while maintaining a strong sense of ownership and accountability.\n\n - Clear communicator who can document technical findings and collaborate across teams.\n\n - Comfortable working in a fast-paced environment where priorities and challenges evolve quickly.\n\n\n\n\nMINIMUM REQUIREMENTS\n\n - 2+ years of experience in robotics, manufacturing, aerospace, automotive, electronics, or another hands-on technical field.\n\n - Experience assembling, maintaining, or repairing electromechanical systems.\n\n - Ability to read and interpret technical drawings, schematics, and work instructions.\n\n - Experience using measurement and diagnostic tools such as calipers, multimeters, torque tools, or similar equipment.\n\n - Ability to work safely around electrical systems, lift components, and perform hands-on work for extended periods.\n\n\n\n\nPREFERRED SKILLS\n\n - Experience working on robotic systems, automation equipment, or complex electromechanical products.\n\n - Experience with wiring harness repair, precision soldering, crimping, or connector assembly.\n\n - Familiarity with command-line tools, hardware diagnostics, or embedded system troubleshooting.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT DOES A SUCCESSFUL 1X TEAM MEMBER LOOK LIKE\n\nTeam members at 1X who thrive here are builders. They move fast, own their work completely, and treat time like it’s the one thing you can’t get back - because it is. They say what they mean, finish what they start, and hold themselves to a standard before anyone has to ask. We push each other to be better, and we do it with honesty and respect.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION RANGE\n\n$25.00 - $34.00 per hour\n\n\n\n\nBENEFITS\n\n - Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage\n\n - Generous paid time off, company holidays, and parental leave\n\n - 401(k) plan with company match (100% on the first 3% of contributions, 50% on the next 2%)\n\n - Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA) and Health Savings Accounts (HSA) options\n\n - Commuter benefits (transit and parking)\n\n - Short-term and long-term disability, and life insurance\n\n - Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, financial, and personal support\n\n - Onsite snacks and catered lunches\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER\n\n1X is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, age, marital status, medical condition, genetic information, disability, military or veteran status, justice system impact, or any other characteristic protected under applicable federal, state, or local law.","description_html":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shift: </strong>Day Shift</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>About 1X</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re building humanoid robots that work in home - doing the chores, handling the tasks, and giving people their time back. Simple, but it’s not.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To do this right, we have to solve robotics, AI, manufacturing - at the same time, at scale, in a form factor that has to be safe enough to live with your family. If you’re inspired by this, you’ll thrive here. We’ve been at this since 2014 and we’re at the point where the hard problems are behind us and the hard work is in front of us.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">NEO is our flagship - a home robot designed to move, learn, and operate in the real world alongside real people. We’re not demoing it - we’re shipping it. We’re excited to meet you, if this excites you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you’ve spent your career working on problems that matter and want to see them actually reach the world - this is that moment. We’re scaling, we’re hiring with intention, and we need people who want to build something that will genuinely change how humans spend their time - safely creating abundance for all.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>About the Team</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Robot Services team is responsible for maintaining and improving the health of our deployed robotic fleet. As robots operate in customer homes and real-world environments, this team diagnoses failures, performs repairs, and partners closely with Engineering to improve reliability, serviceability, and overall fleet performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Your Charter</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Robot Service Technician, you will be responsible for diagnosing, repairing, testing, and validating humanoid robots and their subsystems. Your work will directly impact fleet uptime, product reliability, and the speed at which engineering teams can learn from real-world robot performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Key Outcomes</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Complete high-quality repairs and maintenance activities that return robots to service safely and efficiently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Diagnose mechanical, electrical, and system-level failures while documenting root causes and corrective actions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Execute validation and test procedures to ensure repaired robots meet operational and performance requirements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate service records that support fleet reliability analysis and continuous product improvement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify recurring failure trends and provide actionable feedback to Engineering and Operations teams.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Key Competencies</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong electromechanical troubleshooting and repair skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High attention to detail and craftsmanship when working on precision assemblies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to follow structured processes while maintaining a strong sense of ownership and accountability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear communicator who can document technical findings and collaborate across teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working in a fast-paced environment where priorities and challenges evolve quickly.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Minimum Requirements</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in robotics, manufacturing, aerospace, automotive, electronics, or another hands-on technical field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience assembling, maintaining, or repairing electromechanical systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to read and interpret technical drawings, schematics, and work instructions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience using measurement and diagnostic tools such as calipers, multimeters, torque tools, or similar equipment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work safely around electrical systems, lift components, and perform hands-on work for extended periods.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Preferred Skills</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working on robotic systems, automation equipment, or complex electromechanical products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with wiring harness repair, precision soldering, crimping, or connector assembly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with command-line tools, hardware diagnostics, or embedded system troubleshooting.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What does a successful 1X Team Member look like</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team members at 1X who thrive here are builders. They move fast, own their work completely, and treat time like it’s the one thing you can’t get back - because it is. They say what they mean, finish what they start, and hold themselves to a standard before anyone has to ask. We push each other to be better, and we do it with honesty and respect.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Compensation Range</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$25.00 - $34.00 per hour</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Benefits</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Generous paid time off, company holidays, and parental leave</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) plan with company match (100% on the first 3% of contributions, 50% on the next 2%)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA) and Health Savings Accounts (HSA) options</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Commuter benefits (transit and parking)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Short-term and long-term disability, and life insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, financial, and personal support</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Onsite snacks and catered lunches</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Equal Opportunity Employer</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1X is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, age, marital status, medical condition, genetic information, disability, military or veteran status, justice system impact, or any other characteristic protected under applicable federal, state, or local law.</p>","compensation":[{"type":"salary","summary":"$25 – $43 per hour • Offers Equity","salary_summary":null,"tiers":[{"title":null,"summary":"$25 – $43 per hour • Offers Equity","additional_information":null}]}],"custom_fields":{},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score