{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"greenhouse:andurilindustries:5174895007","source":{"type":"greenhouse","board":"andurilindustries","job_id":"5174895007","source_url":"https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/andurilindustries/jobs","response_hash":"a9f4087a591be92705e5e9aec06070dd92536a61d992b0796a07f4a3667e8ffc","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Anduril","slug":"anduril","lists":["robotics","ai-ml"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Head of Radar, Space","canonical_url":"https://boards.greenhouse.io/andurilindustries/jobs/5174895007?gh_jid=5174895007","apply_url":"https://boards.greenhouse.io/andurilindustries/jobs/5174895007?gh_jid=5174895007","locations":[{"label":"Costa Mesa, California, United States"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":["AFS : Space Engineering : Space Engineering"],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":"11505","internal_job_id":4650559007,"first_published_at":"2026-06-26T12:57:41-04:00","source_updated_at":"2026-08-24T14:07:42-04:00","application_deadline":null,"description_plain":null,"description_html":null,"compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"External Department Name for Job Board":"Radar","Employment Type":"Full-time","ET Talent Identifier":null,"Arsenal Launch Team":null},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":false,"tier":"stretch","score":0,"level":"executive","term":null,"tracks":[],"role_matches":[],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":["Head of"],"configured_tracks":["robotics","ai-ml"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"greenhouse:andurilindustries:5154234007","source":{"type":"greenhouse","board":"andurilindustries","job_id":"5154234007","source_url":"https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/andurilindustries/jobs","response_hash":"28a10c21bdf261e2d9a3abf8e0233876a0b3a38cf9bce6e429ab8e3dd993ccb3","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Anduril","slug":"anduril","lists":["robotics","ai-ml"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"HPC Systems Engineer, Modeling & Simulation","canonical_url":"https://boards.greenhouse.io/andurilindustries/jobs/5154234007?gh_jid=5154234007","apply_url":"https://boards.greenhouse.io/andurilindustries/jobs/5154234007?gh_jid=5154234007","locations":[{"label":"Costa Mesa, California, United States"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":["Hardware Platform : Hardware Engineering Services : Lethality"],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":"10743","internal_job_id":4640523007,"first_published_at":"2026-06-11T09:52:32-04:00","source_updated_at":"2026-08-24T14:07:42-04:00","application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.\n\nAbout the Team\n\nThe Lethality Modeling & Simulation team supports high-consequence engineering decisions through advanced modeling, simulation, and scientific computing. The team works across lethality, warhead effects, shock physics, detonation physics, solid mechanics, and related mission-critical analysis areas.\n\nThis work depends on reliable high-performance computing systems, specialized scientific codes, secure operating environments, and data workflows that allow analysts and engineers to move quickly. The team operates in an on-premises HPC environment and partners closely with engineering, analysis, IT, security, and specialized vendor partners.\n\nAbout the Job\n\nAnduril is looking for an HPC Systems Administrator to support the computing environment used by the Lethality Modeling & Simulation team. This is not a traditional corporate IT administrator role. You will help administer and improve the on-prem HPC systems, scientific code environments, storage, runtime workflows, and tooling that enable analysts to run complex modeling and simulation workloads.\n\nIn this role, you will maintain and troubleshoot scientific computing systems, support Linux/Unix-based infrastructure, help manage storage and compute resources, and partner with analysts to resolve issues across code, nodes, queues, storage, and user workflows. You will also help develop tools, scripts, and data workflows that improve analyst productivity.\n\nThe ideal candidate has experience supporting HPC, scientific computing, research computing, or secure engineering computing environments. This role is scoped for a mid-level to senior individual contributor, with final level determined by depth of HPC experience, independence, technical ownership, and ability to lead improvements across the environment.\n\nWhat You’ll Do\n\n- Administer and support on-prem HPC systems used for lethality modeling and simulation workflows\n\n- Maintain, install, update, and troubleshoot scientific codes and runtime environments\n\n- Diagnose issues across code, compute nodes, operating systems, storage, queues, and user workflows\n\n- Support Linux, Unix, and Windows administration across a specialized engineering computing environment\n\n- Manage or support storage, data movement, and filesystem needs tied to modeling and simulation outputs\n\n- Build scripts, automation, and tools that improve analyst productivity and reduce manual workflow friction\n\n- Partner with analysts, engineers, security teams, and vendor partners to improve reliability, usability, and secure operation of the environment\n\n- Support the team’s path toward classified computing readiness\n\n- Impact You’ll Have\n\n- Enable the Lethality Modeling & Simulation team to spend more time on mission-critical analysis and less time troubleshooting computing environments\n\n- Improve the reliability and repeatability of scientific code execution across HPC systems, storage, and analyst workflows\n\n- Help scale the team’s modeling and simulation capability by building better tooling, automation, and data workflows\n\n- Strengthen the team’s secure computing foundation as Anduril expands into more sensitive and classified analysis environments\n\nRequired Qualifications\n\n- 5+ years of experience administering Linux/Unix systems in HPC, scientific computing, research computing, defense, aerospace, national lab, or similarly complex technical environments\n\n- Hands-on experience supporting compute clusters, scientific codes, engineering software, or modeling and simulation workflows\n\n- Experience with Bash and/or Python scripting for automation, troubleshooting, or workflow support\n\n- Experience with scientific codes or tools such as CTH, ALE3D, Sierra, ParaView, Cubit, VisIt, hydrocodes, solid mechanics codes, or adjacent simulation tools\n\n- Experience with scientific software build/runtime environments, including tools such as CMake, compilers, MPI/OpenMPI, OpenMP, environment modules, or similar technologies\n\n- Working knowledge of storage, filesystems, networking, and secure computing practices, including NFS/NAS, TCP/IP, trusted software sources, and data handling practices\n\n- Bachelor’s or master’s degree in computer science, Computational Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Scientific Computing, or a related technical discipline\n\n- Ability to work onsite and obtain and maintain a U.S. security clearance\n\n- Must be a U.S. Person due to required access to U.S. export controlled information or facilities\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n- Current or prior U.S. security clearance; DOE, DoD, NNSA, or classified computing experience strongly preferred\n\n- Experience in a National Laboratory, DoD research, defense, aerospace, or secure scientific computing environment\n\n- Experience with Slurm or comparable HPC scheduling and cluster management tools\n\n- Experience developing tools that improve analyst, researcher, or engineering productivity\n\nUS Salary Range\n$132,000 — $198,000 USD\n\nThe salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril's total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:\n\nBenefits\n\nAt Anduril, we invest in our people. Our comprehensive, competitive benefits package (available at little to no cost to employees) ensures you’re supported in health, recovery, and whatever comes next. For more information, Explore Our Benefits .\n\nProtecting Yourself from Recruitment Scams\n\nAnduril is committed to maintaining the integrity of our Talent acquisition process and the security of our candidates. We've observed a rise in sophisticated phishing and fraudulent schemes where individuals impersonate Anduril representatives, luring job seekers with false interviews or job offers. These scammers often attempt to extract payment or sensitive personal information.\n\nTo ensure your safety and help you navigate your job search with confidence, please keep the following critical points in mind:\n\n-\nNo Financial Requests: Anduril will never solicit payment or demand personal financial details (such as banking information, credit card numbers, or social security numbers) at any stage of our hiring process. Our legitimate recruitment is entirely free for candidates.\n\n- Please always verify communications:\n\n- Direct from Anduril: If you receive an email from one of our recruiters, it will only come from an @anduril.com address.\n\n- Via Agency Partner: If contacted by a recruiting agency for an Anduril role, their email will clearly identify their agency. If you suspect any suspicious activity, please verify the agency's authenticity by reaching out to contact@anduril.com .\n\n-\nExercise Caution with Unsolicited Outreach: If you receive any communication that appears suspicious, contains grammatical errors, or makes unusual requests, do not engage. Always confirm the sender's email domain is @anduril.com before providing any personal information or clicking on links.\n\n-\nWhat to Do If You Suspect Fraud: Should you encounter any questionable or fraudulent outreach claiming to be from Anduril, please report it immediately to contact@anduril.com . Your proactive caution is invaluable in protecting your personal information and upholding the security and trustworthiness of our recruitment efforts.\n\nData Privacy\n\nTo view Anduril's candidate data privacy policy, please visit https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/ .\n\nBy submitting your application, you consent to Anduril Industries using a third-party service provider to conduct pre-employment risk, integrity, and due diligence screening and assessing potential risks as part of your application process. This third-party service provider provides risk-intelligence services that may include analysis of sanctions and watchlists, adverse media, public-record information, and other lawful open-source or commercial data sources. This third-party service provider does not act as a consumer reporting agency. Use of this provider helps to ensure compliance with applicable laws and protect technology, intellectual property, and organizational security.","description_html":"<div class=\"content-intro\"><p>Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.</p></div><p><strong>About the Team</strong></p>\n<p>The Lethality Modeling &amp; Simulation team supports high-consequence engineering decisions through advanced modeling, simulation, and scientific computing. The team works across lethality, warhead effects, shock physics, detonation physics, solid mechanics, and related mission-critical analysis areas.</p>\n<p>This work depends on reliable high-performance computing systems, specialized scientific codes, secure operating environments, and data workflows that allow analysts and engineers to move quickly. The team operates in an on-premises HPC environment and partners closely with engineering, analysis, IT, security, and specialized vendor partners.</p>\n<p><strong>About the Job</strong></p>\n<p>Anduril is looking for an HPC Systems Administrator to support the computing environment used by the Lethality Modeling &amp; Simulation team. This is not a traditional corporate IT administrator role. You will help administer and improve the on-prem HPC systems, scientific code environments, storage, runtime workflows, and tooling that enable analysts to run complex modeling and simulation workloads.</p>\n<p>In this role, you will maintain and troubleshoot scientific computing systems, support Linux/Unix-based infrastructure, help manage storage and compute resources, and partner with analysts to resolve issues across code, nodes, queues, storage, and user workflows. You will also help develop tools, scripts, and data workflows that improve analyst productivity.</p>\n<p>The ideal candidate has experience supporting HPC, scientific computing, research computing, or secure engineering computing environments. This role is scoped for a mid-level to senior individual contributor, with final level determined by depth of HPC experience, independence, technical ownership, and ability to lead improvements across the environment.</p>\n<p><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Administer and support on-prem HPC systems used for lethality modeling and simulation workflows</li>\n<li>Maintain, install, update, and troubleshoot scientific codes and runtime environments</li>\n<li>Diagnose issues across code, compute nodes, operating systems, storage, queues, and user workflows</li>\n<li>Support Linux, Unix, and Windows administration across a specialized engineering computing environment</li>\n<li>Manage or support storage, data movement, and filesystem needs tied to modeling and simulation outputs</li>\n<li>Build scripts, automation, and tools that improve analyst productivity and reduce manual workflow friction</li>\n<li>Partner with analysts, engineers, security teams, and vendor partners to improve reliability, usability, and secure operation of the environment</li>\n<li>Support the team’s path toward classified computing readiness</li>\n<li><strong><em>Impact You’ll Have</em></strong></li>\n<ul>\n<li>Enable the Lethality Modeling &amp; Simulation team to spend more time on mission-critical analysis and less time troubleshooting computing environments</li>\n<li>Improve the reliability and repeatability of scientific code execution across HPC systems, storage, and analyst workflows</li>\n<li>Help scale the team’s modeling and simulation capability by building better tooling, automation, and data workflows</li>\n<li>Strengthen the team’s secure computing foundation as Anduril expands into more sensitive and classified analysis environments</li>\n</ul>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Required Qualifications</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>5+ years of experience administering Linux/Unix systems in HPC, scientific computing, research computing, defense, aerospace, national lab, or similarly complex technical environments</li>\n<li>Hands-on experience supporting compute clusters, scientific codes, engineering software, or modeling and simulation workflows</li>\n<li>Experience with Bash and/or Python scripting for automation, troubleshooting, or workflow support</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>Experience with scientific codes or tools such as CTH, ALE3D, Sierra, ParaView, Cubit, VisIt, hydrocodes, solid mechanics codes, or adjacent simulation tools</li>\n<li>Experience with scientific software build/runtime environments, including tools such as CMake, compilers, MPI/OpenMPI, OpenMP, environment modules, or similar technologies</li>\n<li>Working knowledge of storage, filesystems, networking, and secure computing practices, including NFS/NAS, TCP/IP, trusted software sources, and data handling practices</li>\n<li>Bachelor’s or master’s degree in computer science, Computational Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Scientific Computing, or a related technical discipline</li>\n<li>Ability to work onsite and obtain and maintain a U.S. security clearance</li>\n<li>Must be a U.S. Person due to required access to U.S. export controlled information or facilities</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Current or prior U.S. security clearance; DOE, DoD, NNSA, or classified computing experience strongly preferred</li>\n<li>Experience in a National Laboratory, DoD research, defense, aerospace, or secure scientific computing environment</li>\n<li>Experience with Slurm or comparable HPC scheduling and cluster management tools</li>\n<li>Experience developing tools that improve analyst, researcher, or engineering productivity</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><div class=\"content-pay-transparency\"><div class=\"pay-input\"><div class=\"title\">US Salary Range</div><div class=\"pay-range\"><span>$132,000</span><span class=\"divider\">&mdash;</span><span>$198,000 USD</span></div></div></div><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">The salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril's total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h3 class=\"detailElios\"><strong>Benefits</strong></h3>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">At Anduril, we invest in our people. Our comprehensive, competitive benefits package (available at little to no cost to employees) ensures you’re supported in health, recovery, and whatever comes next.&nbsp;</span><em><span data-contrast=\"auto\">For more information, <a href=\"https://www.anduril.com/careers\">Explore Our Benefits</a>.</span></em></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div class=\"RichText column1\">\n<h3 class=\"detailElios\"><strong>Protecting Yourself from Recruitment Scams</strong></h3>\n<p class=\"detailElios\">Anduril is committed to maintaining the integrity of our Talent acquisition process and the security of our candidates. We've observed a rise in sophisticated phishing and fraudulent schemes where individuals impersonate Anduril representatives, luring job seekers with false interviews or job offers. These scammers often attempt to extract payment or sensitive personal information.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"RichText column2\">\n<p class=\"detailElios\">To ensure your safety and help you navigate your job search with confidence, please keep the following critical points in mind:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p class=\"detailElios\"><strong>No Financial Requests:&nbsp;</strong>Anduril will never solicit payment or demand personal financial details (such as banking information, credit card numbers, or social security numbers) at any stage of our hiring process. Our legitimate recruitment is entirely free for candidates.</p>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Please always verify communications:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Direct from Anduril: If you receive an email from one of our recruiters, it will <em>only</em> come from an <code>@anduril.com</code> address.</li>\n<li>Via Agency Partner: If contacted by a recruiting agency for an Anduril role, their email will clearly identify their agency. If you suspect any suspicious activity, please verify the agency's authenticity by reaching out to <a href=\"mailto:contact@anduril.com\">contact@anduril.com</a>.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p class=\"detailElios\"><strong>Exercise Caution with Unsolicited Outreach:</strong>&nbsp;If you receive any communication that appears suspicious, contains grammatical errors, or makes unusual requests, do not engage. Always confirm the sender's email domain is @anduril.com before providing any personal information or clicking on links.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p class=\"detailElios\"><strong>What to Do If You Suspect Fraud:</strong>&nbsp;Should you encounter any questionable or fraudulent outreach claiming to be from Anduril, please report it immediately to&nbsp;<a href=\"mailto:contact@anduril.com\">contact@anduril.com</a>. Your proactive caution is invaluable in protecting your personal information and upholding the security and trustworthiness of our recruitment efforts.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3>&nbsp;</h3>\n<h3><strong>Data Privacy</strong></h3>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">To view Anduril's candidate data privacy policy, please visit </span><span data-contrast=\"none\"><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink\"><a href=\"https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/\">https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/</a></span></span><span data-contrast=\"auto\">.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">By submitting your application, you consent to Anduril Industries using a third-party service provider to conduct pre-employment risk, integrity, and due diligence screening and assessing potential risks as part of your application process. This third-party service provider provides risk-intelligence services that may include analysis of sanctions and watchlists, adverse media, public-record information, and other lawful open-source or commercial data sources. This third-party service provider does not act as a consumer reporting agency. Use of this provider helps to ensure compliance with applicable laws and protect technology, intellectual property, and organizational security.</span></p></div>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"External Department Name for Job Board":"Software","Employment Type":"Full-time","ET Talent Identifier":null,"Arsenal Launch Team":null},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Systems Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["robotics","ai-ml"]}}
