ke the Fury unmanned fighter jet and the Barracuda family of advanced effects. The AD&S Vehicle Software team is responsible for the software running on these systems. Our software engineers collaborate with other engineering disciplines to develop software for vehicle control, networking, sensor integration, and telemetry. We are looking for engineers excited to build the foundational vehicle software stack that supports the wide range of AD&S initiatives, from early concept simulation to first flight to live operations to large scale fleet management.\n\nREQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS\n\n- Eligible to obtain and maintain an active U.S. Top Secret security clearance\n\n- BS, MS, or PhD in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Mathematics, Physics, or related field.\n\n- 3+ years of production-grade C++ and/or Rust experience in a Linux development environment\n\n- Experience building software solutions involving significant amounts of data processing and analysis\n\n- Ability to quickly understand and navigate complex systems and established code bases\n\n- A desire to work on critical software that has a real-world impact\n\n- Travel up to 30% of time to build, test, and deploy capabilities in the real world\n\nPREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS\n\n- Strong background with focus in Physics, Mathematics, and/or Motion Planning to inform modeling & simulation (M&S) and physical systems\n\n- Developing and testing multi-agent autonomous systems and deploying in real-world environments.\n\n- Feature and algorithm development with an understanding of behavior trees.\n\n- Developing software/hardware for flight systems and safety critical functionality.\n\n- Distributed communication networks and message standards\n\n- Knowledge of military systems and operational tactics\n\nUS Salary Range\n$166,000 — $220,000 USD\n\nThe salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril's total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:\n\nBenefits\n\nAt Anduril, we invest in our people. Our comprehensive, competitive benefits package (available at little to no cost to employees) ensures you’re supported in health, recovery, and whatever comes next. For more information, Explore Our Benefits .\n\nProtecting Yourself from Recruitment Scams\n\nAnduril is committed to maintaining the integrity of our Talent acquisition process and the security of our candidates. We've observed a rise in sophisticated phishing and fraudulent schemes where individuals impersonate Anduril representatives, luring job seekers with false interviews or job offers. These scammers often attempt to extract payment or sensitive personal information.\n\nTo ensure your safety and help you navigate your job search with confidence, please keep the following critical points in mind:\n\n-\nNo Financial Requests: Anduril will never solicit payment or demand personal financial details (such as banking information, credit card numbers, or social security numbers) at any stage of our hiring process. Our legitimate recruitment is entirely free for candidates.\n\n- Please always verify communications:\n\n- Direct from Anduril: If you receive an email from one of our recruiters, it will only come from an @anduril.com address.\n\n- Via Agency Partner: If contacted by a recruiting agency for an Anduril role, their email will clearly identify their agency. If you suspect any suspicious activity, please verify the agency's authenticity by reaching out to contact@anduril.com .\n\n-\nExercise Caution with Unsolicited Outreach: If you receive any communication that appears suspicious, contains grammatical errors, or makes unusual requests, do not engage. Always confirm the sender's email domain is @anduril.com before providing any personal information or clicking on links.\n\n-\nWhat to Do If You Suspect Fraud: Should you encounter any questionable or fraudulent outreach claiming to be from Anduril, please report it immediately to contact@anduril.com . Your proactive caution is invaluable in protecting your personal information and upholding the security and trustworthiness of our recruitment efforts.\n\nData Privacy\n\nTo view Anduril's candidate data privacy policy, please visit https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/ .\n\nBy submitting your application, you consent to Anduril Industries using a third-party service provider to conduct pre-employment risk, integrity, and due diligence screening and assessing potential risks as part of your application process. This third-party service provider provides risk-intelligence services that may include analysis of sanctions and watchlists, adverse media, public-record information, and other lawful open-source or commercial data sources. This third-party service provider does not act as a consumer reporting agency. Use of this provider helps to ensure compliance with applicable laws and protect technology, intellectual property, and organizational security.","description_html":"<div class=\"content-intro\"><p>Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.</p></div><h3><strong>ABOUT THE TEAM</strong></h3>\n<p>Air Dominance &amp; Strike (AD&amp;S) is responsible for autonomous robotics systems like the Fury unmanned fighter jet and the Barracuda family of advanced effects. The AD&amp;S Vehicle Software team is responsible for the software running on these systems. Our software engineers collaborate with other engineering disciplines to develop software for vehicle control, networking, sensor integration, and telemetry. We are looking for engineers excited to build the foundational vehicle software stack that supports the wide range of AD&amp;S initiatives, from early concept simulation to first flight to live operations to large scale fleet management.</p>\n<h4><strong>REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Eligible to obtain and maintain an active U.S. Top Secret security clearance</li>\n<li>BS, MS, or PhD in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Mathematics, Physics, or related field.</li>\n<li>3+ years of production-grade C++ and/or Rust experience in a Linux development environment</li>\n<li>Experience building software solutions involving significant amounts of data processing and analysis</li>\n<li>Ability to quickly understand and navigate complex systems and established code bases</li>\n<li>A desire to work on critical software that has a real-world impact</li>\n<li>Travel up to 30% of time to build, test, and deploy capabilities in the real world</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><strong>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Strong background with focus in Physics, Mathematics, and/or Motion Planning to inform modeling &amp; simulation (M&amp;S) and physical systems</li>\n<li>Developing and testing multi-agent autonomous systems and deploying in real-world environments.</li>\n<li>Feature and algorithm development with an understanding of behavior trees.</li>\n<li>Developing software/hardware for flight systems and safety critical functionality.</li>\n<li>Distributed communication networks and message standards</li>\n<li>Knowledge of military systems and operational tactics</li>\n</ul><div class=\"content-pay-transparency\"><div class=\"pay-input\"><div class=\"title\">US Salary Range</div><div class=\"pay-range\"><span>$166,000</span><span class=\"divider\">&mdash;</span><span>$220,000 USD</span></div></div></div><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">The salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril's total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h3 class=\"detailElios\"><strong>Benefits</strong></h3>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">At Anduril, we invest in our people. Our comprehensive, competitive benefits package (available at little to no cost to employees) ensures you’re supported in health, recovery, and whatever comes next.&nbsp;</span><em><span data-contrast=\"auto\">For more information, <a href=\"https://www.anduril.com/careers\">Explore Our Benefits</a>.</span></em></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div class=\"RichText column1\">\n<h3 class=\"detailElios\"><strong>Protecting Yourself from Recruitment Scams</strong></h3>\n<p class=\"detailElios\">Anduril is committed to maintaining the integrity of our Talent acquisition process and the security of our candidates. We've observed a rise in sophisticated phishing and fraudulent schemes where individuals impersonate Anduril representatives, luring job seekers with false interviews or job offers. These scammers often attempt to extract payment or sensitive personal information.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"RichText column2\">\n<p class=\"detailElios\">To ensure your safety and help you navigate your job search with confidence, please keep the following critical points in mind:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p class=\"detailElios\"><strong>No Financial Requests:&nbsp;</strong>Anduril will never solicit payment or demand personal financial details (such as banking information, credit card numbers, or social security numbers) at any stage of our hiring process. Our legitimate recruitment is entirely free for candidates.</p>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Please always verify communications:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Direct from Anduril: If you receive an email from one of our recruiters, it will <em>only</em> come from an <code>@anduril.com</code> address.</li>\n<li>Via Agency Partner: If contacted by a recruiting agency for an Anduril role, their email will clearly identify their agency. If you suspect any suspicious activity, please verify the agency's authenticity by reaching out to <a href=\"mailto:contact@anduril.com\">contact@anduril.com</a>.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p class=\"detailElios\"><strong>Exercise Caution with Unsolicited Outreach:</strong>&nbsp;If you receive any communication that appears suspicious, contains grammatical errors, or makes unusual requests, do not engage. Always confirm the sender's email domain is @anduril.com before providing any personal information or clicking on links.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p class=\"detailElios\"><strong>What to Do If You Suspect Fraud:</strong>&nbsp;Should you encounter any questionable or fraudulent outreach claiming to be from Anduril, please report it immediately to&nbsp;<a href=\"mailto:contact@anduril.com\">contact@anduril.com</a>. Your proactive caution is invaluable in protecting your personal information and upholding the security and trustworthiness of our recruitment efforts.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3>&nbsp;</h3>\n<h3><strong>Data Privacy</strong></h3>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">To view Anduril's candidate data privacy policy, please visit </span><span data-contrast=\"none\"><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink\"><a href=\"https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/\">https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/</a></span></span><span data-contrast=\"auto\">.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">By submitting your application, you consent to Anduril Industries using a third-party service provider to conduct pre-employment risk, integrity, and due diligence screening and assessing potential risks as part of your application process. This third-party service provider provides risk-intelligence services that may include analysis of sanctions and watchlists, adverse media, public-record information, and other lawful open-source or commercial data sources. This third-party service provider does not act as a consumer reporting agency. Use of this provider helps to ensure compliance with applicable laws and protect technology, intellectual property, and organizational security.</span></p></div>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"External Department Name for Job Board":"Software","Employment Type":"Full-time","ET Talent Identifier":null,"Arsenal Launch Team":null},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["robotics","ai-ml"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"greenhouse:andurilindustries:5176751007","source":{"type":"greenhouse","board":"andurilindustries","job_id":"5176751007","source_url":"https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/andurilindustries/jobs","response_hash":"db56caa24acc6442a6aae9304f9e22e89234ed8ed78934e7036d4ff397992550","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Anduril","slug":"anduril","lists":["robotics","ai-ml"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Mission Software Engineer, Vehicle Software, Communications","canonical_url":"https://boards.greenhouse.io/andurilindustries/jobs/5176751007?gh_jid=5176751007","apply_url":"https://boards.greenhouse.io/andurilindustries/jobs/5176751007?gh_jid=5176751007","locations":[{"label":"Boston, Massachusetts, United States; Costa Mesa, California, United States"},{"label":"Costa Mesa, California, United States"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":["Air Dominance & Strike : Air Dominance & Strike Engineering : Mission Software Engineering"],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":"2554","internal_job_id":4395701007,"first_published_at":"2026-06-30T00:17:03-04:00","source_updated_at":"2026-08-24T14:07:42-04:00","application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.\n\nABOUT THE TEAM\n\nThe Air Dominance & Strike team at Anduril develops aerial and multi-domain robotic systems. The team is responsible for taking products like Fury (unmanned fighter jet) and Barracuda (air-breathing cruise missile) from concept to product. The team also develops Lattice for Mission Autonomy, Anduril’s premier software platform that enables masses of Fury, Barracuda, and other first and third party robots to collaborate across various missions. We work in close coordination with specialist teams like Perception, Motion Planning, Hardware, and Test Engineering to solve some of the hardest problems facing our customers.\n\nWe're seeking Software Engineers to build the core Command and Control software for our Lattice platform. This team is responsible for bridging the gap between hardware and human operators. Our software runs both on the vehicles managing real-time telemetry, health, and autopilot tasks and on the Ground Control Station enabling operators to plan missions, visualize maps, manage massive fleets, and orchestrate complex autonomous behaviors. We are also pioneering the integration of GenAI agents into our systems, allowing operators to direct autonomous assets using natural language interfaces. This is a highly autonomous role where you will build, ship, and see your code run on physical hardware deployed in the world.\n\nREQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS\n\n- Eligible to obtain and maintain an active U.S. Top Secret security clearance\n\n- BS, MS, or PhD in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Mathematics, Physics, or related field.\n\n- 3+ years of production-grade C++ and/or Rust experience in a Linux development environment\n\n- Integrate autonomous systems with military radio links such as Link 16 and other third-party waveforms\n\n- Build robust link-switching logic that keeps the mission running through degraded RF environments\n\n- Design and implement failure modes for lost-comms scenarios so vehicles act decisively when the link drops\n\n- Experience building software solutions involving significant amounts of data processing and analysis\n\n- Ability to quickly understand and navigate complex systems and established code bases\n\n- A desire to work on critical software that has a real-world impact\n\n- Travel up to 30% of time to build, test, and deploy capabilities in the real world\n\nPREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS\n\n- Strong background with focus in Physics, Mathematics, and/or Motion Planning to inform modeling & simulation (M&S) and physical systems\n\n- Developing and testing multi-agent autonomous systems and deploying in real-world environments.\n\n- Feature and algorithm development with an understanding of behavior trees.\n\n- Developing software/hardware for flight systems and safety critical functionality.\n\n- Distributed communication networks and message standards\n\n- Knowledge of military systems and operational tactics\n\nUS Salary Range\n$166,000 — $220,000 USD\n\nThe salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril's total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:\n\nBenefits\n\nAt Anduril, we invest in our people. Our comprehensive, competitive benefits package (available at little to no cost to employees) ensures you’re supported in health, recovery, and whatever comes next. For more information, Explore Our Benefits .\n\nProtecting Yourself from Recruitment Scams\n\nAnduril is committed to maintaining the integrity of our Talent acquisition process and the security of our candidates. We've observed a rise in sophisticated phishing and fraudulent schemes where individuals impersonate Anduril representatives, luring job seekers with false interviews or job offers. These scammers often attempt to extract payment or sensitive personal information.\n\nTo ensure your safety and help you navigate your job search with confidence, please keep the following critical points in mind:\n\n-\nNo Financial Requests: Anduril will never solicit payment or demand personal financial details (such as banking information, credit card numbers, or social security numbers) at any stage of our hiring process. Our legitimate recruitment is entirely free for candidates.\n\n- Please always verify communications:\n\n- Direct from Anduril: If you receive an email from one of our recruiters, it will only come from an @anduril.com address.\n\n- Via Agency Partner: If contacted by a recruiting agency for an Anduril role, their email will clearly identify their agency. If you suspect any suspicious activity, please verify the agency's authenticity by reaching out to contact@anduril.com .\n\n-\nExercise Caution with Unsolicited Outreach: If you receive any communication that appears suspicious, contains grammatical errors, or makes unusual requests, do not engage. Always confirm the sender's email domain is @anduril.com before providing any personal information or clicking on links.\n\n-\nWhat to Do If You Suspect Fraud: Should you encounter any questionable or fraudulent outreach claiming to be from Anduril, please report it immediately to contact@anduril.com . Your proactive caution is invaluable in protecting your personal information and upholding the security and trustworthiness of our recruitment efforts.\n\nData Privacy\n\nTo view Anduril's candidate data privacy policy, please visit https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/ .\n\nBy submitting your application, you consent to Anduril Industries using a third-party service provider to conduct pre-employment risk, integrity, and due diligence screening and assessing potential risks as part of your application process. This third-party service provider provides risk-intelligence services that may include analysis of sanctions and watchlists, adverse media, public-record information, and other lawful open-source or commercial data sources. This third-party service provider does not act as a consumer reporting agency. Use of this provider helps to ensure compliance with applicable laws and protect technology, intellectual property, and organizational security.","description_html":"<div class=\"content-intro\"><p>Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.</p></div><h3><strong>ABOUT THE TEAM</strong></h3>\n<p>The Air Dominance &amp; Strike team at Anduril develops aerial and multi-domain robotic systems. The team is responsible for taking products like Fury (unmanned fighter jet) and Barracuda (air-breathing cruise missile) from concept to product. The team also develops Lattice for Mission Autonomy, Anduril’s premier software platform that enables masses of Fury, Barracuda, and other first and third party robots to collaborate across various missions. We work in close coordination with specialist teams like Perception, Motion Planning, Hardware, and Test Engineering to solve some of the hardest problems facing our customers.</p>\n<p>We're seeking Software Engineers to build the core Command and Control software for our Lattice platform. This team is responsible for bridging the gap between hardware and human operators. Our software runs both on the vehicles managing real-time telemetry, health, and autopilot tasks and on the Ground Control Station enabling operators to plan missions, visualize maps, manage massive fleets, and orchestrate complex autonomous behaviors. We are also pioneering the integration of GenAI agents into our systems, allowing operators to direct autonomous assets using natural language interfaces. This is a highly autonomous role where you will build, ship, and see your code run on physical hardware deployed in the world.</p>\n<h4><strong>REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Eligible to obtain and maintain an active U.S. Top Secret security clearance</li>\n<li>BS, MS, or PhD in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Mathematics, Physics, or related field.</li>\n<li>3+ years of production-grade C++ and/or Rust experience in a Linux development environment</li>\n<li>Integrate autonomous systems with military radio links such as Link 16 and other third-party waveforms</li>\n<li>Build robust link-switching logic that keeps the mission running through degraded RF environments</li>\n<li>Design and implement failure modes for lost-comms scenarios so vehicles act decisively when the link drops</li>\n<li>Experience building software solutions involving significant amounts of data processing and analysis</li>\n<li>Ability to quickly understand and navigate complex systems and established code bases</li>\n<li>A desire to work on critical software that has a real-world impact</li>\n<li>Travel up to 30% of time to build, test, and deploy capabilities in the real world</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><strong>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Strong background with focus in Physics, Mathematics, and/or Motion Planning to inform modeling &amp; simulation (M&amp;S) and physical systems</li>\n<li>Developing and testing multi-agent autonomous systems and deploying in real-world environments.</li>\n<li>Feature and algorithm development with an understanding of behavior trees.</li>\n<li>Developing software/hardware for flight systems and safety critical functionality.</li>\n<li>Distributed communication networks and message standards</li>\n<li>Knowledge of military systems and operational tactics</li>\n</ul><div class=\"content-pay-transparency\"><div class=\"pay-input\"><div class=\"title\">US Salary Range</div><div class=\"pay-range\"><span>$166,000</span><span class=\"divider\">&mdash;</span><span>$220,000 USD</span></div></div></div><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">The salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril's total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h3 class=\"detailElios\"><strong>Benefits</strong></h3>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">At Anduril, we invest in our people. Our comprehensive, competitive benefits package (available at little to no cost to employees) ensures you’re supported in health, recovery, and whatever comes next.&nbsp;</span><em><span data-contrast=\"auto\">For more information, <a href=\"https://www.anduril.com/careers\">Explore Our Benefits</a>.</span></em></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div class=\"RichText column1\">\n<h3 class=\"detailElios\"><strong>Protecting Yourself from Recruitment Scams</strong></h3>\n<p class=\"detailElios\">Anduril is committed to maintaining the integrity of our Talent acquisition process and the security of our candidates. We've observed a rise in sophisticated phishing and fraudulent schemes where individuals impersonate Anduril representatives, luring job seekers with false interviews or job offers. These scammers often attempt to extract payment or sensitive personal information.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"RichText column2\">\n<p class=\"detailElios\">To ensure your safety and help you navigate your job search with confidence, please keep the following critical points in mind:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p class=\"detailElios\"><strong>No Financial Requests:&nbsp;</strong>Anduril will never solicit payment or demand personal financial details (such as banking information, credit card numbers, or social security numbers) at any stage of our hiring process. Our legitimate recruitment is entirely free for candidates.</p>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Please always verify communications:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Direct from Anduril: If you receive an email from one of our recruiters, it will <em>only</em> come from an <code>@anduril.com</code> address.</li>\n<li>Via Agency Partner: If contacted by a recruiting agency for an Anduril role, their email will clearly identify their agency. If you suspect any suspicious activity, please verify the agency's authenticity by reaching out to <a href=\"mailto:contact@anduril.com\">contact@anduril.com</a>.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p class=\"detailElios\"><strong>Exercise Caution with Unsolicited Outreach:</strong>&nbsp;If you receive any communication that appears suspicious, contains grammatical errors, or makes unusual requests, do not engage. Always confirm the sender's email domain is @anduril.com before providing any personal information or clicking on links.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p class=\"detailElios\"><strong>What to Do If You Suspect Fraud:</strong>&nbsp;Should you encounter any questionable or fraudulent outreach claiming to be from Anduril, please report it immediately to&nbsp;<a href=\"mailto:contact@anduril.com\">contact@anduril.com</a>. Your proactive caution is invaluable in protecting your personal information and upholding the security and trustworthiness of our recruitment efforts.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3>&nbsp;</h3>\n<h3><strong>Data Privacy</strong></h3>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">To view Anduril's candidate data privacy policy, please visit </span><span data-contrast=\"none\"><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink\"><a href=\"https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/\">https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/</a></span></span><span data-contrast=\"auto\">.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">By submitting your application, you consent to Anduril Industries using a third-party service provider to conduct pre-employment risk, integrity, and due diligence screening and assessing potential risks as part of your application process. This third-party service provider provides risk-intelligence services that may include analysis of sanctions and watchlists, adverse media, public-record information, and other lawful open-source or commercial data sources. This third-party service provider does not act as a consumer reporting agency. Use of this provider helps to ensure compliance with applicable laws and protect technology, intellectual property, and organizational security.</span></p></div>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"External Department Name for Job Board":"Software","Employment Type":"Full-time","ET Talent Identifier":null,"Arsenal Launch Team":null},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["robotics","ai-ml"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"greenhouse:andurilindustries:4734570007","source":{"type":"greenhouse","board":"andurilindustries","job_id":"4734570007","source_url":"https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/andurilindustries/jobs","response_hash":"5e368ab5182ea95e837d095034fe2eaa24f5cca912e6d4ee4f4d061599cf62fa","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Anduril","slug":"anduril","lists":["robotics","ai-ml"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Mission Software Engineer, Vehicle Software, Computer Vision","canonical_url":"https://boards.greenhouse.io/andurilindustries/jobs/4734570007?gh_jid=4734570007","apply_url":"https://boards.greenhouse.io/andurilindustries/jobs/4734570007?gh_jid=4734570007","locations":[{"label":"Costa Mesa, California, United States"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":["Air Dominance & Strike : Air Dominance & Strike Engineering : Mission Software Engineering"],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":"3447","internal_job_id":4425751007,"first_published_at":"2025-05-14T14:42:23-04:00","source_updated_at":"2026-08-24T14:07:42-04:00","application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.\n\nABOUT THE TEAM\n\nAir Dominance & Strike (AD&S) is responsible for autonomous robotics systems like the Fury unmanned fighter jet and the Barracuda family of advanced effects. The AD&S Vehicle Software team is responsible for the software running on these systems. Our software engineers collaborate with other engineering disciplines to develop software for vehicle control, networking, sensor integration, and telemetry. We are looking for engineers excited to build the foundational vehicle software stack that supports the wide range of AD&S initiatives, from early concept simulation to first flight to live operations to large scale fleet management.\n\nABOUT THE JOB\n\nWe are seeking a software engineer specialized in machine vision for development of guidance systems on a large air vehicle. Engineers in this role will primarily work on implementing novel image processing algorithms from various image sources and sensors. These will be both conventional and state of the art machine learning approaches. Additionally, the role requires the ability to work with other sensor sources and develop sensor fusion algorithms.\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n- Integrate and write tests for camera calibration code\n\n- Develop and refine algorithms for real-time image processing and analysis.\n\n- Write, test, and maintain high-quality code in Python and C++.\n\n- Optimize software for performance, reliability, and scalability\n\n- Process and evaluate images from live tests used by camera systems in various flight conditions.\n\n- Debug and troubleshoot software and hardware issues as they arise.\n\n- Propose and implement improvements to enhance system performance and capabilities\n\nREQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS\n\n- BS, MS, or PhD in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, Mathematics, Physics, or related field.\n\n- 4+ years of experience writing production software (C or C++ preferred).\n\n- Direct experience with camera systems, calibration, and pose estimation.\n\n- Experience working with IMUs and implementing state fusion algorithms.\n\n- A desire to work on critical software that has a real-world impact\n\n- Eligible to obtain and maintain a U.S. Top Secret security clearance\n\nPREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS\n\n- Experience with SLAM systems.\n\n- Experience with estimation from RADAR or LIDAR systems.\n\n- General exposure to aviation concepts and aircraft design principles.\n\n- Experience working in airgapped environments (without network connectivity)\n\n- Knowledge of defense technology and tactics, especially in the air domain\n\n- Awareness of safety critical software development practices, including DO-178c and/or MIL-HDBK-516C.\n\nUS Salary Range\n$220,000 — $292,000 USD\n\nThe salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril's total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:\n\nBenefits\n\nAt Anduril, we invest in our people. Our comprehensive, competitive benefits package (available at little to no cost to employees) ensures you’re supported in health, recovery, and whatever comes next. For more information, Explore Our Benefits .\n\nProtecting Yourself from Recruitment Scams\n\nAnduril is committed to maintaining the integrity of our Talent acquisition process and the security of our candidates. We've observed a rise in sophisticated phishing and fraudulent schemes where individuals impersonate Anduril representatives, luring job seekers with false interviews or job offers. These scammers often attempt to extract payment or sensitive personal information.\n\nTo ensure your safety and help you navigate your job search with confidence, please keep the following critical points in mind:\n\n-\nNo Financial Requests: Anduril will never solicit payment or demand personal financial details (such as banking information, credit card numbers, or social security numbers) at any stage of our hiring process. Our legitimate recruitment is entirely free for candidates.\n\n- Please always verify communications:\n\n- Direct from Anduril: If you receive an email from one of our recruiters, it will only come from an @anduril.com address.\n\n- Via Agency Partner: If contacted by a recruiting agency for an Anduril role, their email will clearly identify their agency. If you suspect any suspicious activity, please verify the agency's authenticity by reaching out to contact@anduril.com .\n\n-\nExercise Caution with Unsolicited Outreach: If you receive any communication that appears suspicious, contains grammatical errors, or makes unusual requests, do not engage. Always confirm the sender's email domain is @anduril.com before providing any personal information or clicking on links.\n\n-\nWhat to Do If You Suspect Fraud: Should you encounter any questionable or fraudulent outreach claiming to be from Anduril, please report it immediately to contact@anduril.com . Your proactive caution is invaluable in protecting your personal information and upholding the security and trustworthiness of our recruitment efforts.\n\nData Privacy\n\nTo view Anduril's candidate data privacy policy, please visit https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/ .\n\nBy submitting your application, you consent to Anduril Industries using a third-party service provider to conduct pre-employment risk, integrity, and due diligence screening and assessing potential risks as part of your application process. This third-party service provider provides risk-intelligence services that may include analysis of sanctions and watchlists, adverse media, public-record information, and other lawful open-source or commercial data sources. This third-party service provider does not act as a consumer reporting agency. Use of this provider helps to ensure compliance with applicable laws and protect technology, intellectual property, and organizational security.","description_html":"<div class=\"content-intro\"><p>Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.</p></div><h3><strong>ABOUT THE TEAM</strong></h3>\n<p>Air Dominance &amp; Strike (AD&amp;S) is responsible for autonomous robotics systems like the Fury unmanned fighter jet and the Barracuda family of advanced effects. The AD&amp;S Vehicle Software team is responsible for the software running on these systems. Our software engineers collaborate with other engineering disciplines to develop software for vehicle control, networking, sensor integration, and telemetry. We are looking for engineers excited to build the foundational vehicle software stack that supports the wide range of AD&amp;S initiatives, from early concept simulation to first flight to live operations to large scale fleet management.</p>\n<h3>ABOUT THE JOB</h3>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">We are seeking a software engineer specialized in machine vision for development of guidance systems on a large air vehicle. Engineers in this role will primarily work on implementing novel image processing algorithms from various image sources and sensors.&nbsp; These will be both conventional and state of the art machine learning approaches.&nbsp; Additionally, the role requires the ability to work with other sensor sources and develop sensor fusion algorithms.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><br><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Integrate and write tests for camera calibration code</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335551550&quot;:1,&quot;335551620&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559737&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240,&quot;335559740&quot;:259,&quot;335559991&quot;:360}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Develop and refine algorithms for real-time image processing and analysis.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Write, test, and maintain high-quality code in Python and C++.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Optimize software for performance, reliability, and scalability</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Process and evaluate images from live tests used by camera systems in various flight conditions.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Debug and troubleshoot software and hardware issues as they arise.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Propose and implement improvements to enhance system performance and capabilities</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h4>REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><span data-contrast=\"auto\">BS, MS, or PhD in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, Mathematics, Physics, or related field.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><span data-contrast=\"auto\">4+ years of experience writing production software (C or C++ preferred).</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Direct experience with camera systems, calibration, and pose estimation.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Experience working with IMUs and implementing state fusion algorithms.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><span data-contrast=\"auto\">A desire to work on critical software that has a real-world impact</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Eligible to obtain and maintain a U.S. Top Secret security clearance</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h4>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Experience with SLAM systems.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Experience with estimation from RADAR or LIDAR systems.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><span data-contrast=\"auto\">General exposure to aviation concepts and aircraft design principles.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Experience working in airgapped environments (without network connectivity)</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Knowledge of defense technology and tactics, especially in the air domain</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Awareness of safety critical software development practices, including DO-178c and/or MIL-HDBK-516C.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}\">&nbsp;</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p><div class=\"content-pay-transparency\"><div class=\"pay-input\"><div class=\"title\">US Salary Range</div><div class=\"pay-range\"><span>$220,000</span><span class=\"divider\">&mdash;</span><span>$292,000 USD</span></div></div></div><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">The salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril's total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h3 class=\"detailElios\"><strong>Benefits</strong></h3>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">At Anduril, we invest in our people. Our comprehensive, competitive benefits package (available at little to no cost to employees) ensures you’re supported in health, recovery, and whatever comes next.&nbsp;</span><em><span data-contrast=\"auto\">For more information, <a href=\"https://www.anduril.com/careers\">Explore Our Benefits</a>.</span></em></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div class=\"RichText column1\">\n<h3 class=\"detailElios\"><strong>Protecting Yourself from Recruitment Scams</strong></h3>\n<p class=\"detailElios\">Anduril is committed to maintaining the integrity of our Talent acquisition process and the security of our candidates. We've observed a rise in sophisticated phishing and fraudulent schemes where individuals impersonate Anduril representatives, luring job seekers with false interviews or job offers. These scammers often attempt to extract payment or sensitive personal information.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"RichText column2\">\n<p class=\"detailElios\">To ensure your safety and help you navigate your job search with confidence, please keep the following critical points in mind:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p class=\"detailElios\"><strong>No Financial Requests:&nbsp;</strong>Anduril will never solicit payment or demand personal financial details (such as banking information, credit card numbers, or social security numbers) at any stage of our hiring process. Our legitimate recruitment is entirely free for candidates.</p>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Please always verify communications:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Direct from Anduril: If you receive an email from one of our recruiters, it will <em>only</em> come from an <code>@anduril.com</code> address.</li>\n<li>Via Agency Partner: If contacted by a recruiting agency for an Anduril role, their email will clearly identify their agency. If you suspect any suspicious activity, please verify the agency's authenticity by reaching out to <a href=\"mailto:contact@anduril.com\">contact@anduril.com</a>.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p class=\"detailElios\"><strong>Exercise Caution with Unsolicited Outreach:</strong>&nbsp;If you receive any communication that appears suspicious, contains grammatical errors, or makes unusual requests, do not engage. Always confirm the sender's email domain is @anduril.com before providing any personal information or clicking on links.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p class=\"detailElios\"><strong>What to Do If You Suspect Fraud:</strong>&nbsp;Should you encounter any questionable or fraudulent outreach claiming to be from Anduril, please report it immediately to&nbsp;<a href=\"mailto:contact@anduril.com\">contact@anduril.com</a>. Your proactive caution is invaluable in protecting your personal information and upholding the security and trustworthiness of our recruitment efforts.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3>&nbsp;</h3>\n<h3><strong>Data Privacy</strong></h3>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">To view Anduril's candidate data privacy policy, please visit </span><span data-contrast=\"none\"><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink\"><a href=\"https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/\">https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/</a></span></span><span data-contrast=\"auto\">.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">By submitting your application, you consent to Anduril Industries using a third-party service provider to conduct pre-employment risk, integrity, and due diligence screening and assessing potential risks as part of your application process. This third-party service provider provides risk-intelligence services that may include analysis of sanctions and watchlists, adverse media, public-record information, and other lawful open-source or commercial data sources. This third-party service provider does not act as a consumer reporting agency. Use of this provider helps to ensure compliance with applicable laws and protect technology, intellectual property, and organizational security.</span></p></div>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"External Department Name for Job Board":"Software","Employment Type":"Full-time","ET Talent Identifier":null,"Arsenal Launch Team":null},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["robotics","ai-ml"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"greenhouse:andurilindustries:5176752007","source":{"type":"greenhouse","board":"andurilindustries","job_id":"5176752007","source_url":"https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/andurilindustries/jobs","response_hash":"ebf3431b30ffa0d07bef3ab580ac8c623f9a1e71d4455c9f9115b58b3648fd47","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Anduril","slug":"anduril","lists":["robotics","ai-ml"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Mission Software Engineer, Vehicle Software, Consensus","canonical_url":"https://boards.greenhouse.io/andurilindustries/jobs/5176752007?gh_jid=5176752007","apply_url":"https://boards.greenhouse.io/andurilindustries/jobs/5176752007?gh_jid=5176752007","locations":[{"label":"Boston, Massachusetts, United States; Costa Mesa, California, United States"},{"label":"Costa Mesa, California, United States"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":["Air Dominance & Strike : Air Dominance & Strike Engineering : Mission Software Engineering"],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":"2554","internal_job_id":4395701007,"first_published_at":"2026-06-30T00:19:43-04:00","source_updated_at":"2026-08-24T14:07:42-04:00","application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.\n\nABOUT THE TEAM\n\nThe Air Dominance & Strike team at Anduril develops aerial and multi-domain robotic systems. The team is responsible for taking products like Fury (unmanned fighter jet) and Barracuda (air-breathing cruise missile) from concept to product. The team also develops Lattice for Mission Autonomy, Anduril’s premier software platform that enables masses of Fury, Barracuda, and other first and third party robots to collaborate across various missions. We work in close coordination with specialist teams like Perception, Motion Planning, Hardware, and Test Engineering to solve some of the hardest problems facing our customers.\n\nWe're seeking Software Engineers to build the core Command and Control software for our Lattice platform. This team is responsible for bridging the gap between hardware and human operators. Our software runs both on the vehicles managing real-time telemetry, health, and autopilot tasks and on the Ground Control Station enabling operators to plan missions, visualize maps, manage massive fleets, and orchestrate complex autonomous behaviors. We are also pioneering the integration of GenAI agents into our systems, allowing operators to direct autonomous assets using natural language interfaces. This is a highly autonomous role where you will build, ship, and see your code run on physical hardware deployed in the world.\n\nREQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS\n\n- Design and implement consensus protocols (Raft, CRDT, or others) that keep a fleet of autonomous vehicles converging on shared truth over lossy, contested links\n\n- Build the next generation of distributed teaming state: replicated mission data, leader election, and conflict resolution across dozens of nodes with no guaranteed central authority\n\n- Support bothstrong consensus and eventual consistency depending on real-world latency and partition constraints\n\n- Own the failure semantics when partitioned vehicles rejoin the team\n\n- Eligible to obtain and maintain an active U.S. Top Secret security clearance\n\n- BS, MS, or PhD in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Mathematics, Physics, or related field.\n\n- 3+ years of production-grade C++ and/or Rust experience in a Linux development environment\n\n- Experience building software solutions involving significant amounts of data processing and analysis\n\n- Ability to quickly understand and navigate complex systems and established code bases\n\n- A desire to work on critical software that has a real-world impact\n\n- Travel up to 30% of time to build, test, and deploy capabilities in the real world\n\nPREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS\n\n- Strong background with focus in Physics, Mathematics, and/or Motion Planning to inform modeling & simulation (M&S) and physical systems\n\n- Developing and testing multi-agent autonomous systems and deploying in real-world environments.\n\n- Feature and algorithm development with an understanding of behavior trees.\n\n- Developing software/hardware for flight systems and safety critical functionality.\n\n- Distributed communication networks and message standards\n\n- Knowledge of military systems and operational tactics\n\nUS Salary Range\n$166,000 — $220,000 USD\n\nThe salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril's total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:\n\nBenefits\n\nAt Anduril, we invest in our people. Our comprehensive, competitive benefits package (available at little to no cost to employees) ensures you’re supported in health, recovery, and whatever comes next. For more information, Explore Our Benefits .\n\nProtecting Yourself from Recruitment Scams\n\nAnduril is committed to maintaining the integrity of our Talent acquisition process and the security of our candidates. We've observed a rise in sophisticated phishing and fraudulent schemes where individuals impersonate Anduril representatives, luring job seekers with false interviews or job offers. These scammers often attempt to extract payment or sensitive personal information.\n\nTo ensure your safety and help you navigate your job search with confidence, please keep the following critical points in mind:\n\n-\nNo Financial Requests: Anduril will never solicit payment or demand personal financial details (such as banking information, credit card numbers, or social security numbers) at any stage of our hiring process. Our legitimate recruitment is entirely free for candidates.\n\n- Please always verify communications:\n\n- Direct from Anduril: If you receive an email from one of our recruiters, it will only come from an @anduril.com address.\n\n- Via Agency Partner: If contacted by a recruiting agency for an Anduril role, their email will clearly identify their agency. If you suspect any suspicious activity, please verify the agency's authenticity by reaching out to contact@anduril.com .\n\n-\nExercise Caution with Unsolicited Outreach: If you receive any communication that appears suspicious, contains grammatical errors, or makes unusual requests, do not engage. Always confirm the sender's email domain is @anduril.com before providing any personal information or clicking on links.\n\n-\nWhat to Do If You Suspect Fraud: Should you encounter any questionable or fraudulent outreach claiming to be from Anduril, please report it immediately to contact@anduril.com . Your proactive caution is invaluable in protecting your personal information and upholding the security and trustworthiness of our recruitment efforts.\n\nData Privacy\n\nTo view Anduril's candidate data privacy policy, please visit https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/ .\n\nBy submitting your application, you consent to Anduril Industries using a third-party service provider to conduct pre-employment risk, integrity, and due diligence screening and assessing potential risks as part of your application process. This third-party service provider provides risk-intelligence services that may include analysis of sanctions and watchlists, adverse media, public-record information, and other lawful open-source or commercial data sources. This third-party service provider does not act as a consumer reporting agency. Use of this provider helps to ensure compliance with applicable laws and protect technology, intellectual property, and organizational security.","description_html":"<div class=\"content-intro\"><p>Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.</p></div><h3><strong>ABOUT THE TEAM</strong></h3>\n<p>The Air Dominance &amp; Strike team at Anduril develops aerial and multi-domain robotic systems. The team is responsible for taking products like Fury (unmanned fighter jet) and Barracuda (air-breathing cruise missile) from concept to product. The team also develops Lattice for Mission Autonomy, Anduril’s premier software platform that enables masses of Fury, Barracuda, and other first and third party robots to collaborate across various missions. We work in close coordination with specialist teams like Perception, Motion Planning, Hardware, and Test Engineering to solve some of the hardest problems facing our customers.</p>\n<p>We're seeking Software Engineers to build the core Command and Control software for our Lattice platform. This team is responsible for bridging the gap between hardware and human operators. Our software runs both on the vehicles managing real-time telemetry, health, and autopilot tasks and on the Ground Control Station enabling operators to plan missions, visualize maps, manage massive fleets, and orchestrate complex autonomous behaviors. We are also pioneering the integration of GenAI agents into our systems, allowing operators to direct autonomous assets using natural language interfaces. This is a highly autonomous role where you will build, ship, and see your code run on physical hardware deployed in the world.</p>\n<h4><strong>REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Design and implement consensus protocols (Raft, CRDT, or others) that keep a fleet of autonomous vehicles converging on shared truth over lossy, contested links</li>\n<li>Build the next generation of distributed teaming state: replicated mission data, leader election, and conflict resolution across dozens of nodes with no guaranteed central authority</li>\n<li>Support bothstrong consensus and eventual consistency depending on real-world latency and partition constraints</li>\n<li>Own the failure semantics when partitioned vehicles rejoin the team</li>\n<li>Eligible to obtain and maintain an active U.S. Top Secret security clearance</li>\n<li>BS, MS, or PhD in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Mathematics, Physics, or related field.</li>\n<li>3+ years of production-grade C++ and/or Rust experience in a Linux development environment</li>\n<li>Experience building software solutions involving significant amounts of data processing and analysis</li>\n<li>Ability to quickly understand and navigate complex systems and established code bases</li>\n<li>A desire to work on critical software that has a real-world impact</li>\n<li>Travel up to 30% of time to build, test, and deploy capabilities in the real world</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><strong>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Strong background with focus in Physics, Mathematics, and/or Motion Planning to inform modeling &amp; simulation (M&amp;S) and physical systems</li>\n<li>Developing and testing multi-agent autonomous systems and deploying in real-world environments.</li>\n<li>Feature and algorithm development with an understanding of behavior trees.</li>\n<li>Developing software/hardware for flight systems and safety critical functionality.</li>\n<li>Distributed communication networks and message standards</li>\n<li>Knowledge of military systems and operational tactics</li>\n</ul><div class=\"content-pay-transparency\"><div class=\"pay-input\"><div class=\"title\">US Salary Range</div><div class=\"pay-range\"><span>$166,000</span><span class=\"divider\">&mdash;</span><span>$220,000 USD</span></div></div></div><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">The salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril's total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h3 class=\"detailElios\"><strong>Benefits</strong></h3>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">At Anduril, we invest in our people. Our comprehensive, competitive benefits package (available at little to no cost to employees) ensures you’re supported in health, recovery, and whatever comes next.&nbsp;</span><em><span data-contrast=\"auto\">For more information, <a href=\"https://www.anduril.com/careers\">Explore Our Benefits</a>.</span></em></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div class=\"RichText column1\">\n<h3 class=\"detailElios\"><strong>Protecting Yourself from Recruitment Scams</strong></h3>\n<p class=\"detailElios\">Anduril is committed to maintaining the integrity of our Talent acquisition process and the security of our candidates. We've observed a rise in sophisticated phishing and fraudulent schemes where individuals impersonate Anduril representatives, luring job seekers with false interviews or job offers. These scammers often attempt to extract payment or sensitive personal information.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"RichText column2\">\n<p class=\"detailElios\">To ensure your safety and help you navigate your job search with confidence, please keep the following critical points in mind:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p class=\"detailElios\"><strong>No Financial Requests:&nbsp;</strong>Anduril will never solicit payment or demand personal financial details (such as banking information, credit card numbers, or social security numbers) at any stage of our hiring process. Our legitimate recruitment is entirely free for candidates.</p>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Please always verify communications:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Direct from Anduril: If you receive an email from one of our recruiters, it will <em>only</em> come from an <code>@anduril.com</code> address.</li>\n<li>Via Agency Partner: If contacted by a recruiting agency for an Anduril role, their email will clearly identify their agency. If you suspect any suspicious activity, please verify the agency's authenticity by reaching out to <a href=\"mailto:contact@anduril.com\">contact@anduril.com</a>.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p class=\"detailElios\"><strong>Exercise Caution with Unsolicited Outreach:</strong>&nbsp;If you receive any communication that appears suspicious, contains grammatical errors, or makes unusual requests, do not engage. Always confirm the sender's email domain is @anduril.com before providing any personal information or clicking on links.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p class=\"detailElios\"><strong>What to Do If You Suspect Fraud:</strong>&nbsp;Should you encounter any questionable or fraudulent outreach claiming to be from Anduril, please report it immediately to&nbsp;<a href=\"mailto:contact@anduril.com\">contact@anduril.com</a>. Your proactive caution is invaluable in protecting your personal information and upholding the security and trustworthiness of our recruitment efforts.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3>&nbsp;</h3>\n<h3><strong>Data Privacy</strong></h3>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">To view Anduril's candidate data privacy policy, please visit </span><span data-contrast=\"none\"><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink\"><a href=\"https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/\">https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/</a></span></span><span data-contrast=\"auto\">.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">By submitting your application, you consent to Anduril Industries using a third-party service provider to conduct pre-employment risk, integrity, and due diligence screening and assessing potential risks as part of your application process. This third-party service provider provides risk-intelligence services that may include analysis of sanctions and watchlists, adverse media, public-record information, and other lawful open-source or commercial data sources. This third-party service provider does not act as a consumer reporting agency. Use of this provider helps to ensure compliance with applicable laws and protect technology, intellectual property, and organizational security.</span></p></div>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"External Department Name for Job Board":"Software","Employment Type":"Full-time","ET Talent Identifier":null,"Arsenal Launch Team":null},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["robotics","ai-ml"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"greenhouse:andurilindustries:4672911007","source":{"type":"greenhouse","board":"andurilindustries","job_id":"4672911007","source_url":"https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/andurilindustries/jobs","response_hash":"0f91fc52753c0f4aa5ad9de5006987d7b2fa0c8cafd53c1dbb06c47f0e8f9a95","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Anduril","slug":"anduril","lists":["robotics","ai-ml"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Mission Software Engineer, Vehicle Software, Frontend","canonical_url":"https://boards.greenhouse.io/andurilindustries/jobs/4672911007?gh_jid=4672911007","apply_url":"https://boards.greenhouse.io/andurilindustries/jobs/4672911007?gh_jid=4672911007","locations":[{"label":"Costa Mesa, California, United States; Seattle, Washington, United States; Washington, District of Columbia, United States"},{"label":"Costa Mesa, California, United States"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"unknown","departments":["Air Dominance & Strike : Air Dominance & Strike Engineering : Mission Software Engineering"],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":"INTERVIEW","internal_job_id":4395714007,"first_published_at":"2026-04-15T12:17:41-04:00","source_updated_at":"2026-08-24T14:07:42-04:00","application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.\n\nABOUT THE TEAM\n\nAir Dominance & Strike (AD&S) is responsible for autonomous robotics systems like the Fury unmanned fighter jet and the Barracuda family of advanced effects. The AD&S Vehicle Software team is responsible for the software running on these systems. Our software engineers collaborate with other engineering disciplines to develop software for vehicle control, networking, sensor integration, and telemetry. We are looking for engineers excited to build the foundational vehicle software stack that supports the wide range of AD&S initiatives, from early concept simulation to first flight to live operations to large scale fleet management.\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n- Design, build, and deploy a real-time, map-based interface for displaying and interacting with sensor data and commanding physical assets\n\n- Fetch and manage large streams of data while maintaining performant rendering in a low-friction user experience\n\n- Build and design immersive image-viewing experiences in a web-based platform\n\n- Take ownership of initial, well-scoped projects with clear objectives. Work closely with colleagues to deliver results, understanding the importance of teamwork in achieving success.\n\n- Partner with end-users to turn needs into features while balancing user experience with engineering constraints\n\n- Travel up to 15% of time to build, test, and deploy capabilities in the real world\n\nREQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS:\n\n- Eligible to obtain and maintain an active U.S. Top Secret security clearance\n\n- Degree in Computer Science, Operations Research, Electrical Engineering, related technical degree, or equivalent experience\n\n- Experience working on frontend applications, preferably data-intensive or map-based systems\n\n- Proficiency with a programming language such as Javascript or Typescript\n\n- Experience with React\n\n- Broad experience in delivering functional outcomes\n\n- A mindset towards innovative approaches of problem solving\n\nUS Salary Range\n$166,000 — $220,000 USD\n\nThe salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril's total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:\n\nBenefits\n\nAt Anduril, we invest in our people. Our comprehensive, competitive benefits package (available at little to no cost to employees) ensures you’re supported in health, recovery, and whatever comes next. For more information, Explore Our Benefits .\n\nProtecting Yourself from Recruitment Scams\n\nAnduril is committed to maintaining the integrity of our Talent acquisition process and the security of our candidates. We've observed a rise in sophisticated phishing and fraudulent schemes where individuals impersonate Anduril representatives, luring job seekers with false interviews or job offers. These scammers often attempt to extract payment or sensitive personal information.\n\nTo ensure your safety and help you navigate your job search with confidence, please keep the following critical points in mind:\n\n-\nNo Financial Requests: Anduril will never solicit payment or demand personal financial details (such as banking information, credit card numbers, or social security numbers) at any stage of our hiring process. Our legitimate recruitment is entirely free for candidates.\n\n- Please always verify communications:\n\n- Direct from Anduril: If you receive an email from one of our recruiters, it will only come from an @anduril.com address.\n\n- Via Agency Partner: If contacted by a recruiting agency for an Anduril role, their email will clearly identify their agency. If you suspect any suspicious activity, please verify the agency's authenticity by reaching out to contact@anduril.com .\n\n-\nExercise Caution with Unsolicited Outreach: If you receive any communication that appears suspicious, contains grammatical errors, or makes unusual requests, do not engage. Always confirm the sender's email domain is @anduril.com before providing any personal information or clicking on links.\n\n-\nWhat to Do If You Suspect Fraud: Should you encounter any questionable or fraudulent outreach claiming to be from Anduril, please report it immediately to contact@anduril.com . Your proactive caution is invaluable in protecting your personal information and upholding the security and trustworthiness of our recruitment efforts.\n\nData Privacy\n\nTo view Anduril's candidate data privacy policy, please visit https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/ .\n\nBy submitting your application, you consent to Anduril Industries using a third-party service provider to conduct pre-employment risk, integrity, and due diligence screening and assessing potential risks as part of your application process. This third-party service provider provides risk-intelligence services that may include analysis of sanctions and watchlists, adverse media, public-record information, and other lawful open-source or commercial data sources. This third-party service provider does not act as a consumer reporting agency. Use of this provider helps to ensure compliance with applicable laws and protect technology, intellectual property, and organizational security.","description_html":"<div class=\"content-intro\"><p>Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.</p></div><h3><strong>ABOUT THE TEAM</strong></h3>\n<p>Air Dominance &amp; Strike (AD&amp;S) is responsible for autonomous robotics systems like the Fury unmanned fighter jet and the Barracuda family of advanced effects. The AD&amp;S Vehicle Software team is responsible for the software running on these systems. Our software engineers collaborate with other engineering disciplines to develop software for vehicle control, networking, sensor integration, and telemetry. We are looking for engineers excited to build the foundational vehicle software stack that supports the wide range of AD&amp;S initiatives, from early concept simulation to first flight to live operations to large scale fleet management.</p>\n<h4><strong><br>WHAT YOU'LL DO<br></strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Design, build, and deploy a real-time, map-based interface for displaying and interacting with sensor data and commanding physical assets</li>\n<li>Fetch and manage large streams of data while maintaining performant rendering in a low-friction user experience</li>\n<li>Build and design immersive image-viewing experiences in a web-based platform</li>\n<li>Take ownership of initial, well-scoped projects with clear objectives. Work closely with colleagues to deliver results, understanding the importance of teamwork in achieving success.</li>\n<li>Partner with end-users to turn needs into features while balancing user experience with engineering constraints</li>\n<li>Travel up to 15% of time to build, test, and deploy capabilities in the real world</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><strong>REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS:<br></strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Eligible to obtain and maintain an active U.S. Top Secret security clearance</li>\n<li>Degree in Computer Science, Operations Research, Electrical Engineering, related technical degree, or equivalent experience</li>\n<li>Experience working on frontend applications, preferably data-intensive or map-based systems</li>\n<li>Proficiency with a programming language such as Javascript or Typescript</li>\n<li>Experience with React</li>\n<li>Broad experience in delivering functional outcomes</li>\n<li>A mindset towards innovative approaches of problem solving</li>\n</ul><div class=\"content-pay-transparency\"><div class=\"pay-input\"><div class=\"title\">US Salary Range</div><div class=\"pay-range\"><span>$166,000</span><span class=\"divider\">&mdash;</span><span>$220,000 USD</span></div></div></div><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">The salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril's total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h3 class=\"detailElios\"><strong>Benefits</strong></h3>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">At Anduril, we invest in our people. Our comprehensive, competitive benefits package (available at little to no cost to employees) ensures you’re supported in health, recovery, and whatever comes next.&nbsp;</span><em><span data-contrast=\"auto\">For more information, <a href=\"https://www.anduril.com/careers\">Explore Our Benefits</a>.</span></em></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div class=\"RichText column1\">\n<h3 class=\"detailElios\"><strong>Protecting Yourself from Recruitment Scams</strong></h3>\n<p class=\"detailElios\">Anduril is committed to maintaining the integrity of our Talent acquisition process and the security of our candidates. We've observed a rise in sophisticated phishing and fraudulent schemes where individuals impersonate Anduril representatives, luring job seekers with false interviews or job offers. These scammers often attempt to extract payment or sensitive personal information.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"RichText column2\">\n<p class=\"detailElios\">To ensure your safety and help you navigate your job search with confidence, please keep the following critical points in mind:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p class=\"detailElios\"><strong>No Financial Requests:&nbsp;</strong>Anduril will never solicit payment or demand personal financial details (such as banking information, credit card numbers, or social security numbers) at any stage of our hiring process. Our legitimate recruitment is entirely free for candidates.</p>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Please always verify communications:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Direct from Anduril: If you receive an email from one of our recruiters, it will <em>only</em> come from an <code>@anduril.com</code> address.</li>\n<li>Via Agency Partner: If contacted by a recruiting agency for an Anduril role, their email will clearly identify their agency. If you suspect any suspicious activity, please verify the agency's authenticity by reaching out to <a href=\"mailto:contact@anduril.com\">contact@anduril.com</a>.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p class=\"detailElios\"><strong>Exercise Caution with Unsolicited Outreach:</strong>&nbsp;If you receive any communication that appears suspicious, contains grammatical errors, or makes unusual requests, do not engage. Always confirm the sender's email domain is @anduril.com before providing any personal information or clicking on links.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p class=\"detailElios\"><strong>What to Do If You Suspect Fraud:</strong>&nbsp;Should you encounter any questionable or fraudulent outreach claiming to be from Anduril, please report it immediately to&nbsp;<a href=\"mailto:contact@anduril.com\">contact@anduril.com</a>. Your proactive caution is invaluable in protecting your personal information and upholding the security and trustworthiness of our recruitment efforts.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3>&nbsp;</h3>\n<h3><strong>Data Privacy</strong></h3>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">To view Anduril's candidate data privacy policy, please visit </span><span data-contrast=\"none\"><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink\"><a href=\"https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/\">https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/</a></span></span><span data-contrast=\"auto\">.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">By submitting your application, you consent to Anduril Industries using a third-party service provider to conduct pre-employment risk, integrity, and due diligence screening and assessing potential risks as part of your application process. This third-party service provider provides risk-intelligence services that may include analysis of sanctions and watchlists, adverse media, public-record information, and other lawful open-source or commercial data sources. This third-party service provider does not act as a consumer reporting agency. Use of this provider helps to ensure compliance with applicable laws and protect technology, intellectual property, and organizational security.</span></p></div>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"External Department Name for Job Board":"Software","Employment Type":null,"ET Talent Identifier":null,"Arsenal Launch Team":null},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["robotics","ai-ml"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"greenhouse:andurilindustries:4672868007","source":{"type":"greenhouse","board":"andurilindustries","job_id":"4672868007","source_url":"https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/andurilindustries/jobs","response_hash":"1b051f60f26856532da68c0774c378180b953bce9a589d912fb06231ae52bf8b","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Anduril","slug":"anduril","lists":["robotics","ai-ml"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Mission Software Engineer, Vehicle Software, GenSWE","canonical_url":"https://boards.greenhouse.io/andurilindustries/jobs/4672868007?gh_jid=4672868007","apply_url":"https://boards.greenhouse.io/andurilindustries/jobs/4672868007?gh_jid=4672868007","locations":[{"label":"Costa Mesa, California, United States"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":["Air Dominance & Strike : Air Dominance & Strike Engineering : Mission Software Engineering"],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":"2553","internal_job_id":4395691007,"first_published_at":"2025-04-03T18:14:37-04:00","source_updated_at":"2026-08-24T14:07:42-04:00","application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.\n\nABOUT THE TEAM\n\nAir Dominance & Strike (AD&S) is responsible for autonomous robotics systems like the Fury unmanned fighter jet and the Barracuda family of advanced effects. The AD&S Vehicle Software team is responsible for the software running on these systems. Our software engineers collaborate with other engineering disciplines to develop software for vehicle control, networking, sensor integration, and telemetry. We are looking for engineers excited to build the foundational vehicle software stack that supports the wide range of AD&S initiatives, from early concept simulation to first flight to live operations to large scale fleet management.\n\nREQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS\n\n- Eligible to obtain and maintain an active U.S. Top Secret security clearance\n\n- Strong engineering background from industry or school, ideally in areas/fields such as Computer Science, Software Engineering, Mathematics, or Physics\n\n- 3+ years working with a variety of programming languages such as Python, C++, Rust, Go, JavaScript, etc.\n\n- Experience building software solutions involving significant amounts of data processing and analysis\n\n- Ability to quickly understand and navigate complex systems and established code bases\n\n- A desire to work on critical software that has a real-world impact\n\nPREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS\n\n- Strong background with focus in Physics, Mathematics, and/or Motion Planning to inform modeling & simulation (M&S) and physical systems\n\n- Developing and testing multi-agent autonomous systems and deploying in real-world environments\n\n- Feature and algorithm development with an understanding of behavior trees\n\n- Developing software/hardware for flight systems and safety critical functionality\n\n- Distributed communication networks and message standards\n\n- Knowledge of military systems and operational tactics\n\nUS Salary Range\n$166,000 — $220,000 USD\n\nThe salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril's total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:\n\nBenefits\n\nAt Anduril, we invest in our people. Our comprehensive, competitive benefits package (available at little to no cost to employees) ensures you’re supported in health, recovery, and whatever comes next. For more information, Explore Our Benefits .\n\nProtecting Yourself from Recruitment Scams\n\nAnduril is committed to maintaining the integrity of our Talent acquisition process and the security of our candidates. We've observed a rise in sophisticated phishing and fraudulent schemes where individuals impersonate Anduril representatives, luring job seekers with false interviews or job offers. These scammers often attempt to extract payment or sensitive personal information.\n\nTo ensure your safety and help you navigate your job search with confidence, please keep the following critical points in mind:\n\n-\nNo Financial Requests: Anduril will never solicit payment or demand personal financial details (such as banking information, credit card numbers, or social security numbers) at any stage of our hiring process. Our legitimate recruitment is entirely free for candidates.\n\n- Please always verify communications:\n\n- Direct from Anduril: If you receive an email from one of our recruiters, it will only come from an @anduril.com address.\n\n- Via Agency Partner: If contacted by a recruiting agency for an Anduril role, their email will clearly identify their agency. If you suspect any suspicious activity, please verify the agency's authenticity by reaching out to contact@anduril.com .\n\n-\nExercise Caution with Unsolicited Outreach: If you receive any communication that appears suspicious, contains grammatical errors, or makes unusual requests, do not engage. Always confirm the sender's email domain is @anduril.com before providing any personal information or clicking on links.\n\n-\nWhat to Do If You Suspect Fraud: Should you encounter any questionable or fraudulent outreach claiming to be from Anduril, please report it immediately to contact@anduril.com . Your proactive caution is invaluable in protecting your personal information and upholding the security and trustworthiness of our recruitment efforts.\n\nData Privacy\n\nTo view Anduril's candidate data privacy policy, please visit https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/ .\n\nBy submitting your application, you consent to Anduril Industries using a third-party service provider to conduct pre-employment risk, integrity, and due diligence screening and assessing potential risks as part of your application process. This third-party service provider provides risk-intelligence services that may include analysis of sanctions and watchlists, adverse media, public-record information, and other lawful open-source or commercial data sources. This third-party service provider does not act as a consumer reporting agency. Use of this provider helps to ensure compliance with applicable laws and protect technology, intellectual property, and organizational security.","description_html":"<div class=\"content-intro\"><p>Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.</p></div><h3><strong>ABOUT THE TEAM</strong></h3>\n<p>Air Dominance &amp; Strike (AD&amp;S) is responsible for autonomous robotics systems like the Fury unmanned fighter jet and the Barracuda family of advanced effects. The AD&amp;S Vehicle Software team is responsible for the software running on these systems. Our software engineers collaborate with other engineering disciplines to develop software for vehicle control, networking, sensor integration, and telemetry. We are looking for engineers excited to build the foundational vehicle software stack that supports the wide range of AD&amp;S initiatives, from early concept simulation to first flight to live operations to large scale fleet management.</p>\n<h4><strong>REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Eligible to obtain and maintain an active U.S. Top Secret security clearance</li>\n<li>Strong engineering background from industry or school, ideally in areas/fields such as Computer Science, Software Engineering, Mathematics, or Physics</li>\n<li>3+ years working with a variety of programming languages such as Python, C++, Rust, Go, JavaScript, etc.</li>\n<li>Experience building software solutions involving significant amounts of data processing and analysis</li>\n<li>Ability to quickly understand and navigate complex systems and established code bases</li>\n<li>A desire to work on critical software that has a real-world impact</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><strong>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS</strong></h4>\n<ul class=\"p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet\" data-stringify-type=\"unordered-list\" data-indent=\"0\" data-border=\"0\">\n<li data-stringify-indent=\"0\" data-stringify-border=\"0\">Strong background with focus in Physics, Mathematics, and/or Motion Planning to inform modeling &amp; simulation (M&amp;S) and physical systems</li>\n<li data-stringify-indent=\"0\" data-stringify-border=\"0\">Developing and testing multi-agent autonomous systems and deploying in real-world environments</li>\n<li data-stringify-indent=\"0\" data-stringify-border=\"0\">Feature and algorithm development with an understanding of behavior trees</li>\n<li data-stringify-indent=\"0\" data-stringify-border=\"0\">Developing software/hardware for flight systems and safety critical functionality</li>\n<li data-stringify-indent=\"0\" data-stringify-border=\"0\">Distributed communication networks and message standards</li>\n<li data-stringify-indent=\"0\" data-stringify-border=\"0\">Knowledge of military systems and operational tactics</li>\n</ul><div class=\"content-pay-transparency\"><div class=\"pay-input\"><div class=\"title\">US Salary Range</div><div class=\"pay-range\"><span>$166,000</span><span class=\"divider\">&mdash;</span><span>$220,000 USD</span></div></div></div><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">The salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril's total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h3 class=\"detailElios\"><strong>Benefits</strong></h3>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">At Anduril, we invest in our people. Our comprehensive, competitive benefits package (available at little to no cost to employees) ensures you’re supported in health, recovery, and whatever comes next.&nbsp;</span><em><span data-contrast=\"auto\">For more information, <a href=\"https://www.anduril.com/careers\">Explore Our Benefits</a>.</span></em></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div class=\"RichText column1\">\n<h3 class=\"detailElios\"><strong>Protecting Yourself from Recruitment Scams</strong></h3>\n<p class=\"detailElios\">Anduril is committed to maintaining the integrity of our Talent acquisition process and the security of our candidates. We've observed a rise in sophisticated phishing and fraudulent schemes where individuals impersonate Anduril representatives, luring job seekers with false interviews or job offers. These scammers often attempt to extract payment or sensitive personal information.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"RichText column2\">\n<p class=\"detailElios\">To ensure your safety and help you navigate your job search with confidence, please keep the following critical points in mind:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p class=\"detailElios\"><strong>No Financial Requests:&nbsp;</strong>Anduril will never solicit payment or demand personal financial details (such as banking information, credit card numbers, or social security numbers) at any stage of our hiring process. Our legitimate recruitment is entirely free for candidates.</p>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Please always verify communications:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Direct from Anduril: If you receive an email from one of our recruiters, it will <em>only</em> come from an <code>@anduril.com</code> address.</li>\n<li>Via Agency Partner: If contacted by a recruiting agency for an Anduril role, their email will clearly identify their agency. If you suspect any suspicious activity, please verify the agency's authenticity by reaching out to <a href=\"mailto:contact@anduril.com\">contact@anduril.com</a>.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p class=\"detailElios\"><strong>Exercise Caution with Unsolicited Outreach:</strong>&nbsp;If you receive any communication that appears suspicious, contains grammatical errors, or makes unusual requests, do not engage. Always confirm the sender's email domain is @anduril.com before providing any personal information or clicking on links.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p class=\"detailElios\"><strong>What to Do If You Suspect Fraud:</strong>&nbsp;Should you encounter any questionable or fraudulent outreach claiming to be from Anduril, please report it immediately to&nbsp;<a href=\"mailto:contact@anduril.com\">contact@anduril.com</a>. Your proactive caution is invaluable in protecting your personal information and upholding the security and trustworthiness of our recruitment efforts.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3>&nbsp;</h3>\n<h3><strong>Data Privacy</strong></h3>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">To view Anduril's candidate data privacy policy, please visit </span><span data-contrast=\"none\"><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink\"><a href=\"https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/\">https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/</a></span></span><span data-contrast=\"auto\">.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">By submitting your application, you consent to Anduril Industries using a third-party service provider to conduct pre-employment risk, integrity, and due diligence screening and assessing potential risks as part of your application process. This third-party service provider provides risk-intelligence services that may include analysis of sanctions and watchlists, adverse media, public-record information, and other lawful open-source or commercial data sources. This third-party service provider does not act as a consumer reporting agency. Use of this provider helps to ensure compliance with applicable laws and protect technology, intellectual property, and organizational security.</span></p></div>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"External Department Name for Job Board":"Software","Employment Type":"Full-time","ET Talent Identifier":null,"Arsenal Launch Team":null},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["robotics","ai-ml"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"greenhouse:andurilindustries:5158245007","source":{"type":"greenhouse","board":"andurilindustries","job_id":"5158245007","source_url":"https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/andurilindustries/jobs","response_hash":"ff0ddadd44b2970ba228984e32c3701dcf357b7c4c3556cee005f56d6310c457","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Anduril","slug":"anduril","lists":["robotics","ai-ml"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Mission Software Infrastructure Engineer, Active Clearance","canonical_url":"https://boards.greenhouse.io/andurilindustries/jobs/5158245007?gh_jid=5158245007","apply_url":"https://boards.greenhouse.io/andurilindustries/jobs/5158245007?gh_jid=5158245007","locations":[{"label":"Costa Mesa, California, United States; Seattle, Washington, United States; Washington, District of Columbia, United States"},{"label":"Costa Mesa, California, United States"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":["Air Dominance & Strike : Mission Autonomy Engineering : MFX Factory"],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":"10782","internal_job_id":4642438007,"first_published_at":"2026-06-10T00:19:14-04:00","source_updated_at":"2026-08-24T14:07:42-04:00","application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.\n\nABOUT THE TEAM\n\nThe Air Dominance & Strike team at Anduril develops aerial and multi-domain robotic systems. The team is responsible for taking products like Fury (unmanned fighter jet) and Barracuda (air-breathing cruise missile) from concept to product. The team also develops Lattice for Mission Autonomy, Anduril’s premier software platform that enables masses of Fury, Barracuda, and other first and third party robots to collaborate across various missions. We work in close coordination with specialist teams like Perception, Motion Planning, Hardware, and Test Engineering to solve some of the hardest problems facing our customers.\n\nWe are looking for Software Engineers to design, build, and automate the software platforms and tooling that power our development, simulation, and deployment environments. In this role, you will bridge the gap between our core software platforms and the diverse environments ranging from cloud infrastructure to on-premises and edge hardware where our systems run.\n\nREQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS\n\n- Currently hold an active U.S. Secret or above security clearance\n\n- 5+ years of engineering experience with at least 3+ years focused on infrastructure problems\n\n- Bachelors, Masters, or PhD in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Mathematics, Physics, or related field\n\n- Experience with Python and a background in scripting programming languages (Go or Rust exp a plus)\n\n- Experience with Kubernetes or NixOS in production environments\n\n- Ability to quickly understand and navigate complex systems and established code bases\n\n- A desire to work on critical software that has a real-world impact\n\nPREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS\n\n- Strong background with a focus in simulation or high performance compute management\n\n- Experience managing physical rack based deployment\n\n- Experience working with GPU/CPU accelerated workflows\n\n- Knowledge of military systems and operational tactics\n\n- Experience working directly with end users\n\nUS Salary Range\n$166,000 — $220,000 USD\n\nThe salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril's total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:\n\nBenefits\n\nAt Anduril, we invest in our people. Our comprehensive, competitive benefits package (available at little to no cost to employees) ensures you’re supported in health, recovery, and whatever comes next. For more information, Explore Our Benefits .\n\nProtecting Yourself from Recruitment Scams\n\nAnduril is committed to maintaining the integrity of our Talent acquisition process and the security of our candidates. We've observed a rise in sophisticated phishing and fraudulent schemes where individuals impersonate Anduril representatives, luring job seekers with false interviews or job offers. These scammers often attempt to extract payment or sensitive personal information.\n\nTo ensure your safety and help you navigate your job search with confidence, please keep the following critical points in mind:\n\n-\nNo Financial Requests: Anduril will never solicit payment or demand personal financial details (such as banking information, credit card numbers, or social security numbers) at any stage of our hiring process. Our legitimate recruitment is entirely free for candidates.\n\n- Please always verify communications:\n\n- Direct from Anduril: If you receive an email from one of our recruiters, it will only come from an @anduril.com address.\n\n- Via Agency Partner: If contacted by a recruiting agency for an Anduril role, their email will clearly identify their agency. If you suspect any suspicious activity, please verify the agency's authenticity by reaching out to contact@anduril.com .\n\n-\nExercise Caution with Unsolicited Outreach: If you receive any communication that appears suspicious, contains grammatical errors, or makes unusual requests, do not engage. Always confirm the sender's email domain is @anduril.com before providing any personal information or clicking on links.\n\n-\nWhat to Do If You Suspect Fraud: Should you encounter any questionable or fraudulent outreach claiming to be from Anduril, please report it immediately to contact@anduril.com . Your proactive caution is invaluable in protecting your personal information and upholding the security and trustworthiness of our recruitment efforts.\n\nData Privacy\n\nTo view Anduril's candidate data privacy policy, please visit https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/ .\n\nBy submitting your application, you consent to Anduril Industries using a third-party service provider to conduct pre-employment risk, integrity, and due diligence screening and assessing potential risks as part of your application process. This third-party service provider provides risk-intelligence services that may include analysis of sanctions and watchlists, adverse media, public-record information, and other lawful open-source or commercial data sources. This third-party service provider does not act as a consumer reporting agency. Use of this provider helps to ensure compliance with applicable laws and protect technology, intellectual property, and organizational security.","description_html":"<div class=\"content-intro\"><p>Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.</p></div><h3><strong>ABOUT THE TEAM</strong></h3>\n<p>The Air Dominance &amp; Strike team at Anduril develops aerial and multi-domain robotic systems. The team is responsible for taking products like Fury (unmanned fighter jet) and Barracuda (air-breathing cruise missile) from concept to product. The team also develops Lattice for Mission Autonomy, Anduril’s premier software platform that enables masses of Fury, Barracuda, and other first and third party robots to collaborate across various missions. We work in close coordination with specialist teams like Perception, Motion Planning, Hardware, and Test Engineering to solve some of the hardest problems facing our customers.&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span class=\"TextRun SCXW169022619 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"auto\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW169022619 BCX0\">We are looking for </span></span><span class=\"TextRun MacChromeBold SCXW169022619 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"auto\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW169022619 BCX0\">Software Engineers</span></span><span class=\"TextRun SCXW169022619 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"auto\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW169022619 BCX0\">&nbsp;to design, build, and automate the software platforms and tooling that power our development, simulation, and deployment environments. In this role, you will bridge the gap between our core software platforms and the diverse environments</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW169022619 BCX0\">&nbsp;</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW169022619 BCX0\">ranging from cloud infrastructure to on-premises and edge hardware</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW169022619 BCX0\">&nbsp;</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW169022619 BCX0\">where our systems run.&nbsp;</span></span><span class=\"EOP SCXW169022619 BCX0\" data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<h4><strong>REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Currently hold an active U.S. Secret or above security clearance</li>\n<li>5+ years of engineering experience with at least 3+ years focused on infrastructure problems</li>\n<li>Bachelors, Masters, or PhD in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Mathematics, Physics, or related field</li>\n<li>Experience with Python and a background in scripting programming languages (Go or Rust exp a plus)</li>\n<li>Experience with Kubernetes or NixOS in production environments</li>\n<li>Ability to quickly understand and navigate complex systems and established code bases</li>\n<li>A desire to work on critical software that has a real-world impact</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><strong>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Strong background with a focus in simulation or high performance compute management</li>\n<li>Experience managing physical rack based deployment</li>\n<li>Experience working with GPU/CPU accelerated workflows</li>\n<li>Knowledge of military systems and operational tactics</li>\n<li>Experience working directly with end users</li>\n</ul><div class=\"content-pay-transparency\"><div class=\"pay-input\"><div class=\"title\">US Salary Range</div><div class=\"pay-range\"><span>$166,000</span><span class=\"divider\">&mdash;</span><span>$220,000 USD</span></div></div></div><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">The salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril's total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h3 class=\"detailElios\"><strong>Benefits</strong></h3>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">At Anduril, we invest in our people. Our comprehensive, competitive benefits package (available at little to no cost to employees) ensures you’re supported in health, recovery, and whatever comes next.&nbsp;</span><em><span data-contrast=\"auto\">For more information, <a href=\"https://www.anduril.com/careers\">Explore Our Benefits</a>.</span></em></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div class=\"RichText column1\">\n<h3 class=\"detailElios\"><strong>Protecting Yourself from Recruitment Scams</strong></h3>\n<p class=\"detailElios\">Anduril is committed to maintaining the integrity of our Talent acquisition process and the security of our candidates. We've observed a rise in sophisticated phishing and fraudulent schemes where individuals impersonate Anduril representatives, luring job seekers with false interviews or job offers. These scammers often attempt to extract payment or sensitive personal information.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"RichText column2\">\n<p class=\"detailElios\">To ensure your safety and help you navigate your job search with confidence, please keep the following critical points in mind:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p class=\"detailElios\"><strong>No Financial Requests:&nbsp;</strong>Anduril will never solicit payment or demand personal financial details (such as banking information, credit card numbers, or social security numbers) at any stage of our hiring process. Our legitimate recruitment is entirely free for candidates.</p>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Please always verify communications:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Direct from Anduril: If you receive an email from one of our recruiters, it will <em>only</em> come from an <code>@anduril.com</code> address.</li>\n<li>Via Agency Partner: If contacted by a recruiting agency for an Anduril role, their email will clearly identify their agency. If you suspect any suspicious activity, please verify the agency's authenticity by reaching out to <a href=\"mailto:contact@anduril.com\">contact@anduril.com</a>.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p class=\"detailElios\"><strong>Exercise Caution with Unsolicited Outreach:</strong>&nbsp;If you receive any communication that appears suspicious, contains grammatical errors, or makes unusual requests, do not engage. Always confirm the sender's email domain is @anduril.com before providing any personal information or clicking on links.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p class=\"detailElios\"><strong>What to Do If You Suspect Fraud:</strong>&nbsp;Should you encounter any questionable or fraudulent outreach claiming to be from Anduril, please report it immediately to&nbsp;<a href=\"mailto:contact@anduril.com\">contact@anduril.com</a>. Your proactive caution is invaluable in protecting your personal information and upholding the security and trustworthiness of our recruitment efforts.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3>&nbsp;</h3>\n<h3><strong>Data Privacy</strong></h3>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">To view Anduril's candidate data privacy policy, please visit </span><span data-contrast=\"none\"><span data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink\"><a href=\"https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/\">https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/</a></span></span><span data-contrast=\"auto\">.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">By submitting your application, you consent to Anduril Industries using a third-party service provider to conduct pre-employment risk, integrity, and due diligence screening and assessing potential risks as part of your application process. This third-party service provider provides risk-intelligence services that may include analysis of sanctions and watchlists, adverse media, public-record information, and other lawful open-source or commercial data sources. This third-party service provider does not act as a consumer reporting agency. Use of this provider helps to ensure compliance with applicable laws and protect technology, intellectual property, and organizational security.</span></p></div>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"External Department Name for Job Board":"Software","Employment Type":"Full-time","ET Talent Identifier":null,"Arsenal Launch Team":null},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Infrastructure Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Infrastructure"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["robotics","ai-ml"]}}
