{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"greenhouse:anthropic:5358088008","source":{"type":"greenhouse","board":"anthropic","job_id":"5358088008","source_url":"https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/anthropic/jobs","response_hash":"f99165acdb93eab159a1a6f9ac7cd50f3a531f351fe24f067d0d929c4fd333a4","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Anthropic","slug":"anthropic","lists":["ai-ml","ai-infra","research"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Finance & Strategy, Machines","canonical_url":"https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/anthropic/jobs/5358088008","apply_url":"https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/anthropic/jobs/5358088008","locations":[{"label":"San Francisco, CA"},{"label":"San Francisco, California, United States"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"unknown","departments":["Finance"],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":"P-5155","internal_job_id":4517571008,"first_published_at":"2026-08-13T13:29:25-04:00","source_updated_at":"2026-08-21T12:50:38-04:00","application_deadline":null,"description_plain":null,"description_html":null,"compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"Location Type":"On-Site"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":false,"tier":"stretch","score":0,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":[],"role_matches":[],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["ai-ml","ai-infra","research"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"greenhouse:anthropic:5390728008","source":{"type":"greenhouse","board":"anthropic","job_id":"5390728008","source_url":"https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/anthropic/jobs","response_hash":"e74f9e6c86f456c6e81520c273d0dfa60079636733e6e6deb1f0187f641093ab","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Anthropic","slug":"anthropic","lists":["ai-ml","ai-infra","research"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Finance Systems Engineer, Finance and Strategy","canonical_url":"https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/anthropic/jobs/5390728008","apply_url":"https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/anthropic/jobs/5390728008","locations":[{"label":"San Francisco, CA"},{"label":"San Francisco, California, United States"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"unknown","departments":["Finance"],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":"266829","internal_job_id":4532767008,"first_published_at":"2026-08-14T15:29:18-04:00","source_updated_at":"2026-08-21T12:50:55-04:00","application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"About Anthropic\n\nAnthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.\n\nAbout the Role\n\nWe are looking for a Finance & Strategy (FP&A) Systems Engineer to join our Finance Systems team at Anthropic. In this role, you will be responsible for building and maintaining platforms that support our core Financial Planning, Forecasting and Analytics processes. You will bring deep hands-on expertise in EPM platforms like Anaplan, Pigment and data platforms like BigQuery, who writes integrations, tooling, and production code that connect them to Anthropic’s ERP and data warehouse systems. You'll work closely with Corporate Finance & strategy stakeholders to translate business requirements into innovative technical solutions, maintain data integrity, and drive continuous improvements to our financial systems infrastructure.\n\nYou'll manage day-to-day Finance system operations, support critical financial processes and monthly Forecasting cycles, and take on more ambitious system projects over time, including using Claude to automate FP&A work, help build scalable solutions that enable efficient financial planning, forecasting, and reporting as we continue to grow.\n\nResponsibilities\n\nSystems Administration and Support\n\n-\nServe as a primary system administrator for our financial planning platform (Pigment), maintaining system health and optimal performance\n\n-\nManage Finance applications, data, user access & security, system configurations, version management to ensure appropriate controls and governance.\n\n-\nProvide technical support and troubleshooting for end-users, resolving issues and answering system-related questions\n\nSystem Development and Enhancement\n\n-\nDesign, build, and maintain applications, Financial models and workflows with in-house tools and EPM platform like Pigment to support financial planning, budgeting, forecasting, and reporting processes\n\n-\nDevelop and maintain secure dataflows, integrations using Rest APIs to connect FP&A platforms, data warehouse with enterprise systems (e.g., Workday Financials, Salesforce CRM, etc.)\n\n-\nDevelop SQL-based data models, ETL pipelines, and reporting infrastructure to support financial close, forecasting, and business intelligence.\n\nBusiness Partnership and Process Improvement\n\n-\nPartner with Finance & Strategy (FP&A), Accounting, and other Finance teams to understand business problems and use AI tools to build cutting edge solutions\n\n-\nSupport Monthly Forecast, Annual & Long Range planning, Workforce planning, OPEX Forecasting, Balance Sheet & Cash flow forecasting processes.\n\n-\nIdentify and implement process and Finance platform improvements.\n\n-\nParticipate in testing and validation of system changes, ensuring accuracy and reliability\n\n-\nAssist with training and onboarding of new system users\n\nData Management and Quality\n\n-\nEnsure the accuracy and integrity of financial data across systems\n\n-\nDevelop and maintain data validation rules and quality checks\n\n-\nTroubleshoot data discrepancies and work with relevant teams to resolve issues\n\n-\nSupport data migration and transformation activities as needed\n\nMinium Qualifications\n\n-\nHave 8+ years of experience in FP&A systems - EPM platforms, Finance data warehouse, with a focus on financial planning, forecasting and analysis.\n\n-\nHave hands-on experience administering and developing solutions in enterprise planning platforms (e.g., Pigment, Anaplan, Adaptive Planning, or similar EPM tools)\n\n-\nPossess strong engineering and technical skills including advanced SQL and data modeling skills, creating and maintaining system integrations and data pipelines.\n\n-\nHave demonstrated ability to translate business requirements into technical specifications and system designs.\n\n-\nHave a strong understanding of FP&A processes, financial reporting, and accounting principles\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n-\nTechno-functional: you're someone who is a CFA but also a hands on developer.\n\n-\nExperience owning changes inside a shared production codebase alongside a product engineering team\n\n-\nWarehouse and analytics-engineering skills such as dbt, BigQuery, or comparable\n\n-\nExperience building robust Finance applications with LLMs\n\n-\nKnowledge of programming or scripting languages (Python, JavaScript, etc.)\n\n-\nExperience with Financial planning & analysis (CFA), experience with pre-IPO companies, supporting rapid growth and scaling financial systems accordingly.\n\n-\nUnderstanding of financial data security and compliance requirements\n\n-\nCertification in relevant planning platforms (e.g., Pigment, Anaplan Model Builder)\n\n-\nProject management skills and experience leading system implementation workstreams\n\nThe annual compensation range for this role is listed below.\n\nFor sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (\"OTE\") range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.\n\nAnnual Salary:\n$205,000 — $270,000 USD\n\nLogistics\n\nMinimum education: Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience\n\nRequired field of study: A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience\n\nMinimum years of experience: Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position\n\nLocation-based hybrid policy: Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.\n\nVisa sponsorship: We do sponsor visas! However, we aren't able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.\n\nWe encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification. Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed. Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you're interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we're building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.\n\nYour safety matters to us. To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from @anthropic.com email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you're ever unsure about a communication, don't click any links—visit anthropic.com/careers directly for confirmed position openings.\n\nHow we're different\n\nWe believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We're an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.\n\nThe easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI & Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.\n\nCome work with us!\n\nAnthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. Guidance on Candidates' AI Usage: Learn about our policy for using AI in our application process.","description_html":"<div class=\"content-intro\"><h2><strong>About Anthropic</strong></h2>\n<p>Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.</p></div><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2>\n<p>We are looking for a Finance &amp; Strategy (FP&amp;A)&nbsp; Systems Engineer to join our Finance Systems team at Anthropic. In this role, you will be responsible for building and maintaining platforms that support our core Financial Planning, Forecasting and Analytics processes. You will bring deep hands-on expertise in EPM platforms like Anaplan, Pigment and data platforms like BigQuery, who writes integrations, tooling, and production code that connect them to Anthropic’s ERP and data warehouse systems. You'll work closely with Corporate Finance &amp; strategy stakeholders to translate business requirements into innovative technical solutions, maintain data integrity, and drive continuous improvements to our financial systems infrastructure.</p>\n<p>You'll manage day-to-day Finance system operations, support critical financial processes and monthly Forecasting cycles, and take on more ambitious system projects over time, including using Claude to automate FP&amp;A work, help build scalable solutions that enable efficient financial planning, forecasting, and reporting as we continue to grow.</p>\n<h2><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h2>\n<h3><strong>Systems Administration and Support</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Serve as a primary system administrator for our financial planning platform (Pigment), maintaining system health and optimal performance</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Manage Finance applications, data, user access &amp; security,&nbsp; system configurations, version management to ensure appropriate controls and governance.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Provide technical support and troubleshooting for end-users, resolving issues and answering system-related questions</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3><strong>System Development and Enhancement&nbsp;</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Design, build, and maintain applications, Financial&nbsp; models and workflows with in-house tools and EPM platform like Pigment to support financial planning, budgeting, forecasting, and reporting processes</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Develop and maintain secure dataflows, integrations using Rest APIs to connect FP&amp;A platforms, data warehouse with enterprise systems (e.g., Workday Financials, Salesforce CRM, etc.)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Develop SQL-based data models, ETL pipelines, and reporting infrastructure to support financial close, forecasting, and business intelligence.&nbsp;</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3><strong>Business Partnership and Process Improvement</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Partner with Finance &amp; Strategy (FP&amp;A), Accounting, and other Finance teams to understand business problems and use AI tools to build cutting edge solutions</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Support Monthly Forecast, Annual &amp; Long Range planning, Workforce planning, OPEX Forecasting, Balance Sheet &amp; Cash flow forecasting processes.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Identify and implement process and Finance platform&nbsp; improvements.&nbsp;</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Participate in testing and validation of system changes, ensuring accuracy and reliability</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Assist with training and onboarding of new system users</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3><strong>Data Management and Quality</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Ensure the accuracy and integrity of financial data across systems</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Develop and maintain data validation rules and quality checks</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Troubleshoot data discrepancies and work with relevant teams to resolve issues</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Support data migration and transformation activities as needed</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><strong>Minium Qualifications</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Have 8+ years of experience in FP&amp;A systems -&nbsp; EPM platforms, Finance data warehouse, with a focus on financial planning, forecasting and analysis.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Have hands-on experience administering and developing solutions in enterprise planning platforms (e.g., Pigment, Anaplan, Adaptive Planning, or similar EPM tools)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Possess strong engineering and technical skills including advanced SQL and data modeling skills, creating and maintaining system integrations and data pipelines.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Have demonstrated ability to translate business requirements into technical specifications and system designs.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Have a strong understanding of FP&amp;A processes, financial reporting, and accounting principles</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Techno-functional: you're someone who is a CFA but also a hands on developer.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Experience owning changes inside a shared production codebase alongside a product engineering team</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Warehouse and analytics-engineering skills such as dbt, BigQuery, or comparable</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Experience building robust Finance applications with LLMs&nbsp;</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Knowledge of programming or scripting languages (Python, JavaScript, etc.)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Experience with Financial planning &amp; analysis (CFA), experience with pre-IPO companies, supporting rapid growth and scaling financial systems accordingly.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Understanding of financial data security and compliance requirements</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Certification in relevant planning platforms (e.g., Pigment, Anaplan Model Builder)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Project management skills and experience leading system implementation workstreams</p>\n</li>\n</ul><div class=\"content-pay-transparency\"><div class=\"pay-input\"><div class=\"description\"><p>The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (\"OTE\") range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.</p></div><div class=\"title\">Annual Salary:</div><div class=\"pay-range\"><span>$205,000</span><span class=\"divider\">&mdash;</span><span>$270,000 USD</span></div></div></div><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><h2><strong>Logistics</strong></h2>\n<p><strong>Minimum education: </strong>Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience</p>\n<p><strong>Required field of study:&nbsp;</strong>A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience</p>\n<p><strong>Minimum years of experience: </strong>Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position</p>\n<p><strong>Location-based hybrid policy:</strong> Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.</p>\n<p><strong data-stringify-type=\"bold\">Visa sponsorship:</strong>&nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren't able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.</p>\n<p><strong>We encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification.</strong> Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed.&nbsp; Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you're interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we're building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.<br><br><strong data-stringify-type=\"bold\">Your safety matters to us.</strong> To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from&nbsp;@anthropic.com&nbsp;email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you're ever unsure about a communication, don't click any links—visit&nbsp;<u data-stringify-type=\"underline\"><a class=\"c-link c-link--underline\" href=\"http://anthropic.com/careers\" target=\"_blank\" data-stringify-link=\"http://anthropic.com/careers\" data-sk=\"tooltip_parent\" data-remove-tab-index=\"true\">anthropic.com/careers</a></u>&nbsp;directly for confirmed position openings.</p>\n<h2><strong>How we're different</strong></h2>\n<p>We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We're an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.</p>\n<p>The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.</p>\n<h2><strong>Come work with us!</strong></h2>\n<p>Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. <strong data-stringify-type=\"bold\">Guidance on Candidates' AI Usage:</strong>&nbsp;Learn about&nbsp;<a class=\"c-link\" href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance\" target=\"_blank\" data-stringify-link=\"https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance\" data-sk=\"tooltip_parent\">our policy</a> for using AI in our application process.</p></div>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"Location Type":"On-Site"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Systems Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["ai-ml","ai-infra","research"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"greenhouse:anthropic:5357947008","source":{"type":"greenhouse","board":"anthropic","job_id":"5357947008","source_url":"https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/anthropic/jobs","response_hash":"c2d25668c88a52b4b81f64ce7a90c40c3166d111ccb651bc7d36ccc8f32c67c9","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Anthropic","slug":"anthropic","lists":["ai-ml","ai-infra","research"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Finance Systems Engineer, Tax","canonical_url":"https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/anthropic/jobs/5357947008","apply_url":"https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/anthropic/jobs/5357947008","locations":[{"label":"San Francisco, CA | Seattle, WA"},{"label":"San Francisco, California, United States"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"unknown","departments":["Finance"],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":"P-5144","internal_job_id":4517517008,"first_published_at":"2026-08-07T11:01:34-04:00","source_updated_at":"2026-08-21T12:50:38-04:00","application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"About Anthropic\n\nAnthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.\n\nAbout the Role\n\nAnthropic's Tax Technology function sits inside Finance Systems and owns the systems that make every revenue and purchasing motion bookable, taxable, and auditable from day one. We're looking for a tax technologist who builds: someone who already understands how tax systems work and who writes the integrations, tooling, and production code that connect them to Anthropic billing, ERP, and data warehouse systems.\n\nYou'll build across all of tax, including indirect tax, corporate income tax and provision, withholding tax, R&D credits, and transfer pricing. You'll be a foundational hire on a small team, working directly with the Tax Technology Lead and be a trusted partner to our cross functional partners in Tax, Data Science, Billing Engineering and Product, among others. You'll be the key Anthropic tax technology technical resource building and hardening the tax-specific tooling and audit-ready evidence pipelines that allow the function to keep pace as the business grows.\n\nThis role is expected to take on more ambitious projects over time, including using Claude to automate tax work end to end and building internal products that are both high impact and seamless to use for the Tax team.\n\nKey responsibilities\n\n- Own tax-related changes in the billing codebase and the billing-to-tax-engine integration, including withholding tax considerations\n\n- Lead the AP tax engine implementation across ERP-connected purchasing flows: data migration, integration pipelines, parallel-run reconciliation, e-invoicing and go-live validation\n\n- Build and iterate tax-specific products and internal tooling across the full tax stack, including indirect tax reconciliations, provision and research credit data pipelines, transfer pricing datasets, withholding tracking, and exemption and validation tooling\n\n- Own the production connection points between the tax stack and our data infrastructure, feeding the central ingestion layer\n\n- Build SOX-aware IPE and control-total tooling on tax data flows: ingestion control totals, source-to-target tie-outs, and evidence pipelines that stand up to external audit\n\n- Design and build tooling that applies Claude to tax work and gives non-technical tax colleagues self-serve access to data, calculations, and evidence\n\n- Serve as the technical owner for vendor implementation handoffs, in the room during the build and accountable after go-live\n\n- Partner with Billing Engineering, Data Platform, Tax, Treasury and Product to keep the tax stack optimized and compliant as new products and jurisdictions come online\n\nMinimum qualifications\n\n- Hands-on experience building or owning production integrations against billing platforms, ERPs, or enterprise tax or finance systems\n\n- Tax-systems fluency in at least one domain (indirect tax engines, corporate tax provision or compliance tooling, withholding, research credit, or transfer pricing systems), gained at a tax-technology practice, a tax software vendor, or an in-house tax-systems team\n\n- Proficiency writing production-grade Python, with testing and code-review discipline\n\n- SQL proficiency sufficient to build reconciliations and validate data end to end\n\n- Experience building or operating SOX-aware data flows, such as IPE, control totals, or documented and testable pipelines\n\n- Ability to work independently in a constantly changing and fast paced environment\n\n- Ability to work directly with vendors, auditors, engineers, and the tax team without an intermediary\n\nPreferred qualifications\n\n- 7+ years in tax technology, finance systems engineering, or a closely related field\n\n- Experience owning changes inside a shared production codebase alongside a product engineering team\n\n- Warehouse and analytics-engineering skills such as dbt, BigQuery, or comparable\n\n- Breadth across multiple tax domains, including indirect (sales/use, VAT/GST), corporate income tax and provision, withholding, research credit, and transfer pricing data\n\n- Experience building internal tools or interfaces for non-technical finance or tax users\n\n- Experience building with LLMs or applying AI to finance or tax work\n\n- Marketplace, usage-based, or platform billing exposure\n\n- Experience taking over vendor-built systems and hardening them for long-term ownership\n\n- UAT design and change-management experience on finance-systems implementations\n\n- Record of novel AI applications for foundational tax tasks or problems\n\nThe annual compensation range for this role is listed below.\n\nFor sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (\"OTE\") range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.\n\nAnnual Salary:\n$205,000 — $270,000 USD\n\nLogistics\n\nMinimum education: Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience\n\nRequired field of study: A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience\n\nMinimum years of experience: Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position\n\nLocation-based hybrid policy: Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.\n\nVisa sponsorship: We do sponsor visas! However, we aren't able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.\n\nWe encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification. Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed. Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you're interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we're building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.\n\nYour safety matters to us. To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from @anthropic.com email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you're ever unsure about a communication, don't click any links—visit anthropic.com/careers directly for confirmed position openings.\n\nHow we're different\n\nWe believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We're an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.\n\nThe easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI & Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.\n\nCome work with us!\n\nAnthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. Guidance on Candidates' AI Usage: Learn about our policy for using AI in our application process.","description_html":"<div class=\"content-intro\"><h2><strong>About Anthropic</strong></h2>\n<p>Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.</p></div><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2>\n<p>Anthropic's Tax Technology function sits inside Finance Systems and owns the systems that make every revenue and purchasing motion bookable, taxable, and auditable from day one. We're looking for a tax technologist who builds: someone who already understands how tax systems work and who writes the integrations, tooling, and production code that connect them to Anthropic billing, ERP, and data warehouse systems.</p>\n<p>You'll build across all of tax, including indirect tax, corporate income tax and provision, withholding tax, R&amp;D credits, and transfer pricing. You'll be a foundational hire on a small team, working directly with the Tax Technology Lead and be a trusted partner to our cross functional partners in Tax, Data Science, Billing Engineering and Product, among others.&nbsp; You'll be the key Anthropic tax technology technical resource building and hardening the tax-specific tooling and audit-ready evidence pipelines that allow the function to keep pace as the business grows.</p>\n<p>This role is expected to take on more ambitious projects over time, including using Claude to automate tax work end to end and building internal products that are both high impact and seamless to use for the Tax team.</p>\n<h2><strong>Key responsibilities</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Own tax-related changes in the billing codebase and the billing-to-tax-engine integration, including withholding tax considerations</li>\n<li>Lead the AP tax engine implementation across ERP-connected purchasing flows: data migration, integration pipelines, parallel-run reconciliation, e-invoicing and go-live validation</li>\n<li>Build and iterate tax-specific products and internal tooling across the full tax stack, including indirect tax reconciliations, provision and research credit data pipelines, transfer pricing datasets, withholding tracking, and exemption and validation tooling</li>\n<li>Own the production connection points between the tax stack and our data infrastructure, feeding the central ingestion layer</li>\n<li>Build SOX-aware IPE and control-total tooling on tax data flows: ingestion control totals, source-to-target tie-outs, and evidence pipelines that stand up to external audit</li>\n<li>Design and build tooling that applies Claude to tax work and gives non-technical tax colleagues self-serve access to data, calculations, and evidence</li>\n<li>Serve as the technical owner for vendor implementation handoffs, in the room during the build and accountable after go-live</li>\n<li>Partner with Billing Engineering, Data Platform, Tax, Treasury and Product to keep the tax stack optimized and compliant as new products and jurisdictions come online</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><strong>Minimum qualifications</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Hands-on experience building or owning production integrations against billing platforms, ERPs, or enterprise tax or finance systems</li>\n<li>Tax-systems fluency in at least one domain (indirect tax engines, corporate tax provision or compliance tooling, withholding, research credit, or transfer pricing systems), gained at a tax-technology practice, a tax software vendor, or an in-house tax-systems team</li>\n<li>Proficiency writing production-grade Python, with testing and code-review discipline</li>\n<li>SQL proficiency sufficient to build reconciliations and validate data end to end</li>\n<li>Experience building or operating SOX-aware data flows, such as IPE, control totals, or documented and testable pipelines</li>\n<li>Ability to work independently in a constantly changing and fast paced environment</li>\n<li>Ability to work directly with vendors, auditors, engineers, and the tax team without an intermediary</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><strong>Preferred qualifications</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>7+ years in tax technology, finance systems engineering, or a closely related field</li>\n<li>Experience owning changes inside a shared production codebase alongside a product engineering team</li>\n<li>Warehouse and analytics-engineering skills such as dbt, BigQuery, or comparable</li>\n<li>Breadth across multiple tax domains, including indirect (sales/use, VAT/GST), corporate income tax and provision, withholding, research credit, and transfer pricing data</li>\n<li>Experience building internal tools or interfaces for non-technical finance or tax users</li>\n<li>Experience building with LLMs or applying AI to finance or tax work</li>\n<li>Marketplace, usage-based, or platform billing exposure</li>\n<li>Experience taking over vendor-built systems and hardening them for long-term ownership</li>\n<li>UAT design and change-management experience on finance-systems implementations</li>\n<li>Record of novel AI applications for foundational tax tasks or problems</li>\n</ul><div class=\"content-pay-transparency\"><div class=\"pay-input\"><div class=\"description\"><p>The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (\"OTE\") range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.</p></div><div class=\"title\">Annual Salary:</div><div class=\"pay-range\"><span>$205,000</span><span class=\"divider\">&mdash;</span><span>$270,000 USD</span></div></div></div><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><h2><strong>Logistics</strong></h2>\n<p><strong>Minimum education: </strong>Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience</p>\n<p><strong>Required field of study:&nbsp;</strong>A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience</p>\n<p><strong>Minimum years of experience: </strong>Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position</p>\n<p><strong>Location-based hybrid policy:</strong> Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.</p>\n<p><strong data-stringify-type=\"bold\">Visa sponsorship:</strong>&nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren't able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.</p>\n<p><strong>We encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification.</strong> Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed.&nbsp; Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you're interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we're building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.<br><br><strong data-stringify-type=\"bold\">Your safety matters to us.</strong> To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from&nbsp;@anthropic.com&nbsp;email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you're ever unsure about a communication, don't click any links—visit&nbsp;<u data-stringify-type=\"underline\"><a class=\"c-link c-link--underline\" href=\"http://anthropic.com/careers\" target=\"_blank\" data-stringify-link=\"http://anthropic.com/careers\" data-sk=\"tooltip_parent\" data-remove-tab-index=\"true\">anthropic.com/careers</a></u>&nbsp;directly for confirmed position openings.</p>\n<h2><strong>How we're different</strong></h2>\n<p>We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We're an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.</p>\n<p>The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.</p>\n<h2><strong>Come work with us!</strong></h2>\n<p>Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. <strong data-stringify-type=\"bold\">Guidance on Candidates' AI Usage:</strong>&nbsp;Learn about&nbsp;<a class=\"c-link\" href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance\" target=\"_blank\" data-stringify-link=\"https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance\" data-sk=\"tooltip_parent\">our policy</a> for using AI in our application process.</p></div>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"Location Type":"On-Site"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Systems Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["ai-ml","ai-infra","research"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"greenhouse:anthropic:5302966008","source":{"type":"greenhouse","board":"anthropic","job_id":"5302966008","source_url":"https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/anthropic/jobs","response_hash":"c5a8f8a220e4b7ce5d351e7c8e44ada9f24867410731a3b520095b21ff7ad340","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Anthropic","slug":"anthropic","lists":["ai-ml","ai-infra","research"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Forward Deployed Engineer","canonical_url":"https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/anthropic/jobs/5302966008","apply_url":"https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/anthropic/jobs/5302966008","locations":[{"label":"New York City, NY; San Francisco, CA; Seattle, WA"},{"label":"San Francisco, California, United States"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"unknown","departments":["Applied AI"],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":"PIP-266140","internal_job_id":4505476008,"first_published_at":"2026-08-12T16:21:16-04:00","source_updated_at":"2026-08-21T12:50:32-04:00","application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"About Anthropic\n\nAnthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.\n\nAbout the role:\n\nAs a member of the Applied AI team at Anthropic, you will be a Forward Deployed Engineer (FDE) who embeds directly with our most strategic customers to drive transformational AI adoption. You will collaborate closely with customer teams to ship advanced AI applications that solve real world business problems. Our FDEs engage with customers to accelerate the adoption of existing products and create new applications built on our models.\n\nWorking closely with our Post-Sales, Product, and Engineering teams, you'll combine engineering expertise, an understanding of frontier AI applications, and customer-facing skills to understand customer workflows and develop innovative solutions that address complex business challenges while maintaining our high standards for safety and reliability.\n\nYou will sit at the frontier of enterprise AI deployments and serve as one of our founding FDEs who helps to shape our forward-deployed motion. We expect our FDEs to operate autonomously, thrive under ambiguity, and represent Anthropic at the highest level in customer environments. This is a significant responsibility: you’ll play a key role in championing our mission in the enterprise.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n- Work within customer systems to build production applications with Claude models, ensuring that these products meet customer requirements.\n\n- Deliver technical artifacts for customers like MCP servers, sub-agents, and agent skills that will be used in production workflows.\n\n- Provide white glove deployment support for Anthropic products in enterprise environments.\n\n- Identify and codify repeatable deployment patterns and contribute insights back to our Product and Engineering teams.\n\n- Maintain strong knowledge of the latest developments in LLM capabilities, implementation patterns, and AI product development stacks.\n\n- Build long term relationships with customers and proactively identify new opportunities for AI deployment throughout the lifecycle of an engagement.\n\n- Potential Travel (based on location) to customer sites to build in person with customers. - Estimated 25%\n\n- Be a champion for Anthropic’s mission in the field.\n\nYou May Be a Good Fit If You Have:\n\n- 4+ years of experience in a technical, customer facing role such as Forward Deployed Engineer, or as a Software Engineer with consulting experience. Former technical founders are also encouraged to apply.\n\n- Production experience with LLMs including advanced prompt engineering, agent development, evaluation frameworks, and deployment at scale.\n\n- Strong programming skills with proficiency in Python (and ideally in one or more additional languages like Typescript, Java, etc) and experience shipping production applications\n\n- High agency with an ability to navigate ambiguity present in complex organizations.\n\n- High cooperation mindset for cross-organizational collaboration, balancing competing priorities with integrity.\n\n- Passion for advancing safe, beneficial AI systems through creative technical applications.\n\n- Strong communication skills to conduct discovery with customers and to convey technical concepts to diverse stakeholders while maintaining a low ego and collaborative approach.\n\n- A background in financial services, healthcare/life sciences, or another enterprise vertical is a plus.\n\n- Experience with enterprise IT systems and/or AI deployment patterns is a plus.\n\n- Experience working as an FDE or in a professional services context is a plus.\n\nThe annual compensation range for this role is listed below.\n\nFor sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (\"OTE\") range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.\n\nAnnual Salary:\n$280,000 — $320,000 USD\n\nLogistics\n\nMinimum education: Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience\n\nRequired field of study: A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience\n\nMinimum years of experience: Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position\n\nLocation-based hybrid policy: Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.\n\nVisa sponsorship: We do sponsor visas! However, we aren't able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.\n\nWe encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification. Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed. Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you're interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we're building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.\n\nYour safety matters to us. To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from @anthropic.com email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you're ever unsure about a communication, don't click any links—visit anthropic.com/careers directly for confirmed position openings.\n\nHow we're different\n\nWe believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We're an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.\n\nThe easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI & Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.\n\nCome work with us!\n\nAnthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. Guidance on Candidates' AI Usage: Learn about our policy for using AI in our application process.","description_html":"<div class=\"content-intro\"><h2><strong>About Anthropic</strong></h2>\n<p>Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.</p></div><h2><strong>About the role:</strong></h2>\n<p>As a member of the Applied AI team at Anthropic, you will be a Forward Deployed Engineer (FDE) who embeds directly with our most strategic customers to drive transformational AI adoption. You will collaborate closely with customer teams to ship advanced AI applications that solve real world business problems. Our FDEs engage with customers to accelerate the adoption of existing products and create new applications built on our models.</p>\n<p>Working closely with our Post-Sales, Product, and Engineering teams, you'll combine engineering expertise, an understanding of frontier AI applications, and customer-facing skills to understand customer workflows and develop innovative solutions that address complex business challenges while maintaining our high standards for safety and reliability.</p>\n<p>You will sit at the frontier of enterprise AI deployments and serve as one of our founding FDEs who helps to shape our forward-deployed motion. We expect our FDEs to operate autonomously, thrive under ambiguity, and represent Anthropic at the highest level in customer environments. This is a significant responsibility: you’ll play a key role in championing our mission in the enterprise.</p>\n<h2><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Work within customer systems to build production applications with Claude models, ensuring that these products meet customer requirements.</li>\n<li>Deliver technical artifacts for customers like MCP servers, sub-agents, and agent skills that will be used in production workflows.</li>\n<li>Provide white glove deployment support for Anthropic products in enterprise environments.</li>\n<li>Identify and codify repeatable deployment patterns and contribute insights back to our Product and Engineering teams.</li>\n<li>Maintain strong knowledge of the latest developments in LLM capabilities, implementation patterns, and AI product development stacks.</li>\n<li>Build long term relationships with customers and proactively identify new opportunities for AI deployment throughout the lifecycle of an engagement.</li>\n<li>Potential Travel (based on location) to customer sites to build in person with customers. - Estimated 25%&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Be a champion for Anthropic’s mission in the field.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><strong>You May Be a Good Fit If You Have:</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>4+ years of experience in a technical, customer facing role such as Forward Deployed Engineer, or as a Software Engineer with consulting experience. Former technical founders are also encouraged to apply.</li>\n<li>Production experience with LLMs including advanced prompt engineering, agent development, evaluation frameworks, and deployment at scale.</li>\n<li>Strong programming skills with proficiency in Python (and ideally in one or more additional languages like Typescript, Java, etc) and experience shipping production applications&nbsp;</li>\n<li>High agency with an ability to navigate ambiguity present in complex organizations.</li>\n<li>High cooperation mindset for cross-organizational collaboration, balancing competing priorities with integrity.</li>\n<li>Passion for advancing safe, beneficial AI systems through creative technical applications.</li>\n<li>Strong communication skills to conduct discovery with customers and to convey technical concepts to diverse stakeholders while maintaining a low ego and collaborative approach.</li>\n<li>A background in financial services, healthcare/life sciences, or another enterprise vertical is a plus.</li>\n<li>Experience with enterprise IT systems and/or AI deployment patterns is a plus.</li>\n<li>Experience working as an FDE or in a professional services context is a plus.</li>\n</ul><div class=\"content-pay-transparency\"><div class=\"pay-input\"><div class=\"description\"><p>The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (\"OTE\") range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.</p></div><div class=\"title\">Annual Salary:</div><div class=\"pay-range\"><span>$280,000</span><span class=\"divider\">&mdash;</span><span>$320,000 USD</span></div></div></div><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><h2><strong>Logistics</strong></h2>\n<p><strong>Minimum education: </strong>Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience</p>\n<p><strong>Required field of study:&nbsp;</strong>A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience</p>\n<p><strong>Minimum years of experience: </strong>Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position</p>\n<p><strong>Location-based hybrid policy:</strong> Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.</p>\n<p><strong data-stringify-type=\"bold\">Visa sponsorship:</strong>&nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren't able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.</p>\n<p><strong>We encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification.</strong> Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed.&nbsp; Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you're interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we're building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.<br><br><strong data-stringify-type=\"bold\">Your safety matters to us.</strong> To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from&nbsp;@anthropic.com&nbsp;email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you're ever unsure about a communication, don't click any links—visit&nbsp;<u data-stringify-type=\"underline\"><a class=\"c-link c-link--underline\" href=\"http://anthropic.com/careers\" target=\"_blank\" data-stringify-link=\"http://anthropic.com/careers\" data-sk=\"tooltip_parent\" data-remove-tab-index=\"true\">anthropic.com/careers</a></u>&nbsp;directly for confirmed position openings.</p>\n<h2><strong>How we're different</strong></h2>\n<p>We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We're an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.</p>\n<p>The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.</p>\n<h2><strong>Come work with us!</strong></h2>\n<p>Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. <strong data-stringify-type=\"bold\">Guidance on Candidates' AI Usage:</strong>&nbsp;Learn about&nbsp;<a class=\"c-link\" href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance\" target=\"_blank\" data-stringify-link=\"https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance\" data-sk=\"tooltip_parent\">our policy</a> for using AI in our application process.</p></div>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"Location Type":"On-Site"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":[],"role_matches":["Forward Deployed"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["ai-ml","ai-infra","research"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"greenhouse:anthropic:5391016008","source":{"type":"greenhouse","board":"anthropic","job_id":"5391016008","source_url":"https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/anthropic/jobs","response_hash":"5e68b1b3324adf26644aa6c7706abcffa3df448cac471327608a915c38bd0fc6","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Anthropic","slug":"anthropic","lists":["ai-ml","ai-infra","research"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Forward Deployed Engineer","canonical_url":"https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/anthropic/jobs/5391016008","apply_url":"https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/anthropic/jobs/5391016008","locations":[{"label":"Munich, Germany"},{"label":"München, Bavaria, Germany"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"unknown","departments":["Applied AI"],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":"266679","internal_job_id":4532903008,"first_published_at":"2026-08-17T08:05:11-04:00","source_updated_at":"2026-08-21T12:50:57-04:00","application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"About Anthropic\n\nAnthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.\n\nAs a member of the Applied AI team at Anthropic, you will be a Forward Deployed Engineer (FDE) who embeds directly with our most strategic customers to drive transformational AI adoption. You will collaborate closely with customer teams to ship advanced AI applications that solve real world business problems. Our FDEs engage with customers to accelerate the adoption of existing products and create new applications built on our models.\n\nWorking closely with our Post-Sales, Product, and Engineering teams, you'll combine engineering expertise, an understanding of frontier AI applications, and customer-facing skills to understand customer workflows and develop innovative solutions that address complex business challenges while maintaining our high standards for safety and reliability.\n\nYou will sit at the frontier of enterprise AI deployments and serve as one of our founding FDEs who helps to shape our forward-deployed motion. We expect our FDEs to operate autonomously, thrive under ambiguity, and represent Anthropic at the highest level in customer environments. This is a significant responsibility: you’ll play a key role in championing our mission in the enterprise.\n\nResponsibilities\n\n- Work within customer systems to build production applications with Claude models, ensuring that these products meet customer requirements.\n\n- Deliver technical artifacts for customers like MCP servers, sub-agents, and agent skills that will be used in production workflows.\n\n- Provide white glove deployment support for Anthropic products in enterprise environments.\n\n- Identify and codify repeatable deployment patterns and contribute insights back to our Product and Engineering teams.\n\n- Maintain strong knowledge of the latest developments in LLM capabilities, implementation patterns, and AI product development stacks.\n\n- Build long term relationships with customers and proactively identify new opportunities for AI deployment throughout the lifecycle of an engagement.\n\n- Travel frequently (25-50%) to customer sites to build in person with customers.\n\n- Be a champion for Anthropic’s mission in the field.\n\nYou May Be a Good Fit If You Have\n\n- 8+ years of experience in a technical, customer facing role such as Forward Deployed Engineer, or as a Software Engineer with consulting experience. Former technical founders are also encouraged to apply.\n\n- Native German speaker with fluent English proficiency\n\n- Production experience with LLMs including advanced prompt engineering, agent development, evaluation frameworks, and deployment at scale.\n\n- Strong programming skills with proficiency in Python (and ideally in one or more additional languages like TypeScript, Java, etc) and experience shipping production applications\n\n- High agency with an ability to navigate ambiguity present in complex organizations.\n\n- High cooperation mindset for cross-organizational collaboration, balancing competing priorities with integrity.\n\n- Passion for advancing safe, beneficial AI systems through creative technical applications.\n\n- Strong communication skills to conduct discovery with customers and to convey technical concepts to diverse stakeholders while maintaining a low ego and collaborative approach.\n\n- A background in financial services, healthcare/life sciences, or another enterprise vertical is a plus.\n\n- Experience with enterprise IT systems and/or AI deployment patterns is a plus.\n\nLogistics\n\nMinimum education: Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience\n\nRequired field of study: A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience\n\nMinimum years of experience: Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position\n\nLocation-based hybrid policy: Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.\n\nVisa sponsorship: We do sponsor visas! However, we aren't able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.\n\nWe encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification. Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed. Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you're interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we're building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.\n\nYour safety matters to us. To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from @anthropic.com email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you're ever unsure about a communication, don't click any links—visit anthropic.com/careers directly for confirmed position openings.\n\nHow we're different\n\nWe believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We're an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.\n\nThe easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI & Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.\n\nCome work with us!\n\nAnthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. Guidance on Candidates' AI Usage: Learn about our policy for using AI in our application process.","description_html":"<div class=\"content-intro\"><h2><strong>About Anthropic</strong></h2>\n<p>Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.</p></div><div>As a member of the Applied AI team at Anthropic, you will be a Forward Deployed Engineer (FDE) who embeds directly with our most strategic customers to drive transformational AI adoption. You will collaborate closely with customer teams to ship advanced AI applications that solve real world business problems. Our FDEs engage with customers to accelerate the adoption of existing products and create new applications built on our models.<br><br>Working closely with our Post-Sales, Product, and Engineering teams, you'll combine engineering expertise, an understanding of frontier AI applications, and customer-facing skills to understand customer workflows and develop innovative solutions that address complex business challenges while maintaining our high standards for safety and reliability.<br><br>You will sit at the frontier of enterprise AI deployments and serve as one of our founding FDEs who helps to shape our forward-deployed motion. We expect our FDEs to operate autonomously, thrive under ambiguity, and represent Anthropic at the highest level in customer environments. This is a significant responsibility: you’ll play a key role in championing our mission in the enterprise.<br><br><strong>Responsibilities</strong></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Work within customer systems to build production applications with Claude models, ensuring that these products meet customer requirements.</li>\n<li>Deliver technical artifacts for customers like MCP servers, sub-agents, and agent skills that will be used in production workflows.</li>\n<li>Provide white glove deployment support for Anthropic products in enterprise environments.</li>\n<li>Identify and codify repeatable deployment patterns and contribute insights back to our Product and Engineering teams.</li>\n<li>Maintain strong knowledge of the latest developments in LLM capabilities, implementation patterns, and AI product development stacks.</li>\n<li>Build long term relationships with customers and proactively identify new opportunities for AI deployment throughout the lifecycle of an engagement.</li>\n<li>Travel frequently (25-50%) to customer sites to build in person with customers.</li>\n<li>Be a champion for Anthropic’s mission in the field.</li>\n</ul>\n<div><br><br><strong>You May Be a Good Fit If You Have</strong></div>\n<ul>\n<li>8+ years of experience in a technical, customer facing role such as Forward Deployed Engineer, or as a Software Engineer with consulting experience. Former technical founders are also encouraged to apply.</li>\n<li>Native German speaker with fluent English proficiency</li>\n<li>Production experience with LLMs including advanced prompt engineering, agent development, evaluation frameworks, and deployment at scale.</li>\n<li>Strong programming skills with proficiency in Python (and ideally in one or more additional languages like TypeScript, Java, etc) and experience shipping production applications</li>\n<li>High agency with an ability to navigate ambiguity present in complex organizations.</li>\n<li>High cooperation mindset for cross-organizational collaboration, balancing competing priorities with integrity.</li>\n<li>Passion for advancing safe, beneficial AI systems through creative technical applications.</li>\n<li>Strong communication skills to conduct discovery with customers and to convey technical concepts to diverse stakeholders while maintaining a low ego and collaborative approach.</li>\n<li>A background in financial services, healthcare/life sciences, or another enterprise vertical is a plus.</li>\n<li>Experience with enterprise IT systems and/or AI deployment patterns is a plus.</li>\n</ul><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><h2><strong>Logistics</strong></h2>\n<p><strong>Minimum education: </strong>Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience</p>\n<p><strong>Required field of study:&nbsp;</strong>A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience</p>\n<p><strong>Minimum years of experience: </strong>Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position</p>\n<p><strong>Location-based hybrid policy:</strong> Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.</p>\n<p><strong data-stringify-type=\"bold\">Visa sponsorship:</strong>&nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren't able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.</p>\n<p><strong>We encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification.</strong> Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed.&nbsp; Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you're interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we're building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.<br><br><strong data-stringify-type=\"bold\">Your safety matters to us.</strong> To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from&nbsp;@anthropic.com&nbsp;email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you're ever unsure about a communication, don't click any links—visit&nbsp;<u data-stringify-type=\"underline\"><a class=\"c-link c-link--underline\" href=\"http://anthropic.com/careers\" target=\"_blank\" data-stringify-link=\"http://anthropic.com/careers\" data-sk=\"tooltip_parent\" data-remove-tab-index=\"true\">anthropic.com/careers</a></u>&nbsp;directly for confirmed position openings.</p>\n<h2><strong>How we're different</strong></h2>\n<p>We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We're an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.</p>\n<p>The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.</p>\n<h2><strong>Come work with us!</strong></h2>\n<p>Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. <strong data-stringify-type=\"bold\">Guidance on Candidates' AI Usage:</strong>&nbsp;Learn about&nbsp;<a class=\"c-link\" href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance\" target=\"_blank\" data-stringify-link=\"https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance\" data-sk=\"tooltip_parent\">our policy</a> for using AI in our application process.</p></div>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"Location Type":"On-Site"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":[],"role_matches":["Forward Deployed"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["ai-ml","ai-infra","research"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"greenhouse:anthropic:5391021008","source":{"type":"greenhouse","board":"anthropic","job_id":"5391021008","source_url":"https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/anthropic/jobs","response_hash":"5e2342018cbbdf84a667cfdb55f9b2d8633c0864d859d4693ba49e9692674475","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z"},"company":{"name":"Anthropic","slug":"anthropic","lists":["ai-ml","ai-infra","research"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Forward Deployed Engineer","canonical_url":"https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/anthropic/jobs/5391021008","apply_url":"https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/anthropic/jobs/5391021008","locations":[{"label":"Paris, France"},{"label":"Paris, Paris, France"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"unknown","departments":["Applied AI"],"teams":[],"language":"en","requisition_id":"266680","internal_job_id":4532906008,"first_published_at":"2026-08-17T07:59:59-04:00","source_updated_at":"2026-08-21T12:50:58-04:00","application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"About Anthropic\n\nAnthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.\n\nEn tant que membre de l'équipe Applied AI d'Anthropic, vous serez ingénieur en déploiement avancé (FDE) qui s'engage directement auprès de nos clients les plus stratégiques pour favoriser l'adoption de l'IA transformationnelle. Vous collaborerez étroitement avec les équipes de clients pour livrer des applications d'IA avancées qui résolvent des problèmes commerciaux réels. Nos FDE interagissent avec les clients pour accélérer l'adoption des produits existants et créer de nouvelles applications basées sur nos modèles.\n\nEn travaillant en étroite collaboration avec nos équipes post-vente, produit et ingénierie, vous combinerez expertise en ingénierie, compréhension des applications IA de pointe et compétences en contact avec la clientèle pour comprendre les flux de travail clients et développer des solutions innovantes qui répondent à des défis commerciaux complexes tout en respectant nos normes élevées de sécurité et de fiabilité.\n\nVous serez à la pointe des déploiements d'IA en entreprise et vous serez l'une de nos fondatrices FDE qui contribue à façonner notre mouvement de déploiement vers l'avant. Nous attendons de nos FDE qu'ils travaillent de manière autonome, qu'ils s'épanouissent dans l'ambiguïté et qu'ils représentent Anthropic au plus haut niveau dans l'environnement de nos clients. Il s'agit d'une responsabilité importante : vous jouerez un rôle clé en défendant notre mission au sein de l'entreprise.\n\nResponsabilités\n\n- Travailler au sein des systèmes clients pour développer des applications de production avec les modèles Claude, en veillant à ce que ces produits répondent aux exigences des clients.\n\n- Fournir aux clients des artefacts techniques tels que des serveurs MCP, des sous-agents et des compétences d'agent qui seront utilisés dans les flux de travail de production.\n\n- Fournir une assistance au déploiement des produits Anthropic dans les environnements d'entreprise.\n\n- Identifier et codifier des modèles de déploiement reproductibles et fournir des informations à nos équipes Produit et Ingénierie.\n\n- Maintenir une connaissance approfondie des derniers développements en matière de capacités des LLM, de modèles de mise en œuvre et de piles technologiques de développement de produits d'IA.\n\n- Établir des relations à long terme avec les clients et identifier de manière proactive de nouvelles opportunités de déploiement de l'IA tout au long du cycle de vie d'un engagement.\n\n- Se déplacer fréquemment (25 à 50 %) sur les sites des clients afin de nouer des relations personnelles avec eux.\n\n- Être un champion de la mission d'Anthropic sur le terrain.\n\nProfil recherché :\n\n- Vous avez plus de 8 ans d'expérience dans un poste technique en contact avec la clientèle, par exemple en tant qu'ingénieur en déploiement avancé, ou en tant qu'ingénieur logiciel avec une expérience de conseil. Les anciens fondateurs techniques sont également encouragés à poser leur candidature.\n\n- Vous avez de l'expérience en production avec des LLM, incluant l'ingénierie avancée des prompts, le développement d'agents, les cadres d'évaluation et le déploiement à grande échelle.\n\n- Vous avez de solides compétences en programmation avec une maîtrise de Python (et idéalement d'un ou plusieurs autres langages comme TypeScript, Java, etc.) et une expérience de l'expédition d'applications de production.\n\nHaute capacité d'action, capable de surmonter l'ambiguïté qui caractérise les organisations complexes.\n• Esprit de coopération élevé pour la collaboration inter-organisationnelle, équilibrant les priorités concurrentes avec intégrité.\n• Passion pour la promotion de systèmes d'IA sûrs et bénéfiques à travers des applications techniques créatives.\n• Solides compétences en communication pour mener des discussions exploratoires avec les clients et transmettre des concepts techniques à divers intervenants tout en conservant une attitude humble et collaborative.\n• Une expérience dans le domaine des services financiers, des soins de santé/sciences de la vie ou d'un autre secteur d'activité est un atout.\n• Une expérience des systèmes informatiques d'entreprise et/ou des modèles de déploiement de l'IA est un atout.\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nAs a member of the Applied AI team at Anthropic, you will be a Forward Deployed Engineer (FDE) who embeds directly with our most strategic customers to drive transformational AI adoption. You will collaborate closely with customer teams to ship advanced AI applications that solve real world business problems. Our FDEs engage with customers to accelerate the adoption of existing products and create new applications built on our models.\n\nWorking closely with our Post-Sales, Product, and Engineering teams, you'll combine engineering expertise, an understanding of frontier AI applications, and customer-facing skills to understand customer workflows and develop innovative solutions that address complex business challenges while maintaining our high standards for safety and reliability.\n\nYou will sit at the frontier of enterprise AI deployments and serve as one of our founding FDEs who helps to shape our forward-deployed motion. We expect our FDEs to operate autonomously, thrive under ambiguity, and represent Anthropic at the highest level in customer environments. This is a significant responsibility: you’ll play a key role in championing our mission in the enterprise.\n\nResponsibilities\n\n- Work within customer systems to build production applications with Claude models, ensuring that these products meet customer requirements.\n\n- Deliver technical artifacts for customers like MCP servers, sub-agents, and agent skills that will be used in production workflows.\n\n- Provide white glove deployment support for Anthropic products in enterprise environments.\n\n- Identify and codify repeatable deployment patterns and contribute insights back to our Product and Engineering teams.\n\n- Maintain strong knowledge of the latest developments in LLM capabilities, implementation patterns, and AI product development stacks.\n\n- Build long term relationships with customers and proactively identify new opportunities for AI deployment throughout the lifecycle of an engagement.\n\n- Travel frequently (25-50%) to customer sites to build in person with customers.\n\n- Be a champion for Anthropic’s mission in the field.\n\nYou May Be a Good Fit If You Have\n\n- 8+ years of experience in a technical, customer facing role such as Forward Deployed Engineer, or as a Software Engineer with consulting experience. Former technical founders are also encouraged to apply.\n\n- Native French speaker with fluent English proficiency\n\n- Production experience with LLMs including advanced prompt engineering, agent development, evaluation frameworks, and deployment at scale.\n\n- Strong programming skills with proficiency in Python (and ideally in one or more additional languages like TypeScript, Java, etc) and experience shipping production applications\n\n- High agency with an ability to navigate ambiguity present in complex organizations.\n\n- High cooperation mindset for cross-organizational collaboration, balancing competing priorities with integrity.\n\n- Passion for advancing safe, beneficial AI systems through creative technical applications.\n\n- Strong communication skills to conduct discovery with customers and to convey technical concepts to diverse stakeholders while maintaining a low ego and collaborative approach.\n\n- A background in financial services, healthcare/life sciences, or another enterprise vertical is a plus.\n\n- Experience with enterprise IT systems and/or AI deployment patterns is a plus.\n\nLogistics\n\nMinimum education: Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience\n\nRequired field of study: A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience\n\nMinimum years of experience: Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position\n\nLocation-based hybrid policy: Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.\n\nVisa sponsorship: We do sponsor visas! However, we aren't able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.\n\nWe encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification. Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed. Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you're interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we're building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.\n\nYour safety matters to us. To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from @anthropic.com email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you're ever unsure about a communication, don't click any links—visit anthropic.com/careers directly for confirmed position openings.\n\nHow we're different\n\nWe believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We're an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.\n\nThe easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI & Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.\n\nCome work with us!\n\nAnthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. Guidance on Candidates' AI Usage: Learn about our policy for using AI in our application process.","description_html":"<div class=\"content-intro\"><h2><strong>About Anthropic</strong></h2>\n<p>Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.</p></div><div>En tant que membre de l'équipe Applied AI d'Anthropic, vous serez ingénieur en déploiement avancé (FDE) qui s'engage directement auprès de nos clients les plus stratégiques pour favoriser l'adoption de l'IA transformationnelle. Vous collaborerez étroitement avec les équipes de clients pour livrer des applications d'IA avancées qui résolvent des problèmes commerciaux réels. Nos FDE interagissent avec les clients pour accélérer l'adoption des produits existants et créer de nouvelles applications basées sur nos modèles.<br><br>En travaillant en étroite collaboration avec nos équipes post-vente, produit et ingénierie, vous combinerez expertise en ingénierie, compréhension des applications IA de pointe et compétences en contact avec la clientèle pour comprendre les flux de travail clients et développer des solutions innovantes qui répondent à des défis commerciaux complexes tout en respectant nos normes élevées de sécurité et de fiabilité.<br><br>Vous serez à la pointe des déploiements d'IA en entreprise et vous serez l'une de nos fondatrices FDE qui contribue à façonner notre mouvement de déploiement vers l'avant. Nous attendons de nos FDE qu'ils travaillent de manière autonome, qu'ils s'épanouissent dans l'ambiguïté et qu'ils représentent Anthropic au plus haut niveau dans l'environnement de nos clients. Il s'agit d'une responsabilité importante : vous jouerez un rôle clé en défendant notre mission au sein de l'entreprise.<br><br><strong>Responsabilités</strong></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Travailler au sein des systèmes clients pour développer des applications de production avec les modèles Claude, en veillant à ce que ces produits répondent aux exigences des clients.</li>\n<li>Fournir aux clients des artefacts techniques tels que des serveurs MCP, des sous-agents et des compétences d'agent qui seront utilisés dans les flux de travail de production.</li>\n<li>Fournir une assistance au déploiement des produits Anthropic dans les environnements d'entreprise.</li>\n<li>Identifier et codifier des modèles de déploiement reproductibles et fournir des informations à nos équipes Produit et Ingénierie.</li>\n<li>Maintenir une connaissance approfondie des derniers développements en matière de capacités des LLM, de modèles de mise en œuvre et de piles technologiques de développement de produits d'IA.</li>\n<li>Établir des relations à long terme avec les clients et identifier de manière proactive de nouvelles opportunités de déploiement de l'IA tout au long du cycle de vie d'un engagement.</li>\n<li>Se déplacer fréquemment (25 à 50 %) sur les sites des clients afin de nouer des relations personnelles avec eux.</li>\n<li>Être un champion de la mission d'Anthropic sur le terrain.</li>\n</ul>\n<div><strong>Profil recherché :</strong></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Vous avez plus de 8 ans d'expérience dans un poste technique en contact avec la clientèle, par exemple en tant qu'ingénieur en déploiement avancé, ou en tant qu'ingénieur logiciel avec une expérience de conseil. Les anciens fondateurs techniques sont également encouragés à poser leur candidature.</li>\n<li>Vous avez de l'expérience en production avec des LLM, incluant l'ingénierie avancée des prompts, le développement d'agents, les cadres d'évaluation et le déploiement à grande échelle.</li>\n<li>Vous avez de solides compétences en programmation avec une maîtrise de Python (et idéalement d'un ou plusieurs autres langages comme TypeScript, Java, etc.) et une expérience de l'expédition d'applications de production.</li>\n</ul>\n<div>Haute capacité d'action, capable de surmonter l'ambiguïté qui caractérise les organisations complexes.<br>• Esprit de coopération élevé pour la collaboration inter-organisationnelle, équilibrant les priorités concurrentes avec intégrité.<br>• Passion pour la promotion de systèmes d'IA sûrs et bénéfiques à travers des applications techniques créatives.<br>• Solides compétences en communication pour mener des discussions exploratoires avec les clients et transmettre des concepts techniques à divers intervenants tout en conservant une attitude humble et collaborative.<br>• Une expérience dans le domaine des services financiers, des soins de santé/sciences de la vie ou d'un autre secteur d'activité est un atout.<br>• Une expérience des systèmes informatiques d'entreprise et/ou des modèles de déploiement de l'IA est un atout.</div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div>-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br><br>As a member of the Applied AI team at Anthropic, you will be a Forward Deployed Engineer (FDE) who embeds directly with our most strategic customers to drive transformational AI adoption. You will collaborate closely with customer teams to ship advanced AI applications that solve real world business problems. Our FDEs engage with customers to accelerate the adoption of existing products and create new applications built on our models.<br><br>Working closely with our Post-Sales, Product, and Engineering teams, you'll combine engineering expertise, an understanding of frontier AI applications, and customer-facing skills to understand customer workflows and develop innovative solutions that address complex business challenges while maintaining our high standards for safety and reliability.<br><br>You will sit at the frontier of enterprise AI deployments and serve as one of our founding FDEs who helps to shape our forward-deployed motion. We expect our FDEs to operate autonomously, thrive under ambiguity, and represent Anthropic at the highest level in customer environments. This is a significant responsibility: you’ll play a key role in championing our mission in the enterprise.<br><br><strong>Responsibilities</strong></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Work within customer systems to build production applications with Claude models, ensuring that these products meet customer requirements.</li>\n<li>Deliver technical artifacts for customers like MCP servers, sub-agents, and agent skills that will be used in production workflows.</li>\n<li>Provide white glove deployment support for Anthropic products in enterprise environments.</li>\n<li>Identify and codify repeatable deployment patterns and contribute insights back to our Product and Engineering teams.</li>\n<li>Maintain strong knowledge of the latest developments in LLM capabilities, implementation patterns, and AI product development stacks.</li>\n<li>Build long term relationships with customers and proactively identify new opportunities for AI deployment throughout the lifecycle of an engagement.</li>\n<li>Travel frequently (25-50%) to customer sites to build in person with customers.</li>\n<li>Be a champion for Anthropic’s mission in the field.</li>\n</ul>\n<div><strong>You May Be a Good Fit If You Have</strong></div>\n<ul>\n<li>8+ years of experience in a technical, customer facing role such as Forward Deployed Engineer, or as a Software Engineer with consulting experience. Former technical founders are also encouraged to apply.</li>\n<li>Native French speaker with fluent English proficiency</li>\n<li>Production experience with LLMs including advanced prompt engineering, agent development, evaluation frameworks, and deployment at scale.</li>\n<li>Strong programming skills with proficiency in Python (and ideally in one or more additional languages like TypeScript, Java, etc) and experience shipping production applications</li>\n<li>High agency with an ability to navigate ambiguity present in complex organizations.</li>\n<li>High cooperation mindset for cross-organizational collaboration, balancing competing priorities with integrity.</li>\n<li>Passion for advancing safe, beneficial AI systems through creative technical applications.</li>\n<li>Strong communication skills to conduct discovery with customers and to convey technical concepts to diverse stakeholders while maintaining a low ego and collaborative approach.</li>\n<li>A background in financial services, healthcare/life sciences, or another enterprise vertical is a plus.</li>\n<li>Experience with enterprise IT systems and/or AI deployment patterns is a plus.</li>\n</ul><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><h2><strong>Logistics</strong></h2>\n<p><strong>Minimum education: </strong>Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience</p>\n<p><strong>Required field of study:&nbsp;</strong>A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience</p>\n<p><strong>Minimum years of experience: </strong>Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position</p>\n<p><strong>Location-based hybrid policy:</strong> Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.</p>\n<p><strong data-stringify-type=\"bold\">Visa sponsorship:</strong>&nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren't able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.</p>\n<p><strong>We encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification.</strong> Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed.&nbsp; Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you're interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we're building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.<br><br><strong data-stringify-type=\"bold\">Your safety matters to us.</strong> To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from&nbsp;@anthropic.com&nbsp;email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you're ever unsure about a communication, don't click any links—visit&nbsp;<u data-stringify-type=\"underline\"><a class=\"c-link c-link--underline\" href=\"http://anthropic.com/careers\" target=\"_blank\" data-stringify-link=\"http://anthropic.com/careers\" data-sk=\"tooltip_parent\" data-remove-tab-index=\"true\">anthropic.com/careers</a></u>&nbsp;directly for confirmed position openings.</p>\n<h2><strong>How we're different</strong></h2>\n<p>We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We're an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.</p>\n<p>The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.</p>\n<h2><strong>Come work with us!</strong></h2>\n<p>Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. <strong data-stringify-type=\"bold\">Guidance on Candidates' AI Usage:</strong>&nbsp;Learn about&nbsp;<a class=\"c-link\" href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance\" target=\"_blank\" data-stringify-link=\"https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance\" data-sk=\"tooltip_parent\">our policy</a> for using AI in our application process.</p></div>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"Location Type":"On-Site"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T03:47:44.181Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T09:13:58.725Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":[],"role_matches":["Forward Deployed"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["ai-ml","ai-infra","research"]}}
