{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Honolulu-HI/Application-Systems-Engineer_R0240161","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Honolulu-HI/Application-Systems-Engineer_R0240161","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"f5b65f6d196e21f24364fb874c378b2e7a577ae35dffe8328ad787a27bd862e6","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Application Systems Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Honolulu-HI/Application-Systems-Engineer_R0240161","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Honolulu-HI/Application-Systems-Engineer_R0240161","locations":[{"label":"Honolulu, HI"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0240161","internal_job_id":"4281f7c3ce061001b498c145c83d0000","first_published_at":"2026-07-30","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Application Systems Engineer The Opportunity:   \n\nAs an application engineer and administrator on our team, you’ll be integral to architecting, deploying, and operating complex system environments across various DoW clients in the Indo-Pacific. Provide critical administration on C2 systems such as GCCS as well as advanced application tools like Kernos and Maven Smart Systems. Assist in building a modern DevOps and DevSecOps environments and processes to optimize a data centric environment and delivery of decision quality outputs while maintaining rigorous cyber security requirements. You mentor the next set of admin and developers to help them grow into tomorrow’s data architects.\n\nWork with us and build the future of technology for the better.      \n\n   \n\nJoin us. The world  can’t  wait.   \n\n \n\nYou Have:   \n\n- 8+ years of experience application delivery\n\n- Experience with Palantir or Maven \n\n- Experience with Kernos \n\n- Experience in DevOps or DevSecOps delivery \n\n- Experience leading application development teams and projects \n\n- Secret clearance \n\n- HS diploma or GED \n\nNice If You Have:   \n\n- Experience with legacy C2 systems, such as GCCS, TBMCS, AFTADS, or Agile \n\n- Experience with Anduril Lattice \n\n- Experience in Agile software delivery practices \n\n- Knowledge of federal information security policies, standards, procedures, directives, frameworks, federal security authorizations, assessment, and risk management processes for enterprise systems \n\n- Bachelor's degree in an IT, Cybersecurity, or Engineering field \n\n  \n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is   required .  \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Application Systems Engineer<div><div><p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b><span> </span></p></div><div><p><span><span>As an application engineer and administrator on our team, you’ll be integral to architecting, deploying, and operating complex system environments across various DoW clients in the Indo-Pacific. Provide critical administration on C2 systems such as GCCS as well as advanced application tools like Kernos and Maven Smart Systems. Assist in building a modern DevOps and DevSecOps environments and processes to optimize a data centric environment and delivery of decision quality outputs while maintaining rigorous cyber security requirements. You mentor the next set of admin and developers to help them grow into tomorrow’s data architects. </span></span></p></div><p></p><div><p><span><span>Work with us and build the future of technology for the better.</span></span><span><span> </span></span><span><span> </span></span><span> </span></p></div><div><p><span><span> </span></span><span> </span></p></div><div><p><span><span>Join us. The world </span><span>can’t</span><span> wait. </span></span><span> </span></p></div><div><p><span> </span></p></div><div><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b><span> </span></p></div><div><ul><li><p><span><span>8&#43; years of experience application delivery</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience with Palantir or Maven </span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience with Kernos </span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience in DevOps or DevSecOps delivery </span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience leading application development teams and projects </span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Secret clearance </span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>HS diploma or GED </span></span></p></li></ul></div><div><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b><span> </span></p></div></div><div><div><ul><li><p><span><span>Experience with legacy C2 systems, such as GCCS, TBMCS, AFTADS, or Agile </span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience with Anduril Lattice </span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience in Agile software delivery practices </span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Knowledge of federal information security policies, standards, procedures, directives, frameworks, federal security authorizations, assessment, and risk management processes for enterprise systems </span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree in an IT, Cybersecurity, or Engineering field </span></span></p></li></ul></div><div><p><span>  </span></p></div><div><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is<span> </span></span><span>required</span><span>.</span></span><span> </span></p></div></div><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 25 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Systems Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/Applied-AI-Engineer_R0246156","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/Applied-AI-Engineer_R0246156","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"7b1a863dcba9099c2b343928dc4aaaeff40df5f2ac03a8b69687f4ced3128ba8","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Applied AI Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/Applied-AI-Engineer_R0246156","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Belvoir-VA/Applied-AI-Engineer_R0246156","locations":[{"label":"Fort Belvoir, VA"},{"label":"Reston, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246156","internal_job_id":"cdcfc075bb401001a02400efc3a90000","first_published_at":"2026-08-06","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Applied AI Engineer The Opportunity: \nAs an experience d engineer, you know that artifi cia l intelligence (AI) is critical to understanding and processing massive datasets. Your ability to conduct statistical analyses on business processes using ML techniques makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused solution. We need your technical knowledge and desire to problem-solve to support an enterprise-wide application and data capability. As an AI engineer on our national security team, you’ll train, test, deploy, and maintain models that learn from data.\n\nIn this role, you’ll own and define the direction of critical solutions by applying best-fit ML algorithms and technologies. You’ll be part of a large community of AI engineers across the company and collaborate with data engineers, data scientists, solutions architects, and MLOps engineers to deliver world class solutions, including processing data and information at a massive scale. Your skills and extensive technical expertise will guide clients as they navigate the landscape of AI and ML algorithms, tools, and frameworks. \n\nWork with us to solve real-world challenges and define AI strategy for our national security customers.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- 3+ years of experience in sof tware engineering, applied AI and ML, or full-stack development, including AI integrations\n- Experience rapidly prototyping, developing, and iterating on use-case-specific AI solutions such as chat systems, user-facing applications, and domain-specific copilots\n- Experience conducting comprehensive evaluation and tuning of AI outputs, including refining prompts, optimizing retrieval logic, and implementing custom heuristics\n- Experience with Python and building API endpoints such as FastAPI or Flask, or rapid UI frameworks such as Streamlit or Gradio, to demonstrate AI capabilities\n- Ability to work closely with mission integration teams and product stakeholders to translate mission needs into refined, business-facing AI capabilities\n- Ability to pivot quickly between different domains and use cases, adapting AI solutions to various operational requirements\n- TS/SCI clearance\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience with human-in-the-loop ( HITL ) evaluation, AI red teaming, or assessing conversational interfaces for safety and hallucination mitigation\n- Experience with front-end development technologies such as React or TypeScript, to support end-to-end user-facing product delivery\n- Experience deploying and managing analytical dashboards or mechanisms to track user interactions and model performance\n- Knowledge of user experience ( UX ) best practices, including conversational AI and generative interfaces\n- Security+ Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Applied AI Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>As an <span>experience</span>d engineer, you know that artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence (AI) is critical to understanding and processing massive datasets. Your <span>ability to</span> conduct statistical analyses on business processes using ML techniques makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused solution. We need your technical knowledge and desire to problem-solve to support an enterprise-wide application and data capability. As an AI engineer on our national security team, you’ll train, test, deploy, and maintain models that learn from data.</p><p></p><p>In this role, you’ll own and define the direction of critical solutions by applying best-fit ML algorithms and technologies. You’ll be part of a large community of AI engineers across the company and collaborate with data engineers, data scientists, solutions architects, and MLOps engineers to deliver world class solutions, including processing data and information at a massive scale. Your skills and extensive technical expertise will guide clients as they navigate the landscape of AI and ML algorithms, tools, and frameworks. </p><p></p><p>Work with us to solve real-world challenges and define AI strategy for our national security customers.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>  </p><ul><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>tware engineering, applied AI and ML, or full-stack development, including AI integrations</li><li><span>Experience</span> rapidly prototyping, developing, and iterating on use-case-specific AI solutions such as chat systems, user-facing applications, and domain-specific copilots</li><li><span>Experience</span> conducting comprehensive evaluation and tuning of AI outputs, including refining prompts, optimizing retrieval logic, and implementing custom heuristics</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Python and building API endpoints such as FastAPI or Flask, or rapid UI frameworks such as Streamlit or Gradio, to demonstrate AI capabilities</li><li><span>Ability to</span> work closely with mission integration teams and product stakeholders to translate mission needs into refined, business-facing AI capabilities</li><li><span>Ability to</span> pivot quickly between different domains and use cases, adapting AI solutions to various operational requirements</li><li><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></li><li><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>  </p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with human-in-the-loop <span>(</span>HITL<span>)</span> evaluation, AI red teaming, or assessing conversational interfaces for safety and hallucination mitigation</li><li><span>Experience</span> with front-end development technologies such as React or TypeScript, to support end-to-end user-facing product delivery</li><li><span>Experience</span> deploying and managing analytical dashboards or mechanisms to track user interactions and model performance</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> user <span>experience</span> <span>(</span>UX<span>)</span> best practices, including conversational AI and generative interfaces</li><li>Security&#43; <span>Certification</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance is required.</span></p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 18 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":6,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["AI Engineer","Applied AI"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["AI","Applied"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Arlington-VA/Applied-Data-Scientist_R0242962","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Arlington-VA/Applied-Data-Scientist_R0242962","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"e910b59696db68bb953cbe6c98ae5d2acb88ffceccc9ba69432ce22d11151ecf","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Applied Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Applied-Data-Scientist_R0242962","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Applied-Data-Scientist_R0242962","locations":[{"label":"Arlington, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0242962","internal_job_id":"93ded21bf03e10010a8fb01f35f50000","first_published_at":"2026-06-23","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Applied Data Scientist The Opportunity:\nAs a data scientist, you’re excited about building intelligent systems, not just analyzing data. You’re motivated to design, develop , and deploy machine learning and AI-driven capabilities that operate in real-world environments. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist, you’ll transform these data into operational systems by develop ing algorithms, training models, and deploying solutions that perform reliably at scale.\n\nOn our team, you’ll work closely with clients to understand mission needs and translate them into technical solutions. You’ll design and implement machine learning models, build supporting data pipelines, and deploy capabilities into production environments. You’ll apply a mix of statistical met hods, machine learning, and sof tware engineering to deliver end-to-end solutions. You’ll help move beyond analysis to create robust, maintainable AI and ML systems that deliver measurable impact.\n\nWork with us as we use data science for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:    \n- Experience develop ing machine learning or AI algorithms and applying pre-built models\n\n- Experience building and deploying ML and AI solutions into production or operational environments\n\n- Experience designing and implementing end-to-end ML pipelines, including data ingestion, training, evaluation, and deployment\n\n- Experience writing production-quality code in languages, such as Python\n\n- Experience working with structured and unstructured data at scale\n\n- Experience applying techniques such as optimization, simulation, or advanced machine learning met hods\n\n- Experience working in Linux-based or cloud-based environments\n\n- Experience using modern sof tware engineering practices, such as Git, testing, or CI / CD\n\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:    \n- Experience with deep learning, reinforcement learning, or advanced AI techniques\n\n- Experience building or fine-tuning custom models\n\n- Experience with containerization and deployment tools, such as Docker and Kubernetes\n\n- Experience with distributed data processing tools, such as Spark and Kafka\n\n- Experience integrating ML and AI capabilities into larger sof tware systems\n\n- Experience with optimization frameworks or simulation-based modeling\n\n- Experience working with DoW customers\n\n- Experience communicating complex technical concepts to non-technical stakeholders\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information .\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Applied Data Scientist<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b><br />As a data scientist, you’re excited about building intelligent systems, not just analyzing data. You’re motivated to design, <span>develop</span>, and deploy machine learning and AI-driven capabilities that operate in real-world environments. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist, you’ll transform these data into operational systems by <span>develop</span>ing algorithms, training models, and deploying solutions that perform reliably at scale.</p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll work closely with clients to understand mission needs and translate them into technical solutions. You’ll design and implement machine learning models, build supporting data pipelines, and deploy capabilities into production environments. You’ll apply a mix of statistical <span>met</span>hods, machine learning, and <span>sof</span>tware engineering to deliver end-to-end solutions. You’ll help move beyond analysis to create robust, maintainable AI and ML systems that deliver measurable impact.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we use data science for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> <span>develop</span>ing machine learning or AI algorithms and applying pre-built models</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> building and deploying ML and AI solutions into production or operational environments</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> designing and implementing end-to-end ML pipelines, including data ingestion, training, evaluation, and deployment</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> writing production-quality code in languages, such as Python</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> working with structured and unstructured data at scale</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> applying techniques such as optimization, simulation, or advanced machine learning <span>met</span>hods</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> working in Linux-based or cloud-based environments</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> using modern <span>sof</span>tware engineering practices, such as Git, testing, or CI<span>/</span>CD</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span><span> obtain a Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with deep learning, reinforcement learning, or advanced AI techniques</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> building or fine-tuning custom models</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with containerization and deployment tools, such as Docker and Kubernetes</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with distributed data processing tools, such as Spark and Kafka</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> integrating ML and AI capabilities into larger <span>sof</span>tware systems</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with optimization frameworks or simulation-based modeling</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> working with DoW customers</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> communicating complex technical concepts to non-technical stakeholders</p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span>.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Applied"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
