{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Arlington-VA/Artificial-Intelligence---Machine-Learning-Engineer_R0244720","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Arlington-VA/Artificial-Intelligence---Machine-Learning-Engineer_R0244720","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"730f0e4124fb3deda392887b8073206c09b9751da5068de1c77c21f161104956","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Artificial Intelligence & Machine Learning Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Artificial-Intelligence---Machine-Learning-Engineer_R0244720","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Artificial-Intelligence---Machine-Learning-Engineer_R0244720","locations":[{"label":"Arlington, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0244720","internal_job_id":"98fde5d94b9e1000c674bc4b2cd20000","first_published_at":"2026-07-20","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Artificial Intelligence & Machine Learning Engineer The Opportunity: \nAs an experienced AI/ML engineer, you know that modern machine learning requires more than accurate models, it demands strong engineering practices, thoughtful system design, and the ability to build solutions that perform reliably in production. Your ability to conduct statistical analyses, implement AI/ML techniques, and build robust AI/ML pipelines makes you integral to delivering customer‑focused solutions. We need your technical expertise and problem-solving mindset to support AI/ML missions across the federal government. As an AI/ML engineer on our team, you’ll design, train, test, deploy, and maintain end‑to‑end AI/ML systems, ensuring models perform reliably not just in development, but in production. \n\nIn this role, you’ll own and define the direction of mission-critical solutions by selecting best‑fit algorithms, architecting AI/ML pipelines, and applying modern MLOps practices. You’ll be part of a talented team of machine learning engineers across the company and collaborate with data engineers, data scientists, software engineers, and product owners to deliver world class solutions. Your skills and technical leadership will guide clients as they navigate the landscape of AI/ML tools, frameworks, and operational strategies. \n\nWork with us to solve real-world challenges and define AI/ML strategy for the Defense sector and beyond.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:  \n- 4+ years of experience as an Artificial Intelligence/Machine Learning Engineer or Advanced Data Scientist\n\n- Experience deploying and integrating production-grade AI/ML models using tools such as Docker or Kubernetes\n\n- Experience with Large Language Models (LLMs), Deep Learning (DL) or Reinforcement Learning (RL) algorithms, along with frameworks such as TensorFlow, PyTorch, vLLM, and Ollama\n\n- Knowledge of MLOps principles and the design and implementation of machine learning algorithms integrated in operational systems and deployed to production environments\n\n- Ability to train, optimize, and integrate AI/ML algorithms across high throughput text, image, or video data feeds\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience working in cloud environments, such as AWS or Azure\n\n- Experience developing production‑quality ML-enabled software components, such as RESTful APIs, microservices, or real‑time inference pipelines\n\n- Experience with emerging agentic AI frameworks and understanding of how to integrate agent‑based systems into production environments\n\n- TS/SCI clearance \n\n- Master's degree \n\nClearance:    \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.  \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Artificial Intelligence &amp; Machine Learning Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>As an experienced AI/ML engineer, you know that modern machine learning requires more than accurate models, it demands strong engineering practices, thoughtful system design, and the ability to build solutions that perform reliably in production. Your ability to conduct statistical analyses, implement AI/ML techniques, and build robust AI/ML pipelines makes you integral to delivering customer‑focused solutions. We need your technical expertise and problem-solving mindset to support AI/ML missions across the federal government. As an AI/ML engineer on our team, you’ll design, train, test, deploy, and maintain end‑to‑end AI/ML systems, ensuring models perform reliably not just in development, but in production. </p><p></p><p>In this role, you’ll own and define the direction of mission-critical solutions by selecting best‑fit algorithms, architecting AI/ML pipelines, and applying modern MLOps practices. You’ll be part of a talented team of machine learning engineers across the company and collaborate with data engineers, data scientists, software engineers, and product owners to deliver world class solutions. Your skills and technical leadership will guide clients as they navigate the landscape of AI/ML tools, frameworks, and operational strategies. </p><p></p><p>Work with us to solve real-world challenges and define AI/ML strategy for the Defense sector and beyond.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:  </b></p><ul><li><p>4&#43; years of experience as an Artificial Intelligence/Machine Learning Engineer or Advanced Data Scientist</p></li><li><p>Experience deploying and integrating production-grade AI/ML models using tools such as Docker or Kubernetes</p></li><li><p>Experience with Large Language Models (LLMs), Deep Learning (DL) or Reinforcement Learning (RL) algorithms, along with frameworks such as TensorFlow, PyTorch, vLLM, and Ollama</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of MLOps principles and the design and implementation of machine learning algorithms integrated in operational systems and deployed to production environments</p></li><li><p>Ability to train, optimize, and integrate AI/ML algorithms across high throughput text, image, or video data feeds</p></li><li><p>Secret clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:  </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience working in cloud environments, such as AWS or Azure</p></li><li><p>Experience developing production‑quality ML-enabled software components, such as RESTful APIs, microservices, or real‑time inference pipelines</p></li><li><p>Experience with emerging agentic AI frameworks and understanding of how to integrate agent‑based systems into production environments</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance </p></li><li><p>Master&#39;s degree </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b>   </p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.  </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":5,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["Machine Learning","Artificial Intelligence"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Machine Learning"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Wahiawa-HI/Artificial-Intelligence-and-Machine-Learning-Engineer--Senior_R0245163","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Wahiawa-HI/Artificial-Intelligence-and-Machine-Learning-Engineer--Senior_R0245163","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"4e074ce523e06cf0f0b073c1c14d294cf996391e1b5b49b0716dc938407f26a4","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning Engineer, Senior","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Wahiawa-HI/Artificial-Intelligence-and-Machine-Learning-Engineer--Senior_R0245163","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Wahiawa-HI/Artificial-Intelligence-and-Machine-Learning-Engineer--Senior_R0245163","locations":[{"label":"Wahiawa, HI"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"unknown","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245163","internal_job_id":null,"first_published_at":null,"source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":null,"description_html":null,"compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":null,"country":null,"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":false,"tier":"stretch","score":5,"level":"senior","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["Machine Learning","Artificial Intelligence"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Machine Learning"],"exclude_matches":["Senior"],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Uruma-City-Okinawa/Artificial-Intelligence-and-Machine-Learning-Specialist_R0243997","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Uruma-City-Okinawa/Artificial-Intelligence-and-Machine-Learning-Specialist_R0243997","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"21157806ac23fdfc5f2dcd566b79cac19a021e5bdbeaae6645ff4e635db896ce","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning Specialist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Uruma-City-Okinawa/Artificial-Intelligence-and-Machine-Learning-Specialist_R0243997","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Uruma-City-Okinawa/Artificial-Intelligence-and-Machine-Learning-Specialist_R0243997","locations":[{"label":"Uruma City, Okinawa"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0243997","internal_job_id":"2adb8a04dcd21001686ebfa7714f0000","first_published_at":"2026-07-09","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning Specialist The Opportunity:\nAs an artificial intelligence and machine learning (AI / ML) Spe cia list, you will serve as the technical lead for Maven Smart System integration with the client’s branch. This pivotal role will drive the adoption and advancement of enterprise-level AI/ML capabilities across operational and decision-making frameworks, ensuring seamless connectivity between locally developed models and the broader Department of Defense AI ecosystem. The selected candidate will architect, build, and deploy production-grade AI-driven solutions and automated workflows, manage scalable data pipelines, and provide technical leadership to cross-functional teams. Candidates must possess a strong background in sof tware engineering, data engineering, or MLOps, with demonstrated experience in integrating DoD AI systems, deep proficiency in Python, API development, and cloud-based AI / ML platforms. This is an exceptional opportunity to make a significant impact on the operational effectiveness of the Marine Corps through innovative AI / ML integration at the forefront of defense technology.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 3+ years of experience in sof tware engineering, data engineering, or MLOps roles\n- 2+ years of experience integrating with DoD AI systems, including Foundry AIP or Gaia\n- Experience using Python\n- Experience building and consuming APIs such as REST and gRPC, for system-to-system integration\n- Experience architecting end-to-end AI / ML solutions, including data pipelines and operational workflows\n- Experience in designing, building, deploying, and maintaining production-grade AI / ML systems and automated workflows\n- Knowledge of sof tware engineering best practices\n- Secret clearance\n- Bachelor’s degree in CS or Sof tware Engineering\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with MLOps tools and frameworks such as Kubeflow, MLflow, or Airflow\n- Experience with containerization technologies such as Docker and Kubernetes\n- Experience with cloud-based AI / ML platforms, including Azure ML or AWS SageMaker\n- Experience working in government cloud environments\n- Experience developing scalable data pipelines for real-time inference and integration with enterprise-level AI platforms\n- Ability to optimize performance of ML models and data pipelines for speed and scalability\n- Ability to provide technical leadership to sof tware developers and analysts\n- Possession of strong collaboration skills\n- Top Secret clearance\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning Specialist<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>As an artificial intelligence and machine learning (AI<span>/</span>ML) Spe<span>cia</span>list, you will serve as the technical lead for Maven Smart System integration with the client’s branch. This pivotal role will drive the adoption and advancement of enterprise-level AI/ML capabilities across operational and decision-making frameworks, ensuring seamless connectivity between locally developed models and the broader Department of Defense AI ecosystem. The selected candidate will architect, build, and deploy production-grade AI-driven solutions and automated workflows, manage scalable data pipelines, and provide technical leadership to cross-functional teams. Candidates must possess a strong background in <span>sof</span>tware engineering, data engineering, or MLOps, with demonstrated <span>experience</span> in integrating DoD AI systems, deep proficiency in Python, API development, and cloud-based AI<span>/</span>ML platforms. This is an exceptional opportunity to make a significant impact on the operational effectiveness of the Marine Corps through innovative AI<span>/</span>ML integration at the forefront of defense technology.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>tware engineering, data engineering, or MLOps roles</li><li>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> integrating with DoD AI systems, including Foundry AIP or Gaia</li><li><span>Experience</span> using Python</li><li><span>Experience</span> building and consuming APIs such as REST and gRPC, for system-to-system integration</li><li><span>Experience</span> architecting end-to-end AI<span>/</span>ML solutions, including data pipelines and operational workflows</li><li><span>Experience</span> in designing, building, deploying, and maintaining production-grade AI<span>/</span>ML systems and automated workflows</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> <span>sof</span>tware engineering best practices</li><li><span>Secret clearance </span></li><li><span>Bachelor’s degree</span> in CS or <span>Sof</span>tware Engineering</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with MLOps tools and frameworks such as Kubeflow, MLflow, or Airflow</li><li><span>Experience</span> with containerization technologies such as Docker and Kubernetes</li><li><span>Experience</span> with cloud-based AI<span>/</span>ML platforms, including Azure ML or AWS SageMaker</li><li><span>Experience</span> working in government cloud environments</li><li><span>Experience</span> developing scalable data pipelines for real-time inference and integration with enterprise-level AI platforms</li><li><span>Ability to</span> optimize performance of ML models and data pipelines for speed and scalability</li><li><span>Ability to</span> provide technical leadership to <span>sof</span>tware developers and analysts</li><li><span>Possession of</span> strong collaboration skills</li><li><span>Top Secret clearance </span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance: </span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"Japan","id":"8b705da2becf43cfaccc091da0988ab2"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":5,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["Machine Learning","Artificial Intelligence"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Machine Learning"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Honolulu-HI/Artificial-Intelligence-and-Optimization-Engineer_R0245830","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Honolulu-HI/Artificial-Intelligence-and-Optimization-Engineer_R0245830","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"ed48502ca27307a2a1ae76e8de70265a71d170816b3c027cde36c9c357318ec8","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Artificial Intelligence and Optimization Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Honolulu-HI/Artificial-Intelligence-and-Optimization-Engineer_R0245830","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Honolulu-HI/Artificial-Intelligence-and-Optimization-Engineer_R0245830","locations":[{"label":"Honolulu, HI"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245830","internal_job_id":"93645f7db5bc1001ffcd155438dc0000","first_published_at":"2026-07-31","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Artificial Intelligence and Optimization Engineer The Opportunity: \nAs an  experience d engineer, you know that AI is critical to understanding and processing massive datasets. Your  ability to  conduct statistical analyses on business processes using AI / ML techniques makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused solution. We need your technical knowledge and desire to solve problems to support the advancement of AI within the Department of War ( DoW ) .\n\nIn this role, you’ll own and define the direction of mission-critical solutions by applying best-fit AI / ML algorithms, optimization models and technologies. You’ll be part of a talented team of engineers across the company and collaborate with business and technical leaders to deliver world-class AI solutions that solve our nation’s toughest and hardest problems. Your skills and extensive technical expertise will guide our DoW customers as they navigate the landscape of AI / ML algorithms, tools, and frameworks. \n\nWhat You'll Work On:\n- Design and implement AI‑enabled decision support capabilities, including forecasting, optimization, natural language interfaces, and intelligent workflow automation.\n\n- Implement pipelines on AWS GovCloud using SageMaker, Step Functions, and Databricks ML Runtime.\n\n- Build and maintain PySpark and Delta Lake pipelines within a medallion architecture.\n\n- Develop feature stores aligned to governance standards and perform data profiling and quality validation consistent with government data standards.\n\n- Maintain model bias assessments and explainability documentation for all production models.\n\n- Implement model monitoring frameworks for concept drift, data drift, and performance degradation.\n\n- Produce artifacts and monthly model performance reports in accordance with approved formats.\n\n- Collaborate with requirements owner and partner agencies to translate mission requirements into model specifications.\n\n- Coach and mentor junior engineers.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:   \n- 5+ years of  experience  designing, developing, validating, and deploying supervised and unsupervised AI / ML and optimization models delivering in enterprise production environments\n\n- 5+ years of experience  in Python such as scikit-learn, XGBoost, PyTorch, or TensorFlow, PySpark, and SQL\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree  in a Computer Science, Data Science, Statistics, Applied Mathematics, or Engineering field\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience  with Databricks and Palantir products\n\n- Experience  operating within FedRAMP-authorized cloud environments\n\n- Experience  with Terraform, CloudFormation, and CI / CD pipelines such as GitLab CI or AWS CodePipeline\n\n- Experience  with federal or government technology, data, and model standard such as CMMC or RMF\n\n- Experience  with prompt engineering and RAG architecture\n\n- Knowledge of  large language model  ( LLM )  deployment patterns in air-gapped or restricted network environments\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- Master’s degree\n\n- AWS Certified Generative AI Developer - Professional, AWS Certified Machine Learning Engineer, Databricks Certified Professional, or equivalent vendor C ertification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Artificial Intelligence and Optimization Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>As an <span>experience</span>d engineer, you know that AI is critical to understanding and processing massive datasets. Your <span>ability to</span> conduct statistical analyses on business processes using AI<span>/</span>ML techniques makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused solution. We need your technical knowledge and desire to solve problems to support the advancement of AI within the Department of War <span>(</span>DoW<span>)</span>.</p><p></p><p>In this role, you’ll own and define the direction of mission-critical solutions by applying best-fit AI<span>/</span>ML algorithms, optimization models and technologies. You’ll be part of a talented team of engineers across the company and collaborate with business and technical leaders to deliver world-class AI solutions that solve our nation’s toughest and hardest problems. Your skills and extensive technical expertise will guide our DoW customers as they navigate the landscape of AI<span>/</span>ML algorithms, tools, and frameworks. </p><p></p><p><b>What You&#39;ll Work On:</b></p><ul><li><p>Design and implement AI‑enabled decision support capabilities, including forecasting, optimization, natural language interfaces, and intelligent workflow automation.</p></li><li><p>Implement pipelines on AWS GovCloud using SageMaker, Step Functions, and Databricks ML Runtime.</p></li><li><p>Build and maintain PySpark and Delta Lake pipelines within a medallion architecture.</p></li><li><p>Develop feature stores aligned to governance standards and perform data profiling and quality validation consistent with government data standards.</p></li><li><p>Maintain model bias assessments and explainability documentation for all production models.</p></li><li><p>Implement model monitoring frameworks for concept drift, data drift, and performance degradation.</p></li><li><p>Produce artifacts and monthly model performance reports in accordance with approved formats.</p></li><li><p>Collaborate with requirements owner and partner agencies to translate mission requirements into model specifications.</p></li><li><p>Coach and mentor junior engineers.</p></li></ul><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>  </p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> designing, developing, validating, and deploying supervised and unsupervised AI<span>/</span>ML and optimization models delivering in enterprise production environments</p></li><li><p>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in Python such as scikit-learn, XGBoost, PyTorch, or TensorFlow, PySpark, and SQL</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span> in a Computer Science, Data Science, Statistics, Applied Mathematics, or Engineering field</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>  </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Databricks and Palantir products</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> operating within FedRAMP-authorized cloud environments</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Terraform, CloudFormation, and CI<span>/</span>CD pipelines such as GitLab CI or AWS CodePipeline</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with federal or government technology, data, and model standard such as CMMC or RMF</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with prompt engineering and RAG architecture</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> large language model <span>(</span>LLM<span>)</span> deployment patterns in air-gapped or restricted network environments</p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Master’s degree</span></p></li><li><p>AWS Certified Generative AI Developer - Professional, AWS Certified Machine Learning Engineer, Databricks Certified Professional, or <span>equivalent</span> vendor C<span>ertification</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 24 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["Artificial Intelligence"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/Artificial-Intelligence-and-Privacy-Associate-General-Counsel_R0240946","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/Artificial-Intelligence-and-Privacy-Associate-General-Counsel_R0240946","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"c07da2a0f85e6123ed6cddb170373bdb1a9128105eacffafaa44de4ff41bbc47","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Artificial Intelligence and Privacy Associate General Counsel","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Artificial-Intelligence-and-Privacy-Associate-General-Counsel_R0240946","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Artificial-Intelligence-and-Privacy-Associate-General-Counsel_R0240946","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0240946","internal_job_id":"31e03fc9eb56100158513e0814070000","first_published_at":"2026-05-27","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Artificial Intelligence and Privacy Associate General Counsel The Opportunity :\nAre you an attorney who is passionate about Artifi cia l Intelligence ( AI ) and data privacy? Are you looking to combine your legal knowledge with big picture business thinking to empower innovation, drive critical missions, and deliver enduring growth and value? At Booz Allen, you’ll join a global team of experienced professionals driven to excel and realize values-driven change for our clients, colleagues, and communities. We bring bold thinking to complex challenges across analytics and artifi cia l intelligence, cyber, digital solutions, engineering, and advising, and with industries ranging from defense to health, energy to international development.\n\nIn this role, you’ll work closely with the Government Markets and Intellectual Property teams to anticipate business needs and develop practical governance structures with agility and action. You’ll establish t rus ted partnerships with leaders across the company’s Chief Technology Office and collaborate with fellow members of the Legal, Ethics & Compliance team and serve as a thought leader to protect and advance the company’s AI strategy while monitoring and helping business leadership resp ond to the complex, multifaceted, and often novel legal, regulatory, and compliance risks we face today. Guided by Booz Allen’s purpose and values, together we’ll anticipate and proactively prepare for the issues we’ll encounter tomorrow. Due to the nature of work performed within this facility, U.S. citizenship is required.\n\nReady to join a team of problem-solvers to empower innovation and change?\n\nWhat You'll Work On:\n- Advise on legal aspects of the AI Risk Management Program.\n\n- Review AI initiatives to assess risk, propose and communicate precautions to the business while finding paths to success.\n\n- Contribute to our AI policies , risk tolerance, strategy, and ethics in line with our values.\n\n- E nga ge with procurement, risk, technology, cybersecurity, and communications teams to negotiate terms and advise on strategy for legal Business Asso cia te, Data Processing and AI agreements.\n\n- Monitor and resp ond to regulatory changes and federal government directives that impact the use of artifi cia l intelligence.\n\n- Apply knowledge of federal agency rules, executive orders, legislation, and contract clauses to artifi cia l intelligence use.\n\n- Advise on privacy legal issues from GDPR, CCPA, HIPAA, and other regulations related to data use.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 8+ years of experience in a law firm or in-house legal, with subject areas such as artifi cia l intelligence, risk management, machine learning, or data rights\n\n- Experience with privacy laws, frameworks, best practices, and controls such as GDPR, CCPA, BIPA, and HIPAA\n\n- Experience collaborating with cross-functional teams and business leaders to develop comprehensive, business-oriented solutions to problems and tailoring subject matter input to achieve business objectives\n\n- Experience negotiating terms and c ond itions for use of AI technologies\n\n- Knowledge Artifi cia l Intelligence, large language models ( LLMs ) , generative AI, emerging AI risk management frameworks, ethical principles, and emerging U.S., state, and international regulatory regimes\n\n- Ability to e nga ge with technical experts and communicate legal obligations to a technical audience\n\n- J.D. degree\n\n- Active bar admission with any U.S. state bar\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with Federal government contract s\n\n- Experience advising on processes and procedures related to artifi cia l intelligence governance\n\n- Experience working with technical staff, such as engineers, network architects, technical teams, and developers\n\n- Knowledge of AI risk management practices, such as the NIST AI Risk Management Framework\n\n- CIPP or AIGP Certification\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $162,800.00 to $303,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Artificial Intelligence and Privacy Associate General Counsel<p><b><span>The Opportunity</span></b><span>:</span></p><p>Are you an attorney who is passionate about Artifi<span>cia</span>l Intelligence <span>(</span>AI<span>)</span> and data privacy? Are you looking to combine your legal knowledge with big picture business thinking to empower innovation, drive critical missions, and deliver enduring growth and value? At Booz Allen, you’ll join a global team of experienced professionals driven to excel and realize values-driven change for our clients, colleagues, and communities. We bring bold thinking to complex challenges across analytics and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence, cyber, digital solutions, engineering, and advising, and with industries ranging from defense to health, energy to international development.</p><p></p><p>In this role, you’ll work closely with the Government Markets and Intellectual Property teams to anticipate business needs and develop practical governance structures with agility and action. You’ll establish t<span>rus</span>ted partnerships with leaders across the company’s Chief Technology Office and collaborate with fellow members of the Legal, Ethics <span>&amp;</span> Compliance team and serve as a thought leader to protect and advance the company’s AI strategy while monitoring and helping business leadership resp<span>ond</span> to the complex, multifaceted, and often novel legal, regulatory, and compliance risks we face today. Guided by Booz Allen’s purpose and values, together we’ll anticipate and proactively prepare for the issues we’ll encounter tomorrow. Due to the nature of work performed within this facility, U.S. citizenship is required.</p><p></p><p>Ready to join a team of problem-solvers to empower innovation and change?</p><p></p><p><b>What You&#39;ll Work On:</b></p><ul><li><p>Advise on legal aspects of the AI Risk Management Program.</p></li><li><p>Review AI initiatives to assess risk, propose and communicate precautions to the business while finding paths to success.</p></li><li><p>Contribute to our AI <span>policies</span>, risk tolerance, strategy, and ethics in line with our values.</p></li><li><p>E<span>nga</span>ge with procurement, risk, technology, cybersecurity, and communications teams to negotiate terms and advise on strategy for legal Business Asso<span>cia</span>te, Data Processing and AI agreements.</p></li><li><p>Monitor and resp<span>ond</span> to regulatory changes and federal government directives that impact the use of artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence.</p></li><li><p>Apply <span>knowledge of</span> federal agency rules, executive orders, legislation, and contract clauses to artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence use.</p></li><li><p>Advise on privacy legal issues from GDPR, CCPA, HIPAA, and other regulations <span>related</span> to data use.</p></li></ul><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p>8&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in a law <span>firm</span> or in-house legal, with subject areas such as artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence, risk management, machine learning, or data rights</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with privacy laws, frameworks, best practices, and controls such as GDPR, CCPA, BIPA, and HIPAA</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> collaborating with cross-functional teams and business leaders to develop comprehensive, business-oriented solutions to problems and tailoring subject matter input to achieve business objectives</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> negotiating terms and c<span>ond</span>itions for use of AI technologies</p></li><li><p>Knowledge Artifi<span>cia</span>l Intelligence, large language models <span>(</span>LLMs<span>)</span>, generative AI, emerging AI risk management frameworks, ethical principles, and emerging U.S., state, and international regulatory regimes</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> e<span>nga</span>ge with technical experts and communicate legal obligations to a technical audience</p></li><li><p>J.D. degree</p></li><li><p>Active bar admission with any U.S. state bar</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Federal <span>government contract</span>s</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> advising on processes and procedures <span>related</span> to artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence governance</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> working with technical staff, such as engineers, network architects, technical teams, and developers</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> AI risk management practices, such as the NIST AI Risk Management Framework</p></li><li><p>CIPP or AIGP Certification</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $162,800.00 to $303,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"cl