{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/San-Antonio-TX/Artificial-Intelligence-Engineer_R0246367","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/San-Antonio-TX/Artificial-Intelligence-Engineer_R0246367","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"e5ac64737760b1f24ddbd63b2a6d316d369d169550b2eadca2aea35eb76d434f","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Artificial Intelligence Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/San-Antonio-TX/Artificial-Intelligence-Engineer_R0246367","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/San-Antonio-TX/Artificial-Intelligence-Engineer_R0246367","locations":[{"label":"San Antonio, TX"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246367","internal_job_id":"6d3435a3a87a100205d86613de000000","first_published_at":"2026-08-07","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Artificial Intelligence Engineer The Opportunity: \nAs an experience d engineer, you know that machine learning (ML) is critical to understanding and processing massive datasets. Your ability to conduct statistical analyses on business processes using ML techniques makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused solution. We need your technical knowledge and desire to problem-solve to support the Air Force. As an ML engineer on our defensive and offensive cyberspace operations teams, you’ll train, test, deploy, and maintain models that learn from data.   \n\nIn this role, you’ll own and define the direction of mission-critical solutions by applying best-fit ML algorithms and technologies. You’ll be part of a talented team of ML engineers across the company and collaborate with data scientists, data engineers, solutions architects, and developers to deliver world class solutions. As an AI Engineer on our team, you’ll develop AI-native solutions incorporating multiple disciplines spanning across sof tware development, platform integration, and cloud engineering, and the latest AI tooling such as Bedrock or LLM, LangChain or LangGraph, Agentic workflows, and accelerate missions with AI tools. Your skills and extensive technical expertise will guide clients as they navigate the landscape of ML algorithms, tools, and frameworks. \n\nWork with us to solve real-world challenges and define ML strategy for defensive and offensive cyberspace operations.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- 2+ years of experience in ML, data science, data engineering, or sof tware development \n- Experience with integration of LLMs or Agentic workflows within  sof tware stacks\n- Experience with the Agile  sof tware development lifecycle and full-stack web application development  \n- Knowledge of JavaScript or TypeScript, Python, and HTML or CSS     \n- Ability to  solve complex and critical problems, iterate rapidly, and deliver results in both team and individual capacities\n- Ability to travel up to 25% of the time\n- Secret clearance\n- Bachelor's degree in CS or a Science or Mathematics field  \n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Knowledge of AWS, Azure, GCP, Databricks, and Palantir Foundry\n- Top Secret clearance  \n- DoD 8570 Level II Certification  \n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Artificial Intelligence Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>As an <span>experience</span>d engineer, you know that machine learning (ML) is critical to understanding and processing massive datasets. Your <span>ability to</span> conduct statistical analyses on business processes using ML techniques makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused solution. We need your technical knowledge and desire to problem-solve to support the Air Force. As an ML engineer on our defensive and offensive cyberspace operations teams, you’ll train, test, deploy, and maintain models that learn from data.   </p><p></p><p>In this role, you’ll own and define the direction of mission-critical solutions by applying best-fit ML algorithms and technologies. You’ll be part of a talented team of ML engineers across the company and collaborate with data scientists, data engineers, solutions architects, and developers to deliver world class solutions. As an AI Engineer on our team, you’ll develop AI-native solutions incorporating multiple disciplines spanning across <span>sof</span>tware development, platform integration, and cloud engineering, and the latest AI tooling such as Bedrock or LLM, LangChain or LangGraph, Agentic workflows, and accelerate missions with AI tools. Your skills and extensive technical expertise will guide clients as they navigate the landscape of ML algorithms, tools, and frameworks. </p><p></p><p>Work with us to solve real-world challenges and define ML strategy for defensive and offensive cyberspace operations.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>  </p><ul><li>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in ML, data science, data engineering, or <span>sof</span>tware development </li><li><span>Experience</span> with integration of LLMs or Agentic workflows within <span>sof</span>tware stacks</li><li><span>Experience</span> with the Agile <span>sof</span>tware development lifecycle and full-stack web application development  </li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> JavaScript or TypeScript, Python, and HTML or CSS     </li><li><span>Ability to</span> solve complex and critical problems, iterate rapidly, and deliver results in both team and individual capacities</li><li><span>Ability to</span> travel up to 25% of the time</li><li><span>Secret clearance</span></li><li><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span> in CS or a Science or Mathematics field  </li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>  </p><ul><li><span>Knowledge of</span> AWS, Azure, GCP, Databricks, and Palantir Foundry</li><li><span>Top Secret clearance</span> </li><li>DoD 8570 Level II <span>Certification</span> </li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b> </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 17 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["Artificial Intelligence"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/San-Antonio-TX/Artificial-Intelligence-Engineer_R0246377","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/San-Antonio-TX/Artificial-Intelligence-Engineer_R0246377","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"5f1b0c38b3d4c6560e1d5efdef04643c90e07c72abc1a9c883c3bc823dac0161","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Artificial Intelligence Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/San-Antonio-TX/Artificial-Intelligence-Engineer_R0246377","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/San-Antonio-TX/Artificial-Intelligence-Engineer_R0246377","locations":[{"label":"San Antonio, TX"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246377","internal_job_id":"cdcfc075bb40100206925935267e0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-07","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Artificial Intelligence Engineer The Opportunity: \nAs an experienced engineer, you know that machine learning is critical to understanding and processing massive datasets. Your ability to conduct statistical analyses on business processes using ML techniques makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused solution. We need your technical knowledge and desire to problem-solve to support the Air Force. As a machine learning engineer on our defensive and offensive cyberspace operations teams, you’ll train, test, deploy, and maintain models that learn from data.   \n\nIn this role, you’ll own and define the direction of mission-critical solutions by applying best-fit ML algorithms and technologies. You’ll be part of a talented team of machine learning engineers across the company and collaborate with data scientist, data engineers, solutions architects, and developers to deliver world class solutions. As an AI Engineer on our team, you’ll develop AI-native solutions incorporating multiple disciplines spanning across software development, platform integration, and cloud engineering, and the latest AI tooling such as Bedrock or LLM, LangChain or LangGraph, Agentic workflows, and accelerating the missions with AI tools. Your skills and extensive technical expertise will guide clients as they navigate the landscape of ML algorithms, tools, and frameworks. \n\nWork with us to solve real-world challenges and define ML strategy for defensive and offensive cyberspace operations. \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:  \n- 2+ years of experience with machine learning, data science, data engineering, or software development \n\n- Experience with integration of LLMs or Agentic Workflows within software stacks  \n\n- Experience with the Agile software development lifecycle and full-stack web application development \n\n- Knowledge of JavaScript or TypeScript, Python, and HTML or CSS    \n\n- Ability to   solve complex and critical problems, iterate rapidly, and deliver results in both team and individual capacities  \n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree in Computer Science or a Science or Mathematics field  \n\nNice If You Have:  \n- Knowledge of AWS, Azure, GCP, Databricks, and Palantir Foundry\n\n- Top Secret clearance \n\n- DoD 8570 Level II Certification \n\nClearance:    \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.  \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Artificial Intelligence Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>As an experienced engineer, you know that machine learning is critical to understanding and processing massive datasets. Your ability to conduct statistical analyses on business processes using ML techniques makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused solution. We need your technical knowledge and desire to problem-solve to support the Air Force. As a machine learning engineer on our defensive and offensive cyberspace operations teams, you’ll train, test, deploy, and maintain models that learn from data.   </p><p></p><p>In this role, you’ll own and define the direction of mission-critical solutions by applying best-fit ML algorithms and technologies. You’ll be part of a talented team of machine learning engineers across the company and collaborate with data scientist, data engineers, solutions architects, and developers to deliver world class solutions. As an AI Engineer on our team, you’ll develop AI-native solutions incorporating multiple disciplines spanning across software development, platform integration, and cloud engineering, and the latest AI tooling such as Bedrock or LLM, LangChain or LangGraph, Agentic workflows, and accelerating the missions with AI tools. Your skills and extensive technical expertise will guide clients as they navigate the landscape of ML algorithms, tools, and frameworks. </p><p></p><p>Work with us to solve real-world challenges and define ML strategy for defensive and offensive cyberspace operations. </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:  </b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with machine learning, data science, data engineering, or software development </p></li><li><p><span>Experience </span><span>with integration of LLMs or Agentic Workflows within software stacks</span><span> </span></p></li><li><p>Experience with the Agile software development lifecycle and full-stack web application development </p></li><li><p>Knowledge of JavaScript or TypeScript, Python, and HTML or CSS    </p></li><li><p>Ability <span>to</span><span><span> </span>solve complex and critical problems, iterate rapidly, and deliver results in both team and individual capacities</span>  </p></li><li><p>Secret clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree <span>in Computer Science or a Science or Mathematics field</span>  </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:  </b></p><ul><li><p>Knowledge of AWS, Azure, GCP, Databricks, and Palantir Foundry</p></li><li><p>Top Secret clearance </p></li><li><p>DoD 8570 Level II Certification </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b>   </p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.  </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 17 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["Artificial Intelligence"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/El-Segundo-CA/Artificial-Intelligence-Engineer--Mid_R0247598","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/El-Segundo-CA/Artificial-Intelligence-Engineer--Mid_R0247598","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"7dd7348817ddfd37f3fccfadc14276a44f44f1d70fa34cd81dd8dd2f07af60bf","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Artificial Intelligence Engineer, Mid","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/El-Segundo-CA/Artificial-Intelligence-Engineer--Mid_R0247598","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/El-Segundo-CA/Artificial-Intelligence-Engineer--Mid_R0247598","locations":[{"label":"El Segundo, CA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247598","internal_job_id":"71f6309939971001ff303d85e9cf0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-21","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Artificial Intelligence Engineer, Mid The Opportunity:\nGreat AI solutions start with understanding the problem—then designing so met hing that actually works in the real world. As an Artifi cia l Intelligence Engineer on our team, you'll work directly with clients and engineers on national security space missions to turn ambiguous needs into AI architecture solutions you can stand behind. You'll design and help build secure, scalable AI capabilities, including long-context and cache-augmented applications, automation, and model integrations, and make the hard calls on trade-offs, deployment, and responsible use. You'll be the technical voice clients t rus t: the person who can whiteboard the design in the morning and prototype it in the afternoon. You'll help a small, high-initiative team move fast without losing sight of security or mission value. Ready to engineer AI that makes it into the field? This position is located in El Segundo, CA.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 3+ years of experience designing, building, deploying, or integrating sof tware, data, or traditional AI / ML solutions\n\n- Experience translating client or mission needs into technical architectures, solution designs, or implementation plans\n\n- Experience building or integrating AI and machine learning capabilities such as Agentic Retrieval systems, cache-augmented generation ( CAG ) , model APIs, or long-horizon automation into applications or workflows\n\n- Experience with cloud services and modern Sof tware Developer practices, such as AWS or Azure, containers, APIs, or CI / CD\n\n- Ability to independently lead ambiguous AI solutions work, self-manage priorities, solve complex problems, and meet tight deadlines\n\n- Ability to apply pragmatic judgment across technical standards, project flexibility, and emerging technologies\n\n- Ability to communicate technical designs and trade-offs to technical and non-technical stakeholders\n\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree in a STEM field\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience as a solution architect, sales engineer, AI / ML engineer, or technical lead on government, defense, or space programs\n\n- Experience deploying AI or sof tware into secure or government cloud environments such as GovCloud, IL5, or IL6\n\n- Experience with AI prototype development, Knowledge Graphs ( KAG ) , ontological systems, MLOps, or model evaluation\n\n- Experience leading or mentoring small technical teams\n\n- Possession of excellent communication, facilitation, and client-e nga gement skills\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Master's degree in a STEM field\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information .\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Artificial Intelligence Engineer, Mid<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>Great AI solutions start with understanding the problem—then designing so<span>met</span>hing that actually works in the real world. As an Artifi<span>cia</span>l Intelligence Engineer on our team, you&#39;ll work directly with clients and engineers on national security space missions to turn ambiguous needs into AI architecture solutions you can stand behind. You&#39;ll design and help build secure, scalable AI capabilities, including long-context and cache-augmented applications, automation, and model integrations, and make the hard calls on trade-offs, deployment, and responsible use. You&#39;ll be the technical voice clients t<span>rus</span>t: the person who can whiteboard the design in the morning and prototype it in the afternoon. You&#39;ll help a small, high-initiative team move fast without losing sight of security or mission value. Ready to engineer AI that makes it into the field? This position is located in El Segundo, CA.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> designing, building, deploying, or integrating <span>sof</span>tware, data, or traditional AI<span>/</span>ML solutions</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> translating client or mission needs into technical architectures, solution designs, or implementation plans</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> building or integrating AI and machine learning capabilities such as Agentic Retrieval systems, cache-augmented generation <span>(</span>CAG<span>)</span>, model APIs, or long-horizon automation into applications or workflows</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with cloud services and modern <span>Sof</span>tware Developer practices, such as AWS or Azure, containers, APIs, or CI<span>/</span>CD</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> independently lead ambiguous AI solutions work, self-manage priorities, solve complex problems, and meet tight deadlines</p></li><li><p>Ability to apply pragmatic judgment across technical standards, project flexibility, and emerging technologies</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> communicate technical designs and trade-offs to technical and non-technical stakeholders</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span><span> obtain a Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span> in a STEM field</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> as a solution architect, sales engineer, AI<span>/</span>ML engineer, or technical lead on government, defense, or space programs</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> deploying AI or <span>sof</span>tware into secure or government cloud environments such as GovCloud, IL5, or IL6</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with AI prototype development, Knowledge Graphs <span>(</span>KAG<span>)</span>, ontological systems, MLOps, or model evaluation</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> leading or mentoring small technical teams</p></li><li><p><span>Possession of</span> excellent communication, facilitation, and client-e<span>nga</span>gement skills</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Master&#39;s degree</span> in a STEM field</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span>.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 3 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-24T01:56:20.339Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["Artificial Intelligence"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Aurora-CO/Artificial-Intelligence-Software-Engineer_R0247474","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Aurora-CO/Artificial-Intelligence-Software-Engineer_R0247474","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"a5c67faf534bfa0fa36fbdc09a5a74fd3e8da573a762bf141ef60c8e503b53ed","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Artificial Intelligence Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Aurora-CO/Artificial-Intelligence-Software-Engineer_R0247474","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Aurora-CO/Artificial-Intelligence-Software-Engineer_R0247474","locations":[{"label":"Aurora, CO"},{"label":"El Segundo, CA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247474","internal_job_id":"71f6309939971001a739a870d4bb0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-20","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Artificial Intelligence Software Engineer The Opportunity:   \nAs an AI sof tware engineer, you know that good sof tware is more than just a nice-looking interface and data. Today, you need to develop user-focused solutions that increase organizational efficiency and enable better decision-making. Booz Allen is the leading provider of AI services to the nation, and we’re looking for a sof tware engineer like you to create AI and machine learning solutions that help solve the nation’s toughest problems.  \n\nOn our team, you’ll help create and implement complete end-to-end solutions that modernize AI-driven digital engineering capability. You’ll ensure that your team’s solutions consider the broader ecosystem and operating environment as well as future functionality and enhancements. You apply leading-edge principles, theories, and concepts to provide highly innovative solutions. Additionally, you’ll build upon your skillset in areas like LLM frameworks, DevSecOps, and full-stack development.  \n\nReady to transform systems engineering for the better with AI technology?  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.   \n\nYou Have:    \n- 2+ years of experience designing, modifying, developing, writing, and implementing sof tware programming applications using Agile met hods\n- 1+ years of experience working with a full-stack LLM solutions, including RAG implementation, model selection or registry management such as Hugging Face, and LLM frameworks such as LangChain and LlamaIndex, and using embedding models and vector databases\n- Experience with LLM inference engines such as vLLM and llama.cpp\n- Experience with Cursor or AI-assisted coding tools to enhance sof tware or digital engineering development processes\n- Experience with full-stack development, including RESTFul APIs, Node.js, JavaScript, and React\n- Experience with Agile  met hodology and DevSecOps tools such as GitHub Actions, to build and manage CI / CD pipelines\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance\n- Bachelor's degree in a STEM field\n\nNice If You Have:    \n- Experience implementing and utilizing Model Context Protocol ( MCP ) in sof tware or digital engineering projects to enable seamless model interoperability and context management\n- Experience performing systems engineering analysis and developing systems engineering products for government or mission critical systems, including NASA or the DoW\n- Experience with Model-Based Systems Engineering ( MBSE ) development, including using digital engineering tools such as Cameo, MagicDraw, SparxEA, DOORS, and IBM Rhapsody\n- Experience with MagicDraw plug-in development and Teamwork Cloud ( TWC ) administration\n- Experience with MATLAB, STK, Model Center , or Team Center\n- Experience with cloud computing platforms such as AWS, Azure, or GCP\n- Experience with sof tware product testing and QA / QC\n- Experience with Linux\n- Master's degree in Engineering\n- Industry Certification s such as OCSMP, ASEP, GCP, Azure, AWS, and Security+ Certification s\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information . \n\nSkills Assessment\nAs part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Artificial Intelligence Software Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b> </p><p>As an AI <span>sof</span>tware engineer, you know that good <span>sof</span>tware is more than just a nice-looking interface and data. Today, you need to develop user-focused solutions that increase organizational efficiency and enable better decision-making. Booz Allen is the leading provider of AI services to the nation, and we’re looking for a <span>sof</span>tware engineer like you to create AI and machine learning solutions that help solve the nation’s toughest problems.  </p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll help create and implement complete end-to-end solutions that modernize AI-driven digital engineering capability. You’ll ensure that your team’s solutions consider the broader ecosystem and operating environment as well as future functionality and enhancements. You apply leading-edge principles, theories, and concepts to provide highly innovative solutions. Additionally, you’ll build upon your skillset in areas like LLM frameworks, DevSecOps, and full-stack development.  </p><p></p><p>Ready to transform systems engineering for the better with AI technology?  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.   </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:  </span></b> </p><ul><li>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> designing, modifying, developing, writing, and implementing <span>sof</span>tware programming applications using Agile <span>met</span>hods</li><li>1&#43; years of <span>experience</span> working with a full-stack LLM solutions, including RAG implementation, model selection or registry management such as Hugging Face, and LLM frameworks such as LangChain and LlamaIndex, and using embedding models and vector databases</li><li><span>Experience</span> with LLM inference engines such as vLLM and llama.cpp</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Cursor or AI-assisted coding tools to enhance <span>sof</span>tware or digital engineering development processes</li><li><span>Experience</span> with full-stack development, including RESTFul APIs, Node.js, JavaScript, and React</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Agile <span>met</span>hodology and DevSecOps tools such as GitHub Actions, to build and manage CI<span>/</span>CD pipelines</li><li><span>Ability to</span><span> obtain a Secret clearance </span></li><li><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span> in a STEM field</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:  </span></b> </p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> implementing and utilizing Model Context Protocol <span>(</span>MCP<span>)</span> in <span>sof</span>tware or digital engineering projects to enable seamless model interoperability and context management</li><li><span>Experience</span> performing systems engineering analysis and developing systems engineering products for government or mission critical systems, including NASA or the DoW</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Model-Based Systems Engineering <span>(</span>MBSE<span>)</span> development, including using digital engineering tools such as Cameo, MagicDraw, SparxEA, DOORS, and IBM Rhapsody</li><li><span>Experience</span> with MagicDraw plug-in development and Teamwork Cloud <span>(</span>TWC<span>)</span> administration</li><li><span>Experience</span> with MATLAB, STK, Model<span>Center</span>, or Team<span>Center</span></li><li><span>Experience</span> with cloud computing platforms such as AWS, Azure, or GCP</li><li><span>Experience</span> with <span>sof</span>tware product testing and QA<span>/</span>QC</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Linux</li><li><span>Master&#39;s degree</span> in Engineering</li><li>Industry <span>Certification</span>s such as OCSMP, ASEP, GCP, Azure, AWS, and Security&#43; <span>Certification</span>s</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance: </span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span>. </p><p></p>&amp;#xa;Skills Assessment&amp;#xa;As part of Booz Allen’s skills first hiring process, candidates must complete the required skills assessment to ensure they meet the Basic Qualifications for this role. Candidates must complete the assessment and meet the minimum proficiency threshold to continue in the hiring process.&amp;#xa;<p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 4 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T19:35:50.646Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":5,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml","software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer","Artificial Intelligence"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Camp-HM-Smith-HI/Artificial-Intelligence-Solutions-Architect--Lead_R0245811","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Camp-HM-Smith-HI/Artificial-Intelligence-Solutions-Architect--Lead_R0245811","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"6f958e67ab1d62ada27a93a31f9f3d93366406ee9218827d06f77874d6b9006b","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Artificial Intelligence Solutions Architect, Lead","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Camp-HM-Smith-HI/Artificial-Intelligence-Solutions-Architect--Lead_R0245811","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Camp-HM-Smith-HI/Artificial-Intelligence-Solutions-Architect--Lead_R0245811","locations":[{"label":"2 Locations"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"unknown","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245811","internal_job_id":null,"first_published_at":null,"source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":null,"description_html":null,"compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":null,"country":null,"posted_on":"Posted 24 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":false,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"lead","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["Artificial Intelligence"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":["Lead "],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/Artificial-Intelligence-Solutions-Architect--Mid_R0236423","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/Artificial-Intelligence-Solutions-Architect--Mid_R0236423","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"00cc6a2b4050ac707e18f35792c74cd6390d18cbf936906676ded53522f5d97d","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Artificial Intelligence Solutions Architect, Mid","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Artificial-Intelligence-Solutions-Architect--Mid_R0236423","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Artificial-Intelligence-Solutions-Architect--Mid_R0236423","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"},{"label":"Chantilly, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0236423","internal_job_id":"2a6168c869e91001f7b7c3614ec30000","first_published_at":"2026-07-14","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Artificial Intelligence Solutions Architect, Mid The Opportunity:\nDesigns and implements effective AI solution architecture or strategy utilizing approaches of various AI technologies and methods to address clients' business problems and needs, while complying with the organization’s strategies and business goals, and key ethical considerations. Applies specific functional knowledge, working or general industry knowledge. Develops or contributes to solutions to a variety of problems of moderate scope and complexity. Works independently with some guidance, may review or guide activities of more junior employees.\n\nYou Have:\n- 3+ years of experience implementing IT systems, applications, and infrastructure\n\n- 3+ years of experience designing and implementing a highly available, scalable, and resilient enterprise cloud environment\n\n- 2+ years of experience in AI and Data Science using Python programming and big data technologies, including Hive, Q, Bedrock, PySpark, Synapse, or Databricks\n\n- 2+ years of experience using the Amazon AI product tool suite, Sage Maker studio, and Bedrock\n\n- 2+ years of experience using LLMs, GenAI applications, and agentic AI orchestration frameworks\n\n- Knowledge of Big Data solutions, data migration technologies, and processes\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- Bachelor's degree in a Technology field, such as Computer Science or Statistics\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience providing technical guidance to architects and engineers\n\n- Experience working in GCP or Microsoft Azure\n\n- Knowledge of security and compliance requirements for cloud-based solutions, network architecture, and security principles\n\n- Master's degree in technology field such as Computer Science or Statistics preferred\n\n- Security, Cloud, or Software Development Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Artificial Intelligence Solutions Architect, Mid<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p>Designs and implements effective AI solution architecture or strategy utilizing approaches of various AI technologies and methods to address clients&#39; business problems and needs, while complying with the organization’s strategies and business goals, and key ethical considerations. Applies specific functional knowledge, working or general industry knowledge. Develops or contributes to solutions to a variety of problems of moderate scope and complexity. Works independently with some guidance, may review or guide activities of more junior employees.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of experience implementing IT systems, applications, and infrastructure</p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of experience designing and implementing a highly available, scalable, and resilient enterprise cloud environment</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience in AI and Data Science using Python programming and big data technologies, including Hive, Q, Bedrock, PySpark, Synapse, or Databricks</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience using the Amazon AI product tool suite, Sage Maker studio, and Bedrock</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience using LLMs, GenAI applications, and agentic AI orchestration frameworks</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of Big Data solutions, data migration technologies, and processes</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree in a Technology field, such as Computer Science or Statistics</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>Experience providing technical guidance to architects and engineers</p></li><li><p>Experience working in GCP or Microsoft Azure</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of security and compliance requirements for cloud-based solutions, network architecture, and security principles</p></li><li><p>Master&#39;s degree in technology field such as Computer Science or Statistics preferred</p></li><li><p>Security, Cloud, or Software Development Certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["Artificial Intelligence"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/Artificial-Intelligence-Solutions-Architect--Senior_R0236429","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/Artificial-Intelligence-Solutions-Architect--Senior_R0236429","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"63849eb288a37919fc5d3d3090db763f2356e5462a3a960a283128468b67e070","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Artificial Intelligence Solutions Architect, Senior","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Artificial-Intelligence-Solutions-Architect--Senior_R0236429","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Artificial-Intelligence-Solutions-Architect--Senior_R0236429","locations":[{"label":"2 Locations"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"unknown","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0236429","internal_job_id":null,"first_published_at":null,"source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":null,"description_html":null,"compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":null,"country":null,"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":false,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"senior","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["Artificial Intelligence"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":["Senior"],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/El-Segundo-CA/Artificial-Intelligence-Solutions-Engineer_R0244294","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/El-Segundo-CA/Artificial-Intelligence-Solutions-Engineer_R0244294","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"56fef251f36757504bcccd45a61021c4aa0375c54abceb1bbd34f3524218f30f","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Artificial Intelligence Solutions Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/El-Segundo-CA/Artificial-Intelligence-Solutions-Engineer_R0244294","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/El-Segundo-CA/Artificial-Intelligence-Solutions-Engineer_R0244294","locations":[{"label":"El Segundo, CA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0244294","internal_job_id":"9aa9ab4a63ca1000c8ec958c0db10000","first_published_at":"2026-07-17","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Artificial Intelligence Solutions Engineer The Opportunity:\nAs a programmer, you know that machine learning is critical to understanding and processing massive datasets. Your ability to conduct statistical analyses on business processes using ML techniques makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused solution. We need your technical knowledge and desire to solve problems to support the U.S. Space Force under the U.S. Department of War. As an AI Solutions Engineer on our Defense Technology Group, you’ll develop AI-native solutions incorporating multiple disciplines spanning across sof tware development, platform integration, and cloud engineering, and the latest AI tooling such as Bedrock or LLM, LangChain or LangGraph, Agentic workflows, and accelerating the missions with AI tools.\n\nIn this role, you’ll contribute to the direction of mission-critical solutions by applying best-fit AI technologies and emerging AI-native processes or workflows. You’ll grow within a talented team of machine learning engineers across the company and collaborate with full-stack sof tware engineers, data scientists, solutions architects, and defense mission experts to deliver world-class solutions to deliver new sof tware capabilities to our customers with high velocity. Your skills and technical experience will help your clients navigate the landscape of Agentic workflows, AI / ML algorithms, full-stack development, DevSecOps, tools, and frameworks. \n\nWork with us to solve real-world challenges and define AI strategy for the U.S. Space Force.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- 2+ years of experience within machine learning, data science, data engineering, or software development\n\n- Experience with integration of LLMs or Agentic Workflows within sof tware stacks\n\n- Experience with the Agile sof tware development lifecycle and full-stack web application development\n\n- Knowledge of JavaScript or TypeScript, Python, and HTML or CSS\n\n- Ability to solve complex and critical problems, iterate rapidly, and deliver results in both team and individual capacities\n\n- Secret clearance   \n\n- Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or a Science or Mathematics field\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Knowledge of AWS, Azure, GCP, Databricks, and Palantir Foundry\n\nClearance:   \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.  \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Artificial Intelligence Solutions Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As a programmer, you know that machine learning is critical to understanding and processing massive datasets. Your <span>ability to</span> conduct statistical analyses on business processes using ML techniques makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused solution. We need your technical knowledge and desire to solve problems to support the U.S. Space Force under the U.S. Department of War. As an AI Solutions Engineer on our Defense Technology Group, you’ll develop AI-native solutions incorporating multiple disciplines spanning across <span>sof</span>tware development, platform integration, and cloud engineering, and the latest AI tooling such as Bedrock or LLM, LangChain or LangGraph, Agentic workflows, and accelerating the missions with AI tools.</p><p></p><p>In this role, you’ll contribute to the direction of mission-critical solutions by applying best-fit AI technologies and emerging AI-native processes or workflows. You’ll grow within a talented team of machine learning engineers across the company and collaborate with full-stack <span>sof</span>tware engineers, data scientists, solutions architects, and defense mission experts to deliver world-class solutions to deliver new <span>sof</span>tware capabilities to our customers with high velocity. Your skills and technical <span>experience</span> will help your clients navigate the landscape of Agentic workflows, AI<span>/</span>ML algorithms, full-stack development, DevSecOps, tools, and frameworks. </p><p></p><p>Work with us to solve real-world challenges and define AI strategy for the U.S. Space Force.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>  </p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of experience within machine learning, data science, data engineering, or software development</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with integration of LLMs or Agentic Workflows within <span>sof</span>tware stacks</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with the Agile <span>sof</span>tware development lifecycle and full-stack web application development</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> JavaScript or TypeScript, Python, and HTML or CSS</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> solve complex and critical problems, iterate rapidly, and deliver results in both team and individual capacities</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span>  </p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor’s degree</span> in Computer Science or a Science or Mathematics field</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>  </p><ul><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> AWS, Azure, GCP, Databricks, and Palantir Foundry</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b>  </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span> </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["Artificial Intelligence","Solutions Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Belcamp-MD/Artificial-Intelligence-Specialist_R0240999","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Belcamp-MD/Artificial-Intelligence-Specialist_R0240999","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"6aeb397b6ad296d64370f6cf2f343fbe380bc78cce9a5a5651f5fa5ce1506838","fetched_at":"2026-08-24T14:15:46.938Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Artificial Intelligence Specialist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Belcamp-MD/Artificial-Intelligence-Specialist_R0240999","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Belcamp-MD/Artificial-Intelligence-Specialist_R0240999","locations":[{"label":"Belcamp, MD"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0240999","internal_job_id":"e350727b037f10015c8532f4e8b90000","first_published_at":"2026-05-27","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Artificial Intelligence Specialist The Opportunity:\nAs an Artifi cia l Intelligence  ( AI )  spe cia list, you know the value of  current  and emerging AI technologies across the chemical, biological, and material sciences to support the mission. You also know that understanding these technologies and how to apply them is vital to producing chemical and biological defense solutions that enable the success of government clients. At Booz Allen, you can apply your skills and broad AI knowledge to inform strategies and deliver solutions to meet our customers’ needs. Here, you aren’t just developing reports, you're informing the solutions to our nation's most challenging chemical and biological protection missions. \n\nAs the AI Spe cia list on our multidisciplinary team, you will apply specific functional and working industry knowledge of AI tools such as large language models or agentic AI to help our customers meet their mission objectives. You will help ensure AI is properly deployed with the necessary safeguards. You’ll monitor AI assets and identify security gaps. In this role, you will collaborate with key IT stakeholders and leadership to enable deployment of AI capabilities.\n\nBooz Allen is committed to creating an environment where you can expand your career through mentoring, the opportunity to leverage new resources, and the ability to gain in-demand certification s to sharpen your skill set. With opportunities supporting both the private and public sectors across multiple geographies, your career is only limited by your own appetite for exploration. \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have: \n- Experience with AI tools and platforms\n\n- Experience conducting research and presenting results in both written and presentation formats\n\n- Knowledge of AI tools for chemical and biological solutions such as AlphaFold\n\n- Ability to translate AI capabilities and terminology to non-AI experts\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience recommending AI tools and platforms into a project or program\n\n- Knowledge of how AI or ML models are trained\n\n- Ability to present briefings to leadership\n\n- Top Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree in a STEM field\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Artificial Intelligence Specialist<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As an Artifi<span>cia</span>l Intelligence <span>(</span>AI<span>)</span> spe<span>cia</span>list, you know the value of <span>current</span> and emerging AI technologies across the chemical, biological, and material sciences to support the mission. You also know that understanding these technologies and how to apply them is vital to producing chemical and biological defense solutions that enable the success of government clients. At Booz Allen, you can apply your skills and broad AI knowledge to inform strategies and deliver solutions to meet our customers’ needs. Here, you aren’t just developing reports, you&#39;re informing the solutions to our nation&#39;s most challenging chemical and biological protection missions. </p><p></p><p>As the AI Spe<span>cia</span>list on our multidisciplinary team, you will apply specific functional and working industry <span>knowledge of</span> AI tools such as large language models or agentic AI to help our customers meet their mission objectives. You will help ensure AI is properly deployed with the necessary safeguards. You’ll monitor AI assets and identify security gaps. In this role, you will collaborate with key IT stakeholders and leadership to enable deployment of AI capabilities.</p><p></p><p>Booz Allen is committed to creating an environment where you can expand your career through mentoring, the opportunity to leverage new resources, and the <span>ability to</span> gain in-demand <span>certification</span>s to sharpen your skill set. With opportunities supporting both the private and public sectors across multiple geographies, your career is only limited by your own appetite for exploration. </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with AI tools and platforms</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> conducting research and presenting results in both written and presentation formats</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> AI tools for chemical and biological solutions such as AlphaFold</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> translate AI capabilities and terminology to non-AI experts</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> recommending AI tools and platforms into a project or program</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> how AI or ML models are trained</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> present briefings to leadership</p></li><li><p><span>Top Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span> in a STEM field</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"possibly_closed","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-24T14:15:46.938Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","missing_complete_scans":1,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["Artificial Intelligence"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Chantilly-VA/Artificial-Intelligence-Specialist_R0245396","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Chantilly-VA/Artificial-Intelligence-Specialist_R0245396","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"025c01be065d7095eb99e001f43ea8a9d8af15840c3284a69e14d83c21d01866","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Artificial Intelligence Specialist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Artificial-Intelligence-Specialist_R0245396","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Artificial-Intelligence-Specialist_R0245396","locations":[{"label":"Chantilly, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245396","internal_job_id":"45e74e1697ae1001074403f4b15d0000","first_published_at":"2026-07-28","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Artificial Intelligence Specialist The Opportunity:\nProvides advisory services on current and emerging artifi cia l intelligence ( AI ) technologies to support organizational goals and strategy. Applies leading-edge principles, theories, and concepts, and contributes to the develop ment of new principles and concepts. Works on unusually complex problems and provides highly innovative solutions. Operates with substantial latitude for unreviewed action or decision, and mentors or supervises employees in both company and technical competencies.\n\nYou Have:\n- Experience with LLMs, search systems, or RAG architecture\n- Knowledge of AI / ML technologies, packages, and languages such as PyTorch, LangGraph, ClaudeCode, or MLFlow\n- Ability to quickly adapt to change and respond to shifting mission needs and technological advancement\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with project or program management\n- Knowledge of sof tware develop ment best practices, knowledge management systems such as Jira or Confluence\n- Ability to envision, plan, and execute strategies to achieve organizational OKRs\n- Master's degree\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $112,800.00 to $257,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Artificial Intelligence Specialist<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>Provides advisory services on <span>current</span> and emerging artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence <span>(</span>AI<span>)</span> technologies to support organizational goals and strategy. Applies leading-edge principles, theories, and concepts, and contributes to the <span>develop</span>ment of new principles and concepts. Works on unusually complex problems and provides highly innovative solutions. Operates with substantial latitude for unreviewed action or decision, and mentors or supervises employees in both company and technical competencies.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with LLMs, search systems, or RAG architecture</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> AI<span>/</span>ML technologies, packages, and languages such as PyTorch, LangGraph, ClaudeCode, or MLFlow</li><li><span>Ability to</span> quickly adapt to change and respond to shifting mission needs and technological advancement</li><li><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</span></li><li><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with project or program management</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> <span>sof</span>tware <span>develop</span>ment best practices, knowledge management systems such as Jira or Confluence</li><li><span>Ability to</span> envision, plan, and execute strategies to achieve organizational OKRs</li><li><span>Master&#39;s degree</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance: </span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $112,800.00 to $257,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 27 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["Artificial Intelligence"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:R0246422","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"R0246422","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"0d0dc822e69c53302cee74974d4b86c0ecae41db91cde7d05c465de14d80c900","fetched_at":"2026-08-20T07:20:48.759Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Artificial Intelligence/Machine Learning Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/Artificial-Intelligence-Machine-Learning-Engineer_R0246422","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/Artificial-Intelligence-Machine-Learning-Engineer_R0246422","locations":[{"label":"Washington, DC"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246422","internal_job_id":"ce7800f7d1461000c38c4d03e8a60000","first_published_at":"2026-08-17","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Artificial Intelligence/Machine Learning Engineer The Opportunity:\nAs an experienced engineer, you know that agentic AI is transforming how organizations operate, make decisions, and deliver outcomes at speed. Your ability to design and build practical agentic systems that turn manual workflows into AI-enabled solutions makes you an integral part of delivering mission-focused outcomes. We need your technical depth, product mindset, and problem-solving drive to support the National Security Sector Rapid Prototyping team.\n\nIn this role, you will define, design, and deliver mission-relevant agentic AI prototypes in fast, iterative development cycles. You will collaborate with product leads, solution architects, and engineers to build, test, and deploy agent-based solutions that solve high-priority client challenges. You will apply best-fit frameworks and patterns, including agent orchestration, tool use, memory, and retrieval, while balancing solution quality, reliability, and cost.\n\nYou will be part of a small, high-performing team operating in a 4-week prototype lifecycle, where priorities shift quickly and multiple efforts may run in parallel. Success in this role requires adaptability, clear communication, strong execution, and ownership from concept through delivery.\n\nWork with us to solve real-world challenges and shape the future of mission-focused agentic AI.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- Experience building and delivering agentic AI applications in production or prototype environments\n\n- Experience implementing agent orchestration frameworks\n\n- Experience designing and implementing agent loops, tool-calling workflows, and multi-agent interaction patterns\n\n- Knowledge of LLM platforms and providers, including AWS Bedrock and at least one additional provider, such as OpenAI or Ollama\n\n- Knowledge of prompt engineering techniques for reliability, controllability, and task performance\n\n- Knowledge of MCP usage and development, including integration of external tools and capabilities\n\n- Ability to own technical delivery end to end in short-cycle environments, from design through deployment\n\n- Ability to follow code review practices, document work, and maintain clean and reusable code\n\n- HS diploma or GED\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience implementing retrieval patterns for agentic systems, including RAG or GraphRAG is a plus\n\n- Experience building agentic evaluation frameworks, test harnesses, or quality benchmarks\n\n- Experience implementing observability for agentic systems, such as traces, telemetry, and failure analysis\n\n- Knowledge of session and chat memory management strategies across multi-turn workflows\n\n- Ability to design and document lightweight APIs that expose agent capabilities to downstream systems\n\n- Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related technical field\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Artificial Intelligence/Machine Learning Engineer<div><p><b>The Opportunity:</b><br />As an experienced engineer, you know that agentic AI is transforming how organizations operate, make decisions, and deliver outcomes at speed. Your ability to design and build practical agentic systems that turn manual workflows into AI-enabled solutions makes you an integral part of delivering mission-focused outcomes. We need your technical depth, product mindset, and problem-solving drive to support the National Security Sector Rapid Prototyping team.<br /><br />In this role, you will define, design, and deliver mission-relevant agentic AI prototypes in fast, iterative development cycles. You will collaborate with product leads, solution architects, and engineers to build, test, and deploy agent-based solutions that solve high-priority client challenges. You will apply best-fit frameworks and patterns, including agent orchestration, tool use, memory, and retrieval, while balancing solution quality, reliability, and cost.<br /><br />You will be part of a small, high-performing team operating in a 4-week prototype lifecycle, where priorities shift quickly and multiple efforts may run in parallel. Success in this role requires adaptability, clear communication, strong execution, and ownership from concept through delivery.<br /><br />Work with us to solve real-world challenges and shape the future of mission-focused agentic AI.<br /><br />Join us. The world can’t wait.<br /><br /><b>You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>Experience building and delivering agentic AI applications in production or prototype environments</p></li><li><p>Experience implementing agent orchestration frameworks</p></li><li><p>Experience designing and implementing agent loops, tool-calling workflows, and multi-agent interaction patterns</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of LLM platforms and providers, including AWS Bedrock and at least one additional provider, such as OpenAI or Ollama</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of prompt engineering techniques for reliability, controllability, and task performance</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of MCP usage and development, including integration of external tools and capabilities</p></li><li><p>Ability to own technical delivery end to end in short-cycle environments, from design through deployment</p></li><li><p>Ability to follow code review practices, document work, and maintain clean and reusable code</p></li><li><p>HS diploma or GED</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>Experience implementing retrieval patterns for agentic systems, including RAG or GraphRAG is a plus</p></li><li><p>Experience building agentic evaluation frameworks, test harnesses, or quality benchmarks</p></li><li><p>Experience implementing observability for agentic systems, such as traces, telemetry, and failure analysis</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of session and chat memory management strategies across multi-turn workflows</p></li><li><p>Ability to design and document lightweight APIs that expose agent capabilities to downstream systems</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related technical field</p></li></ul></div><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 3 Days Ago"},"status":"closed","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-20T07:20:48.759Z","closed_at":"2026-08-21T07:47:34.705Z","possibly_closed_at":"2026-08-20T19:35:50.646Z","missing_complete_scans":2,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":5,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["ai-ml"],"role_matches":["Machine Learning","Artificial Intelligence"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Machine Learning"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
