{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Colorado-Springs-CO/Chief-Software-Systems-Engineer_R0245907","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Colorado-Springs-CO/Chief-Software-Systems-Engineer_R0245907","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"23cf8e49acab517616f886b6d96a744b7a3d943ecc8b21cbfeddb48db4d7b257","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Chief Software Systems Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Colorado-Springs-CO/Chief-Software-Systems-Engineer_R0245907","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Colorado-Springs-CO/Chief-Software-Systems-Engineer_R0245907","locations":[{"label":"Colorado Springs, CO"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245907","internal_job_id":"cdcfc075bb401000c3455108393c0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-03","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Chief Software Systems Engineer The Opportunity:\nAre you looking for an opportunity to combine your technical skills with big picture thinking to make an impact in national security? You understand your customer’s environment and how to develop the right systems for their mission. Your ability to translate real-world needs into technical specifications makes you an integral part of delivering a customer focused engineering solution.\n\nAs a leader in systems engineering, we’re looking for you to solve complex challenges and shape the client by leading the Systems Engineering Team. Your customer will t rus t you to not only design and develop these systems, but also evolve them with advanced technology solutions. Share your expertise through leadership and mentoring, while broadening your skillset into areas like Common Operating Picture, framework and platform develop ment, Mission Planning, Scheduling, and Execution, and grow your skills by merging COTS sof tware, cloud computing, and AI for decision support, predictive analysis, and weapon s target pairing to create a resilient, robust, and secure sof tware solution for operations. Join our team and create the future of Space Electronic Warfare.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have: \n- 10+ years of experience with leading enterprise systems engineering across the full sof tware develop ment lifecycle, including requirements management, technical integration, validation, and verification\n- 5+ years of experience leading system integration for government furnished, contractor- develop ed, and third-party capabilities\n- Experience leading complex, multi‑contractor integration efforts\n- Experience in cloud‑native architectures, microservices, API governance, and DevSecOps\n- Experience ensuring technical compliance of platform hosted mission applications, SDK evolution, and framework services delivered across capability releases\n- Knowledge of Electronic Warfare systems as an operator, engineer, or develop er, and agile sof tware develop ment using Kanban, Scrum, or SAFE met hodologies\n- Ability to develop the system to the architectural pillars including MOSA, human‑ center ed design augmented by AI / ML, scalable mission continuity, and modular application evolution for complex enterprise systems\n- Ability to oversee develop ment and lifecycle management of API contracts, common data models, and module-integration specifications\n- Top Secret clearance\n- Bachelor's degree in a STEM field\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience with Electronic Warfare systems as an operator, engineer, or system develop er\n- Experience guiding integration and supporting contested-communications environments, multi-domain operations, and distributed operations.\n- Knowledge of cybersecurity engineering and understanding of continuous Authority to Operate and its implication on cybersecurity approvals\n- Knowledge of Zero T rus t Architecture, threat-informed Defense principles, and risk-management constructs\n- TS/SCI clearance\n- Master's degree in Systems Engineering or a STEM field\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Top Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Chief Software Systems Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>Are you looking for an opportunity to combine your technical <span>skills</span> with big picture thinking to make an impact in national security? You understand your customer’s environment and how to <span>develop</span> the right systems for their mission. Your <span>ability to</span> translate real-world needs into technical specifications makes you an integral part of delivering a customer focused engineering solution.</p><p></p><p>As a leader in systems engineering, we’re looking for you to solve complex challenges and shape the client by leading the Systems Engineering Team. Your customer will t<span>rus</span>t you to not only design and <span>develop</span> these systems, but also evolve them with advanced technology solutions. Share your expertise through leadership and mentoring, while broadening your skillset into areas like Common Operating Picture, framework and platform <span>develop</span>ment, Mission Planning, Scheduling, and Execution, and grow your <span>skills</span> by merging COTS <span>sof</span>tware, cloud computing, and AI for decision support, predictive analysis, and <span>weapon</span>s target pairing to create a resilient, robust, and secure <span>sof</span>tware solution for operations. Join our team and create the future of Space Electronic Warfare.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li>10&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with leading enterprise systems engineering across the full <span>sof</span>tware <span>develop</span>ment lifecycle, including requirements management, technical integration, validation, and verification</li><li>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> leading system integration for government furnished, contractor-<span>develop</span>ed, and third-party capabilities</li><li><span>Experience</span> leading complex, multi‑contractor integration efforts</li><li><span>Experience</span> in cloud‑native architectures, microservices, API governance, and DevSecOps</li><li><span>Experience</span> ensuring technical compliance of platform hosted mission applications, SDK evolution, and framework services delivered across capability releases</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> Electronic Warfare systems as an operator, engineer, or <span>develop</span>er, and agile <span>sof</span>tware <span>develop</span>ment using Kanban, Scrum, or SAFE <span>met</span>hodologies</li><li><span>Ability to</span> <span>develop</span> the system to the architectural pillars including MOSA, human‑<span>center</span>ed design augmented by AI<span>/</span>ML, scalable mission continuity, and modular application evolution for complex enterprise systems</li><li><span>Ability to</span> oversee <span>develop</span>ment and lifecycle management of API contracts, common data models, and module-integration specifications</li><li><span>Top Secret clearance</span></li><li><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span> in a STEM field</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with Electronic Warfare systems as an operator, engineer, or system <span>develop</span>er</li><li><span>Experience</span> guiding integration and supporting contested-communications environments, multi-domain operations, and distributed operations.</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> cybersecurity engineering and understanding of continuous Authority to Operate and its implication on cybersecurity approvals</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> Zero T<span>rus</span>t Architecture, threat-informed Defense principles, and risk-management constructs</li><li><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></li><li><span>Master&#39;s degree</span> in Systems Engineering or a STEM field</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Top Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 21 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"executive","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Systems Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
