{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/El-Segundo-CA/Cloud-Systems-Engineer_R0245973","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/El-Segundo-CA/Cloud-Systems-Engineer_R0245973","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"129cbe19460fdf9649559c4374bd9f5d74222200b053cd863647c86e542a7962","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Cloud Systems Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/El-Segundo-CA/Cloud-Systems-Engineer_R0245973","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/El-Segundo-CA/Cloud-Systems-Engineer_R0245973","locations":[{"label":"El Segundo, CA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245973","internal_job_id":"f43e8f6091f81001528bc05b07b00000","first_published_at":"2026-08-19","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Cloud Systems Engineer The Opportunity: \nAre you looking for an opportunity to combine your technical skills with big picture thinking to make an impact in Strategic SATCOM. You understand your customer’s environment and how to develop the right systems for their mission. Your ability to translate real-world needs into technical specifications makes you an integral part of delivering a customer focused engineering solution.  \n\nAs a cloud systems engineer on our team, you will have the chance to advise the government, assess the contractor’s technical approach, identify risks and gaps, and verify that the delivered cloud environment meets mission, cybersecurity, integration, performance, and operational requirements. You’ll share your expertise during acquisition, installation, configuration, and maintenance of a cloud-based system. From resolving interoperability issues across platforms to supporting the acquisition of the system, your talents will be put to good use. Grow your skills by merging cloud engineering and secure networks to create secure cloud environments. Join our team and create the future for satellite communication systems. \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have: \n- 7+ years of experience in developing cloud architecture, systems engineering, and technical oversight across AWS, Azure, hybrid cloud, on-premises, and disconnected environments\n\n- 6+ years of experience supporting complex DoW acquisition, systems engineering, digital transformation, or cloud modernization programs\n\n- Experience integrating security controls into cloud architectures, reviewing assessment evidence, supporting ATO activities, and maintaining continuous monitoring\n\n- Experience supporting DoW Impact Levels: IL4, IL5, or IL6 environments, including classified and disconnected environments\n\n- Knowledge of Zero Trust principles including identity and access management, segmentation, encryption, logging, continuous monitoring, and secure DevSecOps practices\n\n- Ability to use active learning and analytical thinking within a collaborative, cross-functional team environment\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree in CS, Computer Engineering, Information Systems Management, or System Administration\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience with Python or scripting languages for security automation\n\n- Experience developing enterprise cloud-native solutions involving Kubernetes, Docker, Helm, GCP, AWS or Azure\n\n- Experience working in DoW or IC environments\n\n- Experience with hybrid cloud, on-premises cloud, edge computing, and disconnected or limited-bandwidth environments\n\n- Experience defining technical acceptance criteria and supporting design reviews, test readiness reviews, cybersecurity reviews, and government acceptance activities\n\n- Experience translating mission needs into measurable technical, cybersecurity, resilience, availability, and performance requirements\n\n- Knowledge of DevSecOps pipelines, infrastructure as code, automated testing, container security, configuration management, and software supply-chain security\n\n- Master's degree in CS, Computer Engineering, Information Systems Management, or System Administration\n\n- Cloud certification preferred, such as AWS Solutions Architect, Azure Administrator, or Google Professional Cloud Architect\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.  \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Cloud Systems Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>Are you looking for an opportunity to combine your technical skills with big picture thinking to make an impact in Strategic SATCOM. You understand your customer’s environment and how to develop the right systems for their mission. Your ability to translate real-world needs into technical specifications makes you an integral part of delivering a customer focused engineering solution.  </p><p></p><p>As a cloud systems engineer on our team, you will have the chance to advise the government, assess the contractor’s technical approach, identify risks and gaps, and verify that the delivered cloud environment meets mission, cybersecurity, integration, performance, and operational requirements. You’ll share your expertise during acquisition, installation, configuration, and maintenance of a cloud-based system. From resolving interoperability issues across platforms to supporting the acquisition of the system, your talents will be put to good use. Grow your skills by merging cloud engineering and secure networks to create secure cloud environments. Join our team and create the future for satellite communication systems. </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have: </b></p><ul><li><p>7&#43; years of experience in developing cloud architecture, systems engineering, and technical oversight across AWS, Azure, hybrid cloud, on-premises, and disconnected environments</p></li><li><p>6&#43; years of experience supporting complex DoW acquisition, systems engineering, digital transformation, or cloud modernization programs</p></li><li><p>Experience integrating security controls into cloud architectures, reviewing assessment evidence, supporting ATO activities, and maintaining continuous monitoring</p></li><li><p>Experience supporting DoW Impact Levels: IL4, IL5, or IL6 environments, including classified and disconnected environments</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of Zero Trust principles including identity and access management, segmentation, encryption, logging, continuous monitoring, and secure DevSecOps practices</p></li><li><p>Ability to use active learning and analytical thinking within a collaborative, cross-functional team environment</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree in CS, Computer Engineering, Information Systems Management, or System Administration</p><p></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have: </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with Python or scripting languages for security automation</p></li><li><p>Experience developing enterprise cloud-native solutions involving Kubernetes, Docker, Helm, GCP, AWS or Azure</p></li><li><p>Experience working in DoW or IC environments</p></li><li><p>Experience with hybrid cloud, on-premises cloud, edge computing, and disconnected or limited-bandwidth environments</p></li><li><p>Experience defining technical acceptance criteria and supporting design reviews, test readiness reviews, cybersecurity reviews, and government acceptance activities</p></li><li><p>Experience translating mission needs into measurable technical, cybersecurity, resilience, availability, and performance requirements</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of DevSecOps pipelines, infrastructure as code, automated testing, container security, configuration management, and software supply-chain security</p></li><li><p>Master&#39;s degree in CS, Computer Engineering, Information Systems Management, or System Administration</p></li><li><p><span>Cloud certification preferred, such as AWS Solutions Architect, Azure Administrator, or Google Professional Cloud Architect</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.  </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 5 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Systems Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/CMDB-and-Attack-Surface-Management-Support-ServiceNow-Developer_R0241487","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/CMDB-and-Attack-Surface-Management-Support-ServiceNow-Developer_R0241487","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"26093b433ba1ab6bf0e14a5a067457ee3164ec126d944e0d1a35dbf37647b6eb","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"CMDB and Attack Surface Management Support - ServiceNow Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/CMDB-and-Attack-Surface-Management-Support-ServiceNow-Developer_R0241487","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/CMDB-and-Attack-Surface-Management-Support-ServiceNow-Developer_R0241487","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0241487","internal_job_id":"7db64e3672d41001a727714da8fd0000","first_published_at":"2026-06-18","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"CMDB and Attack Surface Management Support - ServiceNow Developer The Opportunity:\nIn this role, you'll design and develop ServiceNow solutions that accelerate Booz Allen's CMDB practice and the Attack Surface Management initiatives that depend on it. With millions of CIs in scope, you'll build configured capability: Workspace views, Platform Analytics dashboards and indicators, Service Catalog items for CMDB requests, CMDB Health and Relationship Health rule configurations, ownership routing, and data quality automation. You'll partner with the ServiceNow Platform Team, ITSM SMEs, and data source owners to convert CMDB-related initiative needs into working ServiceNow solutions, and you'll contribute development effort to SRM and ITSM enhancements as CMDB priorities allow.\n\nYou'll be a key technical contributor on a team focused on bringing stakeholders together around CMDB data they can rely on and trust. You'll partner with ServiceNow Platform administrators to validate Discovery data ingestion and flag pattern or ingestion issues for platform-team refinement, and work with application and infrastructure SMEs to reconcile discovered CI data across sources. You'll develop the dashboards, reporting, and Service Catalog capabilities that the Attack Surface Management Working Group and similar CMDB-dependent initiatives need to inform security and operational prioritization. You'll work in coordination with the ServiceNow Platform Team, augmenting their delivery pipeline and converting initiative demand into ServiceNow-ready work. Due to the nature of work performed within this facility, U.S. citizenship is required.\n\nWhat You’ll Work On:\n\nDevelopment:\n- Design, configure, and develop ServiceNow CMDB solutions including Workspace views, Platform Analytics dashboards and indicators, Service Catalog items, CMDB Health and Relationship Health rule configurations, ownership routing, and data quality automation, in coordination with the ServiceNow Platform Team.\n\n- Build Platform Analytics indicators, KPIs, scorecards, and dashboards that surface CI ownership, completeness, environment classification, health trends, and Attack Surface Management metrics for technical and executive audiences.\n\n- Develop and maintain the CMDB ServiceNow Workspace and Service Catalog items for CMDB-related requests, including new CI registration, ownership change, retirement, and data correction, including form design and the workflows that route them.\n\n- Contribute development effort to SRM and ITSM enhancements as CMDB workload permits, in coordination with the ServiceNow Platform Team.\n\nAnalysis and Integration:\n- Monitor CMDB health and CI relationship health using ServiceNow KPIs, evaluate CI class and sub-class data quality, and perform trending analysis to identify where data quality gaps exist.\n\n- Partner with ServiceNow Platform administrators to validate Discovery data ingestion and flag pattern or ingestion issues for resolution and collaborate with application and infrastructure SMEs and data source owners to reconcile discovered CI data across sources and close data quality gaps at the source.\n\nTranslation and Backlog Support:\n- Translate CMDB-related initiative and governance needs, such as Attack Surface Management, Trusted Enterprise Transformation, and CMDB Health and Workspace governance into ServiceNow-ready business outcomes, requirements, user stories, acceptance criteria, and UAT scenarios.\n\n- Support the CMDB enhancement backlog: intake, structure, prioritization support, dependency tracking, and readiness for ServiceNow Platform Team delivery.\n\n- Support implementation readiness for CMDB-related platform enhancements by validating data mappings, field requirements, reporting needs, and stakeholder acceptance through UAT.\n\nKnowledge Transfer:\n- Develop knowledge articles that help stakeholders self-serve and collaborate with other ITSM SMEs to contribute to the ongoing improvement of the CMDB practice.\n\nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n \nYou Have:\n- 3+ years of experience developing and implementing ServiceNow solutions, including configuration of forms, workflows, business rules, script includes, UI policies, and ACLs, including CMDB or CMDB-adjacent functions, such as ITSM, ITOM, or SecOps integration with CMDB\n\n- 3+ years of experience with ServiceNow CMDB operations, CI relationship health, and data quality, including accuracy, completeness, and consistency, with direct responsibility for CMDB data maintenance, quality checks, and remediation\n\n- 2+ years of experience with ServiceNow Discovery in an analyst capacity, including reviewing discovered CI data, identifying pattern or ingestion issues, and reconciling data from multiple sources\n\n- 2+ years of experience building Performance Analytics or Platform Analytics indicators, KPIs, scorecards, and dashboards\n\n- 2+ years of experience developing ServiceNow Service Catalog items and workflows\n\n- Experience translating operational, security, or governance requirements into ServiceNow-ready user stories, acceptance criteria, dashboards, or UAT plans, and progressing them through Agile delivery, including backlog refinement and sprint planning in Jira or ServiceNow SPM\n\n- Experience with REST and JSON APIs, including with GraphQL\n\n- Experience with ITIL Configuration Management, CSDM framework, and CI lifecycle management principles\n\n- Bachelor's degree in Information Systems or Information Technology\n\n- ServiceNow Certified System Administrator (CSA) Certification and Certified Implementation Specialist – Data Foundations (CIS‑DF) CMDB and CSDM Certification\n\nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience developing Identification and Reconciliation Engine (IRE) rules, including identifier entries, reconciliation rules, and data source precedence for duplicate prevention\n\n- Experience integrating third-party data into the CMDB using Service Graph Connectors or Integration Hub\n\n- Experience with CI Class Manager for CI class, attribute, and relationship model configuration\n\n- Experience with ServiceNow Flow Designer, GlideAjax, and scripted REST APIs in production\n\n- Experience applying the Common Service Data Model (CSDM) methodology in production environments\n\n- Experience with vulnerability data sources integration through ServiceNow Vulnerability Response and vulnerability-to-CI reconciliation in the CMDB\n\n- Possession of strong written communication skills\n\n- ServiceNow Certified Application Developer (CAD) Certification\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"CMDB and Attack Surface Management Support - ServiceNow Developer<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p>In this role, you&#39;ll design and develop ServiceNow solutions that accelerate Booz Allen&#39;s CMDB practice and the Attack Surface Management initiatives that depend on it. With millions of CIs in scope, you&#39;ll build configured capability: Workspace views, Platform Analytics dashboards and indicators, Service Catalog items for CMDB requests, CMDB Health and Relationship Health rule configurations, ownership routing, and data quality automation. You&#39;ll partner with the ServiceNow Platform Team, ITSM SMEs, and data source owners to convert CMDB-related initiative needs into working ServiceNow solutions, and you&#39;ll contribute development effort to SRM and ITSM enhancements as CMDB priorities allow.</p><p></p><p>You&#39;ll be a key technical contributor on a team focused on bringing stakeholders together around CMDB data they can rely on and trust. You&#39;ll partner with ServiceNow Platform administrators to validate Discovery data ingestion and flag pattern or ingestion issues for platform-team refinement, and work with application and infrastructure SMEs to reconcile discovered CI data across sources. You&#39;ll develop the dashboards, reporting, and Service Catalog capabilities that the Attack Surface Management Working Group and similar CMDB-dependent initiatives need to inform security and operational prioritization. You&#39;ll work in coordination with the ServiceNow Platform Team, augmenting their delivery pipeline and converting initiative demand into ServiceNow-ready work. Due to the nature of work performed within this facility, U.S. citizenship is required.</p><p></p><p><b>What You’ll Work On:</b></p><p></p><p><b>Development:</b></p><ul><li><p>Design, configure, and develop ServiceNow CMDB solutions including Workspace views, Platform Analytics dashboards and indicators, Service Catalog items, CMDB Health and Relationship Health rule configurations, ownership routing, and data quality automation, in coordination with the ServiceNow Platform Team.</p></li><li><p>Build Platform Analytics indicators, KPIs, scorecards, and dashboards that surface CI ownership, completeness, environment classification, health trends, and Attack Surface Management metrics for technical and executive audiences.</p></li><li><p>Develop and maintain the CMDB ServiceNow Workspace and Service Catalog items for CMDB-related requests, including new CI registration, ownership change, retirement, and data correction, including form design and the workflows that route them.</p></li><li><p>Contribute development effort to SRM and ITSM enhancements as CMDB workload permits, in coordination with the ServiceNow Platform Team.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Analysis and Integration:</b></p><ul><li><p>Monitor CMDB health and CI relationship health using ServiceNow KPIs, evaluate CI class and sub-class data quality, and perform trending analysis to identify where data quality gaps exist.</p></li><li><p>Partner with ServiceNow Platform administrators to validate Discovery data ingestion and flag pattern or ingestion issues for resolution and collaborate with application and infrastructure SMEs and data source owners to reconcile discovered CI data across sources and close data quality gaps at the source.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Translation and Backlog Support:</b></p><ul><li><p>Translate CMDB-related initiative and governance needs, such as Attack Surface Management, Trusted Enterprise Transformation, and CMDB Health and Workspace governance into ServiceNow-ready business outcomes, requirements, user stories, acceptance criteria, and UAT scenarios.</p></li><li><p>Support the CMDB enhancement backlog: intake, structure, prioritization support, dependency tracking, and readiness for ServiceNow Platform Team delivery.</p></li><li><p>Support implementation readiness for CMDB-related platform enhancements by validating data mappings, field requirements, reporting needs, and stakeholder acceptance through UAT.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Knowledge Transfer:</b></p><ul><li><p>Develop knowledge articles that help stakeholders self-serve and collaborate with other ITSM SMEs to contribute to the ongoing improvement of the CMDB practice.</p></li></ul><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.</p><p><span> </span></p><p><b>You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of experience developing and implementing ServiceNow solutions, including configuration of forms, workflows, business rules, script includes, UI policies, and ACLs, including CMDB or CMDB-adjacent functions, such as ITSM, ITOM, or SecOps integration with CMDB</p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of experience with ServiceNow CMDB operations, CI relationship health, and data quality, including accuracy, completeness, and consistency, with direct responsibility for CMDB data maintenance, quality checks, and remediation</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with ServiceNow Discovery in an analyst capacity, including reviewing discovered CI data, identifying pattern or ingestion issues, and reconciling data from multiple sources</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience building Performance Analytics or Platform Analytics indicators, KPIs, scorecards, and dashboards</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience developing ServiceNow Service Catalog items and workflows</p></li><li><p>Experience translating operational, security, or governance requirements into ServiceNow-ready user stories, acceptance criteria, dashboards, or UAT plans, and progressing them through Agile delivery, including backlog refinement and sprint planning in Jira or ServiceNow SPM</p></li><li><p>Experience with REST and JSON APIs, including with GraphQL</p></li><li><p>Experience with ITIL Configuration Management, CSDM framework, and CI lifecycle management principles</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree in Information Systems or Information Technology</p></li><li><p>ServiceNow Certified System Administrator (CSA) Certification and Certified Implementation Specialist – Data Foundations (CIS‑DF) CMDB and CSDM Certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b> </p><ul><li><p>Experience developing Identification and Reconciliation Engine (IRE) rules, including identifier entries, reconciliation rules, and data source precedence for duplicate prevention</p></li><li><p>Experience integrating third-party data into the CMDB using Service Graph Connectors or Integration Hub</p></li><li><p>Experience with CI Class Manager for CI class, attribute, and relationship model configuration</p></li><li><p>Experience with ServiceNow Flow Designer, GlideAjax, and scripted REST APIs in production</p></li><li><p>Experience applying the Common Service Data Model (CSDM) methodology in production environments</p></li><li><p>Experience with vulnerability data sources integration through ServiceNow Vulnerability Response and vulnerability-to-CI reconciliation in the CMDB</p></li><li><p>Possession of strong written communication skills</p></li><li><p>ServiceNow Certified Application Developer (CAD) Certification</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
