{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Albuquerque-NM/Data-Engineer_R0237241","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Albuquerque-NM/Data-Engineer_R0237241","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"e0138f65f6b04ae23d416a1b4466862bda371da9a845d6b66a752e1a83d71788","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Albuquerque-NM/Data-Engineer_R0237241","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Albuquerque-NM/Data-Engineer_R0237241","locations":[{"label":"Albuquerque, NM"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0237241","internal_job_id":"3519a44894fe1000d0898aa570890000","first_published_at":"2026-08-13","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer The Opportunity :\nEver-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artifi cia l intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an experience d data engineer like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions.\n\nAs a Data Engineer on our team, you’ll implement data engineering activities and strategy on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll design, deploy, and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful.\n\nHere, you’ll work with a multi-disciplinary team of data analysts, engineers, scientists, electrical engineers, test engineers, sof t war e developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll use your experience in analytical exploration and data examination while you help assess, design, build, and maintain scalable data platforms for your clients. You will be responsible for helping develop and maintain database systems, continually seeking opportunities to optimize the organization's data ecosystem, and building custom ETL and ELT workflows as necessary to address critical analytical questions.\n\nWhat You’ll Work On:\n- Collaborate with cross-functional teams to understand business requirements and translate them into technical solutions.\n\n- Implement and manage data governance practices, ensuring data quality, security, and compliance.\n\n- Design, construct, install, test, and maintain highly scalable data management systems, ensuring they meet business requirements and industry practices.\n\n- Employ a variety of languages and tools to marry systems together or try to hunt down opportunities to acquire new data from other systems.\n\n- Interpret and analyze data from various source systems to support data integration and data reporting needs.\n\n- Identify, design, and implement internal process improvements, including automating manual processes, optimizing data delivery, and re-designing infrastructure for greater scalability.\n\n- Develop and optimize database schemas and data models to support analytics and reporting.\n\n- Create data tools for analytics and data scientist team members that assist them in building and optimizing our data products.\n\n- Grow your communication and technical skills by merging consult ing and big data to create data-centric solutions across the testing and evaluation industry.\n\n- Stay updated with industry trends and emerging technologies to propose strategic improvements.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:   \n- 2+ years of experience designing, building, and operating production ETL or ELT pipelines\n\n- 2+ years of experience with DBMS relational databases, including data modeling and schema design\n\n- 2+ years of experience using Python for data processing and automation\n\n- 1+ years of experience with cloud services\n\n- Experience integrating data from RESTful APIs and external data sources\n\n- Experience developing and deploying containerized workloads using Docker\n\n- Experience with workflow orchestration and CI / CD for data workloads\n\n- Experience implementing or contributing to logging, monitoring, alerting, and data validation for production pipelines\n\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- 2+ years of experience with PostgreSQL\n\n- 1+ years of experience with AWS\n\n- Experience with container orchestration platforms, preferably Kubernetes\n\n- Experience with infrastructure-as-code, including Terraform, CloudFormation, or CDK\n\n- Experience with PySpark or distributed data processing frameworks\n\n- Experience with data quality frameworks or automated testing for data pipelines\n\n- Knowledge of security and access controls for cloud-based data systems\n\n- Secret clearance\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information .\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity</span></b><b>:</b></p><p>Ever-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an <span>experience</span>d data engineer like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions.</p><p></p><p>As a Data Engineer on our team, you’ll implement data engineering activities and strategy on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll design, deploy, and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful.</p><p></p><p>Here, you’ll work with a multi-disciplinary team of data analysts, engineers, scientists, electrical engineers, test engineers, <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll use your <span>experience</span> in analytical exploration and data examination while you help assess, design, build, and maintain scalable data platforms for your clients. You will be responsible for helping develop and maintain database systems, continually seeking opportunities to optimize the organization&#39;s data ecosystem, and building custom ETL and ELT workflows as necessary to address critical analytical questions.</p><p></p><p><b>What You’ll Work On:</b></p><ul><li><p>Collaborate with cross-functional teams to understand business requirements and translate them into technical solutions.</p></li><li><p>Implement and manage data governance practices, ensuring data quality, security, and compliance.</p></li><li><p>Design, construct, install, test, and maintain highly scalable data management systems, ensuring they meet business requirements and industry practices.</p></li><li><p>Employ a variety of languages and tools to marry systems together or try to hunt down opportunities to acquire new data from other systems.</p></li><li><p>Interpret and analyze data from various source systems to support data integration and data reporting needs.</p></li><li><p>Identify, design, and implement internal process improvements, including automating manual processes, optimizing data delivery, and re-designing infrastructure for greater scalability.</p></li><li><p>Develop and optimize database schemas and data models to support analytics and reporting.</p></li><li><p>Create data tools for analytics and data scientist team members that assist them in building and optimizing our data products.</p></li><li><p>Grow your communication and technical skills by merging <span>consult</span>ing and big data to create data-centric solutions across the testing and evaluation industry.</p></li><li><p>Stay updated with industry trends and emerging technologies to propose strategic improvements.</p></li></ul><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>  </p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> designing, building, and operating production ETL or ELT pipelines</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with DBMS relational databases, including data modeling and schema design</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> using Python for data processing and automation</p></li><li><p>1&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with cloud services</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> integrating data from RESTful APIs and external data sources</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> developing and deploying containerized workloads using Docker</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with workflow orchestration and CI<span>/</span>CD for data workloads</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> implementing or contributing to logging, monitoring, alerting, and data validation for production pipelines</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span><span> obtain a Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>  </p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with PostgreSQL</p></li><li><p>1&#43; years of experience with AWS</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with container orchestration platforms, preferably Kubernetes</p></li><li><p>Experience with infrastructure-as-code, including Terraform, CloudFormation, or CDK</p></li><li><p>Experience with PySpark or distributed data processing frameworks</p></li><li><p>Experience with data quality frameworks or automated testing for data pipelines</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge</span> of security and access controls for cloud-based data systems</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span>.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 11 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0241523","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0241523","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"b1beb28adf49669da3ce1559efeab97f5bc63d2d53d8b7d44f38d1eea3bfa7f8","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0241523","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0241523","locations":[{"label":"Arlington, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0241523","internal_job_id":"221ce663262a1001b90f5a1f44d90000","first_published_at":"2026-08-19","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer The Opportunity: \nEver-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need a data professional like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence. \n\nAs a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your skills and experience to help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll develop and deploy the pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful.\n\nHere, you’ll work with a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll sharpen your skills in analytical exploration and data examination while you support the assessment, design, developing, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients.\n\nWork with us to use data for good. \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- 2+ years of experience utilizing programming languages, including Python \n\n- Experience developing and maintaining scalable data stores that supply big data in forms needed for business analysis \n\n- Experience with developing scalable data pipelines or ETL/ELT workflows for reporting and analytics \n\n- Experience creating solutions within a collaborative, cross-functional team environment \n\n- Ability to develop scripts and programs for converting various types of data into usable formats and support project team to scale, monitor and operate data platforms \n\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance  \n\n- Bachelor’s degree \n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience deploying analytics workloads on a platform as a service (PaaS) and software as a service (SaaS), including AWS EMR, Redshift, SageMaker, Databricks, SQL Data Warehouse, or machine learning service\n\n- Experience creating software for retrieving, parsing and processing structured and unstructured data \n\n- Experience with distributed or parallel programming frameworks, including Apache Spark or NVIDIA CUDA\n\n- Experience with infrastructure as code frameworks and services, including Terraform or CloudFormation\n\n- Experience developing and presenting complex technical information for technical and non-technical audiences and senior leaders\n\n- Experience developing and deploying large-scale batch and stream analytics pipelines\n\n- Experience working with integrated groups comprised of customer success managers, infrastructure engineers, data scientists, and software engineers\n\n- Master’s degree in CS, Computer Engineering, Mathematics, Data Science, Software Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Physics, or a related field\n\n- Cloud Development Certification such as AWS Solutions Architect or Azure Certification\n\n- Information Security Certification such as Security+ or CISSP Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>Ever-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need a data professional like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence. </p><p></p><p>As a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your skills and experience to help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll develop and deploy the pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful.</p><p></p><p>Here, you’ll work with a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll sharpen your skills in analytical exploration and data examination while you support the assessment, design, developing, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients.</p><p></p><p>Work with us to use data for good. </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of experience utilizing programming languages, including Python </p></li><li><p>Experience developing and maintaining scalable data stores that supply big data in forms needed for business analysis </p></li><li><p>Experience with developing scalable data pipelines or ETL/ELT workflows for reporting and analytics </p></li><li><p>Experience creating solutions within a collaborative, cross-functional team environment </p></li><li><p>Ability to develop scripts and programs for converting various types of data into usable formats and support project team to scale, monitor and operate data platforms </p></li><li><p>Ability to obtain a Secret clearance  </p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience deploying analytics workloads on a platform as a service (PaaS) and software as a service (SaaS), including AWS EMR, Redshift, SageMaker, Databricks, SQL Data Warehouse, or machine learning service</p></li><li><p>Experience creating software for retrieving, parsing and processing structured and unstructured data </p></li><li><p>Experience with distributed or parallel programming frameworks, including Apache Spark or NVIDIA CUDA</p></li><li><p>Experience with infrastructure as code frameworks and services, including Terraform or CloudFormation</p></li><li><p>Experience developing and presenting complex technical information for technical and non-technical audiences and senior leaders</p></li><li><p>Experience developing and deploying large-scale batch and stream analytics pipelines</p></li><li><p>Experience working with integrated groups comprised of customer success managers, infrastructure engineers, data scientists, and software engineers</p></li><li><p>Master’s degree in CS, Computer Engineering, Mathematics, Data Science, Software Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Physics, or a related field</p></li><li><p>Cloud Development Certification such as AWS Solutions Architect or Azure Certification</p></li><li><p>Information Security Certification such as Security&#43; or CISSP Certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 5 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0242536","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0242536","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"a30d5cf2a515292e8ee46e1e1e82d8318123b05b7469634b9bcb2226978a6d61","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0242536","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0242536","locations":[{"label":"Arlington, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0242536","internal_job_id":"9fcb29f624b2100167b23bdc8ec00000","first_published_at":"2026-06-17","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer The Opportunity: \nEver-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artifi cia l intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an experience d data engineer like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions from fraud detection to cancer research, to national intelligence.  \n\nAs a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful. \n\nHere, you’ll work with and guide a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll use your experience in analytical exploration and data examination while you manage the assessment, design, building, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients. \n\nWork with us to use data for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:    \n- 5+ years of experience working in a professional environment\n- 3+ years of experience designing, developing, operationalizing, and maintaining complex data applications at enterprise scale \n- 3+ years of experience creating sof tware for retrieving, parsing, and processing structured and unstructured data \n- 3+ years of experience building scalable ETL or ELT workflows for reporting and analytics \n- Experience creating solutions within a collaborative, cross-functional team environment \n- Experience with Databricks, including Delta Lake, Spark, notebooks, and workflows or jobs\n- Experience with GitLab for version control, CI / CD pipelines, and code review workflows\n- Ability to develop scripts and programs for converting various types of data into usable formats and support project team to scale, monitor, and operate data platforms \n- Secret clearance \n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have:    \n- Experience with UNIX or Linux, including basic commands and Shell scripting \n- Experience with a public cloud, including AWS, Micro sof t Azure, or Google Cloud \n- Experience with distributed data or computing tools, including Spark, Databricks, Hadoop, Hive, AWS EMR, or Kafka \n- Experience working on real-time data and streaming applications  \n- Experience with NoSQL implementation, including MongoDB or Cassandra \n- Experience with data warehousing using AWS Redshift, MySQL, or Snowflake  \n- Experience with Agile engineering practices \n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph \n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>Ever-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an <span>experience</span>d data engineer like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions from fraud detection to cancer research, to national intelligence.  </p><p></p><p>As a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful. </p><p></p><p>Here, you’ll work with and guide a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll use your <span>experience</span> in analytical exploration and data examination while you manage the assessment, design, building, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients. </p><p></p><p>Work with us to use data for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> working in a professional environment</li><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> designing, developing, operationalizing, and maintaining complex data applications at enterprise scale </li><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> creating <span>sof</span>tware for retrieving, parsing, and processing structured and unstructured data </li><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> building scalable ETL or ELT workflows for reporting and analytics </li><li><span>Experience</span> creating solutions within a collaborative, cross-functional team environment </li><li><span>Experience</span> with Databricks, including Delta Lake, Spark, notebooks, and workflows or jobs</li><li><span>Experience</span> with GitLab for version control, CI<span>/</span>CD pipelines, and code review workflows</li><li><span>Ability to</span> develop scripts and programs for converting various types of data into usable formats and support project team to scale, monitor, and operate data platforms </li><li><span>Secret clearance </span></li><li><span>Bachelor’s degree </span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with UNIX or Linux, including basic commands and Shell scripting </li><li><span>Experience</span> with a public cloud, including AWS, Micro<span>sof</span>t Azure, or Google Cloud </li><li><span>Experience</span> with distributed data or computing tools, including Spark, Databricks, Hadoop, Hive, AWS EMR, or Kafka </li><li><span>Experience</span> working on real-time data and streaming applications  </li><li><span>Experience</span> with NoSQL implementation, including MongoDB or Cassandra </li><li><span>Experience</span> with data warehousing using AWS Redshift, MySQL, or Snowflake  </li><li><span>Experience</span> with Agile engineering practices </li><li><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph </span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b> </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0242942","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0242942","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"878a28f2258d96ac584465f0da256f89e5ed1b5783d6910469c6e38049b15109","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0242942","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0242942","locations":[{"label":"Arlington, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0242942","internal_job_id":"f4d78b1c639610015c4cdb82aed70000","first_published_at":"2026-06-24","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer The Opportunity: \nEver-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artifi cia l intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an experience d data engineer like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions from fraud detection to cancer research, to national intelligence.  \n\nAs a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful. \n\nHere, you’ll work with and guide a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll use your experience in analytical exploration and data examination while you manage the assessment, design, building, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients. \n\nWork with us to use data for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:    \n- 5+ years of experience working in a professional environment\n\n- 3+ years of experience designing, developing, operationalizing, and maintaining complex data applications at enterprise scale \n\n- 3+ years of experience creating sof tware for retrieving, parsing, and processing structured and unstructured data \n\n- 3+ years of experience building scalable ETL or ELT workflows for reporting and analytics \n\n- Experience creating solutions within a collaborative, cross-functional team environment \n\n- Experience with Palantir Foundry\n\n- Experience with Databricks, including Delta Lake, Spark, notebooks, and workflows or jobs, and GitLab for version control, CI / CD pipelines, and code review workflows\n\n- Ability to develop scripts and programs for converting various types of data into usable formats and support project team to scale, monitor, and operate data platforms \n\n- Secret clearance \n\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have:    \n- Experience with UNIX or Linux, including basic commands and Shell scripting \n\n- Experience with a public cloud, including AWS, Micro sof t Azure, or Google Cloud \n\n- Experience with distributed data or computing tools, including Spark, Databricks, Hadoop, Hive, AWS EMR, or Kafka \n\n- Experience working on real-time data and streaming applications  \n\n- Experience with NoSQL implementation, including MongoDB or Cassandra \n\n- Experience with data warehousing using AWS Redshift, MySQL, or Snowflake  \n\n- Experience with Agile engineering practices \n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph \n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>Ever-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an <span>experience</span>d data engineer like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions from fraud detection to cancer research, to national intelligence.  </p><p></p><p>As a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful. </p><p></p><p>Here, you’ll work with and guide a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll use your <span>experience</span> in analytical exploration and data examination while you manage the assessment, design, building, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients. </p><p></p><p>Work with us to use data for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> working in a professional environment</p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> designing, developing, operationalizing, and maintaining complex data applications at enterprise scale </p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> creating <span>sof</span>tware for retrieving, parsing, and processing structured and unstructured data </p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> building scalable ETL or ELT workflows for reporting and analytics </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> creating solutions within a collaborative, cross-functional team environment </p></li><li><p>Experience with Palantir Foundry</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Databricks, including Delta Lake, Spark, notebooks, and workflows or jobs, and GitLab for version control, CI<span>/</span>CD pipelines, and code review workflows</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> develop scripts and programs for converting various types of data into usable formats and support project team to scale, monitor, and operate data platforms </p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance </span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor’s degree </span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with UNIX or Linux, including basic commands and Shell scripting </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with a public cloud, including AWS, Micro<span>sof</span>t Azure, or Google Cloud </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with distributed data or computing tools, including Spark, Databricks, Hadoop, Hive, AWS EMR, or Kafka </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> working on real-time data and streaming applications  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with NoSQL implementation, including MongoDB or Cassandra </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with data warehousing using AWS Redshift, MySQL, or Snowflake  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Agile engineering practices </p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph </span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b> </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0245613","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0245613","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"9e267554c318c20f4a997218fd451fe8413330a6f9e539da47e006f93100d13e","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0245613","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0245613","locations":[{"label":"Arlington, VA"},{"label":"San Diego, CA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245613","internal_job_id":"fe4132e52a921001635bdeaf84710000","first_published_at":"2026-08-21","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer The Opportunity: \nEver-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artifi cia l intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need a data professional like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions, from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence. \n\nAs a Data Engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your skills and experience to help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll develop and deploy the pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful.\n\nHere, you’ll work with a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced and agile environment. You’ll sharpen your skills in analytical exploration and data examination while you support the assessment, design, development, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients.\n\nWork with us to use data for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- Experience in data engineering, pipeline development, systems administration or software engineering\n\n- Experience with ETL operations\n\n- Experience with source control and collaboration sof tware, including Git or Atlassian tools \n\n- Experience writing sof tware in programming languages, including Python\n\n- Knowledge of relational and non-relational database technologies, including SQL or GraphQL \n\n- Knowledge of automation and scripting on Linux or Windows operating systems\n\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance \n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience deploying analytics workloads on a platform as a service ( PaaS ) and sof tware as a service ( SaaS ) , including AWS EMR, Redshift, SageMaker, Databricks, SQL Data Warehouse, or Machine Learning service\n\n- Experience with distributed or parallel programming frameworks, including Apache Spark or NVIDIA CUDA\n\n- Experience with infrastructure as code frameworks and services, including Terraform or CloudFormation\n\n- Experience developing and presenting complex technical information for technical and non-technical audiences and senior leaders\n\n- Experience developing and deploying large-scale batch and stream analytics pipelines\n\n- Experience working with integrated groups comprised of customer success managers, infrastructure engineers, data scientists, and sof tware engineers \n\n- Experience with DoD information systems\n\n- Master’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Mathematics, Data Science, Sof tware Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or Physics\n\n- Cloud Development Certification, including AWS Solutions Architect or Azure Certification \n\n- Information Security Certification, including Security+ or CISSP Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>Ever-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need a data professional like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions, from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence. </p><p></p><p>As a Data Engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your skills and experience to help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll develop and deploy the pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful.</p><p></p><p>Here, you’ll work with a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced and agile environment. You’ll sharpen your skills in analytical exploration and data examination while you support the assessment, design, development, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients.</p><p></p><p>Work with us to use data for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience in data engineering, pipeline development, systems administration or software engineering</p></li><li><p>Experience with ETL operations</p></li><li><p>Experience with source control and collaboration <span>sof</span>tware, including Git or Atlassian tools </p></li><li><p>Experience writing <span>sof</span>tware in programming languages, including Python</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of relational and non-relational database technologies, including SQL or GraphQL </p></li><li><p>Knowledge of automation and scripting on Linux or Windows operating systems</p></li><li><p>Ability to obtain a Secret clearance </p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience deploying analytics workloads on a platform as a service <span>(</span>PaaS<span>)</span> and <span>sof</span>tware as a service <span>(</span>SaaS<span>)</span>, including AWS EMR, Redshift, SageMaker, Databricks, SQL Data Warehouse, or Machine Learning service</p></li><li><p>Experience with distributed or parallel programming frameworks, including Apache Spark or NVIDIA CUDA</p></li><li><p>Experience with infrastructure as code frameworks and services, including Terraform or CloudFormation</p></li><li><p>Experience developing and presenting complex technical information for technical and non-technical audiences and senior leaders</p></li><li><p>Experience developing and deploying large-scale batch and stream analytics pipelines</p></li><li><p>Experience working with integrated groups comprised of customer success managers, infrastructure engineers, data scientists, and <span>sof</span>tware engineers </p></li><li><p>Experience with DoD information systems</p></li><li><p>Master’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Mathematics, Data Science, <span>Sof</span>tware Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or Physics</p></li><li><p>Cloud Development Certification, including AWS Solutions Architect or Azure Certification </p></li><li><p>Information Security Certification, including Security&#43; or CISSP Certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 3 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0247120","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0247120","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"7bbfdea37f357744f0a7b250ba50567c98825d99893e23e07823209eb0b08515","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0247120","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0247120","locations":[{"label":"Arlington, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247120","internal_job_id":"ce7800f7d1461000b9f87e6198010000","first_published_at":"2026-08-17","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer The Opportunity: \nEver-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need a data professional like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence. \n\nAs a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your skills and experience to help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll develop and deploy the pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful.\n\nHere, you’ll work with a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll sharpen your skills in analytical exploration and data examination while you support the assessment, design, developing, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- 2+ years of experience utilizing programming languages, including C++, Java, or Python \n\n- 2+ years of experience developing and maintaining scalable data stores that supply big data in forms needed for business analysis \n\n- 1+ years of experience with source control and collaboration software, including Git or Atlassian tools\n\n- Experience with developing scalable ETL and ELT workflows for reporting and analytics \n\n- Knowledge of relational and non-relational database technologies, including SQL or GraphQL\n\n- Ability to develop scripts and programs for converting various types of data into usable formats and support project team to scale, monitor and operate data platforms \n\n- Ability to work in a controlled facility, such as a SIPR space\n\n- Secret clearance  \n\n- Bachelor’s degree \n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience deploying analytics workloads on a platform as a service (PaaS) and software as a service (SaaS), including AWS EMR, Redshift, SageMaker, Databricks, SQL Data Warehouse, or Machine Learning service\n\n- Experience with distributed or parallel programming frameworks, including Apache Spark or NVIDIA CUDA\n\n- Experience with infrastructure as code frameworks and services, including Terraform or CloudFormation\n\n- Experience developing and presenting complex technical information for technical and non-technical audiences and senior leaders\n\n- Experience developing and deploying large-scale batch and stream analytics pipelines\n\n- Experience working with integrated groups comprised of customer success managers, infrastructure engineers, data scientists, and software engineers\n\n- Experience with DoD information systems\n\n- Master’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Mathematics, Data Science, Software Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or Physics\n\n- Cloud Development Certification, including AWS Solutions Architect or Azure Certification, or Information Security Certification, including Security+ or CISSP Certification\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph \n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.  \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>Ever-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need a data professional like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence. </p><p></p><p>As a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your skills and experience to help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll develop and deploy the pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful.</p><p></p><p>Here, you’ll work with a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll sharpen your skills in analytical exploration and data examination while you support the assessment, design, developing, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of experience utilizing programming languages, including C&#43;&#43;, Java, or Python </p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience developing and maintaining scalable data stores that supply big data in forms needed for business analysis </p></li><li><p>1&#43; years of experience with source control and collaboration software, including Git or Atlassian tools</p></li><li><p>Experience with developing scalable ETL and ELT workflows for reporting and analytics </p></li><li><p>Knowledge of relational and non-relational database technologies, including SQL or GraphQL</p></li><li><p>Ability to develop scripts and programs for converting various types of data into usable formats and support project team to scale, monitor and operate data platforms </p></li><li><p>Ability to work in a controlled facility, such as a SIPR space</p></li><li><p>Secret clearance  </p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience deploying analytics workloads on a platform as a service (PaaS) and software as a service (SaaS), including AWS EMR, Redshift, SageMaker, Databricks, SQL Data Warehouse, or Machine Learning service</p></li><li><p>Experience with distributed or parallel programming frameworks, including Apache Spark or NVIDIA CUDA</p></li><li><p>Experience with infrastructure as code frameworks and services, including Terraform or CloudFormation</p></li><li><p>Experience developing and presenting complex technical information for technical and non-technical audiences and senior leaders</p></li><li><p>Experience developing and deploying large-scale batch and stream analytics pipelines</p></li><li><p>Experience working with integrated groups comprised of customer success managers, infrastructure engineers, data scientists, and software engineers</p></li><li><p>Experience with DoD information systems</p></li><li><p>Master’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Mathematics, Data Science, Software Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or Physics</p></li><li><p>Cloud Development Certification, including AWS Solutions Architect or Azure Certification, or Information Security Certification, including Security&#43; or CISSP Certification</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.  </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 7 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0247542","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0247542","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"1e8e19df793c5b89e9b44f7ab8bf49f36dd15111124d46eed5adeedd6e7c9fe6","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0247542","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0247542","locations":[{"label":"Arlington, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247542","internal_job_id":"ae74c1d5954e1001efdaa87a14780000","first_published_at":"2026-08-21","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer The Opportunity: \nEver-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need a data professional like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence. \n\nAs a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your skills and experience to help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll develop and deploy the pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful.\n\nHere, you’ll work with a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll sharpen your skills in analytical exploration and data examination while you support the assessment, design, developing, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients.\n\nWork with us to use data for good. \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- 2+ years of experience within data engineering\n\n- 2+ years of experience developing and maintaining scalable data stores that supply big data in forms needed for business analysis \n\n- Experience utilizing programming languages, including Python\n\n- Experience creating software for retrieving, parsing and processing structured and unstructured data \n\n- Experience with developing scalable ETL/ELT workflows for reporting and analytics \n\n- Experience creating solutions within a collaborative, cross-functional team environment \n\n- Ability to develop scripts and programs for converting various types of data into usable formats and support project team to scale, monitor and operate data platforms \n\n- Secret clearance  \n\n- Bachelor’s degree \n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience deploying analytics workloads on a platform as a service (PaaS) and software as a service (SaaS), including AWS EMR, Redshift, SageMaker, Databricks, SQL Data Warehouse, or machine learning service\n\n- Experience with distributed or parallel programming frameworks, including Apache Spark or NVIDIA CUDA\n\n- Experience with infrastructure as code frameworks and services, including Terraform or CloudFormation\n\n- Experience developing and presenting complex technical information for technical and non-technical audiences and senior leaders\n\n- Experience developing and deploying large-scale batch and stream analytics pipelines\n\n- Experience working with integrated groups comprised of customer success managers, infrastructure engineers, data scientists, and software engineers\n\n- Experience with DoD information systems\n\n- Master’s degree in CS, Computer Engineering, Mathematics, Data Science, Software Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Physics, or a related field\n\n- Cloud Development Certification such as AWS Solutions Architect or Azure Certification\n\n- Information Security Certification such as Security+ or CISSP Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>Ever-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need a data professional like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence. </p><p></p><p>As a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your skills and experience to help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll develop and deploy the pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful.</p><p></p><p>Here, you’ll work with a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll sharpen your skills in analytical exploration and data examination while you support the assessment, design, developing, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients.</p><p></p><p>Work with us to use data for good. </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of experience within data engineering</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience developing and maintaining scalable data stores that supply big data in forms needed for business analysis </p></li><li><p>Experience utilizing programming languages, including Python</p></li><li><p>Experience creating software for retrieving, parsing and processing structured and unstructured data </p></li><li><p>Experience with developing scalable ETL/ELT workflows for reporting and analytics </p></li><li><p>Experience creating solutions within a collaborative, cross-functional team environment </p></li><li><p>Ability to develop scripts and programs for converting various types of data into usable formats and support project team to scale, monitor and operate data platforms </p></li><li><p>Secret clearance  </p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience deploying analytics workloads on a platform as a service (PaaS) and software as a service (SaaS), including AWS EMR, Redshift, SageMaker, Databricks, SQL Data Warehouse, or machine learning service</p></li><li><p>Experience with distributed or parallel programming frameworks, including Apache Spark or NVIDIA CUDA</p></li><li><p>Experience with infrastructure as code frameworks and services, including Terraform or CloudFormation</p></li><li><p>Experience developing and presenting complex technical information for technical and non-technical audiences and senior leaders</p></li><li><p>Experience developing and deploying large-scale batch and stream analytics pipelines</p></li><li><p>Experience working with integrated groups comprised of customer success managers, infrastructure engineers, data scientists, and software engineers</p></li><li><p>Experience with DoD information systems</p></li><li><p>Master’s degree in CS, Computer Engineering, Mathematics, Data Science, Software Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Physics, or a related field</p></li><li><p>Cloud Development Certification such as AWS Solutions Architect or Azure Certification</p></li><li><p>Information Security Certification such as Security&#43; or CISSP Certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 3 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-24T01:56:20.339Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0247559","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0247559","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"11a9ecc0bfb648a3382aea04c34c156dc2ef2b3063e5a13f237fff9ed369332a","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0247559","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Engineer_R0247559","locations":[{"label":"Arlington, VA"},{"label":"San Diego, CA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247559","internal_job_id":"71f6309939971001f852488f8db60000","first_published_at":"2026-08-21","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer The Opportunity: \nEver-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artifi cia l intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need a data professional like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions, from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence. \n\nAs a Data Engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your skills and experience to help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll develop and deploy the pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful.\n\nHere, you’ll work with a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced and agile environment. You’ll sharpen your skills in analytical exploration and data examination while you support the assessment, design, development, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients.\n\nWork with us to use data for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- Experience in data engineering, pipeline development, systems administration, or software engineering\n\n- Experience with ETL operations\n\n- Experience with source control and collaboration sof tware, including Git or Atlassian tools \n\n- Experience writing sof tware in programming languages, including Python\n\n- Knowledge of relational and non-relational database technologies, including SQL or GraphQL \n\n- Knowledge of automation and scripting on Linux or Windows operating systems\n\n- Secret clearance \n\n- Scheduled to obtain Bachelor's degree by December 2026\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience deploying analytics workloads on a platform as a service ( PaaS ) and sof tware as a service ( SaaS ) , including AWS EMR, Redshift, SageMaker, Databricks, SQL Data Warehouse, or Machine Learning service\n\n- Experience with distributed or parallel programming frameworks, including Apache Spark or NVIDIA CUDA\n\n- Experience with infrastructure as code frameworks and services, including Terraform or CloudFormation\n\n- Experience developing and presenting complex technical information for technical and non-technical audiences and senior leaders\n\n- Experience developing and deploying large-scale batch and stream analytics pipelines\n\n- Experience working with integrated groups comprised of customer success managers, infrastructure engineers, data scientists, and sof tware engineers \n\n- Experience with DoD information systems\n\n- Master’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Mathematics, Data Science, Sof tware Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or Physics\n\n- Cloud Development Certification, including AWS Solutions Architect or Azure Certification \n\n- Information Security Certification, including Security+ or CISSP Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>Ever-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need a data professional like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions, from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence. </p><p></p><p>As a Data Engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your skills and experience to help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll develop and deploy the pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful.</p><p></p><p>Here, you’ll work with a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced and agile environment. You’ll sharpen your skills in analytical exploration and data examination while you support the assessment, design, development, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients.</p><p></p><p>Work with us to use data for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience in data engineering, pipeline development, systems administration, or software engineering</p></li><li><p>Experience with ETL operations</p></li><li><p>Experience with source control and collaboration <span>sof</span>tware, including Git or Atlassian tools </p></li><li><p>Experience writing <span>sof</span>tware in programming languages, including Python</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of relational and non-relational database technologies, including SQL or GraphQL </p></li><li><p>Knowledge of automation and scripting on Linux or Windows operating systems</p></li><li><p>Secret clearance </p></li><li><p>Scheduled to obtain Bachelor&#39;s degree by December 2026</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience deploying analytics workloads on a platform as a service <span>(</span>PaaS<span>)</span> and <span>sof</span>tware as a service <span>(</span>SaaS<span>)</span>, including AWS EMR, Redshift, SageMaker, Databricks, SQL Data Warehouse, or Machine Learning service</p></li><li><p>Experience with distributed or parallel programming frameworks, including Apache Spark or NVIDIA CUDA</p></li><li><p>Experience with infrastructure as code frameworks and services, including Terraform or CloudFormation</p></li><li><p>Experience developing and presenting complex technical information for technical and non-technical audiences and senior leaders</p></li><li><p>Experience developing and deploying large-scale batch and stream analytics pipelines</p></li><li><p>Experience working with integrated groups comprised of customer success managers, infrastructure engineers, data scientists, and <span>sof</span>tware engineers </p></li><li><p>Experience with DoD information systems</p></li><li><p>Master’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Mathematics, Data Science, <span>Sof</span>tware Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or Physics</p></li><li><p>Cloud Development Certification, including AWS Solutions Architect or Azure Certification </p></li><li><p>Information Security Certification, including Security&#43; or CISSP Certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 3 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-24T01:56:20.339Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Belcamp-MD/Data-Engineer_R0241931","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Belcamp-MD/Data-Engineer_R0241931","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"e4a7f16241850755acd9f87bf67fc2351c8ff022e477bf53e4204fec9ba7941e","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Belcamp-MD/Data-Engineer_R0241931","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Belcamp-MD/Data-Engineer_R0241931","locations":[{"label":"Belcamp, MD"},{"label":"Aberdeen Proving Ground, MD"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0241931","internal_job_id":"cb5b967f859e10016237d14f3ad20000","first_published_at":"2026-06-10","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer The Opportunity:\nEver-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an experienced data engineer like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence.  \n\nAs a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful. \n\nHere, you’ll work with and guide a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll use your experience in analytical exploration and data examination while you manage the assessment, design, building, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients. \n\nWork with us to use data for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- 5+ years of experience in application development, and designing, developing, operationalizing and maintaining complex data applications at enterprise scale \n\n- 3+ years of experience creating software for retrieving, parsing and processing structured and unstructured data, and building scalable ETL/ELT workflows for reporting and analytics \n\n- Experience with PySpark and Spark SQL \n\n- Experience in creating, maintaining Object Types, Link Types, and Action Types in Foundry Ontology, and with Foundry Workshop and how to debug issues\n\n- Experience creating solutions within a collaborative, cross-functional team environment \n\n- Ability to build and modify data transformations in Palantir Foundry Data Pipeline Builder and Code Repositories\n\n- Ability to read logs, diagnose errors, and troubleshoot issues in Palantir Foundry\n\n- Ability to develop scripts and programs for converting various types of data into usable formats and support project team to scale, monitor and operate data platforms \n\n- Bachelor’s degree  \n\n- Secret clearance\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience with Python, SQL, Scala, or Java \n\n- Experience with UNIX/Linux, including basic commands and Shell scripting \n\n- Experience with a public cloud, including AWS, Microsoft Azure, or Google Cloud \n\n- Experience with distributed data/computing tools including Spark, Databricks, Hadoop, Hive, AWS EMR, or Kafka \n\n- Experience working on real-time data and streaming applications  \n\n- Experience with NoSQL implementation, including MongoDB or Cassandra \n\n- Experience with data warehousing using AWS Redshift, MySQL, or Snowflake  \n\n- Experience with Agile engineering practices \n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p>Ever-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an experienced data engineer like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence.  </p><p></p><p>As a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful. </p><p></p><p>Here, you’ll work with and guide a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll use your experience in analytical exploration and data examination while you manage the assessment, design, building, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients. </p><p></p><p>Work with us to use data for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of experience in application development, and designing, developing, operationalizing and maintaining complex data applications at enterprise scale </p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of experience creating software for retrieving, parsing and processing structured and unstructured data, and building scalable ETL/ELT workflows for reporting and analytics </p></li><li><p><span>Experience with PySpark and Spark SQL </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience in creating, maintaining Object Types, Link Types, and Action Types in Foundry Ontology, and with </span><span>Foundry Workshop and how to debug issues </span></p></li><li><p>Experience creating solutions within a collaborative, cross-functional team environment </p></li><li><p><span>Ability to build and modify data transformations in Palantir Foundry Data Pipeline Builder and Code Repositories</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to read logs, diagnose errors, and troubleshoot issues in Palantir Foundry</span></p></li><li><p>Ability to develop scripts and programs for converting various types of data into usable formats and support project team to scale, monitor and operate data platforms </p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree  </p></li><li><p>Secret clearance</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with Python, SQL, Scala, or Java </p></li><li><p>Experience with UNIX/Linux, including basic commands and Shell scripting </p></li><li><p>Experience with a public cloud, including AWS, Microsoft Azure, or Google Cloud </p></li><li><p>Experience with distributed data/computing tools including Spark, Databricks, Hadoop, Hive, AWS EMR, or Kafka </p></li><li><p>Experience working on real-time data and streaming applications  </p></li><li><p>Experience with NoSQL implementation, including MongoDB or Cassandra </p></li><li><p>Experience with data warehousing using AWS Redshift, MySQL, or Snowflake  </p></li><li><p>Experience with Agile engineering practices </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b> </p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Belcamp-MD/Data-Engineer_R0243265","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Belcamp-MD/Data-Engineer_R0243265","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"99737ee4f4c13d4a17662536efad9ac1f5fc699f13374647df16c4343afd566f","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Belcamp-MD/Data-Engineer_R0243265","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Belcamp-MD/Data-Engineer_R0243265","locations":[{"label":"Belcamp, MD"},{"label":"Aberdeen Proving Ground, MD"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0243265","internal_job_id":"8f3baa969d4a1000bc9ff70957f30000","first_published_at":"2026-06-29","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer The Opportunity:\nEver-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an experienced data engineer like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence.  \n\nAs a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful. \n\nHere, you’ll work with and guide a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll use your experience in analytical exploration and data examination while you manage the assessment, design, building, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients. \n\nWork with us to use data for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- 5+ years of experience in application development, and designing, developing, operationalizing and maintaining complex data applications at enterprise scale \n\n- 3+ years of experience creating software for retrieving, parsing and processing structured and unstructured data, and building scalable ETL and ELT workflows for reporting and analytics \n\n- Experience with PySpark and Spark SQL \n\n- Experience in creating and maintaining Object Types, Link Types, and Action Types in Foundry Ontology, and with Foundry Workshop and debugging issues\n\n- Experience creating solutions within a collaborative, cross-functional team environment \n\n- Ability to build and modify data transformations in Palantir Foundry Data Pipeline Builder and Code Repositories\n\n- Ability to read logs, diagnose errors, and troubleshoot issues in Palantir Foundry\n\n- Ability to develop scripts and programs for converting various types of data into usable formats and support project team to scale, monitor and operate data platforms \n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree  \n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience with Python, SQL, Scala, or Java \n\n- Experience with UNIX and Linux, including basic commands and Shell scripting \n\n- Experience with a public cloud, including AWS, Microsoft Azure, or Google Cloud \n\n- Experience with distributed data and computing tools, including Spark, Databricks, Hadoop, Hive, AWS EMR, or Kafka \n\n- Experience working on real-time data and streaming applications  \n\n- Experience with NoSQL implementation, including MongoDB or Cassandra \n\n- Experience with data warehousing using AWS Redshift, MySQL, or Snowflake  \n\n- Experience with Agile engineering practices \n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p>Ever-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an experienced data engineer like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence.  </p><p></p><p>As a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful. </p><p></p><p>Here, you’ll work with and guide a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll use your experience in analytical exploration and data examination while you manage the assessment, design, building, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients. </p><p></p><p>Work with us to use data for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of experience in application development, and designing, developing, operationalizing and maintaining complex data applications at enterprise scale </p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of experience creating software for retrieving, parsing and processing structured and unstructured data, and building scalable ETL and ELT workflows for reporting and analytics </p></li><li><p><span>Experience with PySpark and Spark SQL </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience in creating and maintaining Object Types, Link Types, and Action Types in Foundry Ontology, and with </span><span>Foundry Workshop and debugging issues </span></p></li><li><p>Experience creating solutions within a collaborative, cross-functional team environment </p></li><li><p><span>Ability to build and modify data transformations in Palantir Foundry Data Pipeline Builder and Code Repositories</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to read logs, diagnose errors, and troubleshoot issues in Palantir Foundry</span></p></li><li><p>Ability to develop scripts and programs for converting various types of data into usable formats and support project team to scale, monitor and operate data platforms </p></li><li><p>Secret clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree  </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with Python, SQL, Scala, or Java </p></li><li><p>Experience with UNIX and Linux, including basic commands and Shell scripting </p></li><li><p>Experience with a public cloud, including AWS, Microsoft Azure, or Google Cloud </p></li><li><p>Experience with distributed data and computing tools, including Spark, Databricks, Hadoop, Hive, AWS EMR, or Kafka </p></li><li><p>Experience working on real-time data and streaming applications  </p></li><li><p>Experience with NoSQL implementation, including MongoDB or Cassandra </p></li><li><p>Experience with data warehousing using AWS Redshift, MySQL, or Snowflake  </p></li><li><p>Experience with Agile engineering practices </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b> </p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0239070","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0239070","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"b628c00a7fdb6d994b4ff5cb55d2339b881eb0262b0dc31e57ab1c3cd9432d03","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0239070","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0239070","locations":[{"label":"Chantilly, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0239070","internal_job_id":"300ac85b20c21001abec3112ee290000","first_published_at":"2026-07-29","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer The Opportunity: \n\nEver-expanding technology and collection methodologies means that there is more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing big data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources.  \n\nAs a Data Engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data available and meaningful. \n\nHere, you’ll work with a multi-disciplinary team of data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment.  \n\nWork with us to use data for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- 3+ years of experience with data pipelines, including data acquisition, data prep, and database architecture\n\n- 3+ years of experience in ETL development using Java, Python, SQL, or Scala\n\n- 2+ years of experience with PostgreSQL or Kafka\n\n- Experience with AWS services\n\n- Experience with designing and implementing, containerizing, and deploying end-to-end automated data and ML pipelines, within a Cloud environment\n\n- Knowledge of the ML lifecycle and concepts to develop an MLOps ecosystem\n\n- Top Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience with Kafka ecosystem tools, such as Kafka Connect and Kafka Streams\n\n- Experience with NiFi  \n\n- Experience with infrastructure-as-code tools, such as Terraform or Ansible\n\n- Experience with Agile development methodologies \n\n- Experience working on real-time data and streaming applications\n\n- Ability to pay strict attention to detail \n\n- Possession of excellent problem-solving and analytical skills\n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Top Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<div><p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p></div><div><p>Ever-expanding technology and collection methodologies means that there is more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing big data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources.  </p><p></p><p>As a Data Engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data available and meaningful. </p><p></p><p>Here, you’ll work with a multi-disciplinary team of data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment.  </p><p></p><p>Work with us to use data for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of experience with data pipelines, including data acquisition, data prep, and database architecture</p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of experience in ETL development using Java, Python, SQL, or Scala</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with PostgreSQL or Kafka</p></li><li><p>Experience with AWS services</p></li><li><p>Experience with designing and implementing, containerizing, and deploying end-to-end automated data and ML pipelines, within a Cloud environment</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of the ML lifecycle and concepts to develop an MLOps ecosystem</p></li><li><p>Top Secret clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with Kafka ecosystem tools, such as Kafka Connect and Kafka Streams</p></li><li><p>Experience with NiFi  </p></li><li><p>Experience with infrastructure-as-code tools, such as Terraform or Ansible</p></li><li><p>Experience with Agile development methodologies </p></li><li><p>Experience working on real-time data and streaming applications</p></li><li><p>Ability to pay strict attention to detail </p></li><li><p>Possession of excellent problem-solving and analytical skills</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b> </p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Top Secret clearance is required.</p></div><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 26 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0241347","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0241347","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"0a480d189f7c3a21313edca8d825b54b1ceb3ac55e7a0fdc815f20b605b79fbd","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0241347","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0241347","locations":[{"label":"Chantilly, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0241347","internal_job_id":"221ce663262a1001ab9071c43ea40000","first_published_at":"2026-06-04","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer The Opportunity: \nEver-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an experienced data engineer like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions, from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence.  \n\nAs a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful. \n\nHere, you’ll work with and guide a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced and agile environment. You’ll use your experience in analytical exploration and data examination while you manage the assessment, design, building, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients. \n\nWork with us to use data for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- 3+ years of experience designing cloud-native data platforms in AWS\n\n- 2+ years of experience designing scalable data lake, warehouse, and analytics solutions\n\n- 2+ years of experience with cloud migration and modernization efforts\n\n- 2+ years of experience with the data pipelines, including data acquisition, data prep, and database architecture\n\n- Experience with data engineering projects supporting data science, AI/ML implementations, and Business Intelligence dashboards\n\n- Experience with non-relational and semi-relational databases\n\n- Experience creating software for retrieving, parsing, and processing structured and unstructured data\n\n- Experience with team lead functions, creating solutions within a collaborative and cross-functional team environment\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- Bachelor's degree in CS \n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience with Pyspark and Spark ecosystems such as Databricks and EMR\n\n- Experience evaluating data analytic or science technologies and platforms\n\n- Experience going through an A&A process or leading modifications\n\n- Experience with Cloud Architecture and evaluating and selecting cloud analytics architectures\n\n- Experience with Data Marts and Data Warehouses and creating, managing, and troubleshooting complex operational data flows\n\n- Experience with Source code management and integration such as GitHub\n\n- Experience with designing, developing, deploying, or testing in Amazon Web Services (AWS)\n\n- Experience with scripting languages such as Python and SQL\n\n- Experience with APIs development\n\n- AWS architecture Certifications such as Solution Architect Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>Ever-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an experienced data engineer like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions, from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence.  </p><p></p><p>As a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful. </p><p></p><p>Here, you’ll work with and guide a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced and agile environment. You’ll use your experience in analytical exploration and data examination while you manage the assessment, design, building, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients. </p><p></p><p>Work with us to use data for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of experience designing cloud-native data platforms in AWS</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience designing scalable data lake, warehouse, and analytics solutions</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with cloud migration and modernization efforts</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with the data pipelines, including data acquisition, data prep, and database architecture</p></li><li><p>Experience with data engineering projects supporting data science, AI/ML implementations, and Business Intelligence dashboards</p></li><li><p>Experience with non-relational and semi-relational databases</p></li><li><p>Experience creating software for retrieving, parsing, and processing structured and unstructured data</p></li><li><p>Experience with team lead functions, creating solutions within a collaborative and cross-functional team environment</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree in CS </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with Pyspark and Spark ecosystems such as Databricks and EMR</p></li><li><p>Experience evaluating data analytic or science technologies and platforms</p></li><li><p>Experience going through an A&amp;A process or leading modifications</p></li><li><p>Experience with Cloud Architecture and evaluating and selecting cloud analytics architectures</p></li><li><p>Experience with Data Marts and Data Warehouses and creating, managing, and troubleshooting complex operational data flows</p></li><li><p>Experience with Source code management and integration such as GitHub</p></li><li><p>Experience with designing, developing, deploying, or testing in Amazon Web Services (AWS)</p></li><li><p>Experience with scripting languages such as Python and SQL</p></li><li><p>Experience with APIs development</p></li><li><p>AWS architecture Certifications such as Solution Architect Certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0245235","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0245235","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"712058ffffc70bb5bba46d200586fc74f8216d03bf51551a7b4e99780f75c9ac","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0245235","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0245235","locations":[{"label":"Chantilly, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245235","internal_job_id":"5fd54a09d5d01000b71469dbbdc10000","first_published_at":"2026-08-10","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer The Opportunity:\nEver-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artifi cia l intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an experience d data engineer like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions from fraud detection to cancer research, to national intelligence.  \n\nAs a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful. \n\nHere, you’ll work with and guide a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll use your experience in analytical exploration and data examination while you manage the assessment, design, building, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients. \n\nWork with us to use data for good\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:    \n- 5+ years of experience creating sof tware for retrieving, parsing, and processing structured and unstructured data \n\n- 3+ years of experience with Python, SQL, Scala, or Java\n\n- 3+ years of experience building scalable ETL / ELT workflows for reporting and analytics \n\n- Experience creating solutions within a collaborative and cross-functional team environment\n\n- Experience using version control tools such as GitLab, GitHub, or Bitbucket\n\n- Ability to develop scripts and programs for converting various types of data into usable formats and support project team to scale, monitor, and operate data platforms\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- HS diploma or GED\n\n- Ability to obtain a Security+ Certification within 30 days of start date\n\nNice If You Have:    \n- Experience with UNIX or Linux, including basic commands and Shell scripting \n\n- Experience with a public cloud, including AWS, Micro sof t Azure, or Google Cloud \n\n- Experience with distributed data or computing tools, including Spark, Databricks, Hadoop, Hive, AWS EMR, or Kafka \n\n- Experience working on real-time data and streaming applications  \n\n- Experience with NoSQL implementation, including MongoDB or Cassandra \n\n- Experience with Databricks\n\n- Experience with data warehousing using AWS Redshift, MySQL, or Snowflake  \n\n- Experience with Agile engineering practices \n\n- Bachelor's degree in a Data or IT- related field\n\n- Security+ Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>Ever-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an <span>experience</span>d data engineer like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions from fraud detection to cancer research, to national intelligence.  </p><p></p><p>As a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful. </p><p></p><p>Here, you’ll work with and guide a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll use your <span>experience</span> in analytical exploration and data examination while you manage the assessment, design, building, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients. </p><p></p><p>Work with us to use data for good</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> creating <span>sof</span>tware for retrieving, parsing, and processing structured and unstructured data </p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with Python, SQL, Scala, or Java</p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> building scalable ETL<span>/</span>ELT workflows for reporting and analytics </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> creating solutions within a collaborative and cross-functional team environment</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> using version control tools such as GitLab, GitHub, or Bitbucket</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> develop scripts and programs for converting various types of data into usable formats and support project team to scale, monitor, and operate data platforms</p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span> with a polygraph</p></li><li><p><span>HS diploma or GED</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> obtain a Security&#43; <span>Certification</span> within 30 days of start date</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with UNIX or Linux, including basic commands and Shell scripting </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with a public cloud, including AWS, Micro<span>sof</span>t Azure, or Google Cloud </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with distributed data or computing tools, including Spark, Databricks, Hadoop, Hive, AWS EMR, or Kafka </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> working on real-time data and streaming applications  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with NoSQL implementation, including MongoDB or Cassandra </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Databricks</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with data warehousing using AWS Redshift, MySQL, or Snowflake  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Agile engineering practices </p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span> in a Data or IT-<span>related</span> field</p></li><li><p>Security&#43; <span>Certification</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 14 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0245362","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0245362","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"e30e31636c8805d4eb7566da8f87fcd4895de81d882c7c0946aea25db95a1250","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0245362","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0245362","locations":[{"label":"Chantilly, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245362","internal_job_id":"e534098ad7cc1000b5fa2cade40d0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-10","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer The Opportunity: \nEver-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an experienced data engineer like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions from fraud detection to cancer research, to national intelligence.  \n\nAs a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful. \nHere, you’ll work with and guide a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll use your experience in analytical exploration and data examination while you manage the assessment, design, building, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients. \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- 5+ years of experience creating software for retrieving, parsing, and processing structured and unstructured data \n\n- 3+ years of experience with Python, SQL, Scala, or Java\n\n- 3+ years of experience building scalable ETL and ELT workflows for reporting and analytics \n\n- Experience creating solutions within a collaborative and cross-functional team environment \n\n- Experience using version control tools, such as GitLab, GitHub, or Bitbucket\n\n- Ability to develop scripts and programs for converting various types of data into usable formats, and support project team to scale, monitor, and operate data platforms\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- HS diploma or GED\n\n- Ability to obtain a Security+ Certification within 6 months of start date\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience with UNIX or Linux, including basic commands and Shell scripting \n\n- Experience with a public cloud, including AWS, Microsoft Azure, or Google Cloud \n\n- Experience with distributed data or computing tools, including Spark, Databricks, Hadoop, Hive, AWS EMR, or Kafka \n\n- Experience working on real-time data and streaming applications  \n\n- Experience with NoSQL implementation, including MongoDB or Cassandra \n\n- Experience with Databricks\n\n- Experience with data warehousing using AWS Redshift, MySQL, or Snowflake  \n\n- Experience with Agile engineering practices \n\n- Bachelor's degree in a Data or IT-related field\n\n- Security+ Certification\n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>Ever-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an experienced data engineer like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions from fraud detection to cancer research, to national intelligence.  </p><p></p><p>As a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful. </p><p>Here, you’ll work with and guide a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll use your experience in analytical exploration and data examination while you manage the assessment, design, building, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients. </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of experience creating software for retrieving, parsing, and processing structured and unstructured data </p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of experience with Python, SQL, Scala, or Java</p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of experience building scalable ETL and ELT workflows for reporting and analytics </p></li><li><p>Experience creating solutions within a collaborative and cross-functional team environment </p></li><li><p>Experience using version control tools, such as GitLab, GitHub, or Bitbucket</p></li><li><p>Ability to develop scripts and programs for converting various types of data into usable formats, and support project team to scale, monitor, and operate data platforms</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</p></li><li><p>HS diploma or GED</p></li><li><p>Ability to obtain a Security&#43; Certification within 6 months of start date</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with UNIX or Linux, including basic commands and Shell scripting </p></li><li><p>Experience with a public cloud, including AWS, Microsoft Azure, or Google Cloud </p></li><li><p>Experience with distributed data or computing tools, including Spark, Databricks, Hadoop, Hive, AWS EMR, or Kafka </p></li><li><p>Experience working on real-time data and streaming applications  </p></li><li><p>Experience with NoSQL implementation, including MongoDB or Cassandra </p></li><li><p>Experience with Databricks</p></li><li><p>Experience with data warehousing using AWS Redshift, MySQL, or Snowflake  </p></li><li><p>Experience with Agile engineering practices </p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree in a Data or IT-related field</p></li><li><p>Security&#43; Certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b> </p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 14 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0245373","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0245373","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"5e72d82e9cb4da3cf700f371e579eba3a76043d64fa3e5be00653c744cc62af7","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0245373","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0245373","locations":[{"label":"Chantilly, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245373","internal_job_id":"5fd54a09d5d01000b703663a75fa0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-10","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer The Opportunity: \nBooz Allen is seeking a Data Engineer to architect, develop, and optimize scalable data pipelines and platforms that transform complex data into actionable insights. In this role, you will lead a team of data engineers to design modern, cloud-native solutions integrating structured and unstructured data across secure environments. \n\nYou will serve as a technical and strategic leader, responsible for building and maintaining enterprise data infrastructure that powers analytics, reporting, and mission-critical decision-making. Collaborating with multidisciplinary teams, you will set engineering standards, ensure data quality, and drive innovation, enabling the organization to leverage data as a secure and strategic asset at scale. \n\nThis position blends technical expertise with leadership responsibilities to deliver high-quality, reliable, and secure data solutions across cloud and distributed systems. \n\nWork with us to use data for good.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- Experience with building and maintaining data pipelines \n\n- Experience with ETL development using NiFi, Python, or Scala\n\n- Experience with SQL, PostgreSQL, or Kafka\n\n- Knowledge of AWS services, including RDS and Aurora \n\n- Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team environment\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- Bachelor’s degree in a Computer Science or Engineering field\n\n- Ability to obtain Security+ Certification within 6 months of hire \n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience with Kafka Connect, Kafka Streams, or other Kafka ecosystem tools\n\n- Experience with NiFi for data flow automation\n\n- Experience with Kubernetes, Helm, ArgoCD, or related orchestration tools \n\n- Experience with monitoring tools2, such as Grafana, Prometheus, or Elasticsearch\n\n- Experience with real-time data and streaming architectures\n\nClearance:  \n Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>Booz Allen is seeking a Data Engineer to architect, develop, and optimize scalable data pipelines and platforms that transform complex data into actionable insights. In this role, you will lead a team of data engineers to design modern, cloud-native solutions integrating structured and unstructured data across secure environments. </p><p></p><p>You will serve as a technical and strategic leader, responsible for building and maintaining enterprise data infrastructure that powers analytics, reporting, and mission-critical decision-making. Collaborating with multidisciplinary teams, you will set engineering standards, ensure data quality, and drive innovation, enabling the organization to leverage data as a secure and strategic asset at scale. </p><p></p><p>This position blends technical expertise with leadership responsibilities to deliver high-quality, reliable, and secure data solutions across cloud and distributed systems. </p><p></p><p>Work with us to use data for good.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with building and maintaining data pipelines </p></li><li><p>Experience with ETL development using NiFi, Python, or Scala</p></li><li><p>Experience with SQL, PostgreSQL, or Kafka</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of AWS services, including RDS and Aurora </p></li><li><p>Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team environment</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree in a Computer Science or Engineering field</p></li><li><p>Ability to obtain Security&#43; Certification within 6 months of hire </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with Kafka Connect, Kafka Streams, or other Kafka ecosystem tools</p></li><li><p>Experience with NiFi for data flow automation</p></li><li><p>Experience with Kubernetes, Helm, ArgoCD, or related orchestration tools </p></li><li><p>Experience with monitoring tools2, such as Grafana, Prometheus, or Elasticsearch</p></li><li><p>Experience with real-time data and streaming architectures</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b> </p><p> Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 14 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0245506","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0245506","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"d696d742fd9b4ae1902f9c2905973e4f1cfc2169fed3bfa842265e2f4352851a","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0245506","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0245506","locations":[{"label":"Chantilly, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245506","internal_job_id":"e596be2e73831000b5a7fd890e030000","first_published_at":"2026-08-10","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer The Opportunity: \nEver-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an experienced data professional like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions, from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence. \n\nAs a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your expertise to help build advanced technology solutions and lead data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll guide data engineering activities by overseeing the development and deployment of pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- 7+ years of experience in application development and designing, developing, operationalizing, and maintaining complex enterprise‑scale data applications\n\n- 5+ years of experience developing software and solutions for retrieving, parsing, and processing structured and unstructured data, including scalable ETL and ELT workflows for reporting and analytics\n\n- Experience developing scripts, programs, and automated processes to convert various data types into usable formats and support scalable, monitored, and reliable data platforms\n\n- Experience with data architecture, data engineering, and enterprise data migration, including leading modernization initiatives and migration efforts involving multiple applications or delivery teams\n\n- Experience with ETL design and optimization using Informatica PowerCenter, including Designer, Workflow Manager, Monitor, mapping, and session development and Informatica Developer for data transformation\n\n- Experience with relational databases, such as SQL Server, Oracle, and PostgreSQL, including SQL development, data modeling, heterogeneous migrations, stored procedures, and performance tuning\n\n- Experience with Linux fundamentals, AWS cloud data architectures such as S3, RDS, cloud‑based processing, and migration and scalable distributed data platforms\n\n- Experience supporting CI/CD and DevOps practices using Git, GitLab, GitHub, pipeline implementation, automated deployments, Ansible, and workflow orchestration, including Control‑M\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- Bachelor’s degree in a Computer Science, Information Systems, or Engineering field\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- 10+ years of experience using Python, SQL, Scala, or Java \n\n- 5+ years of experience with a public cloud, including AWS, Microsoft Azure, or Google Cloud \n\n- 5+ years of experience with Distributed data and computing tools, including Spark, Databricks, Hadoop, Hive, AWS EMR, or Kafka \n\n- 5+ years of experience working on real-time data and streaming applications  \n\n- 5+ years of experience with NoSQL implementation, including MongoDB or Cassandra \n\n- 5+ years of experience with data warehousing, including AWS Redshift, MySQL, or Snowflake \n\n- 5+ years of experience with UNIX and Linux, including basic commands and Shell scripting \n\n- 5+ years of experience with Agile engineering practices \n\n- Experience in executing full data migration lifecycle activities, including unit testing, UAT support, reconciliation, validation, production deployment, and implementing data security controls\n\nClearance:     \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>Ever-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an experienced data professional like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions, from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence. </p><p></p><p>As a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your expertise to help build advanced technology solutions and lead data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll guide data engineering activities by overseeing the development and deployment of pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>7&#43; years of experience in application development and designing, developing, operationalizing, and maintaining complex enterprise‑scale data applications</p></li><li><p>5&#43; years of experience developing software and solutions for retrieving, parsing, and processing structured and unstructured data, including scalable ETL and ELT workflows for reporting and analytics</p></li><li><p>Experience developing scripts, programs, and automated processes to convert various data types into usable formats and support scalable, monitored, and reliable data platforms</p></li><li><p>Experience with data architecture, data engineering, and enterprise data migration, including leading modernization initiatives and migration efforts involving multiple applications or delivery teams</p></li><li><p>Experience with ETL design and optimization using Informatica PowerCenter, including Designer, Workflow Manager, Monitor, mapping, and session development and Informatica Developer for data transformation</p></li><li><p>Experience with relational databases, such as SQL Server, Oracle, and PostgreSQL, including SQL development, data modeling, heterogeneous migrations, stored procedures, and performance tuning</p></li><li><p>Experience with Linux fundamentals, AWS cloud data architectures such as S3, RDS, cloud‑based processing, and migration and scalable distributed data platforms</p></li><li><p>Experience supporting CI/CD and DevOps practices using Git, GitLab, GitHub, pipeline implementation, automated deployments, Ansible, and workflow orchestration, including Control‑M</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree in a Computer Science, Information Systems, or Engineering field</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>10&#43; years of experience using Python, SQL, Scala, or Java </p></li><li><p>5&#43; years of experience with a public cloud, including AWS, Microsoft Azure, or Google Cloud </p></li><li><p>5&#43; years of experience with Distributed data and computing tools, including Spark, Databricks, Hadoop, Hive, AWS EMR, or Kafka </p></li><li><p>5&#43; years of experience working on real-time data and streaming applications  </p></li><li><p>5&#43; years of experience with NoSQL implementation, including MongoDB or Cassandra </p></li><li><p>5&#43; years of experience with data warehousing, including AWS Redshift, MySQL, or Snowflake </p></li><li><p>5&#43; years of experience with UNIX and Linux, including basic commands and Shell scripting </p></li><li><p>5&#43; years of experience with Agile engineering practices </p></li><li><p>Experience in executing full data migration lifecycle activities, including unit testing, UAT support, reconciliation, validation, production deployment, and implementing data security controls</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b> <span class=\"emphasis\">  </span></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 14 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0246480","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0246480","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"c58e10886ecca804e795e9b7d8e7ba17d73cbe023b0a073ca3a3cc48ab8393c2","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0246480","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0246480","locations":[{"label":"Chantilly, VA"},{"label":"Aurora, CO"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246480","internal_job_id":"83b83551a759100100eb8a2e64060000","first_published_at":"2026-08-11","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer The Opportunity: \n\nEver-expanding technology and collection methodologies means that there is more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing big data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources.  \n\nAs a Data Engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data available and meaningful. \n\nHere, you’ll work with a multi-disciplinary team of data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment.  \n\nWork with us to use data for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- 3+ years of experience with data pipelines, including data acquisition, data prep, and database architecture\n\n- 3+ years of experience in ETL development using Java, Python, SQL, or Scala\n\n- 2+ years of experience with PostgreSQL or Kafka\n\n- Experience with AWS services\n\n- Experience with designing and implementing, containerizing, and deploying end-to-end automated data and ML pipelines, within a Cloud environment\n\n- Knowledge of the ML lifecycle and concepts to develop an MLOps ecosystem\n\n- Top Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience with Kafka ecosystem tools, such as Kafka Connect and Kafka Streams\n\n- Experience with NiFi  \n\n- Experience with infrastructure-as-code tools, such as Terraform or Ansible\n\n- Experience with Agile development methodologies \n\n- Experience working on real-time data and streaming applications\n\n- Ability to pay strict attention to detail \n\n- Possession of excellent problem-solving and analytical skills\n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Top Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<div><p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p></div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><p>Ever-expanding technology and collection methodologies means that there is more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing big data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources.  </p><p></p><p>As a Data Engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data available and meaningful. </p><p></p><p>Here, you’ll work with a multi-disciplinary team of data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment.  </p><p></p><p>Work with us to use data for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of experience with data pipelines, including data acquisition, data prep, and database architecture</p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of experience in ETL development using Java, Python, SQL, or Scala</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with PostgreSQL or Kafka</p></li><li><p>Experience with AWS services</p></li><li><p>Experience with designing and implementing, containerizing, and deploying end-to-end automated data and ML pipelines, within a Cloud environment</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of the ML lifecycle and concepts to develop an MLOps ecosystem</p></li><li><p>Top Secret clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with Kafka ecosystem tools, such as Kafka Connect and Kafka Streams</p></li><li><p>Experience with NiFi  </p></li><li><p>Experience with infrastructure-as-code tools, such as Terraform or Ansible</p></li><li><p>Experience with Agile development methodologies </p></li><li><p>Experience working on real-time data and streaming applications</p></li><li><p>Ability to pay strict attention to detail </p></li><li><p>Possession of excellent problem-solving and analytical skills</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b> </p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Top Secret clearance is required.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 13 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0247564","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0247564","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"60eefdde009fa7ef2d4d18911d857466d6df4f2d6fb03d4fd7ad79f5620d9152","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0247564","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Data-Engineer_R0247564","locations":[{"label":"Chantilly, VA"},{"label":"Aurora, CO"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247564","internal_job_id":"ce7800f7d1461001f6512621634e0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-21","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer The Opportunity: \nEver-expanding technology and collection met hodologies means that there is more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing big data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources.  \n\nAs a Data Engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data available and meaningful. \n\nHere, you’ll work with a multi-disciplinary team of data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment.  \n\nWork with us to use data for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:    \n- Experience with data pipelines, including data acquisition, data prep, and database architecture in an academic or professional environment\n\n- Experience with ETL development using Java, Python, SQL, or Scala in an academic or professional environment\n\n- Experience with AWS services in an academic or professional environment\n\n- Experience designing and implementing, containerizing, and deploying end-to-end automated data and ML pipelines within a Cloud environment in an academic or professional environment\n\n- Knowledge of the ML lifecycle and concepts to develop an MLOps ecosystem\n\n- Top Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have:    \n- Experience with Kafka ecosystem tools such as Kafka Connect and Kafka Stream\n\n- Experience with NiFi  \n\n- Experience with infrastructure-as-code tools such as Terraform or Ansible\n\n- Experience with Agile development met hodologies \n\n- Experience working on real-time data and streaming applications\n\n- Ability to pay strict attention to detail \n\n- Possession of excellent problem-solving and analytical skills\n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Top Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<div><p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>Ever-expanding technology and collection <span>met</span>hodologies means that there is more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing big data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources.  </p><p></p><p>As a Data Engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data available and meaningful. </p><p></p><p>Here, you’ll work with a multi-disciplinary team of data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment.  </p><p></p><p>Work with us to use data for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with data pipelines, including data acquisition, data prep, and database architecture in an academic or professional environment</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with ETL development using Java, Python, SQL, or Scala in an academic or professional environment</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with AWS services in an academic or professional environment</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> designing and implementing, containerizing, and deploying end-to-end automated data and ML pipelines within a Cloud environment in an academic or professional environment</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> the ML lifecycle and concepts to develop an MLOps ecosystem</p></li><li><p><span>Top Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor’s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Kafka ecosystem tools such as Kafka Connect and Kafka Stream</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with NiFi  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with infrastructure-as-code tools such as Terraform or Ansible</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Agile development <span>met</span>hodologies </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> working on real-time data and streaming applications</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> pay strict attention to detail </p></li><li><p><span>Possession of</span> excellent problem-solving and analytical skills</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b> </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Top Secret clearance is required.</span></p></div><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 3 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-24T01:56:20.339Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Colorado-Springs-CO/Data-Engineer_R0246414","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Colorado-Springs-CO/Data-Engineer_R0246414","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"75cc96b0abebcf7cd730ec05f162a6edf84243b14d86eec5ea572aae34617be5","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Colorado-Springs-CO/Data-Engineer_R0246414","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Colorado-Springs-CO/Data-Engineer_R0246414","locations":[{"label":"Colorado Springs, CO"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246414","internal_job_id":"e534098ad7cc1000b0c526d0199c0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-17","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer The Opportunity:\nAchieving data dominance provides a critical competitive advantage, espe cia lly in the frontier of space. For USSPACECOM, high-fidelity simulations rely entirely on the quality, speed, and structure of underlying data. We need a dedicated data engineer to build the robust data infrastructure that makes these advanced simulations possible.\n\nAs a data engineer at Booz Allen, you will focus on the foundational layer of our customer’s modeling, simulation, and analysis environment. You will design, build, and deploy the scalable data pipelines that ingest disparate, multi-domain, and multi-classification data sources and transform them into clean, structured schemas. Your work will directly empower our multi-disciplinary team of exercise planners, systems architects, data scientists, and model-based system engineers to draw insights and execute mission-critical models.\n\nWork with us to build the data foundation for the future of space operations.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:    \n- Experience in object-oriented programming such as Python, Java, or C++ and advanced SQL\n\n- Experience integrating APIs, designing data schemas, and normalizing complex, disparate datasets\n\n- Knowledge of database systems and data warehousing principles\n\n- Ability to design, build, and maintain robust ETL / ELT data pipelines at scale\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree in Data Science, Data Engineering, Computer Science, Sof tware Engineering, or a STEM field\n\nNice If You Have:    \n- Experience with infrastructure-as-code ( IaC ) and automation scripts\n\n- Experience integrating with Palantir Foundry or similar enterprise data fabrics\n\n- Experience with streaming data processing such as Apache Kafka or Spark\n\n- Experience working in an Agile engineering environment and supporting MLOps pipelines\n\n- Master’s degree in a quantitative or systems-focused STEM field\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ;   TS/SCI clearance is required.   \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b><br />Achieving data dominance provides a critical competitive advantage, espe<span>cia</span>lly in the frontier of space. For USSPACECOM, high-fidelity simulations rely entirely on the quality, speed, and structure of underlying data. We need a dedicated data engineer to build the robust data infrastructure that makes these advanced simulations possible.</p><p></p><p>As a data engineer at Booz Allen, you will focus on the foundational layer of our customer’s modeling, simulation, and analysis environment. You will design, build, and deploy the scalable data pipelines that ingest disparate, multi-domain, and multi-classification data sources and transform them into clean, structured schemas. Your work will directly empower our multi-disciplinary team of exercise planners, systems architects, data scientists, and model-based system engineers to draw insights and execute mission-critical models.</p><p></p><p>Work with us to build the data foundation for the future of space operations.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> in object-oriented programming such as Python, Java, or C&#43;&#43; and advanced SQL</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> integrating APIs, designing data schemas, and normalizing complex, disparate datasets</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> database systems and data warehousing principles</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> design, build, and maintain robust ETL<span>/</span>ELT data pipelines at scale</p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree in Data Science, Data Engineering, Computer Science, <span>Sof</span>tware Engineering, or a STEM field</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with infrastructure-as-code <span>(</span>IaC<span>)</span> and automation scripts</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> integrating with Palantir Foundry or <span>similar</span> enterprise data fabrics</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with streaming data processing such as Apache Kafka or Spark</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> working in an Agile engineering environment and supporting MLOps pipelines</p></li><li><p><span>Master’s degree</span> in a quantitative or systems-focused STEM field</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance is required.</span>  </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 7 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Dayton-OH/Data-Engineer_R0246721","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Dayton-OH/Data-Engineer_R0246721","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"2da5e795eb647f199715ab33780e74254c9ae35b44d46890778f90a501732426","fetched_at":"2026-08-24T14:15:46.938Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Dayton-OH/Data-Engineer_R0246721","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Dayton-OH/Data-Engineer_R0246721","locations":[{"label":"Dayton, OH"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246721","internal_job_id":"e596be2e73831001505b04bce4ea0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-12","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer The Opportunity: \nEver-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need a data professional like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions, from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence. \n\nAs a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your skills and experience to help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll develop and deploy the pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful.\n\nHere, you’ll work with a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll sharpen your skills in analytical exploration and data examination while you support the assessment, design, developing, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients.\n\nWork with us to use data for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- 5+ years of experience with data architecture, design, or engineering projects \n\n- Experience with cloud migration and modernization efforts and creating automated Extract, Transform, Load (ETL) processes to move data from unstructured source data to application governed storage \n\n- Experience with the data pipelines, including data acquisition, data prep, database architecture, data governance, and data tagging \n\n- Experience with non-relational NoSQL, semi-relational databases, and relational SQL databases  \n\n- Experience with implementing monitoring tools to maintain data integrity, fix broken pipelines, and handle missing or corrupt information and designing scalable data lake, warehouse, and analytics solutions \n\n- Experience integrating AI/ML capabilities into production workflows or operator tooling, such as LLM enabled assistants, model augmented decision aids, or automation solutions  \n\n- Knowledge of AWS services, such as S3, IAM, EventBridge, Step Functions, or Lambda \n\n- Ability to work both within a team and independently to manage tasks with minimal supervision \n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree in Computer Science or technical discipline\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience evaluating data analytic or science technologies and platforms \n\n- Experience designing cloud-native data platforms in AWS  \n\n- Experience with Cloud Architecture and evaluating and selecting cloud analytics architectures \n\n- Experience with Data Marts and Data Warehouses and creating, managing, and troubleshooting complex operational data flows \n\n- Experience with ETL tools, such as dbt and Airflow  \n\n- Experience with Source code management and integration such as GitHub \n\n- Experience with CI/CD practices  \n\n- Experience with programming languages such as Python, Rust, C++, Java, etc. \n\n- Experience with API development \n\n- AWS architecture Certifications such as Solution Architect Certification \n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.  \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>Ever-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need a data professional like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions, from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence. </p><p></p><p>As a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your skills and experience to help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll develop and deploy the pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful.</p><p></p><p>Here, you’ll work with a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll sharpen your skills in analytical exploration and data examination while you support the assessment, design, developing, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients.</p><p></p><p>Work with us to use data for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of experience with data architecture, design, or engineering projects </p></li><li><p>Experience with cloud migration and modernization efforts and creating automated Extract, Transform, Load (ETL) processes to move data from unstructured source data to application governed storage </p></li><li><p>Experience with the data pipelines, including data acquisition, data prep, database architecture, data governance, and data tagging </p></li><li><p>Experience with non-relational NoSQL, semi-relational databases, and relational SQL databases  </p></li><li><p>Experience with implementing monitoring tools to maintain data integrity, fix broken pipelines, and handle missing or corrupt information and designing scalable data lake, warehouse, and analytics solutions </p></li><li><p>Experience integrating AI/ML capabilities into production workflows or operator tooling, such as LLM enabled assistants, model augmented decision aids, or automation solutions  </p></li><li><p>Knowledge of AWS services, such as S3, IAM, EventBridge, Step Functions, or Lambda </p></li><li><p>Ability to work both within a team and independently to manage tasks with minimal supervision </p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science or technical discipline</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience evaluating data analytic or science technologies and platforms </p></li><li><p>Experience designing cloud-native data platforms in AWS  </p></li><li><p>Experience with Cloud Architecture and evaluating and selecting cloud analytics architectures </p></li><li><p>Experience with Data Marts and Data Warehouses and creating, managing, and troubleshooting complex operational data flows </p></li><li><p>Experience with ETL tools, such as dbt and Airflow  </p></li><li><p>Experience with Source code management and integration such as GitHub </p></li><li><p>Experience with CI/CD practices  </p></li><li><p>Experience with programming languages such as Python, Rust, C&#43;&#43;, Java, etc. </p></li><li><p>Experience with API development </p></li><li><p>AWS architecture Certifications such as Solution Architect Certification </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b> </p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI<b> </b>clearance is required.  </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 12 Days Ago"},"status":"possibly_closed","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-24T14:15:46.938Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","missing_complete_scans":1,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Fayetteville-NC/Data-Engineer_R0236980","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Fayetteville-NC/Data-Engineer_R0236980","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"05d3756d65031221fda3ae72790306f62465db666e5a441b6f0d17b42d318b6c","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fayetteville-NC/Data-Engineer_R0236980","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fayetteville-NC/Data-Engineer_R0236980","locations":[{"label":"Fayetteville, NC"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0236980","internal_job_id":"70a5cd4ae69e1001eea4d11e15ab0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-04","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer The Opportunity : \nEver-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artifi cia l intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an experience d data engineer like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions from fraud detection to cancer research, to national intelligence.  \n\nAs a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful. \n\nHere, you’ll work with and guide a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll use your experience in analytical exploration and data examination while you manage the assessment, design, building, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients. \n\nWork with us to use data for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:  \n- Experience developing and maintaining ETL and ELT processes from various sources, ensuring data quality and consistency across systems \n- Experience building data pipelines for batch and streaming workflows\n- Experience building and managing a data catalog, including integrating APIs and securing access using OAuth2\n- Experience with programming languages such as Python and SQL, for processing, scripting, automation, and optimization\n- Experience creating solutions within a collaborative, cross-functional team environment \n- Ability to deploy internationally for up to 90 days\n- Ability to travel CONUS up to 25% of the time\n- TS/SCI clearance\n- HS diploma or GED\n\n​ Nice If You Have:    \n- Experience with Palantir Foundry\n- Experience with a public cloud, including AWS, Micro sof t Azure, or Google Cloud \n- Experience with Docker and Kubernetes\n- Experience implementing CI / CD best practices\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.   \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity</span></b><b>: </b></p><p>Ever-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an <span>experience</span>d data engineer like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions from fraud detection to cancer research, to national intelligence.  </p><p></p><p>As a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful. </p><p></p><p>Here, you’ll work with and guide a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll use your <span>experience</span> in analytical exploration and data examination while you manage the assessment, design, building, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients. </p><p></p><p>Work with us to use data for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b> </p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> developing and maintaining ETL and ELT processes from various sources, ensuring data quality and consistency across systems </li><li><span>Experience</span> building data pipelines for batch and streaming workflows</li><li><span>Experience</span> building and managing a data catalog, including integrating APIs and securing access using OAuth2</li><li><span>Experience</span> with programming languages such as Python and SQL, for processing, scripting, automation, and optimization</li><li><span>Experience</span> creating solutions within a collaborative, cross-functional team environment </li><li><span>Ability to</span> deploy internationally for up to 90 days</li><li><span>Ability to</span> travel CONUS up to 25% of the time</li><li><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></li><li><span>HS diploma or GED</span></li></ul><p></p><p>​<b><span>Nice If You Have:</span>   </b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with Palantir Foundry</li><li><span>Experience</span> with a public cloud, including AWS, Micro<span>sof</span>t Azure, or Google Cloud </li><li><span>Experience</span> with Docker and Kubernetes</li><li><span>Experience</span> implementing CI<span>/</span>CD best practices</li><li><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b> </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance is required.</span>  </p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 20 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Fayetteville-NC/Data-Engineer_R0239251","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Fayetteville-NC/Data-Engineer_R0239251","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"bbf1811873a5455a9a5ad5cba369e59cd383867e08905272082c667254e88d10","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fayetteville-NC/Data-Engineer_R0239251","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fayetteville-NC/Data-Engineer_R0239251","locations":[{"label":"Fayetteville, NC"},{"label":"Fort Benning, GA"},{"label":"Virginia Beach, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0239251","internal_job_id":"15ef08f0fea41000b51fdb6bd7df0000","first_published_at":"2026-06-22","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer The Opportunity:\nRapid advances in IoT, machine learning, and artifi cia l intelligence mean organizations have access to more data than ever before—both structured and unstructured. Turning that data into actionable insight requires strong engineering, thoughtful design, and scalable platforms.\n\nAs a senior Data Engineer at Booz Allen, you will design and build data platforms and pipelines that power mission-critical outcomes. You will work on complex, high-impact programs that help clients solve real-world challenges with data.\n\nYou’ll collaborate with analysts, AI engineers, develop ers, and stakeholders in a fast-paced, agile environment. In this role, you will lead technical efforts across assessment, design, develop ment, and sustainment of scalable data platforms while mentoring teammates and driving best practices.\n\nWhat You’ll Work On:\n- Design, build, and maintain scalable data pipelines and platforms.\n- Develop secure, efficient Python for data processing, automation, and warehousing.\n- Migrate and integrate data from on-premises systems to cloud environments.\n- Implement CI / CD pipelines to automate build, test, and deployment workflows.\n- Develop SQL scripts and stored procedures for data processing and transformation.\n- Apply data modeling best practices.\n- Support data governance, met adata tagging, and access controls.\n- Partner with cross-functional teams to deliver end-to-end data solutions.\n- Provide technical guidance in a complex enterprise environment.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 2+ years of experience as a data engineer supporting large-scale enterprise systems\n- Experience writing clean, secure, and efficient Python for data engineering use cases\n- Experience moving data from on-prem environments to the cloud and automating develop ment workflows, including building, deploying, or managing applications\n- Experience with CI / CD practices\n- Experience with SQL, including stored procedures and data modeling\n- Experience with data governance and data tagging\n- Knowledge of AWS services, such as S3, IAM, EventBridge, Step Functions, or Lambda\n- Ability to work independently and manage tasks with minimal supervision\n- TS/SCI clearance\n- HS diploma or GED\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience  with Pipeline Builder, AIP, and Foundry's application develop ment ecosystem\n- Experience with ETL tools, such as dbt and Airflow\n- Experience with NoSQL and graph databases, and DevOps tools and automation practices\n- Experience designing and building data warehouses\n- Experience working in multiple SDLC models, including Agile, Waterfall, Iterative, or Spiral\n- Experience with open table formats, such as Apache Iceberg\n- Experience with infrastructure-as-code, including Terraform or CloudFormation\n- Knowledge of data lakes and lakehouse architectures and database performance concepts, such as partitioning\n- Knowledge of Zero T rus t and attribute-based access control ( ABAC )  \n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>Rapid advances in IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence mean organizations have access to more data than ever before—both structured and unstructured. Turning that data into actionable insight requires strong engineering, thoughtful design, and scalable platforms.</p><p></p><p>As a senior Data Engineer at Booz Allen, you will design and build data platforms and pipelines that power mission-critical outcomes. You will work on complex, high-impact programs that help clients solve real-world challenges with data.</p><p></p><p>You’ll collaborate with analysts, AI engineers, <span>develop</span>ers, and stakeholders in a fast-paced, agile environment. In this role, you will lead technical efforts across assessment, design, <span>develop</span>ment, and sustainment of scalable data platforms while mentoring teammates and driving best practices.</p><p></p><p><b>What You’ll Work On:</b></p><ul><li>Design, build, and maintain scalable data pipelines and platforms.</li><li><span>Develop</span> secure, efficient Python for data processing, automation, and warehousing.</li><li>Migrate and integrate data from on-premises systems to cloud environments.</li><li>Implement CI<span>/</span>CD pipelines to automate build, test, and deployment workflows.</li><li><span>Develop</span> SQL scripts and stored procedures for data processing and transformation.</li><li>Apply data modeling best practices.</li><li>Support data governance, <span>met</span>adata tagging, and access controls.</li><li>Partner with cross-functional teams to deliver end-to-end data solutions.</li><li>Provide technical guidance in a complex enterprise environment.</li></ul><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> as a data engineer supporting large-scale enterprise systems</li><li><span>Experience</span> writing clean, secure, and efficient Python for data engineering use cases</li><li><span>Experience</span> moving data from on-prem environments to the cloud and automating <span>develop</span>ment workflows, including building, deploying, or managing applications</li><li><span>Experience</span> with CI<span>/</span>CD practices</li><li><span>Experience</span> with SQL, including stored procedures and data modeling</li><li><span>Experience</span> with data governance and data tagging</li><li><span>Knowledge</span> of AWS services, such as S3, IAM, EventBridge, Step Functions, or Lambda</li><li><span>Ability to</span> work independently and manage tasks with minimal supervision</li><li><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></li><li><span>HS diploma or GED</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with Pipeline Builder, AIP, and Foundry&#39;s application <span>develop</span>ment ecosystem</li><li><span>Experience</span> with ETL tools, such as dbt and Airflow</li><li><span>Experience</span> with NoSQL and graph databases, and DevOps tools and automation practices</li><li><span>Experience</span> designing and building data warehouses</li><li><span>Experience</span> working in multiple SDLC models, including Agile, Waterfall, Iterative, or Spiral</li><li><span>Experience</span> with open table formats, such as Apache Iceberg</li><li><span>Experience</span> with infrastructure-as-code, including Terraform or CloudFormation</li><li><span>Knowledge</span> of data lakes and lakehouse architectures and database performance concepts, such as partitioning</li><li><span>Knowledge</span> of Zero T<span>rus</span>t and attribute-based access control <span>(</span>ABAC<span>)</span> </li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> TS/SCI <span>clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Fayetteville-NC/Data-Engineer_R0241674","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Fayetteville-NC/Data-Engineer_R0241674","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"b75e002d1d72a72816ba0ba664c7cc7091dc6c49996bc84dbe1fd0d7d4240a39","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fayetteville-NC/Data-Engineer_R0241674","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fayetteville-NC/Data-Engineer_R0241674","locations":[{"label":"Fayetteville, NC"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0241674","internal_job_id":"cb5b967f859e1000b6001bc3d83b0000","first_published_at":"2026-06-08","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer Job Description:\nWe are seeking a highly skilled Data Engineer to join our support Data team and enable reliable, governed, and high-performing data products on the Army enterprise data platforms. This role plays a cru cia l part in improving decision-making, readiness visibility, and reporting across Army missions by focusing on data ingestion, transformation, cleaning, quality checks, lineage, and production operations of data while maintaining compliance with platform governance and DoD security requirements.\n\nAs the Data Engineer, you will build and operate data pipelines for structured, semi-structured, and unstructured data sources. You'll be cleaning and preparing raw data to ensure accuracy and consistency, followed by applying transformations such as normalization, joins, and incremental loads to create reliable and optimized datasets for downstream analytics and reporting.\n\nThe role also requires implementing robust systems for data-quality checks, lineage capture, and monitoring, while troubleshooting pipeline failures through root-cause analysis. You will create and maintain incident response runbooks and optimize routine operations. The position will also involve analyzing and adhering to governance practices, such as permissions management, encryption protocols, and audit logging, ensuring compliance with DoD policies and standards.\n\nCollaboration will be essential, as you will translate mission requirements into technical solutions, develop design documentation for platform adoption, and partner with stakeholders to uphold data quality and governance standards. Using Army data tools, including Pipeline Builder, Code Repositories, Workshop, Slate, and Machinery, you’ll deliver robust, scalable data products that drive Army readiness and success.\n\nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 2+ years of experience in data engineering or database management\n- Experience in develop ing scalable ETL / ELT workflows for analytics and reporting\n- Experience in Vantage or Foundry components, including Pipeline Builder, Code Repositories, Workshop, Slate, and Machinery\n- Knowledge of Agile engineering practices\n- Ability to implement data-quality controls, lineage tracking, monitoring workflows, and runbook management\n- Secret clearance\n- Bachelor’s degree in a Computer Science, Data Science, or Engineering field\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience operating in DoD environments, such as NIPR, SIPR, or JWICS, and with Army mission data domains and stewardship practices\n- Experience with governance practices, including permissions management, encryption protocols, and compliance documentation\n- Experience in programming languages such as Python, Java, or C++\n- Experience with distributed data tools\n- Experience with cloud platforms\n- Experience with Unix or Linux, including Shell scripting and basic command-line\n- Knowledge of data warehousing tools\n- Knowledge of Agile engineering practices\n- Master’s degree a plus\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<p><b>Job Description:</b></p><p>We are seeking a highly skilled Data Engineer to join our support Data team and enable reliable, governed, and high-performing data products on the Army enterprise data platforms. This role plays a cru<span>cia</span>l part in improving decision-making, readiness visibility, and reporting across Army missions by focusing on data ingestion, transformation, cleaning, quality checks, lineage, and production operations of data while maintaining compliance with platform governance and DoD security requirements.</p><p></p><p>As the Data Engineer, you will build and operate data pipelines for structured, semi-structured, and unstructured data sources. You&#39;ll be cleaning and preparing raw data to ensure accuracy and consistency, followed by applying transformations such as normalization, joins, and incremental loads to create reliable and optimized datasets for downstream analytics and reporting.</p><p></p><p>The role also requires implementing robust systems for data-quality checks, lineage capture, and monitoring, while troubleshooting pipeline failures through root-cause analysis. You will create and maintain incident response runbooks and optimize routine operations. The position will also involve analyzing and adhering to governance practices, such as permissions management, encryption protocols, and audit logging, ensuring compliance with DoD <span>policies</span> and standards.</p><p></p><p>Collaboration will be essential, as you will translate mission requirements into technical solutions, <span>develop</span> design documentation for platform adoption, and partner with stakeholders to uphold data quality and governance standards. Using Army data tools, including Pipeline Builder, Code Repositories, Workshop, Slate, and Machinery, you’ll deliver robust, scalable data products that drive Army readiness and success.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in data engineering or database management</li><li><span>Experience</span> in <span>develop</span>ing scalable ETL<span>/</span>ELT workflows for analytics and reporting</li><li><span>Experience</span> in Vantage or Foundry components, including Pipeline Builder, Code Repositories, Workshop, Slate, and Machinery</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> Agile engineering practices</li><li><span>Ability to</span> implement data-quality controls, lineage tracking, monitoring workflows, and runbook management</li><li><span>Secret clearance</span></li><li><span>Bachelor’s degree</span> in a Computer Science, Data Science, or Engineering field</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> operating in DoD environments, such as NIPR, SIPR, or JWICS, and with Army mission data domains and stewardship practices</li><li><span>Experience</span> with governance practices, including permissions management, encryption protocols, and compliance documentation</li><li><span>Experience</span> in programming languages such as Python, Java, or C&#43;&#43;</li><li><span>Experience</span> with distributed data tools</li><li><span>Experience</span> with cloud platforms</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Unix or Linux, including Shell scripting and basic command-line</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> data warehousing tools</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> Agile engineering practices</li><li><span>Master’s degree</span> a plus</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b><br /><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Fayetteville-NC/Data-Engineer_R0247124","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Fayetteville-NC/Data-Engineer_R0247124","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"6bc5158f00ea5281f5c897bb44d4277df645d5d3bd3c31b0304ed467b12f3aea","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fayetteville-NC/Data-Engineer_R0247124","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fayetteville-NC/Data-Engineer_R0247124","locations":[{"label":"Fayetteville, NC"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247124","internal_job_id":"ae74c1d5954e1000b7fbad99c2b70000","first_published_at":"2026-08-17","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer The Opportunity: \nA well‑architected, fully secured data ecosystem is essential for enabling the Department of War (DoW) to execute its mission with precision, speed, and resilience. As a Database Engineer specializing in Zero Trust, you serve as a critical technical leader ensuring that enterprise and mission‑critical data systems remain secure, scalable, and aligned with evolving operational demands.\n \nIn this role, you apply deep expertise in database architecture, data security, access control, and automation to design, implement, and maintain trusted data environments across complex, multi‑domain infrastructures. You collaborate closely with subject matter experts, mission owners, cybersecurity teams, and platform engineers to translate strategic objectives into robust, Zero Trust‑aligned data solutions that protect sensitive information at every layer.\n \nAs a Zero Trust Database Engineer, you play a pivotal role in the design, integration, and operationalization of secure data architectures that enable mission systems to operate with confidence even under contested or degraded conditions. Your work strengthens the DoW’s ability to defend, detect, and respond across the full spectrum of operations while advancing the department’s long‑term modernization strategy.\n \nThis position places you at the intersection of data engineering, cybersecurity, and mission readiness, offering the opportunity to shape the future of secure data operations while continuously expanding your technical mastery.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- 5+ years of experience in database engineering with a primary focus on security rather than just performance\n\n- Experience with integrating databases with enterprise Identity Providers (IdP) and managing complex RBAC and ABAC models\n\n- Experience with the DoD Zero Trust Strategy\n\n- Experience with TLS 1.3, PKI, HSMs, and transparent data encryption \n\n- Ability to map technical controls to the Data and Visibility pillars\n\n- TS/SCI clearance \n\n- HS diploma or GED\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience with system design, including scalability and reliability\n\n- Experience with database encryption, including field-level encryption\n\n- Experience with securing managed database services such as RDS, Aurora, and Azure SQL using cloud-native security tools\n\n- Experience with HashiCorp Vault, Beyond Trust, or AWS Secrets Manager\n\n- Experience with embedding database security checks directly into CI/CD pipelines\n\nClearance:    \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.  \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p><span><span>A well‑architected, fully secured data ecosystem is essential for enabling the Department of War (DoW) to execute its mission with precision, speed, and resilience. As a Database Engineer specializing in Zero Trust, you serve as a critical technical leader ensuring that enterprise and mission‑critical data systems remain secure, scalable, and aligned with evolving operational demands.</span></span></p><p><span><span> </span></span></p><p><span><span>In this role, you apply deep expertise in database architecture, data security, access control, and automation to design, implement, and maintain trusted data environments across complex, multi‑domain infrastructures. You collaborate closely with subject matter experts, mission owners, cybersecurity teams, and platform engineers to translate strategic objectives into robust, Zero Trust‑aligned data solutions that protect sensitive information at every layer.</span></span></p><p><span><span> </span></span></p><p><span><span>As a Zero Trust Database Engineer, you play a pivotal role in the design, integration, and operationalization of secure data architectures that enable mission systems to operate with confidence even under contested or degraded conditions. Your work strengthens the DoW’s ability to defend, detect, and respond across the full spectrum of operations while advancing the department’s long‑term modernization strategy.</span></span></p><p><span><span> </span></span></p><p><span><span>This position places you at the intersection of data engineering, cybersecurity, and mission readiness, offering the opportunity to shape the future of secure data operations while continuously expanding your technical mastery.</span></span></p><p></p><p><span>Join us. The world can’t wait. </span></p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p><span><span>5&#43; years of experience in database engineering with a primary focus on security rather than just performance</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience with integrating databases with enterprise Identity Providers (IdP) and managing complex RBAC and ABAC models</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience with the DoD Zero Trust Strategy </span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience with TLS 1.3, PKI, HSMs, and transparent data encryption </span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Ability to map technical controls to the Data and Visibility pillars</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>TS/SCI clearance </span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>HS diploma or GED</span></span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p><span><span>Experience with system design, including scalability and reliability</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience with database encryption, including field-level encryption</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience with securing managed database services such as RDS, Aurora, and Azure SQL using cloud-native security tools</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience with HashiCorp Vault, Beyond Trust, or AWS Secrets Manager</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience with embedding database security checks directly into CI/CD pipelines</span></span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b>   </p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.  </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 7 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Fort-Meade-MD/Data-Engineer_R0241771","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Fort-Meade-MD/Data-Engineer_R0241771","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"4c8b7af66ee56e6b8d81ba23652e980801eee0992b55f10ddccdef3ec35443b1","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Meade-MD/Data-Engineer_R0241771","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Meade-MD/Data-Engineer_R0241771","locations":[{"label":"Fort Meade, MD"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0241771","internal_job_id":"8d303c4688181001f5dc2e8dd3320000","first_published_at":"2026-07-01","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer The Opportunity: \nEver-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that   there’s   more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when   it’s   gathered from disparate sources. We need an experienced data professional like you to help our clients find answers in their data to   impact   important missions—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence.   \n\nAs a data engineer at Booz Allen,   you’ll   use your   expertise   to help build advanced technology solutions and lead data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry.   You’ll   guide data engineering activities by overseeing the development and deployment of pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful.  \n\nIn this role,   you’ll   collaborate closely with AI Model Engineers, Network and Cloud Architects, the ISSE, and other technical leaders to guide the development of scalable, mission‑aligned data pipelines.   You’ll   apply your   expertise   in data engineering, exploratory analysis, and feature development to shape how datasets are assessed, designed, transformed, and   maintained   for AI/ML workloads. While supporting a cross‑functional technical environment,   you’ll   help ensure high‑quality, well‑governed data flows that enable reliable model performance across operational, research, and enterprise systems.  \n\nWork with us to use data for good.  \n\nYou Have:\n- 6+ years of experience as a data engineer\n\n- Experience designing, implementing, and   maintaining   scalable data pipelines for structured and unstructured data\n\n- Experience preparing validated, normalized, and secure datasets for AI/ML model development\n\n- Experience implementing data governance practices, including access control, lineage tracking, and dataset documentation\n\n- Experience developing dashboards and metrics for data and pipeline monitoring\n\n- E xperience building automated ETL workflows and CI/CD pipelines for data processes\n\n- Experience   optimizing   data workflows across on‑prem, cloud, or hybrid environments\n\n- Ability to   monitor   and improve pipeline performance in coordination with operations teams\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph  \n\n- HS diploma or GED and 6+ years of experience with data normalization and data pipelines, or Bachelor’s degree and 4+ years of experience with data normalization and data pipelines\n\nNice If You Have:\n- 10+ years of experience as a data engineer\n\n- Experience with distributed data and compute tools, such as Spark, Databricks, Hadoop, Hive, or Kafka\n\n- Experience with cloud environments, such as AWS   or   Azure\n\n- Experience developing real‑time or streaming data applications  \n\n- Experience evaluating emerging technologies for data processing or AI/ML workflows\n\n- Experience working in environments with security, compliance, or ISSE oversight  \n\n- Experience developing or supporting visualization tools and frameworks  \n\n- Experience supporting AI/ML model development pipelines  \n\n- Bachelor’s degree  \n\nClearance:\n\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><div><p><span><span>Ever-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that<span> </span></span><span>there’s</span><span><span> </span>more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when<span> </span></span><span>it’s</span><span><span> </span>gathered from disparate sources. We need an experienced data professional like you to help our clients find answers in their data to<span> </span></span><span>impact</span><span><span> </span>important missions—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence. </span></span><span> </span></p><p></p></div><div><p><span><span>As a data engineer at Booz Allen,<span> </span></span><span>you’ll</span><span><span> </span>use your<span> </span></span><span>expertise</span><span><span> </span>to help build advanced technology solutions and lead data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry.<span> </span></span><span>You’ll</span><span><span> </span>guide data engineering activities by overseeing the development and deployment of pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful.</span></span><span> </span></p><p></p></div><div><p><span><span>In this role,<span> </span></span><span>you’ll</span><span><span> </span>collaborate closely with AI Model Engineers, Network and Cloud Architects, the ISSE, and other technical leaders to guide the development of scalable, mission‑aligned data pipelines.<span> </span></span><span>You’ll</span><span><span> </span>apply your<span> </span></span><span>expertise</span><span><span> </span>in data engineering, exploratory analysis, and feature development to shape how datasets are assessed, designed, transformed, and<span> </span></span><span>maintained</span><span><span> </span>for AI/ML workloads. While supporting a cross‑functional technical environment,<span> </span></span><span>you’ll</span><span><span> </span>help ensure high‑quality, well‑governed data flows that enable reliable model performance across operational, research, and enterprise systems.</span></span><span> </span></p><p></p></div><div><p><span><span>Work with us to use data for good.</span></span><span> </span></p><p></p></div><div><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><div><ul><li><p><span><span>6&#43; years of experience as a data engineer</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience designing, implementing, and<span> </span></span><span>maintaining</span><span><span> </span>scalable data pipelines for structured and unstructured data</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience preparing validated, normalized, and secure datasets for AI/ML model development</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience implementing data governance practices, including access control, lineage tracking, and dataset documentation</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience developing dashboards and metrics for data and pipeline monitoring</span></span></p></li><li><p>E<span><span>xperience building automated ETL workflows and CI/CD pipelines for data processes</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience<span> </span></span><span>optimizing</span><span><span> </span>data workflows across on‑prem, cloud, or hybrid environments</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Ability to<span> </span></span><span>monitor</span><span><span> </span>and improve pipeline performance in coordination with operations teams</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</span></span><span> </span></p></li><li><p><span>HS diploma or GED and 6&#43; years of experience with data normalization and data pipelines, or Bachelor’s degree and 4&#43; years of experience with data normalization and data pipelines</span></p></li></ul></div><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p><span><span>10&#43; years of experience as a data engineer</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience with distributed data and compute tools, such as Spark, Databricks, Hadoop, Hive, or Kafka</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience with cloud environments, such as AWS</span><span><span> </span>or</span><span><span> </span>Azure</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience developing real‑time or streaming data applications</span></span><span> </span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience evaluating emerging technologies for data processing or AI/ML workflows</span></span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience working in environments with security, compliance, or ISSE oversight</span></span><span> </span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience developing or supporting visualization tools and frameworks</span></span><span> </span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Experience supporting AI/ML model development pipelines</span></span><span> </span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Bachelor’s degree </span></span><span> </span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p></div><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Fort-Meade-MD/Data-Engineer_R0244467","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Fort-Meade-MD/Data-Engineer_R0244467","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"371e0237977e430cdf80014b3b34aa2f066ed22d9027ce038065e52a5d0d2f8b","fetched_at":"2026-08-24T14:15:46.938Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Meade-MD/Data-Engineer_R0244467","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Meade-MD/Data-Engineer_R0244467","locations":[{"label":"Fort Meade, MD"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0244467","internal_job_id":"b3c781f6607110015402fd83f3d10000","first_published_at":"2026-07-15","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer The Opportunity: \nEver-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. Given the expansion of big data analytics, new challenges are emerging for the integration of data sets. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an experienced data engineer like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions—from cyber risk identification to acquisition programs to DOW mission decomposition.  \n\nAs a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful. \n\nHere, you’ll work with and guide a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll use your experience in analytical exploration and data examination while you manage the assessment, design, building, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients. \n\nWork with us to use data for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- 4+ years of experience with Python, PySpark, SQL, and Databricks\n\n- 2+ years of experience with data engineering and analytics, delivering actionable insights and performance metrics\n\n- 2+ years of experience working within the Maven Smart System (MSS), developing or supporting mission-focused data workflows, applications, and analytic capabilities\n\n- Experience integrating, transforming, and validating data from multiple structured and semi-structured sources using APIs, SQL, and modern data engineering practices\n\n- Experience developing scalable data pipelines, data models, and data products that support operational planning, analytics, and executive decision-making\n\n- Experience working with large, complex datasets while ensuring data quality, performance, and reliability\n\n- Ability to communicate complex technical concepts clearly and effectively to technical teams, operators and executive stakeholders\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience using DoD data platforms such as Advana and Qlik for data integration, ingestion, and visualization\n\n- Experience with the Defense Acquisition Visibility Environment (DAVE)\n\n- Experience documenting data analytics processes and maintaining reproducible analytic methods\n\n- Experience engaging data owners to establish sharing agreements that enable the establishment of data pipelines\n\n- Experience applying machine learning or natural language processing to operational or intelligence data\n\n- Experience with DoD and Intelligence Community data ecosystems and collaboration with interagency partners\n\n- Experience developing data governance frameworks and standards\n\n- Knowledge of cybersecurity data and analytics\n\nClearance:    \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>Ever-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. Given the expansion of big data analytics, new challenges are emerging for the integration of data sets. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an experienced data engineer like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions—from cyber risk identification to acquisition programs to DOW mission decomposition.  </p><p></p><p>As a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful. </p><p></p><p>Here, you’ll work with and guide a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll use your experience in analytical exploration and data examination while you manage the assessment, design, building, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients. </p><p></p><p>Work with us to use data for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>4&#43; years of experience with Python, PySpark, SQL, and Databricks</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with data engineering and analytics, delivering actionable insights and performance metrics</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience working within the Maven Smart System (MSS), developing or supporting mission-focused data workflows, applications, and analytic capabilities</p></li><li><p>Experience integrating, transforming, and validating data from multiple structured and semi-structured sources using APIs, SQL, and modern data engineering practices</p></li><li><p>Experience developing scalable data pipelines, data models, and data products that support operational planning, analytics, and executive decision-making</p></li><li><p>Experience working with large, complex datasets while ensuring data quality, performance, and reliability</p></li><li><p>Ability to communicate complex technical concepts clearly and effectively to technical teams, operators and executive stakeholders</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience using DoD data platforms such as Advana and Qlik for data integration, ingestion, and visualization</p></li><li><p>Experience with the Defense Acquisition Visibility Environment (DAVE)</p></li><li><p>Experience documenting data analytics processes and maintaining reproducible analytic methods</p></li><li><p>Experience engaging data owners to establish sharing agreements that enable the establishment of data pipelines</p></li><li><p>Experience applying machine learning or natural language processing to operational or intelligence data</p></li><li><p>Experience with DoD and Intelligence Community data ecosystems and collaboration with interagency partners</p></li><li><p>Experience developing data governance frameworks and standards</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of cybersecurity data and analytics</p><p></p></li></ul><p><b>Clearance:</b>   </p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"possibly_closed","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-24T14:15:46.938Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","missing_complete_scans":1,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Honolulu-HI/Data-Engineer_R0240103","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Honolulu-HI/Data-Engineer_R0240103","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"8adea794a8a9e64cb48750868a252c9d5ba2f0c87ea0b1953a58ccc5be41a557","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Honolulu-HI/Data-Engineer_R0240103","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Honolulu-HI/Data-Engineer_R0240103","locations":[{"label":"Honolulu, HI"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0240103","internal_job_id":"5762f2ff5b9c1001a898d17975c20000","first_published_at":"2026-08-24","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer The Opportunity: \nEver-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an experienced data professional like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions, from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence. \n\nAs a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your expertise to help build advanced technology solutions and lead data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll guide data engineering activities by overseeing the development and deployment of pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful.\n\nHere, you’ll mentor a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll use your expertise in analytical exploration and data examination while you oversee the assessment, design, building, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients.\n\nWork with us to use data for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- 10+ years of experience architecting and delivering AI enabled mission or enterprise systems, including data integration, secure compute environments, and operator facing applications in restricted or classified settings \n\n- 10+ years of experience designing and deploying data pipelines, ontologies, and application workflows on platforms such as Palantir Foundry or Gotham, including air gapped, degraded connectivity, or multiclassification environments \n\n- 10+ years of experience developing secure analytics ecosystems, including log pipelines, monitoring frameworks, operational dashboards, or intelligence fusion platforms in greenfield or legacy modernization efforts \n\n- 10+ years of experience implementing DevSecOps practices, including containerization, orchestration, CI/CD, and automated testing within constrained or limited toolchain environments \n\n- 10+ years of experience integrating AI/ML capabilities into production workflows or operator tooling, such as LLM enabled assistants, model augmented decision aids, or automation solutions \n\n- 10+ years of experience making architectural tradeoffs under constrained mission conditions, including limited infrastructure, fragmented networks, evolving requirements, or high-pressure operational timelines \n\n- Experience rapidly learning unfamiliar technologies, developing hands on proficiency, and guiding engineering teams through full lifecycle implementation \n\n- Experience communicating architectural decisions and solution impacts to engineering teams, government clients, and senior nontechnical stakeholders \n\n- Secret clearance \n\n- Bachelor’s degree \n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience supporting multi cloud, multi enclave, or multiclassification architectures, including environments spanning NIPR, SIPR, JWICS, or coalition networks \n\n- Experience contributing to major defense programs or largescale systems integration efforts, including navigating acquisition, compliance, or bureaucratic constraints \n\n- Experience supporting DoD installations, operational units, or C2 systems in environments with incomplete documentation, degraded systems, or inconsistent technical baselines \n\n- Experience developing agentic workflows, automation pipelines, or custom tooling that improved engineering velocity or reduced operator burden \n\n- Experience serving as a senior technical lead or architect responsible for end-to-end solution delivery \n\n- Experience working on tiger teams, flyaway teams, or rapid response engineering missions requiring accelerated delivery under complex conditions \n\n- Top Secret clearance\n\n- Architecture frameworks Certifications such as AWS, Palantir Foundry or Gotham, or Kubernetes Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>Ever-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an experienced data professional like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions, from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence. </p><p></p><p>As a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your expertise to help build advanced technology solutions and lead data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll guide data engineering activities by overseeing the development and deployment of pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful.</p><p></p><p>Here, you’ll mentor a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll use your expertise in analytical exploration and data examination while you oversee the assessment, design, building, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients.</p><p></p><p>Work with us to use data for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>10&#43; years of experience architecting and delivering AI enabled mission or enterprise systems, including data integration, secure compute environments, and operator facing applications in restricted or classified settings </p></li><li><p>10&#43; years of experience designing and deploying data pipelines, ontologies, and application workflows on platforms such as Palantir Foundry or Gotham, including air gapped, degraded connectivity, or multiclassification environments </p></li><li><p>10&#43; years of experience developing secure analytics ecosystems, including log pipelines, monitoring frameworks, operational dashboards, or intelligence fusion platforms in greenfield or legacy modernization efforts </p></li><li><p>10&#43; years of experience implementing DevSecOps practices, including containerization, orchestration, CI/CD, and automated testing within constrained or limited toolchain environments </p></li><li><p>10&#43; years of experience integrating AI/ML capabilities into production workflows or operator tooling, such as LLM enabled assistants, model augmented decision aids, or automation solutions </p></li><li><p>10&#43; years of experience making architectural tradeoffs under constrained mission conditions, including limited infrastructure, fragmented networks, evolving requirements, or high-pressure operational timelines </p></li><li><p>Experience rapidly learning unfamiliar technologies, developing hands on proficiency, and guiding engineering teams through full lifecycle implementation </p></li><li><p>Experience communicating architectural decisions and solution impacts to engineering teams, government clients, and senior nontechnical stakeholders </p></li><li><p>Secret clearance </p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience supporting multi cloud, multi enclave, or multiclassification architectures, including environments spanning NIPR, SIPR, JWICS, or coalition networks </p></li><li><p>Experience contributing to major defense programs or largescale systems integration efforts, including navigating acquisition, compliance, or bureaucratic constraints </p></li><li><p>Experience supporting DoD installations, operational units, or C2 systems in environments with incomplete documentation, degraded systems, or inconsistent technical baselines </p></li><li><p>Experience developing agentic workflows, automation pipelines, or custom tooling that improved engineering velocity or reduced operator burden </p></li><li><p>Experience serving as a senior technical lead or architect responsible for end-to-end solution delivery </p></li><li><p>Experience working on tiger teams, flyaway teams, or rapid response engineering missions requiring accelerated delivery under complex conditions </p></li><li><p>Top Secret clearance</p></li><li><p>Architecture frameworks Certifications such as AWS, Palantir Foundry or Gotham, or Kubernetes Certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted Today"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
