d data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll use your experience in analytical exploration and data examination while you manage the assessment, design, building, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients.  \n\nWork with us to use big data for good. \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- Experience with SQL, Java, or Python and Spark\n\n- Experience in working with highly structured data\n\n- Ability to manipulate data across different tables\n\n- Knowledge of different data types and the different sources of data\n\n- Knowledge of modeling and how to make that data usable for meeting mission requirements\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience with advanced data modeling, including entity resolution\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer, Mid<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>Ever-expanding te<span>chn</span>ology like IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing big data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an experienced data engineer like you to help our clients find answers in their big data to impact important missions—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence.   </p><p></p><p>As a big data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful.  </p><p></p><p>Here, you’ll work with and guide a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll use your experience in analytical exploration and data examination while you manage the assessment, design, building, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients.  </p><p></p><p>Work with us to use big data for good. </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:   </span></b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with SQL, Java, or Python and Spark</p></li><li><p>Experience in working with highly structured data</p></li><li><p>Ability to manipulate data across different tables</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of different data types and the different sources of data</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of modeling and how to make that data usable for meeting mission requirements</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:   </span></b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with advanced data modeling, including entity resolution</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Tampa-FL/Data-Engineer--Mid_R0245461","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Tampa-FL/Data-Engineer--Mid_R0245461","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"c2a3ac0125a81968374a2ae0c41addf00300e780d0ccc365c6ffe080d3d05b59","fetched_at":"2026-08-24T14:15:46.938Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer, Mid","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Tampa-FL/Data-Engineer--Mid_R0245461","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Tampa-FL/Data-Engineer--Mid_R0245461","locations":[{"label":"Tampa, FL"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245461","internal_job_id":"fe4132e52a9210010a6f0e99e5a00000","first_published_at":"2026-08-18","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer, Mid The Opportunity: \nEver-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need a data professional like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence. \n\nAs an experienced engineer, you know that machine learning is critical to understanding and processing massive datasets. Your ability to conduct mathematical, statistical, and business process analyses using ML techniques makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused solution. As a machine learning engineer on our data team, you’ll train, test, deploy, and maintain models that organize, clean, and learn from data.\n\nIn this role, you’ll own and define the direction of mission-critical solutions by applying best-fit digital and ML algorithms and technologies. You’ll be part of a talented team of AI, ML, and data engineers across the company and collaborate with other developers to deliver world class solutions to senior military officials. Your skills and extensive technical expertise will guide customers as they navigate complex geopolitical landscapes, operations, and missions.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:   \n- 2+ years of experience in a professional work environment working with interdisciplinary teams\n\n- 2+ years of experience with designing, developing, operationalizing, and maintaining complex data applications at enterprise scale\n\n- 2+ years of experience with designing, developing, operationalizing, and maintaining complex relational databases at enterprise scale\n\n- Experience creating software for retrieving, parsing, and processing structured and unstructured data\n\n- Experience coding in either Python, R, or R Studio, and SQL\n\n- Experience building scalable ETL and ELT workflows including scripting and translating between multiple file formats\n\n- Experience with public clouds such as AWS, Microsoft Azure, or Google Cloud\n\n- Ability to develop scripts and programs for converting various types of data into usable formats and support project team to scale, monitor, and operate data platforms\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience at a Combatant Command\n\n- Experience with distributed data scripting, and computing tools including Databricks, Spark, AWS EMR, Kafka, Bash and Scala\n\n- Experience with NoSQL implementation, including MongoDB\n\n- Experience with data warehousing using AWS Redshift, MySQL, PostgreSQL, or Snowflake\n\n- Experience with Java and .NET\n\n- Experience with working on real-time data and streaming applications\n\n- Experience with Agile engineering practices\n\n- Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills\n\n- Possession of excellent organization and time management skills to handle multiple tasks simultaneously\n\n- Master's degree\n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer, Mid<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>Ever-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need a data professional like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence. </p><p></p><p>As an experienced engineer, you know that machine learning is critical to understanding and processing massive datasets. Your ability to conduct mathematical, statistical, and business process analyses using ML techniques makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused solution. As a machine learning engineer on our data team, you’ll train, test, deploy, and maintain models that organize, clean, and learn from data.</p><p></p><p>In this role, you’ll own and define the direction of mission-critical solutions by applying best-fit digital and ML algorithms and technologies. You’ll be part of a talented team of AI, ML, and data engineers across the company and collaborate with other developers to deliver world class solutions to senior military officials. Your skills and extensive technical expertise will guide customers as they navigate complex geopolitical landscapes, operations, and missions.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of experience in a professional work environment working with interdisciplinary teams</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with designing, developing, operationalizing, and maintaining complex data applications at enterprise scale</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with designing, developing, operationalizing, and maintaining complex relational databases at enterprise scale</p></li><li><p>Experience creating software for retrieving, parsing, and processing structured and unstructured data</p></li><li><p>Experience coding in either Python, R, or R Studio, and SQL</p></li><li><p>Experience building scalable ETL and ELT workflows including scripting and translating between multiple file formats</p></li><li><p>Experience with public clouds such as AWS, Microsoft Azure, or Google Cloud</p></li><li><p>Ability to develop scripts and programs for converting various types of data into usable formats and support project team to scale, monitor, and operate data platforms</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience at a Combatant Command</p></li><li><p>Experience with distributed data scripting, and computing tools including Databricks, Spark, AWS EMR, Kafka, Bash and Scala</p></li><li><p>Experience with NoSQL implementation, including MongoDB</p></li><li><p>Experience with data warehousing using AWS Redshift, MySQL, PostgreSQL, or Snowflake</p></li><li><p>Experience with Java and .NET</p></li><li><p>Experience with working on real-time data and streaming applications</p></li><li><p>Experience with Agile engineering practices</p></li><li><p>Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills</p></li><li><p>Possession of excellent organization and time management skills to handle multiple tasks simultaneously</p></li><li><p>Master&#39;s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b> </p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 6 Days Ago"},"status":"possibly_closed","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-24T14:15:46.938Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","missing_complete_scans":1,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Washington-DC/Data-Engineer--Mid_R0247241","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Washington-DC/Data-Engineer--Mid_R0247241","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"2802e8ed32c757e665b0cee55feca4606e088c5ac0b170620f7e672f901f31d4","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Engineer, Mid","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/Data-Engineer--Mid_R0247241","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/Data-Engineer--Mid_R0247241","locations":[{"label":"Washington, DC"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247241","internal_job_id":"26f0e5a9193a100109fabb61ff500000","first_published_at":"2026-08-18","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Engineer, Mid The Opportunity:\nEver-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an experienced data engineer like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence.\n\nAs a Data Engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful. \n\nHere, you’ll work with and guide a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll use your experience in analytical exploration and data examination while you manage the assessment, design, building, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients. \n\nWork with us to use data for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:   \n- 2+ years of experience with major data science languages such as Python and R\n\n- 2+ years of experience retrieving, merging, and analyzing structured and unstructured data sources from APIs and databases through Python, R, or SQL\n\n- Experience with Large Language Models (LLMs) and Generative AI (GenAI)\n\n- Experience preparing data for use with AI or GenAI models\n\n- Experience with data analytics, data mining, statistical analysis, or AI and ML\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- Bachelor’s degree and 3+ years of experience in data engineering, or 7+ years of experience in data engineering in lieu of a degree\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience streamlining existing workflows by integrating LLMs and GenAI\n\n- Experience conducting data architecture and ETL for the DoD or a federal agency\n\n- Experience evaluating AI and ML model performance\n\n- Experience with intelligence analysis\n\nClearance:   \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required. \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Engineer, Mid<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p>Ever-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need an experienced data engineer like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence.</p><p></p><p>As a Data Engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll deploy and develop pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful. </p><p></p><p>Here, you’ll work with and guide a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll use your experience in analytical exploration and data examination while you manage the assessment, design, building, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients. </p><p></p><p>Work with us to use data for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with major data science languages such as Python and R</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience retrieving, merging, and analyzing structured and unstructured data sources from APIs and databases through Python, R, or SQL</p></li><li><p>Experience with Large Language Models (LLMs) and Generative AI (GenAI)</p></li><li><p>Experience preparing data for use with AI or GenAI models</p></li><li><p>Experience with data analytics, data mining, statistical analysis, or AI and ML</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree and 3&#43; years of experience in data engineering, or 7&#43; years of experience in data engineering in lieu of a degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience streamlining existing workflows by integrating LLMs and GenAI</p></li><li><p>Experience conducting data architecture and ETL for the DoD or a federal agency</p></li><li><p>Experience evaluating AI and ML model performance</p></li><li><p>Experience with intelligence analysis</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b>  </p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 6 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"class