{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Alexandria-VA/Data-Scientist_R0241357","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Alexandria-VA/Data-Scientist_R0241357","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"7465c316be0e1448ea262ab58b8500202f5350e8440d1814c6102361cf4c2037","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Alexandria-VA/Data-Scientist_R0241357","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Alexandria-VA/Data-Scientist_R0241357","locations":[{"label":"Alexandria, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0241357","internal_job_id":"cb5b967f859e1000c961120e07d70000","first_published_at":"2026-06-08","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist The Opportunity:  \nAs a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data. \n\nOn our team, you’ll use your analytical skills and data science knowledge to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle.\n\nYou'll be responsible for developing data products by sourcing data from authoritative sources, developing visual narratives of the data, and briefing data products to senior leaders at the DoW. You will work with a cross-discipline team to provide critical analytics to enable successful execution of IT portfolio management.\n\nWork with us as we use data science for good.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:   \n- 5+ years of experience with data science or analytics\n\n- Experience with the DoW\n\n- Experience with Databricks, Tableau, SQL, Python, or Qlik\n\n- Experience working within the WDP, including designing and maintaining dashboards, developing metrics, and ingesting, cleaning, transforming and loading data into WDP\n\n- Experience presenting data products to DoW senior leadership\n\n- Secret clearance   \n\n- Bachelor’s degree \n\nNice If You Have:   \n- 2+ years of experience with Machine Learning, AI or NLP\n\n- Experience with GitLab\n\n- Ability to translate complex data analytics methodologies to non-technical audiences\n\n- Ability to pay strict attention to detail\n\n- Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills\n\n- Possession of excellent organization skills\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b>The Opportunity: </b> </p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data. </p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your analytical skills and data science knowledge to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle.</p><p></p><p>You&#39;ll be responsible for developing data products by sourcing data from authoritative sources, developing visual narratives of the data, and briefing data products to senior leaders at the DoW. You will work with a cross-discipline team to provide critical analytics to enable successful execution of IT portfolio management.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we use data science for good.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of experience with data science or analytics</p></li><li><p>Experience with the DoW</p></li><li><p>Experience with Databricks, Tableau, SQL, Python, or Qlik</p></li><li><p>Experience working within the WDP, including designing and maintaining dashboards, developing metrics, and ingesting, cleaning, transforming and loading data into WDP</p></li><li><p>Experience presenting data products to DoW senior leadership</p></li><li><p>Secret clearance   </p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with Machine Learning, AI or NLP</p></li><li><p>Experience with GitLab</p></li><li><p>Ability to translate complex data analytics methodologies to non-technical audiences</p></li><li><p>Ability to pay strict attention to detail</p></li><li><p>Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills</p></li><li><p>Possession of excellent organization skills</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Alexandria-VA/Data-Scientist_R0241418","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Alexandria-VA/Data-Scientist_R0241418","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"acaae4076e249459215ea940498a8fc2620f1297de23a14299394c8f21ecfa3b","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Alexandria-VA/Data-Scientist_R0241418","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Alexandria-VA/Data-Scientist_R0241418","locations":[{"label":"Alexandria, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0241418","internal_job_id":"768377881ab310010bec7d5934050000","first_published_at":"2026-06-02","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist The Opportunity:  \nAs a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data. \n\nOn our team, you’ll use your leadership skills and data science expertise to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll guide teammates and lead the development of algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to advise your clients as they make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  \n\nWork with us as we use data science for good.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:   \n- 3+ years of experience with using programming languages to manipulate and analyze data, including Python, R, and SQL \n\n- Experience with deploying and maintaining user-facing or user-accessible models \n\n- Experience with data cleansing, data analytics, inferential statistics, programming, data visualization, and system integration to provide data solutions \n\n- Experience with developing data visualizations, dashboards, or lightweight web applications to communicate key insights \n\n- Knowledge of research design principles \n\n- Knowledge of analytic methods and methodological tools used in applied mathematics, computer programming, or data visualization    \n\n- Ability to apply supervised and unsupervised machine learning algorithms on structured and unstructured datasets \n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph  \n\n- Bachelor’s degree \n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience with project management, project planning, and technical documentation \n\n- Knowledge of psychometric theory and assessment validation methodologies such as Item Response Theory and Factor Analysis \n\n- Knowledge of data strategy and data governance \n\n- Ability to advise clients on the acquisition of data, data management, and data infrastructure \n\n- Ability to execute projects and tasks with minimal guidance and supervision  \n\nClearance:    \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b>The Opportunity:  </b></p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data. </p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your leadership skills and data science expertise to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll guide teammates and lead the development of algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to advise your clients as they make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  </p><p></p><p>Work with us as we use data science for good.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of experience with using programming languages to manipulate and analyze data, including Python, R, and SQL </p></li><li><p>Experience with deploying and maintaining user-facing or user-accessible models </p></li><li><p>Experience with data cleansing, data analytics, inferential statistics, programming, data visualization, and system integration to provide data solutions </p></li><li><p>Experience with developing data visualizations, dashboards, or lightweight web applications to communicate key insights </p></li><li><p>Knowledge of research design principles </p></li><li><p>Knowledge of analytic methods and methodological tools used in applied mathematics, computer programming, or data visualization    </p></li><li><p>Ability to apply supervised and unsupervised machine learning algorithms on structured and unstructured datasets </p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph  </p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with project management, project planning, and technical documentation </p></li><li><p>Knowledge of psychometric theory and assessment validation methodologies such as Item Response Theory and Factor Analysis </p></li><li><p>Knowledge of data strategy and data governance </p></li><li><p>Ability to advise clients on the acquisition of data, data management, and data infrastructure </p></li><li><p>Ability to execute projects and tasks with minimal guidance and supervision  </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b>   </p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Alexandria-VA/Data-Scientist_R0241573","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Alexandria-VA/Data-Scientist_R0241573","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"47d905fc4e32c9ec1279a94101d7a66080bb25fa27c9db8d13e14f4fc381d270","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Alexandria-VA/Data-Scientist_R0241573","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Alexandria-VA/Data-Scientist_R0241573","locations":[{"label":"Alexandria, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0241573","internal_job_id":"7db64e3672d41001b49e794bba180000","first_published_at":"2026-06-04","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist The Opportunity: \nIn this role, you will apply data science techniques and met hods and leverage a suite of data-driven tools to aid the client’s service leadership and subject matter experts to increase decision space, understand strategic risk, and develop courses of action. Employ expert judgment, adaptable met hodologies, repeatable analytic processes, and enterprise-wide collaboration to provide routine, spe cia l interest, and alert-triggered campaign assessments, and when necessary, facilitate and synchronize enterprise-level campaign adjustment. You will help DoD senior leadership mobilize for long-term campaigning, marshal DoD resources and actions against desired strategic outcomes, and maneuver the department with greater precision and effect to persistently pursue opportunity and mitigate risk vis-a-vis the pacing rival. Analysts are tasked with utilizing a flexible and foundational toolset that will add value across campaigning topics. Analysts will blend functional area knowledge with an ability to identify data sources, manipulate data, use data analytics tools, understand and anticipate strategic intent, and communicate with senior DoD leaders.\n\nAs a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi cia l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges across private and public sectors from fraud detection to cancer research, to national intelligence, we need a seasoned data scientist like you to help find the answers in the data.\n\nOn our team, you’ll use your leadership skills and data science expertise to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs in order to then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll guide and mentor your team as you oversee the develop ment of algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to advise your clients as they make informed decisions. As a technical leader, you’ll identify new opportunities to use data science solutions to help your clients meet their toughest challenges. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.\n\nWhat You'll Work On:  \n- Design and execute statistical analyses on large, complex datasets from multiple sources. \n\n- Develop production-quality data visualizations, plots, and dashboards for technical and executive audiences. \n\n- Lead data science projects from scoping through delivery, ensuring analytical rigor and alignment with mission objectives. \n\n- Collaborate with stakeholders to translate strategic questions into analytical approaches and deliver actionable insights. \n\n- Respond to ad-hoc analytical requests while managing competing priorities and deadlines in an agile workflow. \n\n- Mentor junior data scientists and establish best practices for reproducible, well-documented analyses. \n\n- Communicate complex statistical findings to both technical teams and senior DoD leadership. \n\nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n\nYou Have:  \n- 6+ years of experience with data science, statistical analysis, or quantitative research\n\n- 6+ years of experience with the develop ment of algorithms, leveraging R or Python in data analysis libraries, including pandas, NumPy, scikit-learn, or Tidyverse\n\n- 6+ years of experience analyzing structured and unstructured data sources\n\n- Experience with statistics, including hypothesis testing, regression analysis, experimental design, and uncertainty quantification\n\n- Experience with data management in SQL, including managing large-scale data across multiple databases and data warehouses\n\n- Experience working with large-scale datasets and distributed computing frameworks, including Spark or DASK\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience with Natural Language Processing ( NLP ) techniques, such as text classification or entity recognition \n\n- Experience with geospatial data analysis\n\n- Experience with Databricks for data science workflows, including building and scaling analytical pipelines, collaborating in notebooks, and integrating with Spark for large-scale data processing \n\n- Experience with data engineering principles, including ETL design, orchestration, and data pipeline architecture, to effectively partner with engineering teams \n\n- Experience working with the U.S. Department of Defense or the Intelligence Community \n\n- Experience with graph analytics, network analysis, or anomaly detection techniques \n\n- Experience with version control, such as Git, and reproducible research practices \n\n- Knowledge of machine learning model develop ment and deployment practices \n\n- Possession of excellent written and verbal communication skills\n\n- Master's degree in Statistics, Computer Science, Data Science, or Economics\n\nClearance: \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>In this role, you will apply data science techniques and <span>met</span>hods and leverage a suite of data-driven tools to aid the client’s service leadership and subject matter experts to increase decision space, understand strategic risk, and <span>develop</span> courses of action. Employ expert judgment, adaptable <span>met</span>hodologies, repeatable analytic processes, and enterprise-wide collaboration to provide routine, spe<span>cia</span>l interest, and alert-triggered campaign assessments, and when necessary, facilitate and synchronize enterprise-level campaign adjustment. You will help DoD senior leadership mobilize for long-term campaigning, marshal DoD resources and actions against <span>desired</span> strategic outcomes, and maneuver the department with greater precision and effect to persistently pursue opportunity and mitigate risk vis-a-vis the pacing rival. Analysts are tasked with utilizing a flexible and foundational toolset that will add value across campaigning topics. Analysts will blend functional area knowledge with an <span>ability to</span> identify data sources, manipulate data, use data analytics tools, understand and anticipate strategic intent, and communicate with senior DoD leaders.</p><p></p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges across private and public sectors from fraud detection to cancer research, to national intelligence, we need a seasoned data scientist like you to help find the answers in the data.</p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your leadership <span>skills</span> and data science expertise to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs in order to then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll guide and mentor your team as you oversee the <span>develop</span>ment of algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to advise your clients as they make informed decisions. As a technical leader, you’ll identify new opportunities to use data science solutions to help your clients meet their toughest challenges. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.</p><p></p><p><b>What You&#39;ll Work On:</b> </p><ul><li><p>Design and execute statistical analyses on large, complex datasets from multiple sources. </p></li><li><p><span>Develop</span> production-quality data visualizations, plots, and dashboards for technical and executive audiences. </p></li><li><p>Lead data science projects from scoping through delivery, ensuring analytical rigor and alignment with mission objectives. </p></li><li><p>Collaborate with stakeholders to translate strategic questions into analytical approaches and deliver actionable insights. </p></li><li><p>Respond to ad-hoc analytical requests while managing competing priorities and deadlines in an agile workflow. </p></li><li><p>Mentor junior data scientists and establish best practices for reproducible, well-documented analyses. </p></li><li><p>Communicate complex statistical findings to both technical teams and senior DoD leadership. </p></li></ul><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.</p><p><br /><b><span>You Have:  </span></b></p><ul><li><p>6&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with data science, statistical analysis, or quantitative research</p></li><li><p>6&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with the <span>develop</span>ment of algorithms, leveraging R or Python in data analysis libraries, including pandas, NumPy, scikit-learn, or Tidyverse</p></li><li><p>6&#43; years of <span>experience</span> analyzing structured and unstructured data sources</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with statistics, including hypothesis testing, regression analysis, experimental design, and uncertainty quantification</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with data management in SQL, including managing large-scale data across multiple databases and data warehouses</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> working with large-scale datasets and distributed computing frameworks, including Spark or DASK</p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span></p></li></ul><p><br /><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span>  </b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Natural Language Processing <span>(</span>NLP<span>)</span> techniques, such as text classification or entity recognition </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with geospatial data analysis</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Databricks for data science workflows, including building and scaling analytical pipelines, collaborating in notebooks, and integrating with Spark for large-scale data processing </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with data engineering principles, including ETL design, orchestration, and data pipeline architecture, to effectively partner with engineering teams </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> working with the U.S. Department of Defense or the Intelligence Community </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with graph analytics, network analysis, or anomaly detection techniques </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with version control, such as Git, and reproducible research practices </p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> machine learning model <span>develop</span>ment and deployment practices </p></li><li><p><span>Possession of</span> excellent written and verbal communication <span>skills</span></p></li><li><p><span>Master&#39;s degree</span> in Statistics, Computer Science, Data Science, or Economics</p></li></ul><p><br /><b><span>Clearance: </span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Alexandria-VA/Data-Scientist_R0242719","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Alexandria-VA/Data-Scientist_R0242719","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"45ff81077b44b7092b5fee3906f19b3b34f0f4c63295c58fd9dd740e529e93d8","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Alexandria-VA/Data-Scientist_R0242719","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Alexandria-VA/Data-Scientist_R0242719","locations":[{"label":"Alexandria, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0242719","internal_job_id":"691a3fab28b11000c8ebc80171d80000","first_published_at":"2026-06-22","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist The Opportunity:  \nAs a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors, from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence, we need you to help find the answers in the data. \n\nOn our team, you’ll use your analytical skills and data science knowledge to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You'll be responsible for developing data products by sourcing data from authoritative sources, developing visual narratives of the data, and briefing data products to senior leaders at the DoW. You will work with a cross-discipline team to provide critical analytics to enable successful execution of IT portfolio management.\n\nWork with us as we use data science for good.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:   \n- 5+ years of experience with data science or analytics\n\n- Experience with the DoW\n\n- Experience with Databricks, Tableau, SQL, Python, or Qlik\n\n- Experience working within the WDP, including designing and maintaining dashboards, developing metrics, and ingesting, cleaning, transforming and loading data into WDP\n\n- Experience presenting data products to DoW senior leadership\n\n- Secret clearance   \n\n- Bachelor’s degree \n\nNice If You Have:   \n- 2+ years of experience with Machine Learning, AI, or NLP\n\n- Experience with GitLab\n\n- Ability to translate complex data analytics methodologies to non-technical audiences\n\n- Ability to pay strict attention to detail\n\n- Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills\n\n- Possession of excellent organization skills\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b>The Opportunity: </b> </p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors, from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence, we need you to help find the answers in the data. </p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your analytical skills and data science knowledge to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You&#39;ll be responsible for developing data products by sourcing data from authoritative sources, developing visual narratives of the data, and briefing data products to senior leaders at the DoW. You will work with a cross-discipline team to provide critical analytics to enable successful execution of IT portfolio management.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we use data science for good.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of experience with data science or analytics</p></li><li><p>Experience with the DoW</p></li><li><p>Experience with Databricks, Tableau, SQL, Python, or Qlik</p></li><li><p>Experience working within the WDP, including designing and maintaining dashboards, developing metrics, and ingesting, cleaning, transforming and loading data into WDP</p></li><li><p>Experience presenting data products to DoW senior leadership</p></li><li><p>Secret clearance   </p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with Machine Learning, AI, or NLP</p></li><li><p>Experience with GitLab</p></li><li><p>Ability to translate complex data analytics methodologies to non-technical audiences</p></li><li><p>Ability to pay strict attention to detail</p></li><li><p>Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills</p></li><li><p>Possession of excellent organization skills</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Alexandria-VA/Data-Scientist_R0247486","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Alexandria-VA/Data-Scientist_R0247486","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"9af432e0b365bad3920844d80306f9c237ffff2024d04f5a9ea9124b5207a7e0","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Alexandria-VA/Data-Scientist_R0247486","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Alexandria-VA/Data-Scientist_R0247486","locations":[{"label":"Alexandria, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247486","internal_job_id":"ae74c1d5954e1001aab4881e25980000","first_published_at":"2026-08-20","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist The Opportunity: \nIn this role, you will apply data science techniques and met hods and leverage a suite of data-driven tools to aid the client’s service leadership and subject matter experts to increase decision space, understand strategic risk, and develop courses of action. Employ expert judgment, adaptable met hodologies, repeatable analytic processes, and enterprise-wide collaboration to provide routine, spe cia l interest, and alert-triggered campaign assessments, and when necessary, facilitate and synchronize enterprise-level campaign adjustment. You will help DoD senior leadership mobilize for long-term campaigning, marshal DoD resources and actions against desired strategic outcomes, and maneuver the department with greater precision and effect to persistently pursue opportunity and mitigate risk vis-a-vis the pacing rival. Analysts are tasked with utilizing a flexible and foundational toolset that will add value across campaigning topics. Analysts will blend functional area knowledge with an ability to identify data sources, manipulate data, use data analytics tools, understand and anticipate strategic intent, and communicate with senior DoD leaders.\n\nAs a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi cia l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges across private and public sectors from fraud detection to cancer research, to national intelligence, we need a seasoned data scientist like you to help find the answers in the data.\n\nOn our team, you’ll use your leadership skills and data science expertise to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs in order to then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll guide and mentor your team as you oversee the develop ment of algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to advise your clients as they make informed decisions. As a technical leader, you’ll identify new opportunities to use data science solutions to help your clients meet their toughest challenges. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.\n\nWhat You'll Work On:  \n- Design and execute statistical analyses on large, complex datasets from multiple sources. \n\n- Develop production-quality data visualizations, plots, and dashboards for technical and executive audiences. \n\n- Lead data science projects from scoping through delivery, ensuring analytical rigor and alignment with mission objectives. \n\n- Collaborate with stakeholders to translate strategic questions into analytical approaches and deliver actionable insights. \n\n- Respond to ad-hoc analytical requests while managing competing priorities and deadlines in an agile workflow. \n\n- Mentor junior data scientists and establish best practices for reproducible, well-documented analyses. \n\n- Communicate complex statistical findings to both technical teams and senior DoD leadership. \n\nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n\nYou Have:  \n- 6+ years of experience with data science, statistical analysis, or quantitative research\n\n- 6+ years of experience with the develop ment of algorithms, leveraging R or Python in data analysis libraries, including pandas, NumPy, scikit-learn, or Tidyverse\n\n- 6+ years of experience analyzing structured and unstructured data sources\n\n- Experience with statistics, including hypothesis testing, regression analysis, experimental design, and uncertainty quantification\n\n- Experience with data management in SQL, including managing large-scale data across multiple databases and data warehouses\n\n- Experience working with large-scale datasets and distributed computing frameworks, including Spark or DASK\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience with Natural Language Processing ( NLP ) techniques, such as text classification or entity recognition \n\n- Experience with geospatial data analysis\n\n- Experience with Databricks for data science workflows, including building and scaling analytical pipelines, collaborating in notebooks, and integrating with Spark for large-scale data processing \n\n- Experience with data engineering principles, including ETL design, orchestration, and data pipeline architecture, to effectively partner with engineering teams \n\n- Experience working with the U.S. Department of Defense or the Intelligence Community \n\n- Experience with graph analytics, network analysis, or anomaly detection techniques \n\n- Experience with version control, such as Git, and reproducible research practices \n\n- Knowledge of machine learning model develop ment and deployment practices \n\n- Possession of excellent written and verbal communication skills\n\n- Master's degree in Statistics, Computer Science, Data Science, or Economics\n\nClearance: \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>In this role, you will apply data science techniques and <span>met</span>hods and leverage a suite of data-driven tools to aid the client’s service leadership and subject matter experts to increase decision space, understand strategic risk, and <span>develop</span> courses of action. Employ expert judgment, adaptable <span>met</span>hodologies, repeatable analytic processes, and enterprise-wide collaboration to provide routine, spe<span>cia</span>l interest, and alert-triggered campaign assessments, and when necessary, facilitate and synchronize enterprise-level campaign adjustment. You will help DoD senior leadership mobilize for long-term campaigning, marshal DoD resources and actions against <span>desired</span> strategic outcomes, and maneuver the department with greater precision and effect to persistently pursue opportunity and mitigate risk vis-a-vis the pacing rival. Analysts are tasked with utilizing a flexible and foundational toolset that will add value across campaigning topics. Analysts will blend functional area knowledge with an <span>ability to</span> identify data sources, manipulate data, use data analytics tools, understand and anticipate strategic intent, and communicate with senior DoD leaders.</p><p></p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges across private and public sectors from fraud detection to cancer research, to national intelligence, we need a seasoned data scientist like you to help find the answers in the data.</p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your leadership <span>skills</span> and data science expertise to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs in order to then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll guide and mentor your team as you oversee the <span>develop</span>ment of algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to advise your clients as they make informed decisions. As a technical leader, you’ll identify new opportunities to use data science solutions to help your clients meet their toughest challenges. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.</p><p></p><p><b>What You&#39;ll Work On:</b> </p><ul><li><p>Design and execute statistical analyses on large, complex datasets from multiple sources. </p></li><li><p><span>Develop</span> production-quality data visualizations, plots, and dashboards for technical and executive audiences. </p></li><li><p>Lead data science projects from scoping through delivery, ensuring analytical rigor and alignment with mission objectives. </p></li><li><p>Collaborate with stakeholders to translate strategic questions into analytical approaches and deliver actionable insights. </p></li><li><p>Respond to ad-hoc analytical requests while managing competing priorities and deadlines in an agile workflow. </p></li><li><p>Mentor junior data scientists and establish best practices for reproducible, well-documented analyses. </p></li><li><p>Communicate complex statistical findings to both technical teams and senior DoD leadership. </p></li></ul><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.</p><p><br /><b><span>You Have:  </span></b></p><ul><li><p>6&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with data science, statistical analysis, or quantitative research</p></li><li><p>6&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with the <span>develop</span>ment of algorithms, leveraging R or Python in data analysis libraries, including pandas, NumPy, scikit-learn, or Tidyverse</p></li><li><p>6&#43; years of <span>experience</span> analyzing structured and unstructured data sources</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with statistics, including hypothesis testing, regression analysis, experimental design, and uncertainty quantification</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with data management in SQL, including managing large-scale data across multiple databases and data warehouses</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> working with large-scale datasets and distributed computing frameworks, including Spark or DASK</p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span></p></li></ul><p><br /><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span>  </b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Natural Language Processing <span>(</span>NLP<span>)</span> techniques, such as text classification or entity recognition </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with geospatial data analysis</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Databricks for data science workflows, including building and scaling analytical pipelines, collaborating in notebooks, and integrating with Spark for large-scale data processing </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with data engineering principles, including ETL design, orchestration, and data pipeline architecture, to effectively partner with engineering teams </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> working with the U.S. Department of Defense or the Intelligence Community </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with graph analytics, network analysis, or anomaly detection techniques </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with version control, such as Git, and reproducible research practices </p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> machine learning model <span>develop</span>ment and deployment practices </p></li><li><p><span>Possession of</span> excellent written and verbal communication <span>skills</span></p></li><li><p><span>Master&#39;s degree</span> in Statistics, Computer Science, Data Science, or Economics</p></li></ul><p><br /><b><span>Clearance: </span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 4 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T19:35:50.646Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Scientist_R0241242","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Scientist_R0241242","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"0137d06db125e8d4018cdaa17be8e966a07a5d86da75c21f4793dde9f7cbd88e","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Scientist_R0241242","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Scientist_R0241242","locations":[{"label":"Arlington, VA"},{"label":"Beavercreek, OH"},{"label":"Lexington Park, MD"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0241242","internal_job_id":"221ce663262a1000c78bb6a144440000","first_published_at":"2026-06-01","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist The Opportunity:\nAs a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi cia l intelligence ( AI ) . In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a Data Scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors from fraud detection to cancer research, to national intelligence, we need you to help find the answers in the data. \n\nOn our team, you’ll use your analytical skills and data science knowledge to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll develop algorithms and systems and use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to help clients make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  \n\nWork with us as we use data science for good.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:\n- 2+ years of experience with data cleansing, analysis, visualization, API connections, or data mining\n- 2+ years of experience analyzing structured and unstructured data\n- 1+ years of experience working with Python, including leveraging several different libraries such as Pandas or Numpy\n- Experience develop ing predictive data models, quantitative analyses, or natural language processing\n- Experience using cloud data tools within AWS, Azure, or Oracle\n- Secret clearance\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with engineering AI solutions, including accessing Large Language Model ( LLM ) APIs, self-hosting LLMs, fine-tuning LLMs, or implementing Model Context Protocol\n- Experience working with the War Data Platform, USAF VAULT, or Palantir Foundry\n- Experience with distributed data and computing tools, including MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL\n- Experience writing Infrastructure-as-Code leveraging Terraform or similar tools\n- Experience working with DoW clients\n- Experience develop ing visually compelling PowerPoint decks and other products to support client delivery\n- Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills\n- TS/SCI clearance \n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence <span>(</span>AI<span>)</span>. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a Data Scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors from fraud detection to cancer research, to national intelligence, we need you to help find the answers in the data. </p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your analytical <span>skills</span> and data science knowledge to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll <span>develop</span> algorithms and systems and use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to help clients make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  </p><p></p><p>Work with us as we use data science for good.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with data cleansing, analysis, visualization, API connections, or data mining</li><li>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> analyzing structured and unstructured data</li><li>1&#43; years of <span>experience</span> working with Python, including leveraging several different libraries such as Pandas or Numpy</li><li><span>Experience</span> <span>develop</span>ing predictive data models, quantitative analyses, or natural language processing</li><li><span>Experience</span> using cloud data tools within AWS, Azure, or Oracle</li><li><span>Secret clearance</span></li><li><span>Bachelor’s degree</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with engineering AI solutions, including accessing Large Language Model <span>(</span>LLM<span>)</span> APIs, self-hosting LLMs, fine-tuning LLMs, or implementing Model Context Protocol</li><li><span>Experience</span> working with the War Data Platform, USAF VAULT, or Palantir Foundry</li><li><span>Experience</span> with distributed data and computing tools, including MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL</li><li><span>Experience</span> writing Infrastructure-as-Code leveraging Terraform or <span>similar</span> tools</li><li><span>Experience</span> working with DoW clients</li><li><span>Experience</span> <span>develop</span>ing visually compelling PowerPoint decks <span>and other</span> products to support client delivery</li><li><span>Possession of</span> excellent verbal and written communication <span>skills</span></li><li><span>TS/SCI clearance </span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b> <br /><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Scientist_R0242009","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Scientist_R0242009","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"20e9f2f0d3175eebaf65fdc0e0713e6ea0ca7dd3712cbefa57d5c231f0ec61e0","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Scientist_R0242009","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Scientist_R0242009","locations":[{"label":"Arlington, VA"},{"label":"Alexandria, VA"},{"label":"Washington, DC"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0242009","internal_job_id":"1076cb28ebff1001aa774b4c8bc20000","first_published_at":"2026-08-20","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist The Opportunity:  \nAs a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi cia l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data. \n\nOn our team, you’ll use your analytical skills and data science knowledge to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll develop algorithms and systems and use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to help clients make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  \n\nWork with us as we use data science for good.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:    \n- 2+ years of experience with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining \n\n- 2+ years of experience with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis \n\n- Experience analyzing structured and unstructured data sources  \n\n- Experience developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses, and visualization of targeted data sources \n\n- Knowledge of Machine Learning, Artifi cia l Intelligence, or Natural Language Processing (NLP)\n\n- Knowledge of text mining or machine learning techniques \n\n- Secret clearance    \n\n- Bachelor’s degree \n\nNice If You Have:    \n- 2+ years of experience in the development of algorithms leveraging R, Python, SQL, or NoSQL \n\n- 2+ years of experience with distributed data or computing tools, including Databricks, MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Apache Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL \n\n- 2+ years of experience with Machine Learning, AI, or NLP \n\n- Experience with Palantir Foundry\n\n- Experience with visualization packages, including Plotly, Seaborn, or ggplot2 \n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph   \n\n- Master’s degree   \n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b> </p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data. </p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your analytical skills and data science knowledge to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll develop algorithms and systems and use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to help clients make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  </p><p></p><p>Work with us as we use data science for good.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining </p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> analyzing structured and unstructured data sources  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses, and visualization of targeted data sources </p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> Machine Learning, Artifi<span>cia</span>l Intelligence, or Natural Language Processing (NLP)</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> text mining or machine learning techniques </p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span>   </p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor’s degree </span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in the development of algorithms leveraging R, Python, SQL, or NoSQL </p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with distributed data or computing tools, including Databricks, MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Apache Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL </p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with Machine Learning, AI, or NLP </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Palantir Foundry</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with visualization packages, including Plotly, Seaborn, or ggplot2 </p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</span>  </p></li><li><p><span>Master’s degree</span>  </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b> </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 4 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Scientist_R0242010","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Scientist_R0242010","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"439d304153cc483e701557611c46427cfa011307b265c8c0b9685adb4d5d0269","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Scientist_R0242010","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Scientist_R0242010","locations":[{"label":"Arlington, VA"},{"label":"Alexandria, VA"},{"label":"Washington, DC"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0242010","internal_job_id":"5055376632821001aafd5391866a0000","first_published_at":"2026-06-17","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist The Opportunity:  \nAs a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi cia l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data. \n\nOn our team, you’ll use your analytical skills and data science knowledge to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll develop algorithms and systems and use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to help clients make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  \n\nWork with us as we use data science for good.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:    \n- 2+ years of experience with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining \n\n- 2+ years of experience with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis \n\n- Experience analyzing structured and unstructured data sources  \n\n- Experience developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses, and visualization of targeted data sources \n\n- Knowledge of Machine Learning, Artifi cia l Intelligence, or Natural Language Processing (NLP)\n\n- Knowledge of text mining or machine learning techniques \n\n- TS/SCI clearance    \n\n- Bachelor’s degree \n\nNice If You Have:    \n- 2+ years of experience in the development of algorithms leveraging R, Python, SQL, or NoSQL \n\n- 2+ years of experience with distributed data or computing tools, including Databricks, MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Apache Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL \n\n- 2+ years of experience with Machine Learning, AI, or NLP \n\n- Experience with Palantir Foundry\n\n- Experience with visualization packages, including Plotly, Seaborn, or ggplot2 \n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph   \n\n- Master’s degree   \n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b> </p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data. </p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your analytical skills and data science knowledge to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll develop algorithms and systems and use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to help clients make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  </p><p></p><p>Work with us as we use data science for good.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining </p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> analyzing structured and unstructured data sources  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses, and visualization of targeted data sources </p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> Machine Learning, Artifi<span>cia</span>l Intelligence, or Natural Language Processing (NLP)</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> text mining or machine learning techniques </p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span>   </p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor’s degree </span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in the development of algorithms leveraging R, Python, SQL, or NoSQL </p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with distributed data or computing tools, including Databricks, MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Apache Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL </p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with Machine Learning, AI, or NLP </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Palantir Foundry</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with visualization packages, including Plotly, Seaborn, or ggplot2 </p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</span>  </p></li><li><p><span>Master’s degree</span>  </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b> </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> TS/SCI<span> clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
