d lead the development of algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to advise your clients as they make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  \n\nWork with us as we use data science for good.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:   \n- 5+ years of experience with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining \n\n- 5+ years of experience analyzing structured and unstructured data\n\n- 3+ years of experience with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis\n\n- Experience wrangling data from disparate databases and APIs for analysis\n\n- Experience developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses, and visualization of targeted data sources  \n\n- Experience leading the development of solutions to complex problems\n\n- Experience with natural language processing, text mining, or machine learning techniques \n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- Bachelor’s degree \n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience in the development of algorithms leveraging Python and SQL\n\n- Experience with engineering AI solutions, including accessing Large Language Model ( LLM ) APIs, self-hosting LLMs, fine-tuning LLMs, or implementing Model Context Protocol\n\n- Experience developing production-quality machine learning models or pipelines\n\n- Experience with distributed data or computing frameworks such as Apache Spark, Hadoop MapReduce, or HPCC ECL\n\n- Experience with Python data science and visualization packages\n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b>The Opportunity:  </b></p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data. </p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your leadership skills and data science expertise to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll guide teammates and lead the development of algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to advise your clients as they make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  </p><p></p><p>Work with us as we use data science for good.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of experience with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining </p></li><li><p>5&#43; years of experience analyzing structured and unstructured data</p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of experience with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis</p></li><li><p>Experience wrangling data from disparate databases and APIs for analysis</p></li><li><p>Experience developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses, and visualization of targeted data sources  </p></li><li><p>Experience leading the development of solutions to complex problems</p></li><li><p>Experience with natural language processing, text mining, or machine learning techniques </p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</span></p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience in the development of algorithms leveraging Python and SQL</p></li><li><p>Experience with engineering AI solutions, including accessing Large Language Model <span>(</span>LLM<span>)</span> APIs, self-hosting LLMs, fine-tuning LLMs, or implementing Model Context Protocol</p></li><li><p>Experience developing production-quality machine learning models or pipelines</p></li><li><p>Experience with distributed data or computing frameworks such as Apache Spark, Hadoop MapReduce, or HPCC ECL</p></li><li><p>Experience with Python data science and visualization packages</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b> </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/Data-Scientist_R0236797","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/Data-Scientist_R0236797","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"52567f7f6023d52174f57c34dd62171254de0048ab4dddbeda33b3c8b68fec86","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Data-Scientist_R0236797","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Data-Scientist_R0236797","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0236797","internal_job_id":"11f32f468ca7100162e14bc744dd0000","first_published_at":"2026-07-14","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist The Opportunity:  \nAs a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi cia l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data.\n\nOn our team, you’ll use your leadership skills and data science expertise to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll guide teammates and lead the development of algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to advise your clients as they make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.\n\nWork with us as we use data science for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:    \n- Experience with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining \n- Experience analyzing structured and unstructured data\n- Experience with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis\n- Experience wrangling data from disparate databases and APIs for analysis\n- Experience developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses, and visualization of targeted data sources  \n- Experience leading the development of solutions to complex problems\n- Experience with natural language processing, text mining, or machine learning techniques \n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n- Bachelor’s degree \n\nNice If You Have:    \n- Experience in the development of algorithms leveraging Python and SQL\n- Experience with engineering AI solutions, including accessing Large Language Model ( LLM ) APIs, self-hosting LLMs, fine-tuning LLMs, or implementing Model Context Protocol\n- Experience developing production-quality machine learning models or pipelines\n- Experience with distributed data or computing frameworks such as Apache Spark, Hadoop MapReduce, or HPCC ECL\n- Experience with Python data science and visualization packages\n\nClearance :  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b><span>The Opportunity:  </span></b></p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data.</p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your leadership skills and data science <span>expertise</span> to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll guide teammates and lead the development of algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to advise your clients as they make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep <span>understanding</span> of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we use data science for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining </li><li><span>Experience</span> analyzing structured and unstructured data</li><li><span>Experience</span> with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis</li><li><span>Experience</span> wrangling data from disparate databases and APIs for analysis</li><li><span>Experience</span> developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses, and visualization of targeted data sources  </li><li><span>Experience</span> leading the development of solutions to complex problems</li><li><span>Experience</span> with natural language processing, text mining, or machine learning techniques </li><li><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</span></li><li><span>Bachelor’s degree </span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> in the development of algorithms leveraging Python and SQL</li><li><span>Experience</span> with engineering AI solutions, including accessing Large Language Model <span>(</span>LLM<span>)</span> APIs, self-hosting LLMs, fine-tuning LLMs, or implementing Model Context Protocol</li><li><span>Experience</span> developing production-quality machine learning models or pipelines</li><li><span>Experience</span> with distributed data or computing frameworks such as Apache Spark, Hadoop MapReduce, or HPCC ECL</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Python data science and visualization packages</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance</span></b><b>:</b> </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/Data-Scientist_R0238939","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/Data-Scientist_R0238939","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"3b25aa2d2972c835dd3d4a9b4f7d8aa24703777c0197334531d6c1a64234d53b","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Data-Scientist_R0238939","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Data-Scientist_R0238939","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0238939","internal_job_id":"cea92b3de0eb100156ba46c0c0050000","first_published_at":"2026-08-05","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist The Opportunity:\nAs an analytics professional, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence. If you care about moving a mission forward as much as advancing the field of data science, this is the opportunity for you. Your deep AI and analytics expertise and advisory mindset, coupled with an original approach to your work, will help clients and stakeholders make sense of their data and encourage actionable results. We’re looking for someone like you to perform complex data exploration and analytics projects through your experience with mathematics and programming.\n\nAs an advanced data scientist and researcher on our Security team, you'll apply innovative AI methodologies to make a real-world impact on real-world problems. You’ll grow your expertise in data science and shape the future of analytics by working in a collaborative environment to solve some of the nation's hardest problems.\n\nWe’ll keep you sharp and moving forward in your career, with access to the latest tools and opportunities to publish or present at conferences. Whether you’re using AI to improve government processes or providing better services to the public, you’ll guide a team that serves critical missions from end to end.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:  \n- Experience with coding in Python\n\n- Experience with ML operations pipelines\n\n- Knowledge of mathematics and statistics, including theory of probability, statistical inference, algorithms, and linear algebra\n\n- Ability to derive variational inference procedure mathematically for a novel model and implement the inference procedure in a framework, including PyTorch, TensorFlow, or Numpy\n\n- Ability to move between theory and practice\n\n- Ability to rapidly learn new technical domains and apply them to machine learning problems\n\n- Active TS/SCI clearance; willingness to take a polygraph exam\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience with application areas of machine learning, including computer vision, natural language processing, and learning on graphs\n\n- Experience with Modern ML and Research Direction\n\n- Experience with advance and emerging architectures\n\n- Experience with Foundation Models and Representation Learning\n\n- Experience with Scientific or Physics Based Modeling\n\n- Knowledge of cloud system, including AWS\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p>As an analytics professional, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence. If you care about moving a mission forward as much as advancing the field of data science, this is the opportunity for you. Your deep AI and analytics expertise and advisory mindset, coupled with an original approach to your work, will help clients and stakeholders make sense of their data and encourage actionable results. We’re looking for someone like you to perform complex data exploration and analytics projects through your experience with mathematics and programming.</p><p><br />As an advanced data scientist and researcher on our Security team, you&#39;ll apply innovative AI methodologies to make a real-world impact on real-world problems. You’ll grow your expertise in data science and shape the future of analytics by working in a collaborative environment to solve some of the nation&#39;s hardest problems.</p><p></p><p>We’ll keep you sharp and moving forward in your career, with access to the latest tools and opportunities to publish or present at conferences. Whether you’re using AI to improve government processes or providing better services to the public, you’ll guide a team that serves critical missions from end to end.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:  </b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience with coding in Python</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with ML operations pipelines</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of mathematics and statistics, including theory of probability, statistical inference, algorithms, and linear algebra</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to derive variational inference procedure mathematically for a novel model and implement the inference procedure in a framework, including PyTorch, TensorFlow, or Numpy</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to move between theory and practice</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to rapidly learn new technical domains and apply them to machine learning problems</span></p></li><li><p>Active TS/SCI clearance; willingness to take a polygraph exam</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:  </b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience with application areas of machine learning, including computer vision, natural language processing, and learning on graphs</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with Modern ML and Research Direction </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with advance and emerging architectures</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with Foundation Models and Representation Learning</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with Scientific or Physics Based Modeling</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of cloud system, including AWS</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 19 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Monterey-CA/Data-Scientist_R0243945","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Monterey-CA/Data-Scientist_R0243945","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"948eb07f96b1ed51e36a733091b25c74bbe7b5a810e8863d0bb894dfd1079f05","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Monterey-CA/Data-Scientist_R0243945","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Monterey-CA/Data-Scientist_R0243945","locations":[{"label":"Monterey, CA"},{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0243945","internal_job_id":"3f97bb3042741001a331b20524b80000","first_published_at":"2026-07-16","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist The Opportunity:  \nAs a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors, from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence, we need you to help find the answers in the data. \n\nOn our team, you’ll use your analytical skills and data science knowledge to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll develop algorithms and systems and use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to help clients make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  \nWork with us as we use data science for good.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:   \n- 2+ years of experience with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining \n\n- 2+ years of experience with utilization of Python programming language for data analysis\n\n- Experience analyzing structured and unstructured data sources  \n\n- Experience developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses, and visualization of targeted data sources\n\n- Experience with Machine Learning, Artificial Intelligence, or Natural Language Processing\n\n- Knowledge of various simulation techniques such as discreet event simulation, Monte Carlo simulation, and agent-based modeling\n\n- Secret clearance   \n\n- Bachelor’s degree \n\nNice If You Have:   \n- 2+ years of experience in the development of algorithms leveraging R, SAS, SQL, or NoSQL \n\n- 2+ years of experience with distributed data and computing tools, including Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Spark, or MySQL\n\n- 2+ years of experience with Machine Learning, AI, or NLP\n\n- Experience with visualization packages, including Contour, Vertex, Workshop, or Grafana\n\n- Experience with U.S. Army or DoW datasets\n\n- Master’s degree \n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b>The Opportunity: </b> </p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors, from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence, we need you to help find the answers in the data. </p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your analytical skills and data science knowledge to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll develop algorithms and systems and use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to help clients make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  </p><p>Work with us as we use data science for good.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining </p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with utilization of Python programming language for data analysis</p></li><li><p>Experience analyzing structured and unstructured data sources  </p></li><li><p>Experience developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses, and visualization of targeted data sources</p></li><li><p>Experience with Machine Learning, Artificial Intelligence, or Natural Language Processing</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of various simulation techniques such as discreet event simulation, Monte Carlo simulation, and agent-based modeling</p></li><li><p>Secret clearance   </p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of experience in the development of algorithms leveraging R, SAS, SQL, or NoSQL </p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with distributed data and computing tools, including Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Spark, or MySQL</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with Machine Learning, AI, or NLP</p></li><li><p>Experience with visualization packages, including Contour, Vertex, Workshop, or Grafana</p></li><li><p>Experience with U.S. Army or DoW datasets</p></li><li><p>Master’s degree </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Norfolk-VA/Data-Scientist_R0245322","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Norfolk-VA/Data-Scientist_R0245322","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"db249d9b81bddc95dab6df92a34dfab4c50c4adbcc805e614d380f79e7a8a77d","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Norfolk-VA/Data-Scientist_R0245322","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Norfolk-VA/Data-Scientist_R0245322","locations":[{"label":"Norfolk, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245322","internal_job_id":"d2fc07c005731000b9ec8ebcdf000000","first_published_at":"2026-08-19","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist The Opportunity: \nDesign and implement effective AI solution architecture utilizing approaches of various AI technologies and met hods to address Marine Corps operational needs. Apply advanced technical expertise and full industry knowledge. Develop innovative solutions to complex problems. Work without considerable direction. Mentor and supervise team members, as needed. Contribute to the direction of critical solutions by applying best-fit ML algorithms and technologies. Help your clients navigate the landscape of ML algorithms, tools, and frameworks. \n\nYou Have: \n- 2+ years of experience with artifi cia l intelligence, data science, machine learning engineering, sof tware engineering, data research, or data analytics \n- Experience with sof tware develop ment or engineering, including in an academic or professional environment \n- Experience with big data technologies, such as Spark, Hadoop, or Databricks\n- Experience with a programming language, including Python, C#, or Java \n- Ability to create solutions within a collaborative, cross-functional team environment \n- Ability to develop scripts and programs for converting various types of data into usable formats and support project team to scale, monitor, and operate data platforms \n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance \n- Bachelor's degree \n  \nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience with generative and agentic AI technologies, such as LLMs, MCP, LangChain, or LangGraph \n- Experience with embedded systems programming in C, C++, or Rus t \n- Ability to develop and maintain scalable data stores that supply big data in forms needed for business analysis \n- Ability to create sof tware for retrieving, parsing, and processing structured and unstructured data\n- Master’s degree \n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information .\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>Design and implement effective AI solution architecture utilizing approaches of various AI technologies and <span>met</span>hods to address Marine Corps operational needs. Apply advanced technical expertise and full industry knowledge. <span>Develop</span> innovative solutions to complex problems. Work without considerable direction. Mentor and supervise team members, as needed. Contribute to the direction of critical solutions by applying best-fit ML algorithms and technologies. Help your clients navigate the landscape of ML algorithms, tools, and frameworks. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence, data science, machine learning engineering, <span>sof</span>tware engineering, data research, or data analytics </li><li><span>Experience</span> with <span>sof</span>tware <span>develop</span>ment or engineering, including in an academic or professional environment </li><li><span>Experience</span> with big data technologies, such as Spark, Hadoop, or Databricks</li><li><span>Experience</span> with a programming language, including Python, C#, or Java </li><li><span>Ability to</span> create solutions within a collaborative, cross-functional team environment </li><li><span>Ability to</span> <span>develop</span> scripts and programs for converting various types of data into usable formats and support project team to scale, monitor, and operate data platforms </li><li><span>Ability to</span><span> obtain a Secret clearance </span></li><li><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree </span></li></ul><p><b>  <br /><span>Nice If You Have:</span> </b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with generative and agentic AI technologies, such as LLMs, MCP, LangChain, or LangGraph </li><li><span>Experience</span> with embedded systems programming in C, C&#43;&#43;, or <span>Rus</span>t </li><li><span>Ability to</span> <span>develop</span> and maintain scalable data stores that supply big data in forms needed for business analysis </li><li><span>Ability to</span> create <span>sof</span>tware for retrieving, parsing, and processing structured and unstructured data</li><li><span>Master’s degree </span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance: </span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span>.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 5 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Shaw-AFB-SC/Data-Scientist_R0245391","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Shaw-AFB-SC/Data-Scientist_R0245391","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"879c9d735b0021f8d4dd244616ed23c7f26fa01844efd4b042b6c230634a43ac","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Shaw-AFB-SC/Data-Scientist_R0245391","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Shaw-AFB-SC/Data-Scientist_R0245391","locations":[{"label":"Shaw AFB, SC"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245391","internal_job_id":"2b414f219eed1000c7fc0c9c22510000","first_published_at":"2026-08-10","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist The Opportunity:  \nAs a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi cia l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors, from fraud detection to cancer research, to national intelligence, we need you to help find the answers in the data. \n\nOn our team, you’ll use your leadership skills and data science expertise to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll guide teammates and lead the development of algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to advise your clients as they make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  \n\nWork with us as we use data science for good.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:    \n- 5+ years of experience with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining \n- 5+ years of experience analyzing structured and unstructured data sources  \n- Experience with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis, including Python or SQL\n- Experience developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses, and visualization of targeted data sources  \n- Experience leading the development of solutions to complex programs \n- Experience with natural language processing, text mining, or machine learning techniques \n- Secret clearance \n- Bachelor’s degree \n\nNice If You Have:    \n- Experience in the development of algorithms leveraging R, Python, or SQL or NoSQL \n- Experience with distributed data and computing tools, including MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL  \n- Experience with visualization packages, including Plotly, Seaborn, or ggplot2 \n- TS/SCI clearance\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.  \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b><span>The Opportunity:  </span></b></p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors, from fraud detection to cancer research, to national intelligence, we need you to help find the answers in the data. </p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your leadership skills and data science expertise to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll guide teammates and lead the development of algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to advise your clients as they make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  </p><p></p><p>Work with us as we use data science for good.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining </li><li>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> analyzing structured and unstructured data sources  </li><li><span>Experience</span> with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis, including Python or SQL</li><li><span>Experience</span> developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses, and visualization of targeted data sources  </li><li><span>Experience</span> leading the development of solutions to complex programs </li><li><span>Experience</span> with natural language processing, text mining, or machine learning techniques </li><li><span>Secret clearance </span></li><li><span>Bachelor’s degree </span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> in the development of algorithms leveraging R, Python, or SQL or NoSQL </li><li><span>Experience</span> with distributed data and computing tools, including MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL  </li><li><span>Experience</span> with visualization packages, including Plotly, Seaborn, or ggplot2 </li><li><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span>  </p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 14 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Stuttgart-Baden-Wurttemberg/Data-Scientist_R0245919","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Stuttgart-Baden-Wurttemberg/Data-Scientist_R0245919","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"aa928c436d2f010f5179f56a540d95dbb963594c891dd279aa1baa2150d37efc","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Stuttgart-Baden-Wurttemberg/Data-Scientist_R0245919","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Stuttgart-Baden-Wurttemberg/Data-Scientist_R0245919","locations":[{"label":"Stuttgart, Baden-Wurttemberg"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245919","internal_job_id":"f43e8f6091f81000c1b012d5a65d0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-03","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist The Opportunity:\nAs a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi cia l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data.\n\nOn our team, you’ll use your analytical skills and data science knowledge to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll develop algorithms and systems and use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to help clients make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.\n\nWork with us as we use data science for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 3+ years of experience develop ing and maintaining machine learning, AI‑driven, or data‑centric applications\n- 3+ years of experience designing, building, and operationalizing data and ML pipelines in production environments\n- 3+ years of experience retrieving, parsing, and processing structured, semi‑structured, and unstructured data to support analytics, feature engineering, and model develop ment\n- 3+ years of experience integrating large language models ( LLMs ) into analytic and ML workflows, including prompt design, inference orchestration, and automated data processing\n- Experience collaborating within cross‑functional teams, such as data scientists, ML engineers, analysts, and platform engineers, to deliver end‑to‑end DS or ML solutions\n- Secret clearance\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have:\n- 3+ years of experience with Python, SQL, or TypeScript in data or ML engineering contexts\n- 3+ years of experience with UI / UX design\n- 3+ years of experience working with geospatial datasets, spatial analytics, or geospatial ML workflows\n- 3+ years of experience with distributed data and compute ecosystems, such as Spark, Databricks, Hadoop, Hive, AWS EMR, and Kafka, for large‑scale ML workloads\n- Experience operating in a Combatant Command or international mission‑focused environment and applying DS or ML met hods to operational decision‑making\n- Experience using Palantir Foundry for data modeling, pipeline develop ment, or operational analytics\n- TS/SCI clearance preferred\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data.</p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your analytical <span>skills</span> and data science knowledge to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll <span>develop</span> algorithms and systems and use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to help clients make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we use data science for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> <span>develop</span>ing and maintaining machine learning, AI‑driven, or data‑centric applications</li><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> designing, building, and operationalizing data and ML pipelines in production environments</li><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> retrieving, parsing, and processing structured, semi‑structured, and unstructured data to support analytics, feature engineering, and model <span>develop</span>ment</li><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> integrating large language models <span>(</span>LLMs<span>)</span> into analytic and ML workflows, including prompt design, inference orchestration, and automated data processing</li><li><span>Experience</span> collaborating within cross‑functional teams, such as data scientists, ML engineers, analysts, and platform engineers, to deliver end‑to‑end DS or ML solutions</li><li><span>Secret clearance</span></li><li><span>Bachelor’s degree</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with Python, SQL, or TypeScript in data or ML engineering contexts</li><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with UI<span>/</span>UX design</li><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> working with geospatial datasets, spatial analytics, or geospatial ML workflows</li><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with distributed data and compute ecosystems, such as Spark, Databricks, Hadoop, Hive, AWS EMR, and Kafka, for large‑scale ML workloads</li><li><span>Experience</span> operating in a Combatant Command or international mission‑focused environment and applying DS or ML <span>met</span>hods to operational decision‑making</li><li><span>Experience</span> using Palantir Foundry for data modeling, pipeline <span>develop</span>ment, or operational analytics</li><li><span>TS/SCI clearance</span> preferred</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"Germany","id":"dcc5b7608d8644b3a93716604e78e995"},"posted_on":"Posted 21 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Tampa-FL/Data-Scientist_R0245472","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Tampa-FL/Data-Scientist_R0245472","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"6f89e6c0c7f844490aee18c522782d61b76f31bbafbacc7018539dfbc88eeb15","fetched_at":"2026-08-24T14:15:46.938Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Tampa-FL/Data-Scientist_R0245472","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Tampa-FL/Data-Scientist_R0245472","locations":[{"label":"Tampa, FL"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245472","internal_job_id":"45e74e1697ae10010e6a08f2091c0000","first_published_at":"2026-07-28","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist The Opportunity:\nAs a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by machine learning and artifi cia l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. We need you to help find the answers in the data.\n\nOn our team, you’ll use your analytical skills and data science knowledge to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll develop algorithms and systems and use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to help clients make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:    \n- 5+ years of experience with programming languages including R, Python, or C\n- Experience designing, develop ing, or leveraging relational databases ( RDBMS ) such as PostgreSQL or MS SQL\n- Experience creating sof tware for retrieving, parsing and processing structured and unstructured data, and develop ing scalable ETL / ELT workflows for reporting and analytics \n- Experience programming and coding mathematical models\n- Experience with data visualization tools and best practices\n- Knowledge of the Sof tware Develop ment Life Cycle, testing, and version control\n- Ability to cleanse data and develop scripts and programs for converting various types of data into usable formats\n- Ability to work in a cross-functional team, prioritize multiple work tasks, deliver products on time within and to quality standards\n- TS/SCI clearance\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:    \n- Experience supporting DoD organizations\n- Experience using and deploying machine learning algorithms, including natural language processing ( NLP )\n- Experience with web develop ment frameworks, including Shiny, Django, or Flask\n- Experience with data lakes, data warehouses, or data lake houses\n- Experience with cloud services, including AWS or Azure\n- Experience working in an Agile develop ment environment collaborating with Application Develop ers, Infrastructure Engineers, and stakeholders\n- Experience with CI / CD, including Git, Jenkins, and Docker\n- Experience with distributed data and computing tools such as Spark, Databricks, Hadoop, Hive, AWS EMR, or Kafka\n- Experience with NoSQL implementation using MongoDB or Cassandra \n- Experience with data warehousing, including AWS Redshift, MySQL, or Snowflake \n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by machine learning and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. We need you to help find the answers in the data.</p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your analytical <span>skills</span> and data science knowledge to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll <span>develop</span> algorithms and systems and use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to help clients make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with programming languages including R, Python, or C</li><li><span>Experience</span> designing, <span>develop</span>ing, or leveraging relational databases <span>(</span>RDBMS<span>)</span> such as PostgreSQL or MS SQL</li><li><span>Experience</span> creating <span>sof</span>tware for retrieving, parsing and processing structured and unstructured data, and <span>develop</span>ing scalable ETL<span>/</span>ELT workflows for reporting and analytics </li><li><span>Experience</span> programming and coding mathematical models</li><li><span>Experience</span> with data visualization tools and best practices</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> the <span>Sof</span>tware <span>Develop</span>ment Life Cycle, testing, and version control</li><li><span>Ability to</span> cleanse data and <span>develop</span> scripts and programs for converting various types of data into usable formats</li><li><span>Ability to</span> work in a cross-functional team, prioritize multiple work tasks, deliver products on time within and to quality standards</li><li><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></li><li><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> supporting DoD organizations</li><li><span>Experience</span> using and deploying machine learning algorithms, including natural language processing <span>(</span>NLP<span>)</span></li><li><span>Experience</span> with web <span>develop</span>ment frameworks, including Shiny, Django, or Flask</li><li><span>Experience</span> with data lakes, data warehouses, or data lake houses</li><li><span>Experience</span> with cloud services, including AWS or Azure</li><li><span>Experience</span> working in an Agile <span>develop</span>ment environment collaborating with Application <span>Develop</span>ers, Infrastructure Engineers, and stakeholders</li><li><span>Experience</span> with CI<span>/</span>CD, including Git, Jenkins, and Docker</li><li><span>Experience</span> with distributed data and computing tools such as Spark, Databricks, Hadoop, Hive, AWS EMR, or Kafka</li><li><span>Experience</span> with NoSQL implementation using MongoDB or Cassandra </li><li><span>Experience</span> with data warehousing, including AWS Redshift, MySQL, or Snowflake </li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 27 Days Ago"},"status":"possibly_closed","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-24T14:15:46.938Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","missing_complete_scans":1,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0241352","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0241352","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"b9cbd58488dbe2a0821b40f3e71ba12b0edcc2d3ff31fbf3e9d2623bdba85120","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0241352","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0241352","locations":[{"label":"Washington, DC"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0241352","internal_job_id":"ccf31037218f1000bbd646b4a6e60000","first_published_at":"2026-08-11","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist The Opportunity :\nAs a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi cia l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a Data Scientist at Booz Allen, you can turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need a seasoned data scientist like you to help find the answers in the data. \n\nOn our team, you’ll use your leadership skills and data science expertise to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll guide and mentor your team as you oversee the development of algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to advise your clients as they make informed decisions. As a technical leader, you’ll identify new opportunities to use data science solutions to help your clients meet their toughest challenges. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used. \n\nWork with us as we use data science for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:    \n- Experience with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining\n\n- Experience with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis\n\n- Experience analyzing structured and unstructured data sources  \n\n- Experience developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses, and visualization of targeted data sources\n\n- Experience with natural language processing, text mining, or machine learning techniques\n\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree \n\nNice If You Have:    \n- Experience with the development of algorithms leveraging R, Python, or SQL and NoSQL\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b><span>The Opportunity</span></b><b>:</b></p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a Data Scientist at Booz Allen, you can turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need a seasoned data scientist like you to help find the answers in the data. </p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your leadership skills and data science expertise to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll guide and mentor your team as you oversee the development of algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to advise your clients as they make informed decisions. As a technical leader, you’ll identify new opportunities to use data science solutions to help your clients meet their toughest challenges. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used. </p><p></p><p>Work with us as we use data science for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> analyzing structured and unstructured data sources  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses, and visualization of targeted data sources</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with natural language processing, text mining, or machine learning techniques</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to obtain a Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor’s degree </span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with the development of algorithms leveraging R, Python, or SQL and NoSQL</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 13 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0242769","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0242769","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"4b46591fd7eee6694fc06a3e7ec1e7d8c05b975bd31099ebd17e556c90d5218c","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0242769","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0242769","locations":[{"label":"Washington, DC"},{"label":"Reston, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0242769","internal_job_id":"b497c26d3cec100103f8c717680c0000","first_published_at":"2026-06-23","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist The Opportunity:  \nAs a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi cia l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors from fraud detection to cancer research, to national intelligence, we need you to help find the answers in the data. \n\nOn our team, you’ll use your analytical skills to help create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll work with and learn from your teammates as you develop algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers so that your clients can make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.\n\nWork with us as we use data science for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:    \n- Experience with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, data science, or data mining \n\n- Experience with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis such as Python, R, or SQL\n\n- Knowledge of statistical analysis, predictive modeling, and machine learning met hods\n\n- Ability to design and develop automated analytic sof tware, techniques, and algorithms\n\n- TS/SCI clearance  \n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:    \n- Experience working with GEOINT, HUMINT, MASINT, OSINT, and SIGINT and the data and tools asso cia ted with these disciplines\n\n- Experience with intelligence or operations analysis in the DoD or Intelligence Community\n\n- Experience creating ETL pipelines, including querying APIs, cleaning and conditioning data, and creating schemas for data storage\n\n- Knowledge of version control tools, including Git, GitLab, GitHub, or Bitbucket\n\n- Knowledge of DevOps, including CI / CD pipelines and Jenkins\n\n- Ability to use data visualization tools, including COTS sof tware such as Tableau, Power BI, or ArcGIS, or FOSS libraries such as seaborn, matplotlib, or ggplot\n\n- Possession of excellent written and verbal communication skills \n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph   \n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b><span>The Opportunity:  </span></b></p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors from fraud detection to cancer research, to national intelligence, we need you to help find the answers in the data. </p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your analytical skills to help create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll work with and learn from your teammates as you develop algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers so that your clients can make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we use data science for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, data science, or data mining </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis such as Python, R, or SQL</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> statistical analysis, predictive modeling, and machine learning <span>met</span>hods</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> design and develop automated analytic <span>sof</span>tware, techniques, and algorithms</p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span> </p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> working with GEOINT, HUMINT, MASINT, OSINT, and SIGINT and the data and tools asso<span>cia</span>ted with these disciplines</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with intelligence or operations analysis in the DoD or Intelligence Community</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> creating ETL pipelines, including querying APIs, cleaning and conditioning data, and creating schemas for data storage</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> version control tools, including Git, GitLab, GitHub, or Bitbucket</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> DevOps, including CI<span>/</span>CD pipelines and Jenkins</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> use data visualization tools, including COTS <span>sof</span>tware such as Tableau, Power BI, or ArcGIS, or FOSS libraries such as seaborn, matplotlib, or ggplot</p></li><li><p><span>Possession of</span> excellent written and verbal communication skills </p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</span>  </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0245950","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0245950","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"9bb939f71c61af1b8395d1456fb1b0098746777ce34936e0b60a05b56932502c","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0245950","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0245950","locations":[{"label":"Washington, DC"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245950","internal_job_id":"cdcfc075bb401001031d71096e150000","first_published_at":"2026-08-04","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist The Opportunity:\nAs a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi cia l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors, from fraud detection to cancer research, to national intelligence, we need you to help find the answers in the data. \n\nOn our team, you’ll use your analytical skills and data science knowledge to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll develop algorithms and systems and use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to help clients make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:    \n- Experience using data science programming languages such as Python, R, or SQL\n- Experience creating ETL pipelines, including querying APIs, cleaning and conditioning data, and creating schemas for data storage\n- Experience with version control tools, including git, GitLab, GitHub, or Bitbucket\n- Knowledge of statistical analysis, predictive modeling, and machine learning met hods\n- Ability to design and develop automated analytic sof tware, techniques, and algorithms\n- Ability to develop solutions and integrate and extend free and open-source sof tware ( FOSS ) or COTS products\n- Ability to generate data visualizations with tools such as Tableau, Power BI, or ArcGIS\n- Active TS/SCI clearance; willingness to take a polygraph exam\n- HS diploma or GED and 7+ years of experience in data science, or Bachelor’s degree and 3+ years of experience in data science\n\nNice If You Have:    \n- Experience working with GEOINT, HUMINT, MASINT, OSINT, and SIGINT, and the data and tools asso cia ted with these disciplines\n- Experience with intelligence or operations analysis in the DoW or Intelligence Community\n- Knowledge of DevOps, including CI / CD pipelines and Jenkins\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph \n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.   \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors, from fraud detection to cancer research, to national intelligence, we need you to help find the answers in the data. </p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your analytical skills and data science knowledge to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll develop algorithms and systems and use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to help clients make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> using data science programming languages such as Python, R, or SQL</li><li><span>Experience</span> creating ETL pipelines, including querying APIs, cleaning and conditioning data, and creating schemas for data storage</li><li><span>Experience</span> with version control tools, including git, GitLab, GitHub, or Bitbucket</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> statistical analysis, predictive modeling, and machine learning <span>met</span>hods</li><li><span>Ability to</span> design and develop automated analytic <span>sof</span>tware, techniques, and algorithms</li><li><span>Ability to</span> develop solutions and integrate and extend free and open-source <span>sof</span>tware <span>(</span>FOSS<span>)</span> or COTS products</li><li><span>Ability to</span> generate data visualizations with tools such as Tableau, Power BI, or ArcGIS</li><li><span>Active TS/SCI clearance; willingness to take a polygraph exam </span></li><li>HS diploma or GED and 7&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in data science, or <span>Bachelor’s degree</span> and 3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in data science</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> working with GEOINT, HUMINT, MASINT, OSINT, and SIGINT, and the data and tools asso<span>cia</span>ted with these disciplines</li><li><span>Experience</span> with intelligence or operations analysis in the DoW or Intelligence Community</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> DevOps, including CI<span>/</span>CD pipelines and Jenkins</li><li><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph </span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance is required.</span>  </p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 20 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0246054","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0246054","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"ab8733c71b6f97025406bcd69cc1225f704c2e99664202cd2c5563daeffda341","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0246054","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0246054","locations":[{"label":"Washington, DC"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246054","internal_job_id":"cdcfc075bb40100151f5443281a60000","first_published_at":"2026-08-18","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist The Opportunity:\nAs a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi cia l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors, from fraud detection to cancer research, to national intelligence, we need you to help find the answers in the data. \n\nOn our team, you’ll use your analytical skills and data science knowledge to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll develop algorithms and systems and use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to help clients make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.\n\nWork with us as we use data science for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:  \n- 2+ years of experience with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis \n- 1+ years of experience with R or Python \n- Experience analyzing structured and unstructured data sources  \n- Experience using scientific met hods to inform qualitative and quantitative analyses  \n- Ability to work effectively in a collaborative and fast-paced environment \n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have:    \n- Experience with VS Code, GitHub, Jira, or Confluence\n- Experience with data gathering, cleansing, and parsing \n- Knowledge of DoD intelligence processes, activities, standards, and analytic tools\n- Ability to work in Windows and Linux OS environments   \n- Bachelor's degree in Operations Research, Applied Mathematics, or Data Science \n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $48,000.00 to $98,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors, from fraud detection to cancer research, to national intelligence, we need you to help find the answers in the data. </p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your analytical skills and data science knowledge to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll develop algorithms and systems and use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to help clients make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we use data science for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b> </p><ul><li>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis </li><li>1&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with R or Python </li><li><span>Experience</span> analyzing structured and unstructured data sources  </li><li><span>Experience</span> using scientific <span>met</span>hods to inform qualitative and quantitative analyses  </li><li><span>Ability to</span> work effectively in a collaborative and fast-paced environment </li><li><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph </span></li><li><span>Bachelor’s degree </span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with VS Code, GitHub, Jira, or Confluence</li><li><span>Experience</span> with data gathering, cleansing, and parsing </li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> DoD intelligence processes, activities, standards, and analytic tools</li><li><span>Ability to</span> work in Windows and Linux OS environments   </li><li><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span> in Operations Research, Applied Mathematics, or Data Science </li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b><br /><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</span></p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $48,000.00 to $98,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 6 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0246170","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0246170","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"4a8a6eeea409005cb6692d38e9699e21f5d9e59b5aa8a2af4e2bdfe2aa7c13c8","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0246170","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0246170","locations":[{"label":"Washington, DC"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246170","internal_job_id":"e596be2e7383100107a1604a357f0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-18","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist The Opportunity:\nAs a Full Stack Developer, you will enjoy a collaborative environment where you work closely with others in an organization that encourages and values collaboration, mentoring, and continuous learning. You will have the opportunity to leverage and grow your hands-on software engineering expertise as you contribute to real challenges across a variety of domains.\n\nOn our team, you’ll use your leadership skills and software engineering expertise to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs and then dig into their requirements to build solutions for their complex problems. You’ll guide teammates and lead the development of applications and systems. If you are passionate about building innovative web applications and thrive in a collaborative environment, we encourage you to apply for this Full Stack Developer position.\n \nJoin us. The world can’t wait.   \n \nYou Have:  \n- 8+ years of experience in software engineering, including developing, testing, integrating, or maintaining software applications \n\n- 5+ years of experience developing applications using an object-oriented programming language \n\n- 4+ years of experience developing web applications using frontend technologies or frameworks, such as React or Angular \n\n- Experience developing or integrating backend services and RESTful APIs \n\n- Experience developing applications using relational databases, such as PostgreSQL, and working with SQL \n\n- Experience working with automated build, test, or CI/CD processes \n\n- Experience working within Agile software development environments using methodologies such as Scrum or Kanban \n\n- Experience using software development and task management tools, such as Jira \n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph \n\n- Bachelor's degree in a Computer Science, Engineering, or Information Technology field or 10+ years of experience with software engineering in lieu of a degree \n\nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience developing production applications with Python \n\n- Experience developing enterprise web applications \n\n- Experience with microservices, distributed systems, or event-driven architectures \n\n- Experience with Infrastructure as Code technologies such as CloudFormation \n\n- Experience building or maintaining CI/CD pipelines, such as GitLab, GitHub Actions, or Jenkins \n\n- Experience with Kubernetes or other container orchestration technologies \n\n- Experience with automated unit, integration, or end-to-end testing \n\n- Experience with application authentication, authorization, logging, monitoring, or observability \n\n- Experience working in DevSecOps software delivery environments \n\n- Experience leading projects and mentoring, teaching junior staff members  \n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information. TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required. \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p><span>As a Full Stack Developer, you will enjoy a collaborative environment where you work closely with others in an organization that encourages and values collaboration, mentoring, and continuous learning. You will have the opportunity to leverage and grow your hands-on software engineering expertise as you contribute to real challenges across a variety of domains.</span></p><p></p><p><span>On our team, you’ll use your leadership skills and software engineering expertise to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs and then dig into their requirements to build solutions for their complex problems. You’ll guide teammates and lead the development of applications and systems. If you are passionate about building innovative web applications and thrive in a collaborative environment, we encourage you to apply for this Full Stack Developer position.</span></p><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Join us. The world can’t wait.   </span></p><p><span> </span></p><p><b>You Have:</b> </p><ul><li><p><span>8&#43; years of experience in software engineering, including developing, testing, integrating, or maintaining software applications </span></p></li><li><p><span>5&#43; years of experience developing applications using an object-oriented programming language </span></p></li><li><p><span>4&#43; years of experience developing web applications using frontend technologies or frameworks, such as React or Angular </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience developing or integrating backend services and RESTful APIs </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience developing applications using relational databases, such as PostgreSQL, and working with SQL </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience working with automated build, test, or CI/CD processes </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience working within Agile software development environments using methodologies such as Scrum or Kanban </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience using software development and task management tools, such as Jira </span></p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph </span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree in a Computer Science, Engineering, or Information Technology field or 10&#43; years of experience with software engineering in lieu of a degree </span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b> </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience developing production applications with Python </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience developing enterprise web applications </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with microservices, distributed systems, or event-driven architectures </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with Infrastructure as Code technologies such as CloudFormation </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience building or maintaining CI/CD pipelines, such as GitLab, GitHub Actions, or Jenkins </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with Kubernetes or other container orchestration technologies </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with automated unit, integration, or end-to-end testing </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with application authentication, authorization, logging, monitoring, or observability </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience working in DevSecOps software delivery environments </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience leading projects and mentoring, teaching junior staff members  </span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information. TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 6 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0247048","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0247048","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"3c9995b5b4dc6c6fbd80c768a2293d1ee2a6754e94b0ba61fbb2cbd794078940","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0247048","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0247048","locations":[{"label":"Washington, DC"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247048","internal_job_id":"83b83551a7591001f1261e27359c0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-14","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist The Opportunity:\nAs a Full Stack Developer, you will enjoy a collaborative environment where you work closely with others in an organization that encourages and values collaboration, mentoring, and continuous learning. You will have the opportunity to leverage and grow your hands-on software engineering expertise as you contribute to real challenges across a variety of domains.\n\nOn our team, you’ll use your leadership skills and software engineering expertise to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs and then dig into their requirements to build solutions for their complex problems. You’ll guide teammates and lead the development of applications and systems. If you are passionate about building innovative web applications and thrive in a collaborative environment, we encourage you to apply for this Full Stack Developer position.\n \nJoin us. The world can’t wait.   \n \nYou Have:  \n- 8+ years of experience in software engineering, including developing, testing, integrating, or maintaining software applications \n\n- Experience developing applications using an object-oriented programming language \n\n- Experience developing web applications using frontend technologies or frameworks, such as React or Angular \n\n- Experience developing or integrating backend services and RESTful APIs \n\n- Experience developing applications using relational databases, such as PostgreSQL, and working with SQL \n\n- Experience working with automated build, test, or CI/CD processes   \n\n- Top Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience developing production applications with Python \n\n- Experience developing enterprise web applications \n\n- Experience with microservices, distributed systems, or event-driven architectures \n\n- Experience with Infrastructure as Code technologies such as CloudFormation \n\n- Experience building or maintaining CI/CD pipelines, such as GitLab, GitHub Actions, or Jenkins \n\n- Experience with Kubernetes or other container orchestration technologies \n\n- Experience with automated unit, integration, or end-to-end testing \n\n- Experience with application authentication, authorization, logging, monitoring, or observability \n\n- Experience working within Agile software development environments using methodologies such as Scrum or Kanban \n\n- Experience using software development and task management tools, such as Jira\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information. Top Secret clearance is required. \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p><span>As a Full Stack Developer, you will enjoy a collaborative environment where you work closely with others in an organization that encourages and values collaboration, mentoring, and continuous learning. You will have the opportunity to leverage and grow your hands-on software engineering expertise as you contribute to real challenges across a variety of domains.</span></p><p></p><p><span>On our team, you’ll use your leadership skills and software engineering expertise to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs and then dig into their requirements to build solutions for their complex problems. You’ll guide teammates and lead the development of applications and systems. If you are passionate about building innovative web applications and thrive in a collaborative environment, we encourage you to apply for this Full Stack Developer position.</span></p><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Join us. The world can’t wait.   </span></p><p><span> </span></p><p><b>You Have:</b> </p><ul><li><p><span>8&#43; years of experience in software engineering, including developing, testing, integrating, or maintaining software applications </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience developing applications using an object-oriented programming language </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience developing web applications using frontend technologies or frameworks, such as React or Angular </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience developing or integrating backend services and RESTful APIs </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience developing applications using relational databases, such as PostgreSQL, and working with SQL </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience working with automated build, test, or CI/CD processes </span><span> </span></p></li><li><p><span>Top Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree </span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b> </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience developing production applications with Python </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience developing enterprise web applications </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with microservices, distributed systems, or event-driven architectures </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with Infrastructure as Code technologies such as CloudFormation </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience building or maintaining CI/CD pipelines, such as GitLab, GitHub Actions, or Jenkins </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with Kubernetes or other container orchestration technologies </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with automated unit, integration, or end-to-end testing </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with application authentication, authorization, logging, monitoring, or observability </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience working within Agile software development environments using methodologies such as Scrum or Kanban </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience using software development and task management tools, such as Jira</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information. Top Secret clearance is required. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 10 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0247406","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0247406","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"e9815fa36edd72b97cc4fd9ebd8bd2eb447f2241bdd313f4d709eb228b749373","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0247406","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0247406","locations":[{"label":"Washington, DC"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247406","internal_job_id":"26f0e5a9193a100164d3223d0b930000","first_published_at":"2026-08-19","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist The Opportunity: \nDesign and implement effective AI solution architecture utilizing approaches of various AI technologies and met hods to address Marine Corps operational needs. Apply advanced technical expertise and full industry knowledge. Develop innovative solutions to complex problems. Work without considerable direction. Mentor and supervise team members, as needed. Contribute to the direction of critical solutions by applying best-fit ML algorithms and technologies. Help your clients navigate the landscape of ML algorithms, tools, and frameworks. \n\nYou Have: \n- 2+ years of experience with artifi cia l intelligence, data science, machine learning engineering, sof tware engineering, data research, or data analytics \n\n- Experience with sof tware develop ment or engineering, including in an academic or professional environment \n\n- Experience with big data technologies, such as Spark, Hadoop, or Databricks\n\n- Experience with a programming language, including Python, C#, or Java \n\n- Ability to create solutions within a collaborative, cross-functional team environment \n\n- Ability to develop scripts and programs for converting various types of data into usable formats and support project team to scale, monitor, and operate data platforms \n\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance \n\n- Bachelor's degree \n\n  \nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience with generative and agentic AI technologies, such as LLMs, MCP, LangChain, or LangGraph \n\n- Experience with embedded systems programming in C, C++, or Rus t \n\n- Ability to develop and maintain scalable data stores that supply big data in forms needed for business analysis \n\n- Ability to create sof tware for retrieving, parsing, and processing structured and unstructured data\n\n- Master’s degree \n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information .\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>Design and implement effective AI solution architecture utilizing approaches of various AI technologies and <span>met</span>hods to address Marine Corps operational needs. Apply advanced technical expertise and full industry knowledge. <span>Develop</span> innovative solutions to complex problems. Work without considerable direction. Mentor and supervise team members, as needed. Contribute to the direction of critical solutions by applying best-fit ML algorithms and technologies. Help your clients navigate the landscape of ML algorithms, tools, and frameworks. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence, data science, machine learning engineering, <span>sof</span>tware engineering, data research, or data analytics </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with <span>sof</span>tware <span>develop</span>ment or engineering, including in an academic or professional environment </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with big data technologies, such as Spark, Hadoop, or Databricks</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with a programming language, including Python, C#, or Java </p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> create solutions within a collaborative, cross-functional team environment </p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> <span>develop</span> scripts and programs for converting various types of data into usable formats and support project team to scale, monitor, and operate data platforms </p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span><span> obtain a Secret clearance </span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree </span></p></li></ul><p><b>  <br /><span>Nice If You Have:</span> </b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with generative and agentic AI technologies, such as LLMs, MCP, LangChain, or LangGraph </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with embedded systems programming in C, C&#43;&#43;, or <span>Rus</span>t </p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> <span>develop</span> and maintain scalable data stores that supply big data in forms needed for business analysis </p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> create <span>sof</span>tware for retrieving, parsing, and processing structured and unstructured data</p></li><li><p><span>Master’s degree </span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance: </span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span>.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 5 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0247637","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0247637","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"87c3ddd3801bba7dbbec9550eac8152ce6bf1ee68b983800259617eb2f0bb9af","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0247637","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Washington-DC/Data-Scientist_R0247637","locations":[{"label":"Washington, DC"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247637","internal_job_id":"89522cba336b1000b79af1ee313e0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-24","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist The Opportunity:  \nAs a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data. \n\nOn our team, you’ll use your analytical skills and data science knowledge to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll develop algorithms and systems and use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to help clients make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  \n\nWork with us as we use data science for good.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:   \n- Experience with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, software engineering or data mining \n\n- Experience with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis, including Python\n\n- Experience analyzing structured and unstructured data sources  \n\n- Experience developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses or visualization of targeted data sources, including machine learning models\n\n- Knowledge of Machine Learning, Artificial Intelligence, or Natural Language Processing  \n\n- Knowledge of text mining or machine learning techniques \n\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance   \n\n- Bachelor’s degree \n\nNice If You Have:   \n- 2+ years of experience in the development of algorithms leveraging R, Python, or SQL and NoSQL \n\n- 2+ years of experience with Distributed data and computing tools, including MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL \n\n- 2+ years of experience with Machine Learning, AI or NLP \n\n- Experience with visualization packages, including Plotly, Seaborn, or ggplot2 \n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph  \n\n- Master’s degree  \n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b>The Opportunity: </b> </p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data. </p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your analytical skills and data science knowledge to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll develop algorithms and systems and use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to help clients make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  </p><p></p><p>Work with us as we use data science for good.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, software engineering or data mining </p></li><li><p>Experience with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis, including Python</p></li><li><p>Experience analyzing structured and unstructured data sources  </p></li><li><p>Experience developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses or visualization of targeted data sources, including machine learning models</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of Machine Learning, Artificial Intelligence, or Natural Language Processing  </p></li><li><p>Knowledge of text mining or machine learning techniques </p></li><li><p>Ability to obtain a Secret clearance   </p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of experience in the development of algorithms leveraging R, Python, or SQL and NoSQL </p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with Distributed data and computing tools, including MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL </p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with Machine Learning, AI or NLP </p></li><li><p>Experience with visualization packages, including Plotly, Seaborn, or ggplot2 </p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph  </p></li><li><p>Master’s degree  </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b> </p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.</p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted Today"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Wiesbaden-Hesse/Data-Scientist_R0241822","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Wiesbaden-Hesse/Data-Scientist_R0241822","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"c59d121e0dd917373061d34fb731ce3e8735b99fd37c7ba9a227347db611c94e","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Wiesbaden-Hesse/Data-Scientist_R0241822","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Wiesbaden-Hesse/Data-Scientist_R0241822","locations":[{"label":"Wiesbaden, Hesse"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0241822","internal_job_id":"cb5b967f859e100108e187fd9f230000","first_published_at":"2026-08-12","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist The Opportunity:  \nAs a Data Scientist Operating and supporting a four-star Army Headquarters, you'll bring your technical, computer science, data analysis, and data science expertise to collaborate, design and build innovative Solutions at an Army Service Component Command in support of operations in Europe and Africa.\n\nAs a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities.\n\nOn our team, you’ll use your analytical skills and data science knowledge to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll develop algorithms and systems and use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to help clients make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  \n\nWhat You'll Work On:\n- Perform data cleansing, data integration, and data quality assurance activities to maintain the accuracy and integrity of large datasets.\n\n- Develop and maintain Foundry pipelines using Pipeline Builder to ingest, transform, and integrate data.\n\n- Build modular applications and workflows leveraging Python, and Foundry AIP.\n\n- Assist in providing training to guide stakeholders in using Maven Smart System applications.\n\n- Support testing, debugging, and performance tuning of Foundry applications.\n\n- Troubleshoot data-related problems and provide innovative solutions to address complex data challenges.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:   \n- 5+ years of experience utilizing programming and querying languages, including Python, R, Scala, or SQL\n\n- 5+ years of experience developing and maintaining data applications for reporting and analytics\n\n- Experience creating workflows for retrieving, parsing, and processing structured and unstructured data\n\n- Experience creating solutions within a collaborative and cross-functional team environment\n\n- Experience with Maven Smart System or Palantir tools, such as Foundry\n\n- Ability to manage tasks and projects independently with minimal guidance and direction\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree in computer science, data science, or mathematics\n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience with distributed data and computer tools including Spark, Databricks, Hadoop, Hive, AWS EMR, or Kafka\n\n- Experience with data visualization or geospatial tools, such as Tableau, Qlik, PowerBI, or ArcGIS\n\n- Experience working within a Combatant Command or other DoW organizations\n\n- Top Secret clearance\n\n- Master's degree in computer science, data science, or mathematics\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b>The Opportunity: </b> </p><p>As a Data Scientist Operating and supporting a four-star Army Headquarters, you&#39;ll bring your technical, computer science, data analysis, and data science expertise to collaborate, design and build innovative Solutions at an Army Service Component Command in support of operations in Europe and Africa.</p><p></p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities.</p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your analytical skills and data science knowledge to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll develop algorithms and systems and use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to help clients make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  </p><p></p><p><b><span>What You&#39;ll Work On:</span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Perform data cleansing, data integration, and data quality assurance activities to maintain the accuracy and integrity of large datasets.</span></p></li><li><p><span>Develop and maintain Foundry pipelines using Pipeline Builder to ingest, transform, and integrate data.</span></p></li><li><p><span>Build modular applications and workflows leveraging Python, and Foundry AIP.</span></p></li><li><p><span>Assist in providing training to guide stakeholders in using Maven Smart System applications.</span></p></li><li><p><span>Support testing, debugging, and performance tuning of Foundry applications.</span></p></li><li><p><span>Troubleshoot data-related problems and provide innovative solutions to address complex data challenges.</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p><span>5&#43; years of experience utilizing programming and querying languages, including Python, R, Scala, or SQL</span></p></li><li><p><span>5&#43; years of experience developing and maintaining data applications for reporting and analytics</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience creating workflows for retrieving, parsing, and processing structured and unstructured data</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience creating solutions within a collaborative and cross-functional team environment</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with Maven Smart System or Palantir tools, such as Foundry</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to manage tasks and projects independently with minimal guidance and direction</span></p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor’s degree in computer science, data science, or mathematics</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience with distributed data and computer tools including Spark, Databricks, Hadoop, Hive, AWS EMR, or Kafka</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with data visualization or geospatial tools, such as Tableau, Qlik, PowerBI, or ArcGIS</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience working within a Combatant Command or other DoW organizations</span></p></li><li><p><span>Top Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Master&#39;s degree in computer science, data science, or mathematics</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"Germany","id":"dcc5b7608d8644b3a93716604e78e995"},"posted_on":"Posted 12 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Wiesbaden-Hesse/Data-Scientist_R0245414","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Wiesbaden-Hesse/Data-Scientist_R0245414","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"082bda2b9f387d6cba7599aa84ebbd5cde33112a2763f542de332f91fa3b4401","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Wiesbaden-Hesse/Data-Scientist_R0245414","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Wiesbaden-Hesse/Data-Scientist_R0245414","locations":[{"label":"Wiesbaden, Hesse"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245414","internal_job_id":"45e74e1697ae1000cc7249a73ac80000","first_published_at":"2026-07-27","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist The Opportunity:\nAs a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi cia l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors, from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence, we need you to help find the answers in the data. \n\nOn our team, you’ll use your leadership skills and data science expertise to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll guide teammates and lead the development of algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to advise your clients as they make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.\n\nWork with us as we use data science for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 5+ years of experience with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining \n\n- 5+ years of experience with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis \n\n- 5+ years of experience analyzing structured and unstructured data sources  \n\n- Experience developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses, and visualization of targeted data sources  \n\n- Experience leading the development of solutions to complex programs \n\n- Experience with natural language processing, text mining, or machine learning techniques \n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have:    \n- Experience with Maven Smart Systems\n\n- Experience supporting the Department of War\n\n- Experience with Army and or Military Operational and Strategic planning\n\n- Experience in the development of algorithms leveraging R, Python, SQL, or NoSQL \n\n- Experience with distributed data and computing tools, including MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL  \n\n- Experience with visualization packages, including Plotly, Seaborn, or ggplot2 \n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\nClearance :\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors, from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence, we need you to help find the answers in the data. </p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your leadership skills and data science expertise to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll guide teammates and lead the development of algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to advise your clients as they make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we use data science for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining </p></li><li><p>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis </p></li><li><p>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> analyzing structured and unstructured data sources  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses, and visualization of targeted data sources  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> leading the development of solutions to complex programs </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with natural language processing, text mining, or machine learning techniques </p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor’s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Maven Smart Systems</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> supporting the Department of War</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Army and or Military Operational and Strategic planning</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> in the development of algorithms leveraging R, Python, SQL, or NoSQL </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with distributed data and computing tools, including MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with visualization packages, including Plotly, Seaborn, or ggplot2 </p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance</span></b><span>:</span></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"Germany","id":"dcc5b7608d8644b3a93716604e78e995"},"posted_on":"Posted 28 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:R0246228","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"R0246228","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"9413fada4dda28b03611219c7c6dff29d8ede6ba86f276acedba62b3df733850","fetched_at":"2026-08-20T07:20:48.759Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Scientist_R0246228","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Data-Scientist_R0246228","locations":[{"label":"Arlington, VA"},{"label":"Alexandria, VA"},{"label":"Washington, DC"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246228","internal_job_id":"6d3435a3a87a1001b1cff87c880f0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-11","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist The Opportunity:  \nAs a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi cia l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data. \n\nOn our team, you’ll use your analytical skills and data science knowledge to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll develop algorithms and systems and use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to help clients make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  \n\nWork with us as we use data science for good.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:    \n- 2+ years of experience with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining \n\n- 2+ years of experience with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis \n\n- Experience analyzing structured and unstructured data sources  \n\n- Experience developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses, and visualization of targeted data sources \n\n- Knowledge of Machine Learning, Artifi cia l Intelligence, or Natural Language Processing ( NLP )\n\n- Knowledge of text mining or machine learning techniques \n\n- TS/SCI clearance    \n\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have:    \n- 2+ years of experience in the development of algorithms leveraging R, Python, SQL, or NoSQL \n\n- 2+ years of experience with distributed data or computing tools, including Databricks, MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Apache Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL \n\n- 2+ years of experience with Machine Learning, AI, or NLP \n\n- Experience with Palantir Foundry\n\n- Experience with visualization packages, including Plotly, Seaborn, or ggplot2 \n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph   \n\n- Master’s degree   \n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b> </p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data. </p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your analytical skills and data science knowledge to create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll develop algorithms and systems and use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to help clients make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  </p><p></p><p>Work with us as we use data science for good.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining </p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> analyzing structured and unstructured data sources  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses, and visualization of targeted data sources </p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> Machine Learning, Artifi<span>cia</span>l Intelligence, or Natural Language Processing <span>(</span>NLP<span>)</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> text mining or machine learning techniques </p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span>   </p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor’s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b>   </p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in the development of algorithms leveraging R, Python, SQL, or NoSQL </p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with distributed data or computing tools, including Databricks, MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Apache Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL </p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with Machine Learning, AI, or NLP </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Palantir Foundry</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with visualization packages, including Plotly, Seaborn, or ggplot2 </p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</span>  </p></li><li><p><span>Master’s degree</span>  </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b> </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 9 Days Ago"},"status":"closed","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-20T07:20:48.759Z","closed_at":"2026-08-21T07:47:34.705Z","possibly_closed_at":"2026-08-20T19:35:50.646Z","missing_complete_scans":2,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Edgewood-MD/Data-Scientist---365-Developer_R0243435","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Edgewood-MD/Data-Scientist---365-Developer_R0243435","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"4934a81565bad5ea03ce904f09b550daf37509a810c1f5e4def26e9899e5a37c","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist & 365 Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Edgewood-MD/Data-Scientist---365-Developer_R0243435","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Edgewood-MD/Data-Scientist---365-Developer_R0243435","locations":[{"label":"Edgewood, MD"},{"label":"Belcamp, MD"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0243435","internal_job_id":"8f3baa969d4a10011af0106b8ef30000","first_published_at":"2026-06-30","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist & 365 Developer The Opportunity:\nAs a Data Scientist and 365 Developer supporting the U.S. Army, your primary focus will be building, enhancing, and sustaining Army applications for a wide range of mission stakeholders. You will integrate AI‑enabled analytics and Army Vantage capabilities into applications and workflows to support digital modernization and improve how the Army automates processes, generates insights, and makes data‑driven decisions. You will conduct verification and validation testing, deliver updates and enhancements, and manage a ticketing system to resolve user issues efficiently and keep applications mission‑ready.\n\nYou will perform advanced data mining to aggregate, transform, and analyze large datasets — summarizing information, identifying correlations, grouping data through clustering, and detecting anomalies that may inform operational decisions. In parallel, you will carry out data preprocessing to prepare datasets for analysis or integration into larger frameworks, including handling missing values, removing duplicates, and standardizing formats to ensure consistency and usability. You will also explore systems and Army platforms such as Vantage to identify opportunities for improved analytics, visualization, and enterprise data integration in support of CPE programs.\n\nBeyond analytics, you will develop, update, and maintain Army 365 SharePoint sites, lists, and document libraries in both unclassified and classified environments to support enterprise data management. This includes managing user permissions across SharePoint, Qlik, and Power Apps to maintain secure, appropriate access. You will maintain and update template files that capture key data elements across 18 core capability areas and ensure they align with Power Apps and other enterprise tools. To strengthen data governance, you will refine portfolio definitions, data dictionaries, and glossaries, ensuring consistent terminology and structure across Army systems and analytical platforms.\n\nThrough this work, you will enhance the U.S. Army's digital ecosystem by improving data quality, enabling AI‑supported insights, and delivering reliable tools that empower mission partners with the information they need to act with confidence.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 2+ years of experience with data exploration, cleaning, analysis, visualization, or data mining\n\n- 2+ years of experience with statistical or general‑purpose programming languages for data analysis\n\n- Experience with Army data platforms, including Vantage\n\n- Experience analyzing structured and unstructured data sources\n\n- Experience developing predictive models, quantitative analyses, or visualization of mission‑ relevant datasets\n\n- Experience with machine learning, artifi cia l intelligence, natural language processing, text‑mining techniques, or applying AI‑assisted analytics such as generative AI or LLMs to enhance workflows\n\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have:\n- 2+ years of experience developing algorithms leveraging R, Python, or SQL / NoSQL\n\n- 2+ years of experience with distributed data or computing tools such as MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL\n\n- 2+ years of experience with machine learning, AI, or NLP\n\n- Experience with visualization packages such as Plotly, Seaborn, or ggplot2\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information .\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist &amp; 365 Developer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As a Data Scientist and 365 Developer supporting the U.S. Army, your primary focus will be building, enhancing, and sustaining Army applications for a wide range of mission stakeholders. You will integrate AI‑enabled analytics and Army Vantage capabilities into applications and workflows to support digital modernization and improve how the Army automates processes, generates insights, and makes data‑driven decisions. You will conduct verification and validation testing, deliver updates and enhancements, and manage a ticketing system to resolve user issues efficiently and keep applications mission‑ready.</p><p></p><p>You will perform advanced data mining to aggregate, transform, and analyze large datasets — summarizing information, identifying correlations, grouping data through clustering, and detecting anomalies that may inform operational decisions. In parallel, you will carry out data preprocessing to prepare datasets for analysis or integration into larger frameworks, including handling missing values, removing duplicates, and standardizing formats to ensure consistency and usability. You will also explore systems and Army platforms such as Vantage to identify opportunities for improved analytics, visualization, and enterprise data integration in support of CPE programs.</p><p></p><p>Beyond analytics, you will develop, update, and maintain Army 365 SharePoint sites, lists, and document libraries in both unclassified and classified environments to support enterprise data management. This includes managing user permissions across SharePoint, Qlik, and Power Apps to maintain secure, appropriate access. You will maintain and update template files that capture key data elements across 18 core capability areas and ensure they align with Power Apps <span>and other</span> enterprise tools. To strengthen data governance, you will refine portfolio definitions, data dictionaries, and glossaries, ensuring consistent terminology and structure across Army systems and analytical platforms.</p><p></p><p>Through this work, you will enhance the U.S. Army&#39;s digital ecosystem by improving data quality, enabling AI‑supported insights, and delivering reliable tools that empower mission partners with the information they need to act with confidence.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with data exploration, cleaning, analysis, visualization, or data mining</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with statistical or general‑purpose programming languages for data analysis</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Army data platforms, including Vantage</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> analyzing structured and unstructured data sources</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> developing predictive models, quantitative analyses, or visualization of mission‑<span>relevant</span> datasets</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with machine learning, artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence, natural language processing, text‑mining techniques, or applying AI‑assisted analytics such as generative AI or LLMs to enhance workflows</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span><span> obtain a Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor’s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> developing algorithms leveraging R, Python, or SQL<span>/</span>NoSQL</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with distributed data or computing tools such as MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with machine learning, AI, or NLP</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with visualization packages such as Plotly, Seaborn, or ggplot2</p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span> with a polygraph</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span>.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":5,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data","software"],"role_matches":["Developer","Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Fort-Meade-MD/Data-Scientist-Network-Analyst_R0243036","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Fort-Meade-MD/Data-Scientist-Network-Analyst_R0243036","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"bca2a232ecd953cbd5bfc61087b4a02b32dc1a6552e93dcb93cffa2dc7ccd55b","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist Network Analyst","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Meade-MD/Data-Scientist-Network-Analyst_R0243036","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fort-Meade-MD/Data-Scientist-Network-Analyst_R0243036","locations":[{"label":"Fort Meade, MD"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0243036","internal_job_id":"691a3fab28b11001b2cb683aac690000","first_published_at":"2026-06-25","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist Network Analyst The Opportunity:\nDo you enjoy the thrill of the hunt? Are you motivated by the head-to-head challenge of gaining access to well-protected networks? As a network exploitation professional, you know that understanding the adversaries’ tactics, techniques, and procedures are crucial to producing the intel that enables the success of mission owners. At Booz Allen, you can apply your vulnerability analysis, network mapping, exploitation, defensive, and IT logging process experience to execute offensive cyber operations that inform our nation’s most critical security missions.\n\nAs a data scientist, this role would require building rapid analytic methodologies and tools in support of solving highly technical analytic intelligence problems. You'll work in a fast-paced environment with tight deadlines and high levels of uncertainty. You'll work with analysts and intelligence data sets closely to find new and innovative means of generating analytic findings. You'll work with developers to automate and streamline the methodologies they create into deployable and scalable solutions. You'll develop data visualizations from various data sources and tool suites with an emphasis on simplicity and interoperability. You'll also perform gap analysis and act as a key advisor for a new comprehensive data strategy for clients with an emphasis on providing analytic intelligence solutions.\n\nSafeguard the future with us and develop offensive cyber operations that are essential to providing national security for today and tomorrow.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 6+ years of experience in network analysis\n\n- Experience in scripting languages, including Perl and Python\n\n- Experience in the Transmission Control Protocol or Internet Protocol (TCP/IP) suite\n\n- Experience with networking components configuration\n\n- Knowledge of multiple operating system environments\n\n- Knowledge of server service platforms, including web, e-mail, and Domain Name System (DNS)\n\n- Knowledge of routed and switched environments and internet protocol (IP) concepts\n\n- Knowledge of complex and multi-source quantitative analysis\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- HS diploma or GED\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist Network Analyst<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p>Do you enjoy the thrill of the hunt? Are you motivated by the head-to-head challenge of gaining access to well-protected networks? As a network exploitation professional, you know that understanding the adversaries’ tactics, techniques, and procedures are crucial to producing the intel that enables the success of mission owners. At Booz Allen, you can apply your vulnerability analysis, network mapping, exploitation, defensive, and IT logging process experience to execute offensive cyber operations that inform our nation’s most critical security missions.</p><p></p><p>As a data scientist, this role would require building rapid analytic methodologies and tools in support of solving highly technical analytic intelligence problems. You&#39;ll work in a fast-paced environment with tight deadlines and high levels of uncertainty. You&#39;ll work with analysts and intelligence data sets closely to find new and innovative means of generating analytic findings. You&#39;ll work with developers to automate and streamline the methodologies they create into deployable and scalable solutions. You&#39;ll develop data visualizations from various data sources and tool suites with an emphasis on simplicity and interoperability. You&#39;ll also perform gap analysis and act as a key advisor for a new comprehensive data strategy for clients with an emphasis on providing analytic intelligence solutions.</p><p></p><p>Safeguard the future with us and develop offensive cyber operations that are essential to providing national security for today and tomorrow.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>6&#43; years of experience in network analysis</p></li><li><p>Experience in scripting languages, including Perl and Python</p></li><li><p>Experience in the Transmission Control Protocol or Internet Protocol (TCP/IP) suite</p></li><li><p>Experience with networking components configuration</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of multiple operating system environments</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of server service platforms, including web, e-mail, and Domain Name System (DNS)</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of routed and switched environments and internet protocol (IP) concepts</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of complex and multi-source quantitative analysis</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</p></li><li><p>HS diploma or GED</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/San-Antonio-TX/Data-Scientist--Junior_R0247418","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/San-Antonio-TX/Data-Scientist--Junior_R0247418","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"8a3b05982982b7337110976cfa9b4028b8029916b45dd0064216df0a01151dfc","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Data Scientist, Junior","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/San-Antonio-TX/Data-Scientist--Junior_R0247418","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/San-Antonio-TX/Data-Scientist--Junior_R0247418","locations":[{"label":"San Antonio, TX"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247418","internal_job_id":"ae74c1d5954e10016807f86dfbf00000","first_published_at":"2026-08-19","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Data Scientist, Junior The Opportunity:  \nAs a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data. \n\nOn our team, you’ll use your analytical skills to help create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll work with and learn from your teammates as you develop algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers so that your clients can make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  \n\nWork with us as we use data science for good. \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:   \n- Experience with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining  \n\n- Experience with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis \n\n- Knowledge of structured and unstructured data sources  \n\n- Knowledge of Machine Learning, Artificial Intelligence, or Natural Language Processing  \n\n- Ability to develop predictive data models, quantitative analyses and visualization of targeted data sources \n\n- Ability to deploy natural language processing, text mining, or machine learning techniques \n\n- TS/SCI clearance    \n\n- Bachelor’s degree \n\nNice If You Have:   \n- Experience in the development of algorithms leveraging R, Python, or SQL/NoSQL \n\n- Experience with distributed data and computing tools, including MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL  \n\n- Experience with visualization packages, including Plotly, Seaborn, or ggplot2 \n\n- DoD 8570 IAT Level II Certification\n\nClearance:   \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Data Scientist, Junior<p><b>The Opportunity:  </b></p><p>As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a data scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data. </p><p></p><p>On our team, you’ll use your analytical skills to help create real-world impact. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll work with and learn from your teammates as you develop algorithms and systems. You’ll use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers so that your clients can make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.  </p><p></p><p>Work with us as we use data science for good. </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining  </p></li><li><p>Experience with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis </p></li><li><p>Knowledge of structured and unstructured data sources  </p></li><li><p>Knowledge of Machine Learning, Artificial Intelligence, or Natural Language Processing  </p></li><li><p>Ability to develop predictive data models, quantitative analyses and visualization of targeted data sources </p></li><li><p>Ability to deploy natural language processing, text mining, or machine learning techniques </p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance    </p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience in the development of algorithms leveraging R, Python, or SQL/NoSQL </p></li><li><p>Experience with distributed data and computing tools, including MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL  </p></li><li><p>Experience with visualization packages, including Plotly, Seaborn, or ggplot2 </p></li><li><p>DoD 8570 IAT Level II Certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b>  </p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 5 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
