{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Chantilly-VA/Kubernetes-Platform-Engineer_R0242275","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Chantilly-VA/Kubernetes-Platform-Engineer_R0242275","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"d1d736b860243e0962f6aa929d9c97f9f258cf20151f8b0a140928bd0d1afcf1","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Kubernetes Platform Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Kubernetes-Platform-Engineer_R0242275","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Kubernetes-Platform-Engineer_R0242275","locations":[{"label":"Chantilly, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0242275","internal_job_id":"691a3fab28b11000bce5e536bde90000","first_published_at":"2026-06-30","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Kubernetes Platform Engineer The Opportunity:\nEveryone is trying to “harness the cloud,” but not everyone knows how. As a DevOps engineer, you’re eager to develop, manage, and secure a container platform that meets your client’s needs and takes advantage of cloud capabilities. We need you to develop container management sof tware to solve some of our clients’ toughest challenges. \n \nAs a senior platform DevOps engineer at Booz Allen, you can use your technical skills to affect mission-forward change. On our team, you’ll hone your skills using the latest cloud technologies as you look for ways to improve your client’s environment with current container sof tware to ensure seamless orchestration. Using your DevOps platform experience , you’ll support your team as you inform strategy and design while ensuring standards are met throughout the containerization process.\n\nYou’ll recommend resources that will help your client manage and securely adopt containers. Additionally, you’ll continue to strengthen your DevOps skills while supporting the development of critical cloud platforms. This position is located in Chantilly, VA.\n\nWork with us to use cloud platform technology for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 5+ years of experience in platform engineering or systems engineering within classified environments\n\n- 5+ years of experience with AWS, including IAM, VPC, EC2, ELB / ALB / NLB, and CloudWatch\n\n- 5+ years of experience with cloud environments, programming languages, and supporting CI / CD\n\n- Experience operating production Kubernetes clusters\n\n- Experience  with Linux‑based systems such as RedHat or CentOS and scripting languages such as Python or Bash\n\n- Experience creating technical documentation, system diagrams, and SOPs \n\n- Knowledge of Kubernetes networking, container registry management, and image‑hardening approaches\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- HS diploma or GED and 9+ years of experience in DevSecOps or Bachelor's degree and 5+ years of experience in DevSecOps\n\nNice If You Have:\n- E xperience with using AI tools for development\n\n- Experience supporting Intelligence Community mission partners\n\n- Experience operating AWS EKS\n\n- Knowledge of  cloud‑native tooling or vulnerability‑analysis concepts\n\n- Knowledge of modernization frameworks used across mission programs\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Kubernetes Platform Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>Everyone is trying to “harness the cloud,” but not everyone knows how. As a DevOps engineer, you’re eager to develop, manage, and secure a container platform that meets your client’s needs and takes advantage of cloud capabilities. We need you to develop container management <span>sof</span>tware to solve some of our clients’ toughest challenges. <br /> <br />As a senior platform DevOps engineer at Booz Allen, you can use your technical skills to affect mission-forward change. On our team, you’ll hone your skills using the latest cloud technologies as you look for ways to improve your client’s environment with <span>current</span> container <span>sof</span>tware to ensure seamless orchestration. Using your DevOps platform <span>experience</span>, you’ll support your team as you inform strategy and design while ensuring standards are <span>met</span> throughout the containerization process.</p><p></p><p>You’ll recommend resources that will help your client manage and securely adopt containers. Additionally, you’ll continue to strengthen your DevOps skills while supporting the development of critical cloud platforms. This position is located in Chantilly, VA.</p><p></p><p>Work with us to use cloud platform technology for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in platform engineering or systems engineering within classified environments</p></li><li><p>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with AWS, including IAM, VPC, EC2, ELB<span>/</span>ALB<span>/</span>NLB, and CloudWatch</p></li><li><p>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with cloud environments, programming languages, and supporting CI<span>/</span>CD</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> operating production Kubernetes clusters</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Linux‑based systems such as RedHat or CentOS and scripting languages such as Python or Bash</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> creating technical documentation, system diagrams, and SOPs </p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> Kubernetes networking, container registry management, and image‑hardening approaches</p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</span></p></li><li><p><span>HS diploma or GED and 9&#43; years of experience in DevSecOps or Bachelor&#39;s degree and 5&#43; years of experience in DevSecOps</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p>E<span>xperience with using AI tools for development</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> supporting Intelligence Community mission partners</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> operating AWS EKS</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> cloud‑native tooling or vulnerability‑analysis concepts</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> modernization frameworks used across mission programs</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Platform Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Platform"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Fayetteville-NC/Kubernetes-Platform-Engineer_R0245381","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Fayetteville-NC/Kubernetes-Platform-Engineer_R0245381","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"8325f57e09b5487f490a548d6cde97a0bca6bbcdf6c79651f8572f77376ba75a","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Kubernetes Platform Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fayetteville-NC/Kubernetes-Platform-Engineer_R0245381","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Fayetteville-NC/Kubernetes-Platform-Engineer_R0245381","locations":[{"label":"Fayetteville, NC"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245381","internal_job_id":"d2fc07c005731000bfd8f20edf300000","first_published_at":"2026-07-27","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Kubernetes Platform Engineer The Opportunity:\nManage, administer, support, and enhance cloud environments, ensuring continuous improvement and rapid problem resolution. Apply advanced skills, extensive te chn ical expertise, and full industry knowledge. Develop innovative solutions to complex problems. Work without considerable direction, mentor, and supervise team members.\n\nYou Have:\n- 3+ years of experience with Kubernetes\n\n- Experience with Docker\n\n- Experience with version control\n\n- Experience with CI / CD\n\n- Knowledge of Terraform\n\n- Ability to obtain a Top Secret clearance\n\n- HS diploma or GED\n\n- Ability to obtain DoD 8570 IAT Level II Certification within 2 months of hire date\n\n \nNice If You Have:\n- Experience managing and deploying applications in an air-gapped environment\n\n- Experience with Agile development methodologies and working on Agile teams using collaboration tools, including Jira, Confluence, or Discourse\n\n- Experience creating and c ond ucting automated unit and system integration tests to identify and provide feedback on failed modules and components\n\n- Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills, to communicate te chn ical ideas and deliver briefings with cross-functional teams\n\n- Possession of excellent listening skills\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information .\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Kubernetes Platform Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p>Manage, administer, support, and enhance cloud environments, ensuring continuous improvement and rapid problem resolution. Apply advanced skills, extensive te<span>chn</span>ical expertise, and full industry knowledge. Develop innovative solutions to complex problems. Work without considerable direction, mentor, and supervise team members.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>3&#43; years of experience with Kubernetes</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with Docker</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with version control </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with CI<span>/</span>CD </span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of Terraform</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to obtain a Top Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>HS diploma or GED</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to obtain DoD 8570 IAT Level II Certification within 2 months of hire date</span></p></li></ul><p><span> </span></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience managing and deploying applications in an air-gapped environment</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with Agile development methodologies and working on Agile teams using collaboration tools, including Jira, Confluence, or Discourse</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience creating and c<span>ond</span>ucting automated unit and system integration tests to identify and provide feedback on failed modules and components</span></p></li><li><p><span>Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills, to communicate te<span>chn</span>ical ideas and deliver briefings with cross-functional teams</span></p></li><li><p><span>Possession of excellent listening skills</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 28 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Platform Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Platform"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Wright-Patterson-AFB-OH/Kubernetes-Platform-Engineer_R0246966","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Wright-Patterson-AFB-OH/Kubernetes-Platform-Engineer_R0246966","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"828820f6c39927794d98af0bab0ee1eacc4b242eb17c669d604360368954d361","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Kubernetes Platform Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Wright-Patterson-AFB-OH/Kubernetes-Platform-Engineer_R0246966","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Wright-Patterson-AFB-OH/Kubernetes-Platform-Engineer_R0246966","locations":[{"label":"Wright Patterson AFB, OH"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246966","internal_job_id":"83b83551a7591001b25bb80594610000","first_published_at":"2026-08-13","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Kubernetes Platform Engineer The Opportunity:\nEveryone is trying to “harness the cloud,” but not everyone knows how. As a DevOps engineer, you’re eager to develop, manage, and secure a container platform that meets your client’s needs and takes advantage of cloud capabilities. We need you to develop container management software to solve some of our clients’ toughest challenges. \n \nAs a senior platform DevOps engineer at Booz Allen, you can use your technical skills to affect mission-forward change. On our team, you’ll hone your skills using the latest cloud technologies as you look for ways to improve your client’s environment with current container software to ensure seamless orchestration. Using your DevOps platform experience, you’ll support your team as you inform strategy and design while ensuring standards are met throughout the containerization process.\n\nYou’ll recommend resources that will help your client manage and securely adopt containers. Additionally, you’ll continue to strengthen your DevOps skills while supporting the development of critical cloud platforms. This position is located in Dayton, OH.\n\nWork with us to use cloud platform technology for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:  \n- 10+ years of experience in platform engineering or systems engineering within classified environments\n\n- 5+ years of experience with cloud environments, programming languages, and supporting CI/CD\n\n- Experience supporting Kubernetes networking, including concepts such as Services, Ingress, network policies, load balancing, DNS, and Container Network Interface (CNI) technologies\n\n- Experience designing and troubleshooting networks supporting containerized or microservices-based applications\n\n- Experience with network automation and Infrastructure as Code, using technologies such as Python, Ansible, or Terraform\n\n- Experience operating production Kubernetes clusters and creating technical documentation, system diagrams, and SOPs \n\n- Experience with Linux‑based systems such as RedHat or CentOS, Linux administration and networking particularly in environments supporting Kubernetes or container platforms, and scripting languages such as Python or Bash\n\n- Knowledge of Kubernetes networking, container registry management, and image‑hardening approaches\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- HS diploma or GED\n\n  \nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience operating AWS EKS\n\n- Experience managing and deploying applications in an air-gapped environment\n\n- Experience with Agile development methodologies and working on Agile teams using collaboration tools, including Jira, Confluence, or Discourse\n\n- Experience with technologies such as Calico, Cilium, Flannel, Istio, service mesh, VMware NSX, Cisco ACI, F5, cloud networking, Helm, Terraform, and GitOps\n\n- Knowledge of cloud‑native tooling or vulnerability‑analysis concepts\n\n- Knowledge of modernization frameworks used across mission programs\n\n- Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Engineering, Cybersecurity, or technical discipline\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Kubernetes Platform Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p>Everyone is trying to “harness the cloud,” but not everyone knows how. As a DevOps engineer, you’re eager to develop, manage, and secure a container platform that meets your client’s needs and takes advantage of cloud capabilities. We need you to develop container management software to solve some of our clients’ toughest challenges. <br /> <br />As a senior platform DevOps engineer at Booz Allen, you can use your technical skills to affect mission-forward change. On our team, you’ll hone your skills using the latest cloud technologies as you look for ways to improve your client’s environment with current container software to ensure seamless orchestration. Using your DevOps platform experience, you’ll support your team as you inform strategy and design while ensuring standards are met throughout the containerization process.</p><p></p><p>You’ll recommend resources that will help your client manage and securely adopt containers. Additionally, you’ll continue to strengthen your DevOps skills while supporting the development of critical cloud platforms. This position is located in Dayton, OH.</p><p></p><p>Work with us to use cloud platform technology for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:  </b></p><ul><li><p>10&#43; years of experience in platform engineering or systems engineering within classified environments</p></li><li><p>5&#43; years of experience with cloud environments, programming languages, and supporting CI/CD</p></li><li><p>Experience supporting Kubernetes networking, including concepts such as Services, Ingress, network policies, load balancing, DNS, and Container Network Interface (CNI) technologies</p></li><li><p>Experience designing and troubleshooting networks supporting containerized or microservices-based applications</p></li><li><p>Experience with network automation and Infrastructure as Code, using technologies such as Python, Ansible, or Terraform</p></li><li><p>Experience operating production Kubernetes clusters and creating technical documentation, system diagrams, and SOPs </p></li><li><p>Experience with Linux‑based systems such as RedHat or CentOS, Linux administration and networking particularly in environments supporting Kubernetes or container platforms, and scripting languages such as Python or Bash</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of Kubernetes networking, container registry management, and image‑hardening approaches</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance</p></li><li><p>HS diploma or GED</p></li></ul><p>  </p><p><b>Nice If You Have:  </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience operating AWS EKS</p></li><li><p>Experience managing and deploying applications in an air-gapped environment</p></li><li><p>Experience with Agile development methodologies and working on Agile teams using collaboration tools, including Jira, Confluence, or Discourse</p></li><li><p>Experience with technologies such as Calico, Cilium, Flannel, Istio, service mesh, VMware NSX, Cisco ACI, F5, cloud networking, Helm, Terraform, and GitOps</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of cloud‑native tooling or vulnerability‑analysis concepts</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of modernization frameworks used across mission programs</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Engineering, Cybersecurity, or technical discipline</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 11 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included"