{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Suffolk-VA/Model-and-Simulation-Software-Engineer_R0245326","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Suffolk-VA/Model-and-Simulation-Software-Engineer_R0245326","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"249d47fc302465d1c0db53b706c2a28bb766401344ac7cf3c0e831554afa9049","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Model and Simulation Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Suffolk-VA/Model-and-Simulation-Software-Engineer_R0245326","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Suffolk-VA/Model-and-Simulation-Software-Engineer_R0245326","locations":[{"label":"Suffolk, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245326","internal_job_id":"d2fc07c005731000ba994c4e71360000","first_published_at":"2026-07-30","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Model and Simulation Software Engineer The Opportunity: \nYou will play a critical role in advancing our Modeling and Simulation (M&S) capabilities by designing, developing, and integrating AI‑enabled models that support complex wargaming and operational decision‑making for the DoW. Using core software engineering principles, you’ll build scalable simulation components, create realistic behavioral and environmental models, and integrate diverse data sources to drive high‑fidelity outcomes. You’ll collaborate closely with analysts, domain experts, and other engineers to ensure that models accurately represent real‑world conditions and evolving mission needs.\n\nAs part of this effort, you’ll apply full‑stack engineering skills to shape the technical vision for next‑generation M&S systems by evaluating new frameworks, enhancing simulation performance, and implementing architectures that support future extensibility. Your contributions will directly influence how clients explore scenarios, assess alternatives, and derive insights from complex simulation environments.\n\nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- Experience with developing software in Java, C++, C, and or C#\n\n- Experience with version control, documentation practices, and GitLab workflows\n\n- Experience working in Linux environments\n\n- Knowledge of the Distributed Interactive Simulation (DIS) networking protocol\n\n- Knowledge of COTS and GOTS Modeling & Simulation (M&S) and data tools, such as Modern Air Combat Environment (MACE), Mission Object Configuration Tool (MOCT), Virtual Reality Scene Generator (VRSG), and various Image Generators (IG) for data transformation, configuration, and standardization\n\n- Knowledge of combat weapons systems including aircraft, ground‑based radars, and surface‑to‑air systems\n\n- Ability to write clean, efficient source code for new applications and enhance existing codebases\n\n- Ability to support the evaluation, selection, and integration of M&S tools\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- HS diploma or GED\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience developing AFSIM scripts to tailor model behaviors and scenario configurations\n\n- Experience with TAK products\n\n- Experience working within the SOF communities\n\n- Experience building and managing containers\n\n- Experience building DevSecOps environments or pipelines\n\n- Knowledge of scenario development and analytical assessments of combat weapon systems using Live, Virtual, and Constructive (LVC) simulation tools\n\n- Ability to distill, summarize, and communicate complex technical insights related to model library management and dissemination\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Model and Simulation Software Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><div><p>You will play a critical role in advancing our Modeling and Simulation (M&amp;S) capabilities by designing, developing, and integrating AI‑enabled models that support complex wargaming and operational decision‑making for the DoW. Using core software engineering principles, you’ll build scalable simulation components, create realistic behavioral and environmental models, and integrate diverse data sources to drive high‑fidelity outcomes. You’ll collaborate closely with analysts, domain experts, and other engineers to ensure that models accurately represent real‑world conditions and evolving mission needs.</p><p></p><p>As part of this effort, you’ll apply full‑stack engineering skills to shape the technical vision for next‑generation M&amp;S systems by evaluating new frameworks, enhancing simulation performance, and implementing architectures that support future extensibility. Your contributions will directly influence how clients explore scenarios, assess alternatives, and derive insights from complex simulation environments.</p></div><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience with developing software in Java, C&#43;&#43;, C, and or C#</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with version control, documentation practices, and GitLab workflows</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience working in Linux environments</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of the Distributed Interactive Simulation (DIS) networking protocol</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of COTS and GOTS Modeling &amp; Simulation (M&amp;S) and data tools, such as Modern Air Combat Environment (MACE), Mission Object Configuration Tool (MOCT), Virtual Reality Scene Generator (VRSG), and various Image Generators (IG) for data transformation, configuration, and standardization</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of combat weapons systems including aircraft, ground‑based radars, and surface‑to‑air systems</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to write clean, efficient source code for new applications and enhance existing codebases</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to support the evaluation, selection, and integration of M&amp;S tools</span></p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>HS diploma or GED </span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience developing AFSIM scripts to tailor model behaviors and scenario configurations</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with TAK products</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience working within the SOF communities</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience building and managing containers</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience building DevSecOps environments or pipelines</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of scenario development and analytical assessments of combat weapon systems using Live, Virtual, and Constructive (LVC) simulation tools</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to distill, summarize, and communicate complex technical insights related to model library management and dissemination</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 25 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Suffolk-VA/Model-and-Simulation-Software-Engineer_R0245332","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Suffolk-VA/Model-and-Simulation-Software-Engineer_R0245332","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"aa40d42ade35a95b76ea43a8f300c7d83de898f57c979fb78bee3dfa17c91275","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Model and Simulation Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Suffolk-VA/Model-and-Simulation-Software-Engineer_R0245332","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Suffolk-VA/Model-and-Simulation-Software-Engineer_R0245332","locations":[{"label":"Suffolk, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245332","internal_job_id":"45e74e1697ae1000b8495c2bbcc00000","first_published_at":"2026-08-04","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Model and Simulation Software Engineer The Opportunity: \nYou will play a critical role in advancing our Modeling and Simulation (M&S) capabilities by designing, developing, and integrating AI‑enabled models that support complex wargaming and operational decision‑making for the DoW. Using core software engineering principles, you’ll build scalable simulation components, create realistic behavioral and environmental models, and integrate diverse data sources to drive high‑fidelity outcomes. You’ll collaborate closely with analysts, domain experts, and other engineers to ensure that models accurately represent real‑world conditions and evolving mission needs.\n\nAs part of this effort, you’ll apply full‑stack engineering skills to shape the technical vision for next‑generation M&S systems by evaluating new frameworks, enhancing simulation performance, and implementing architectures that support future extensibility. Your contributions will directly influence how clients explore scenarios, assess alternatives, and derive insights from complex simulation environments.\n\nJoin us. The world can't wait. \n\nYou Have:\n- Experience with developing software in Java, C++, C, or C#\n\n- Experience with version control, documentation practices, and GitLab workflows\n\n- Experience working in Linux environments\n\n- Knowledge of the Distributed Interactive Simulation (DIS) networking protocol\n\n- Knowledge of COTS and GOTS Modeling & Simulation (M&S) and data tools, such as Modern Air Combat Environment (MACE), Mission Object Configuration Tool (MOCT), Virtual Reality Scene Generator (VRSG), and various Image Generators (IG) for data transformation, configuration, and standardization\n\n- Knowledge of combat weapons systems including aircraft, ground‑based radars, and surface‑to‑air systems\n\n- Ability to write clean, efficient source code for new applications and enhance existing codebases\n\n- Ability to support the evaluation, selection, and integration of M&S tools\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- HS diploma or GED\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience developing AFSIM scripts to tailor model behaviors and scenario configurations\n\n- Experience with TAK products\n\n- Experience working within the SOF communities\n\n- Experience building and managing containers\n\n- Experience building DevSecOps environments or pipelines\n\n- Knowledge of scenario development and analytical assessments of combat weapon systems using Live, Virtual, and Constructive (LVC) simulation tools\n\n- Ability to distill, summarize, and communicate complex technical insights related to model library management and dissemination\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Model and Simulation Software Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><div><p>You will play a critical role in advancing our Modeling and Simulation (M&amp;S) capabilities by designing, developing, and integrating AI‑enabled models that support complex wargaming and operational decision‑making for the DoW. Using core software engineering principles, you’ll build scalable simulation components, create realistic behavioral and environmental models, and integrate diverse data sources to drive high‑fidelity outcomes. You’ll collaborate closely with analysts, domain experts, and other engineers to ensure that models accurately represent real‑world conditions and evolving mission needs.</p><p></p><p>As part of this effort, you’ll apply full‑stack engineering skills to shape the technical vision for next‑generation M&amp;S systems by evaluating new frameworks, enhancing simulation performance, and implementing architectures that support future extensibility. Your contributions will directly influence how clients explore scenarios, assess alternatives, and derive insights from complex simulation environments.</p></div><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience with developing software in Java, C&#43;&#43;, C, or C#</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with version control, documentation practices, and GitLab workflows</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience working in Linux environments</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of the Distributed Interactive Simulation (DIS) networking protocol</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of COTS and GOTS Modeling &amp; Simulation (M&amp;S) and data tools, such as Modern Air Combat Environment (MACE), Mission Object Configuration Tool (MOCT), Virtual Reality Scene Generator (VRSG), and various Image Generators (IG) for data transformation, configuration, and standardization</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of combat weapons systems including aircraft, ground‑based radars, and surface‑to‑air systems</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to write clean, efficient source code for new applications and enhance existing codebases</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to support the evaluation, selection, and integration of M&amp;S tools</span></p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>HS diploma or GED</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience developing AFSIM scripts to tailor model behaviors and scenario configurations</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with TAK products</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience working within the SOF communities</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience building and managing containers</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience building DevSecOps environments or pipelines</span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of scenario development and analytical assessments of combat weapon systems using Live, Virtual, and Constructive (LVC) simulation tools</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to distill, summarize, and communicate complex technical insights related to model library management and dissemination</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 20 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/China-Lake-CA/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0239355","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/China-Lake-CA/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0239355","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"985d6ddfe7980d6d59e59acf79d0333e0dc2e57649eccd316450819f81096d6f","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Model Based Systems Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/China-Lake-CA/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0239355","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/China-Lake-CA/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0239355","locations":[{"label":"China Lake, CA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0239355","internal_job_id":"6a0b6aa3b5851001f90ae3f78e6b0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-12","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Model Based Systems Engineer The Opportunity :\nAre you looking for an opportunity to combine your technical skills with big picture thinking to make an impact in national security? You understand your customer’s environment and how to develop the right systems for their mission. Your ability to translate real-world needs into technical specifications makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused engineering solution.  \n\nAs a systems engineer on our team, you’ll have the chance to shape Integrated System Architecture development processes. Your customer will t rus t you to not only design and develop these systems, but also evolve them with advanced technology solutions. On our team, you’ll be able to broaden your skill set into areas like MBSE and systems engineering. You will create, integrate, and apply interdisciplinary digital models of products from concept throughout the product lifecycle. You’ll apply advanced skills, extensive technical expertise, and full industry knowledge . You’ll develop innovative solutions to complex problems and work without considerable direction.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have: \n- 3+ years of experience performing systems engineering analysis and developing systems engineering products for DoD or government systems\n\n- 2+ years of experience with practical Model Based Systems Engineering ( MBSE ) met hodologies for the development of technical specifications, interface control documents, and system architecture, including using digital engineering tools such as Cameo Enterprise Architect or MagicDraw, SparxEA, DOORS, or IBM rhapsody and Teamwork Cloud\n\n- Experience participating in architecture working groups and technical interchange meetings to communicate and review architectural models\n\n- Ability to perform multiple systems engineering functions in support of design reviews and requirements verification \n\n- Ability to analyze and model complex systems architectures, ensuring all components and interfaces are accurately represented\n\n- Ability to work effectively in a team-oriented environment and collaborate with stakeholders, engineers, and program managers to gather requirements and understand system interactions\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree in a STEM field\n\nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience with U.S. Navy systems engineering\n\n- Experience creating automated deliverable artifacts such as technical reports, custom documents, or dashboards using model-based tools\n\n- Knowledge of MagicGrid, Unified Architecture Framework  ( UAF ) , and DoD Architecture Framework  ( DoDAF ) met hodologies\n\n- Possession of excellent communication, interpersonal, and presentation skills\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- Master’s degree in Engineering\n\n- INCOSE ASEP and OCSMP 2 Certification s\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Model Based Systems Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity</span></b><b>:</b></p><p>Are you looking for an opportunity to combine your technical skills with big picture thinking to make an impact in national security? You understand your customer’s environment and how to develop the right systems for their mission. Your <span>ability to</span> translate real-world needs into technical specifications makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused engineering solution.  </p><p></p><p>As a systems engineer on our team, you’ll have the chance to shape Integrated System Architecture development processes. Your customer will t<span>rus</span>t you to not only design and develop these systems, but also evolve them with advanced technology solutions. On our team, you’ll be able to broaden your skill set into areas like MBSE and systems engineering. You will create, integrate, and apply interdisciplinary digital models of products from concept throughout the product lifecycle. You’ll apply advanced skills, extensive technical expertise, and full industry <span>knowledge</span>. You’ll develop innovative solutions to complex problems and work without considerable direction.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> performing systems engineering analysis and developing systems engineering products for DoD or government systems</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with practical Model Based Systems Engineering <span>(</span>MBSE<span>)</span> <span>met</span>hodologies for the development of technical specifications, interface control documents, and system architecture, including using digital engineering tools such as Cameo Enterprise Architect or MagicDraw, SparxEA, DOORS, or IBM rhapsody and Teamwork Cloud</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> participating in architecture working groups and technical interchange meetings to communicate and review architectural models</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> perform multiple systems engineering functions in support of design reviews and requirements verification </p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> analyze and model complex systems architectures, ensuring all components and interfaces are accurately represented</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> work effectively in a team-oriented environment and collaborate with stakeholders, engineers, and program managers to gather requirements and understand system interactions</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span> in a STEM field</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b> </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with U.S. Navy systems engineering</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> creating automated deliverable artifacts such as technical reports, custom documents, or dashboards using model-based tools</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge</span> of MagicGrid, Unified Architecture Framework <span>(</span>UAF<span>)</span>, and DoD Architecture Framework <span>(</span>DoDAF<span>)</span> <span>met</span>hodologies</p></li><li><p><span>Possession of</span> excellent communication, interpersonal, and presentation skills</p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Master’s degree</span> in Engineering</p></li><li><p>INCOSE ASEP and OCSMP 2 <span>Certification</span>s</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 12 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Systems Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Langley-AFB-VA/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0241821","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Langley-AFB-VA/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0241821","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"cd76d3e658119e9822476f75832784954059c4440b649be4da781138bca885b0","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Model Based Systems Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Langley-AFB-VA/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0241821","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Langley-AFB-VA/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0241821","locations":[{"label":"Langley AFB, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0241821","internal_job_id":"da27679bc1171001071aa4171c230000","first_published_at":"2026-06-09","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Model Based Systems Engineer The Opportunity:\nCreates, integrates, and applies interdisciplinary digital models of products from concept throughout the product lifecycle. Applies advanced advisory skills and extensive technical expertise with full industry knowledge. Develops innovative solutions to complex problems. Works without considerable direction. Mentors and may supervise team members.\n\nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 3+ years of experience performing systems engineering analysis and developing systems engineering products for DoW or government systems or capabilities\n\n- 2+ years of experience with practical Model Based Systems Engineering for the development of technical specifications, interface control documents, and system architecture, including using digital engineering tools such as Cameo\n\n- Experience developing enterprise or mission architectures using the Unified Architecture Framework (UAF)\n\n- Ability to critically think through the use of mission architectures and mission engineering threads to inform analysis and generate assessments that answer investigative questions pertaining to alternatives analysis, cause and effect, or capability gap identification\n\n- Ability to communicate and establish collaborative relationships with government clients\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree in Science, Technology, Engineering, or Mathematics\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with Model-Based Verification and Validation\n\n- Experience with MATLAB, STK, ModelCenter, or TeamCenter\n\n- Ability to identify, analyze, and resolve technical risks and issues, develop technical reports, and collaborate with government and other stakeholders to implement recommended solutions\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- Master’s degree in Engineering\n\n- OMG Certified Systems Model Professional (OCSMP) Certification\n\n- INCOSE SE Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Model Based Systems Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p>Creates, integrates, and applies interdisciplinary digital models of products from concept throughout the product lifecycle. Applies advanced advisory skills and extensive technical expertise with full industry knowledge. Develops innovative solutions to complex problems. Works without considerable direction. Mentors and may supervise team members.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of experience performing systems engineering analysis and developing systems engineering products for DoW or government systems or capabilities</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with practical Model Based Systems Engineering for the development of technical specifications, interface control documents, and system architecture, including using digital engineering tools such as Cameo</p></li><li><p>Experience developing enterprise or mission architectures using the Unified Architecture Framework (UAF)</p></li><li><p>Ability to critically think through the use of mission architectures and mission engineering threads to inform analysis and generate assessments that answer investigative questions pertaining to alternatives analysis, cause and effect, or capability gap identification</p></li><li><p>Ability to communicate and establish collaborative relationships with government clients</p></li><li><p>Secret clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree in Science, Technology, Engineering, or Mathematics</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with Model-Based Verification and Validation</p></li><li><p>Experience with MATLAB, STK, ModelCenter, or TeamCenter</p></li><li><p>Ability to identify, analyze, and resolve technical risks and issues, develop technical reports, and collaborate with government and other stakeholders to implement recommended solutions</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance</p></li><li><p>Master’s degree in Engineering</p></li><li><p>OMG Certified Systems Model Professional (OCSMP) Certification</p></li><li><p>INCOSE SE Certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Systems Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
