{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Aurora-CO/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0237165","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Aurora-CO/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0237165","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"8cff7e99aca8824a8dd9546b9cf1e79fc7048b8ecf708aa54df2e81c01728414","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Model-Based Systems Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Aurora-CO/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0237165","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Aurora-CO/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0237165","locations":[{"label":"Aurora, CO"},{"label":"Colorado Springs, CO"},{"label":"El Segundo, CA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0237165","internal_job_id":"9b3a2a0253721002053c451e00a50000","first_published_at":"2026-07-14","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Model-Based Systems Engineer The Opportunity:\nCreate, integrate, and apply interdisciplinary digital models of products from concept throughout the product lifecycle. Apply advanced consult ing skills or extensive technical expertise and full industry knowledge . Develop innovative solutions to complex problems. Work without considerable direction. Mentor and may supervise team members.\n\nYou Have:\n- 3+ years of experience with large-scale missions and systems engineering and integration\n\n- 3+ years of experience performing systems engineering analysis and developing systems engineering products for DoD or government systems\n\n- 3+ years of experience with practical MBSE for the development of technical specifications, interface control documents, and system architecture, including using digital engineering tools such as Cameo or MagicDraw, SparxEA, DOORS, or IBM Rhapsody\n\n- Ability to perform multiple systems engineering and program management functions in support of design reviews and requirements verification \n\n- Ability to communicate and establish collaborative relationships with government clients, Federally Funded Research and Development  Center s  ( FFRDC ) , and asso cia te contractor teammates to achieve program goals\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree in a Science, Technology, Engineering, or Mathematics field\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with Model-Based Verification and Validation\n\n- Experience with MATLAB, STK, Model Center , or Team Center\n\n- Experience analyzing and translating system requirements into design\n\n- Knowledge of Systems Modeling Language ( SysML )  and DoD Architecture Framework  ( DoDAF )\n\n- Ability to identify, analyze, and resolve technical risks and issues, develop technical reports, and collaborate with government  and other stakeholders to implement recommended solutions \n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- Master’s degree in Engineering\n\n- OMG Certified Systems Model Professional  ( OCSMP )   Certification\n\n- INCOSE SE Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,900.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Model-Based Systems Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>Create, integrate, and apply interdisciplinary digital models of products from concept throughout the product lifecycle. Apply advanced <span>consult</span>ing skills or extensive technical expertise and full industry <span>knowledge</span>. Develop innovative solutions to complex problems. Work without considerable direction. Mentor and may supervise team members.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with large-scale missions and systems engineering and integration</p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> performing systems engineering analysis and developing systems engineering products for DoD or government systems</p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with practical MBSE for the development of technical specifications, interface control documents, and system architecture, including using digital engineering tools such as Cameo or MagicDraw, SparxEA, DOORS, or IBM Rhapsody</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> perform multiple systems engineering and program management functions in support of design reviews and requirements verification </p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> communicate and establish collaborative relationships with government clients, Federally Funded Research and Development <span>Center</span>s <span>(</span>FFRDC<span>)</span>, and asso<span>cia</span>te contractor teammates to achieve program goals</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span> in a Science, Technology, Engineering, or Mathematics field</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Model-Based Verification and Validation</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with MATLAB, STK, Model<span>Center</span>, or Team<span>Center</span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> analyzing and translating system requirements into design</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge</span> of Systems Modeling Language <span>(</span>SysML<span>)</span> and DoD Architecture Framework <span>(</span>DoDAF<span>)</span></p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> identify, analyze, and resolve technical risks and issues, develop technical reports, and collaborate with government <span>and other</span> stakeholders to implement recommended solutions </p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Master’s degree</span> in Engineering</p></li><li><p>OMG Certified Systems Model Professional <span>(</span>OCSMP<span>)</span> <span>Certification</span></p></li><li><p>INCOSE SE <span>Certification</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,900.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Systems Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Beavercreek-OH/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0247258-1","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Beavercreek-OH/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0247258-1","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"b399da5a438d62bb808d605713ab1ead4475d2017d612b8e3bde1e8e23caa90b","fetched_at":"2026-08-21T07:47:34.705Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Model-Based Systems Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Beavercreek-OH/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0247258-1","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Beavercreek-OH/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0247258-1","locations":[{"label":"Beavercreek, OH"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247258","internal_job_id":"ce7800f7d14610010ae1d9d34ee30001","first_published_at":"2026-08-18","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Model-Based Systems Engineer The Opportunity:\nAre you looking for an opportunity to combine your technical skills with big picture thinking to make an impact on advancing Model-Based Systems Engineering ( MBSE ) practices to help build a digital engineering (DE) cloud platform ecosystem for the DoD? You understand your customer’s environment and how to architect and develop, with the support of DevSecOps engineers, the right DE ecosystem for their mission. Your ability to translate real-world needs into technical specifications makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused DE solution.\n\nAs a Model-Based Systems Engineer on our team, you’ll work with Booz Allen colleagues and the U.S. Air Force to enable science and technology digital transformation. Your customer will t rus t you to not only analyze, evaluate, architect, and assist the government with modeling these DE capabilities and systems, but also identifying areas requiring urgent mitigation up-front and early, or suggesting ways to enhance user experience to develop this system with advanced technology solutions. Grow your skills by merging innovative engineering met hodologies and cross-disciplinary coordination to create tomorrow’s solutions. Join our team and create the future of digital transformation in the Air Force. \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 5+ years of experience designing and architecting large-scale, cloud-based applications, including leading architecture sessions and providing implementation guidance\n- Experience using an MBSE approach to manage system definitions and technical baselines\n- Knowledge of industry-accepted standards and best practices for strategic planning, portfolio management, and architecture development and management, including UAF, EA, DoDAF, BPMN, UML, SysML, ERD, and IDEF met hods\n- Knowledge of developing and reviewing enterprise architecture, including in support of transformation, system development, and governance and compliance of IT systems for the DoD such as FISMA or the Clinger-Cohen Act\n- Ability to comprehend stakeholder needs effectively and communicate them via architecture models\n- Ability to successfully work on cross-functional projects and teams\n- Secret clearance\n- Bachelor’s degree in a STEM field\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience working with solution architects to decompose application components and determine how to leverage various technologies found with modern cloud services\n- Experience with advanced analytics, data science, including MI, ML, or RPA, integration, API, microservices, and user experience\n- Experience supporting overall systems engineering and integration efforts for the DoD, government agencies, or commer cia l programs\n- Experience with Agile met hodologies, including sprint planning, creating, and completing user stories and tasks, and using common Agile tools such as Jira\n- Knowledge of systems engineering standards, including IEEE 15288.1 and IEEE 15288.2\n- Master’s degree\n- INCOSE Systems Engineering Professional ( SEP ) Certification s such as Asso cia te SEP ( ASEP ) , Certified SEP ( CSEP ) , and Expert SEP ( ESEP ) Certification s\n- SysML Certification s such as OCSMP Model User ( MU ) , Model Builder Fundamental ( MBF ) , Model Builder Intermediate ( MBI ) , and Model Builder Advanced ( MBA ) Certification s\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Model-Based Systems Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>Are you looking for an opportunity to combine your technical skills with big picture thinking to make an impact on advancing Model-Based Systems Engineering <span>(</span>MBSE<span>)</span> practices to help build a digital engineering (DE) cloud platform ecosystem for the DoD? You understand your customer’s environment and how to architect and develop, with the support of DevSecOps engineers, the right DE ecosystem for their mission. Your <span>ability to</span> translate real-world needs into technical specifications makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused DE solution.</p><p></p><p>As a Model-Based Systems Engineer on our team, you’ll work with Booz Allen colleagues and the U.S. Air Force to enable science and technology digital transformation. Your customer will t<span>rus</span>t you to not only analyze, evaluate, architect, and assist the government with modeling these DE capabilities and systems, but also identifying areas requiring urgent mitigation up-front and early, or suggesting ways to enhance user <span>experience</span> to develop this system with advanced technology solutions. Grow your skills by merging innovative engineering <span>met</span>hodologies and cross-disciplinary coordination to create tomorrow’s solutions. Join our team and create the future of digital transformation in the Air Force. </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> designing and architecting large-scale, cloud-based applications, including leading architecture sessions and providing implementation guidance</li><li><span>Experience</span> using an MBSE approach to manage system definitions and technical baselines</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> industry-accepted standards and best practices for strategic planning, portfolio management, and architecture development and management, including UAF, EA, DoDAF, BPMN, UML, SysML, ERD, and IDEF <span>met</span>hods</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> developing and reviewing enterprise architecture, including in support of transformation, system development, and governance and compliance of IT systems for the DoD such as FISMA or the Clinger-Cohen Act</li><li><span>Ability to</span> comprehend stakeholder needs effectively and communicate them via architecture models</li><li><span>Ability to</span> successfully work on cross-functional projects and teams</li><li><span>Secret clearance</span></li><li><span>Bachelor’s degree</span> in a STEM field</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> working with solution architects to decompose application components and determine how to leverage various technologies found with modern cloud services</li><li><span>Experience</span> with advanced analytics, data science, including MI, ML, or RPA, integration, API, microservices, and user <span>experience</span></li><li><span>Experience</span> supporting overall systems engineering and integration efforts for the DoD, government agencies, or commer<span>cia</span>l programs</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Agile <span>met</span>hodologies, including sprint planning, creating, and completing user stories and tasks, and using common Agile tools such as Jira</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> systems engineering standards, including IEEE 15288.1 and IEEE 15288.2</li><li><span>Master’s degree</span></li><li>INCOSE Systems Engineering Professional <span>(</span>SEP<span>)</span> <span>Certification</span>s such as Asso<span>cia</span>te SEP <span>(</span>ASEP<span>)</span>, Certified SEP <span>(</span>CSEP<span>)</span>, and Expert SEP <span>(</span>ESEP<span>)</span> <span>Certification</span>s</li><li>SysML <span>Certification</span>s such as OCSMP Model User <span>(</span>MU<span>)</span>, Model Builder Fundamental <span>(</span>MBF<span>)</span>, Model Builder Intermediate <span>(</span>MBI<span>)</span>, and Model Builder Advanced <span>(</span>MBA<span>)</span> <span>Certification</span>s</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance: </span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 3 Days Ago"},"status":"closed","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-21T07:47:34.705Z","closed_at":"2026-08-24T14:15:46.938Z","possibly_closed_at":"2026-08-24T01:56:20.339Z","missing_complete_scans":2,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Systems Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Colorado-Springs-CO/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0245999","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Colorado-Springs-CO/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0245999","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"baefe5f8f5cf7f0258aa1676bc37669883ee27c41f84c69166dbcc7d34f88174","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Model-Based Systems Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Colorado-Springs-CO/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0245999","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Colorado-Springs-CO/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0245999","locations":[{"label":"Colorado Springs, CO"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245999","internal_job_id":"cdcfc075bb401001117e8bab0f9f0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-04","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Model-Based Systems Engineer The Opportunity:\nDevelop , modify, and run high-fidelity simulations of space- related Command and Control ( C2 ) programs to inform modeling, wargaming, operational concepts and force design recommendations for the United States Space Force ( USSF ) . Identify elements of an entire C2 architecture and apply analytical met hods and tools using Python, MATLAB, government sof tware such as Advanced Framework for Simulation, Integration, Modeling ( AFSIM ) , or other internal modeling and simulation platforms. Develop new tools, scripts, and simulator features to improve operational scenario generation, data analysis, and simulation capability. Analyze USSF designs, requirements, research system technical details, and t race existing models to understand strengths and limitations of sof tware tools. Leverage expertise in space operations and joint operations to merge models into wargame simulations. Collaborate with subject matter experts spe cia lizing in Space Domain Awareness, Satellite Communications, and Orbital Warfare to develop comprehensive operational scenarios and detailed vignettes that systematically break down C2 architecture operations. Perform quantitative analysis of simulation outputs, Measures of Performance ( MOPs ) , Measures of Effectiveness ( MOEs ) , timelines, attrition, and mission outcomes.\n\nYou Have:\n- 6+ years of experience using advanced analytical tools such as Python, MATLAB, or AFSIM\n- 3+ years of experience in Orbital Warfare, Space Domain Awareness, Missile Warning, or Satellite Communications operations\n- Experience develop ing MOEs, MOPs, and analytic frameworks for simulation activities\n- Experience building adaptable sof tware prototypes to construct operational scenarios and vignettes\n- Knowledge of operational doctrine, and tactics, techniques, and procedures to inform scenario develop ment\n- Active TS/SCI clearance; willingness to take a polygraph exam\n- Bachelor's degree in Physical Science, Engineering, Physics, Mathematics, Operational Research, or Computer Science\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with USSF and DoW Force Design process, or Unified Combatant Command requirements\n- Experience supporting USSF and other DoW space agency spe cia l access program activities\n- Master's degree preferred ; Doctorate degree a plus\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Model-Based Systems Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p><span>Develop</span>, modify, and run high-fidelity simulations of space-<span>related</span> Command and Control <span>(</span>C2<span>)</span> programs to inform modeling, wargaming, operational concepts and force design recommendations for the United States Space Force <span>(</span>USSF<span>)</span>. Identify elements of an entire C2 architecture and apply analytical <span>met</span>hods and tools using Python, MATLAB, government <span>sof</span>tware such as Advanced Framework for Simulation, Integration, Modeling <span>(</span>AFSIM<span>)</span>, <span>or other</span> internal modeling and simulation platforms. <span>Develop</span> new tools, scripts, and simulator features to improve operational scenario generation, data analysis, and simulation capability. Analyze USSF designs, requirements, research system technical details, and t<span>race</span> existing models to understand strengths and limitations of <span>sof</span>tware tools. Leverage expertise in space operations and joint operations to merge models into wargame simulations. Collaborate with subject matter experts spe<span>cia</span>lizing in Space Domain Awareness, Satellite Communications, and Orbital Warfare to <span>develop</span> comprehensive operational scenarios and detailed vignettes that systematically break down C2 architecture operations. Perform quantitative analysis of simulation outputs, Measures of Performance <span>(</span>MOPs<span>)</span>, Measures of Effectiveness <span>(</span>MOEs<span>)</span>, timelines, attrition, and mission outcomes.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li>6&#43; years of <span>experience</span> using advanced analytical tools such as Python, MATLAB, or AFSIM</li><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in Orbital Warfare, Space Domain Awareness, Missile Warning, or Satellite Communications operations</li><li><span>Experience</span> <span>develop</span>ing MOEs, MOPs, and analytic frameworks for simulation activities</li><li><span>Experience</span> building adaptable <span>sof</span>tware prototypes to construct operational scenarios and vignettes</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> operational doctrine, and tactics, techniques, and procedures to inform scenario <span>develop</span>ment</li><li><span>Active TS/SCI clearance; willingness to take a polygraph exam</span></li><li><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span> in Physical Science, Engineering, Physics, Mathematics, Operational Research, or Computer Science</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with USSF and DoW Force Design process, or Unified Combatant Command requirements</li><li><span>Experience</span> supporting USSF <span>and other</span> DoW space agency spe<span>cia</span>l access program activities</li><li><span>Master&#39;s degree</span> preferred<span>;</span> <span>Doctorate degree</span> a plus</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b><br /><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 20 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Systems Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/El-Segundo-CA/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0244101","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/El-Segundo-CA/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0244101","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"090fa1129f8324d74e718f019635bf67bd70f9718b34fb6c61766bd63b5ab4db","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Model-Based Systems Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/El-Segundo-CA/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0244101","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/El-Segundo-CA/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0244101","locations":[{"label":"El Segundo, CA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0244101","internal_job_id":"186c347b6c0e1001b3d49ef2eae70000","first_published_at":"2026-07-15","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Model-Based Systems Engineer The Opportunity:\nCreate, integrate, and apply interdisciplinary digital models of products from concept throughout the product lifecycle. Apply advanced consult ing skills or extensive technical expertise, including full industry knowledge. Develop innovative solutions to complex problems. Work without considerable direction and mentor and supervise team members.\n\nYou Have:\n- 5+ years of experience developing or defining architectures that integrate MBSE tools, simulation environments, data repositories, and lifecycle management systems\n- 4+ years of experience performing systems engineering analysis and developing systems engineering products for DoD or government systems\n- 3+ years of experience with practical MBSE for the development of technical specifications, interface control documents, and system architecture, including using digital engineering tools such as Cameo or MagicDraw, SparxEA, DOORS, or IBM Rhapsody\n- Ability to define and maintain the enterprise architecture for a digital engineering ecosystem\n- Ability to communicate and establish collaborative relationships with government clients, Federally Funded Research and Development Center s ( FFRDC ) , and asso cia te contractor teammates to achieve program goals\n- Top Secret clearance\n- Bachelor's degree in a STEM field\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with Model-Based Verification and Validation\n- Experience analyzing and translating system requirements into design\n- Knowledge of Systems Modeling Language  ( SysML )  and DoD Architecture Framework ( DoDAF )\n- Ability to identify, analyze, and resolve technical risks and issues, develop technical reports, and collaborate with government and other stakeholders to implement recommended solutions \n- TS/SCI clearance\n- Master’s degree in Engineering\n- OMG Certified Systems Model Professional  ( OCSMP )   Certification\n- INCOSE SE Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Top Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Model-Based Systems Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>Create, integrate, and apply interdisciplinary digital models of products from concept throughout the product lifecycle. Apply advanced <span>consult</span>ing skills or extensive technical expertise, including full industry knowledge. Develop innovative solutions to complex problems. Work without considerable direction and mentor and supervise team members.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> developing or defining architectures that integrate MBSE tools, simulation environments, data repositories, and lifecycle management systems</li><li>4&#43; years of <span>experience</span> performing systems engineering analysis and developing systems engineering products for DoD or government systems</li><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with practical MBSE for the development of technical specifications, interface control documents, and system architecture, including using digital engineering tools such as Cameo or MagicDraw, SparxEA, DOORS, or IBM Rhapsody</li><li><span>Ability to</span> define and maintain the enterprise architecture for a digital engineering ecosystem</li><li><span>Ability to</span> communicate and establish collaborative relationships with government clients, Federally Funded Research and Development <span>Center</span>s <span>(</span>FFRDC<span>)</span>, and asso<span>cia</span>te contractor teammates to achieve program goals</li><li><span>Top Secret clearance</span></li><li><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span> in a STEM field</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with Model-Based Verification and Validation</li><li><span>Experience</span> analyzing and translating system requirements into design</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> Systems Modeling Language <span>(</span>SysML<span>)</span> and DoD Architecture Framework <span>(</span>DoDAF<span>)</span></li><li><span>Ability to</span> identify, analyze, and resolve technical risks and issues, develop technical reports, and collaborate with government <span>and other</span> stakeholders to implement recommended solutions </li><li><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></li><li><span>Master’s degree</span> in Engineering</li><li>OMG Certified Systems Model Professional <span>(</span>OCSMP<span>)</span> <span>Certification</span></li><li>INCOSE SE <span>Certification</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance: </span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Top Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Systems Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/San-Diego-CA/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0245808","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/San-Diego-CA/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0245808","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"a7a62f2337ca71207762e806388b76adb1dd2c4bf3545b78dfe8eb776efc5411","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Model-Based Systems Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/San-Diego-CA/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0245808","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/San-Diego-CA/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer_R0245808","locations":[{"label":"San Diego, CA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245808","internal_job_id":"93645f7db5bc1002010eee3648e90000","first_published_at":"2026-08-12","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Model-Based Systems Engineer The Opportunity: \nAre you looking for an opportunity to combine your technical skills with big picture thinking to make an impact in national security and veteran’s access to health care? You understand your customer’s environment and how to develop the right systems for their mission. Your ability to translate real-world needs into technical specifications makes you an integral part of delivering a customer focused engineering solution.  \n\nAs a systems engineer on our team, you have the chance to shape the customer mission by leading the engineering effort. Your customer will trust you to not only design and develop these systems but also evolve them with advanced technology solutions. On our team, you’ll be able to broaden your skillset into areas such as technology. Grow your skills by merging area of familiarity and area of growth to create deliverable a solution. Join our team and create the future of mission area and system type in the industry. \n\nCreate, integrate, and apply interdisciplinary digital models of products from concept throughout the product lifecycle. Apply advanced skills, extensive technical expertise, and full industry knowledge. Develop innovative solutions to complex problems. Work without considerable direction and mentor and supervise team members.\n\nYou Have:\n- 2+ years of experience developing or defining architectures that integrate MBSE tools, simulation environments, data repositories, and lifecycle management systems\n\n- 2+ years of experience performing systems engineering analysis and developing systems engineering products for DoD or government systems\n\n- 2+ years of experience with practical MBSE for the development of technical specifications, interface control documents, and system architecture, including using digital engineering tools such as Cameo, MagicDraw, SparxEA, DOORS, or IBM Rhapsody\n\n- 2+ years of experience analyzing and translating system requirements into design\n\n- Experience in building models and views aligned to PDR, CDR, and TRR\n\n- Ability to define and maintain the enterprise architecture for a digital engineering ecosystem\n\n- Ability to communicate and establish collaborative relationships with government clients, Federally Funded Research and Development Centers (FFRDC), and associate contractor teammates to achieve program goals\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree in a STEM field or 4+ years of experience with MBSE\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with Model-Based Verification and Validation\n\n- Experience with Modular Open Systems Approach (MOSA)\n\n- Knowledge of Systems Modeling Language (SysML) and DoD Architecture Framework (DoDAF)\n\n- Ability to work to meet deliverables using agile workflows  \n\n- Ability to identify, analyze, and resolve technical risks and issues, develop technical reports, and collaborate with government and other stakeholders to implement recommended solutions \n\n- Master’s degree in Engineering\n\n- OMG Certified Systems Model Professional (OCSMP) Certification\n\n- INCOSE SE Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,900.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Model-Based Systems Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>Are you looking for an opportunity to combine your technical skills with big picture thinking to make an impact in national security and veteran’s access to health care? You understand your customer’s environment and how to develop the right systems for their mission. Your ability to translate real-world needs into technical specifications makes you an integral part of delivering a customer focused engineering solution.  </p><p></p><p>As a systems engineer on our team, you have the chance to shape the customer mission by leading the engineering effort. Your customer will trust you to not only design and develop these systems but also evolve them with advanced technology solutions. On our team, you’ll be able to broaden your skillset into areas such as technology. Grow your skills by merging area of familiarity and area of growth to create deliverable a solution. Join our team and create the future of mission area and system type in the industry. </p><div><p></p><p>Create, integrate, and apply interdisciplinary digital models of products from concept throughout the product lifecycle. Apply advanced skills, extensive technical expertise, and full industry knowledge. Develop innovative solutions to complex problems. Work without considerable direction and mentor and supervise team members.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have: </b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of experience developing or defining architectures that integrate MBSE tools, simulation environments, data repositories, and lifecycle management systems</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience performing systems engineering analysis and developing systems engineering products for DoD or government systems</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with practical MBSE for the development of technical specifications, interface control documents, and system architecture, including using digital engineering tools such as Cameo, MagicDraw, SparxEA, DOORS, or IBM Rhapsody</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience analyzing and translating system requirements into design</p></li><li><p>Experience in building models and views aligned to PDR, CDR, and TRR</p></li><li><p>Ability to define and maintain the enterprise architecture for a digital engineering ecosystem</p></li><li><p>Ability to communicate and establish collaborative relationships with government clients, Federally Funded Research and Development Centers (FFRDC), and associate contractor teammates to achieve program goals</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree in a STEM field or 4&#43; years of experience with MBSE</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have: </b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with Model-Based Verification and Validation</p></li><li><p>Experience with Modular Open Systems Approach (MOSA)</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of Systems Modeling Language (SysML) and DoD Architecture Framework (DoDAF)</p></li><li><p>Ability to work to meet deliverables using agile workflows  </p></li><li><p>Ability to identify, analyze, and resolve technical risks and issues, develop technical reports, and collaborate with government and other stakeholders to implement recommended solutions </p></li><li><p>Master’s degree in Engineering</p></li><li><p>OMG Certified Systems Model Professional (OCSMP) Certification</p></li><li><p>INCOSE SE Certification</p></li></ul></div><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,900.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 12 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Systems Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Lexington-Park-MD/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer--Mid_R0238485","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Lexington-Park-MD/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer--Mid_R0238485","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"9b7ba9f2531d0e8cdc3f90574eaf8cc34f542a8ffd6d3c6246e75f40e68e4135","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Model-Based Systems Engineer, Mid","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Lexington-Park-MD/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer--Mid_R0238485","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Lexington-Park-MD/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer--Mid_R0238485","locations":[{"label":"Lexington Park, MD"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0238485","internal_job_id":"cecbc10db59e10019fae67e1ce9d0000","first_published_at":"2026-07-27","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Model-Based Systems Engineer, Mid The Opportunity:\nAre you looking for an opportunity to combine your te chn ical skills with big-picture thi nk ing to make an impact in national defense? You understand your customer’s environment and how to develop the right systems for their mission. Your ability to translate real-world needs into te chn ical specifications makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused engineering solution.\n\nAs a Model-Based Systems Engineer ( MBSE ) on our team, you have the chance to engineer systems to support our client’s digital engineering mission. You will provide engineering te chn ical direction for problem definition, analysis, requirement development, and implementation for complex systems in the engineering discipline required to meet te chn ical objectives. You have the chance to design model-based systems and develop digital twin models and architectures in support of government defense systems. Your te chn ical expertise will be vital as you evaluate and modernize how our clients go about li nk ing digital tools and te chn iques with system engineering, fostering a new way of cybersecurity and product development. You’ll develop your skills in MBSE while gaining experience across a complex and integrated system. Grow your skills by merging your system and digital engineering skills to create new and innovative solutions for our clients. Join our team and help turn requirements into accomplishments that drive change.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have: \n- 1+ years of experience with Systems Engineering, Integration, and MBSE\n\n- 1+ years of experience using digital engineering tools to design DoD systems\n\n- Experience with architecting solutions from user requirements and use cases to be applied across a systems engineering life cycle\n\n- Experience with modeling tools, including Magic Draw or Cameo, Sparx Enterprise Architect, or IBM Rhapsody\n\n- Experience with the practical application of Unified Modeling Language ( UML ) or Systems Modeling Language ( SysML )\n\n- Ability to use MBSE tools and processes to create and manage tailored MBSE artifacts that capture analysis and the resulting engineering decisions and trades made during acquisition and development\n\n- Ability to work eﬀectively in a multi-disciplinary, dynamic team environment, including internal staff, external contractors, and government clients to increase the use of MBSE for client acquisition programs\n\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience with supporting acquisition programs and government clients\n\n- Experience with extending systems models into other tools for analysis, including MATLAB, Simuli nk , or STK, and model-based product support, including Teamcenter or Windchill\n\n- Experience with scripting languages, including the Velocity Template Language\n\n- Experience using system models during government engineering reviews and other system engineering disciplines, including configuration management, risk management, cybersecurity, and cyber certification processes\n\n- Knowledge of modular open systems approach ( MOSA ) design principles and te chn ologies, DoD architecture standards and framework, and Agile systems engineering methods and tools\n\n- Knowledge of DoDD 5000.01, DoDI 5000.02, the System Development Life Cycle, and object-oriented programming languages, including C++, Java, or Python\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Master's degree in Engineering, Science, or Mathematics\n\n- Object Management Group ( OMG ) Certified System Modeling Language Professional ( OCSMP ) Model User or Builder Certification\n\n- INCOSE Systems Engineering Professional Certification, including ASEP, CSEP, or ESEP Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.\n\nID17-G","description_html":"Model-Based Systems Engineer, Mid<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>Are you looking for an opportunity to combine your te<span>chn</span>ical skills with big-picture thi<span>nk</span>ing to make an impact in national defense? You understand your customer’s environment and how to develop the right systems for their mission. Your ability to translate real-world needs into te<span>chn</span>ical specifications makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused engineering solution.</p><p></p><p>As a Model-Based Systems Engineer <span>(</span>MBSE<span>)</span> on our team, you have the chance to engineer systems to support our client’s digital engineering mission. You will provide engineering te<span>chn</span>ical direction for problem definition, analysis, requirement development, and implementation for complex systems in the engineering discipline required to meet te<span>chn</span>ical objectives. You have the chance to design model-based systems and develop digital twin models and architectures in support of government defense systems. Your te<span>chn</span>ical expertise will be vital as you evaluate and modernize how our clients go about li<span>nk</span>ing digital tools and te<span>chn</span>iques with system engineering, fostering a new way of cybersecurity and product development. You’ll develop your skills in MBSE while gaining experience across a complex and integrated system. Grow your skills by merging your system and digital engineering skills to create new and innovative solutions for our clients. Join our team and help turn requirements into accomplishments that drive change.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have: </b></p><ul><li><p>1&#43; years of experience with Systems Engineering, Integration, and MBSE</p></li><li><p>1&#43; years of experience using digital engineering tools to design DoD systems</p></li><li><p>Experience with architecting solutions from user requirements and use cases to be applied across a systems engineering life cycle</p></li><li><p>Experience with modeling tools, including Magic Draw or Cameo, Sparx Enterprise Architect, or IBM Rhapsody</p></li><li><p>Experience with the practical application of Unified Modeling Language <span>(</span>UML<span>)</span> or Systems Modeling Language <span>(</span>SysML<span>)</span></p></li><li><p>Ability to use MBSE tools and processes to create and manage tailored MBSE artifacts that capture analysis and the resulting engineering decisions and trades made during acquisition and development</p></li><li><p>Ability to work eﬀectively in a multi-disciplinary, dynamic team environment, including internal staff, external contractors, and government clients to increase the use of MBSE for client acquisition programs</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to obtain a Secret clearance </span></p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b> </p><ul><li><p>Experience with supporting acquisition programs and government clients</p></li><li><p>Experience with extending systems models into other tools for analysis, including MATLAB, Simuli<span>nk</span>, or STK, and model-based product support, including Teamcenter or Windchill</p></li><li><p>Experience with scripting languages, including the Velocity Template Language</p></li><li><p>Experience using system models during government engineering reviews and other system engineering disciplines, including configuration management, risk management, cybersecurity, and cyber certification processes</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of modular open systems approach <span>(</span>MOSA<span>)</span> design principles and te<span>chn</span>ologies, DoD architecture standards and framework, and Agile systems engineering methods and tools</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of DoDD 5000.01, DoDI 5000.02, the System Development Life Cycle, and object-oriented programming languages, including C&#43;&#43;, Java, or Python</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p>Master&#39;s degree in Engineering, Science, or Mathematics</p></li><li><p>Object Management Group <span>(</span>OMG<span>)</span> Certified System Modeling Language Professional <span>(</span>OCSMP<span>)</span> Model User or Builder Certification</p></li><li><p>INCOSE Systems Engineering Professional Certification, including ASEP, CSEP, or ESEP Certification</p></li></ul><p><br /><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>ID17-G","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 28 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Systems Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Lexington-Park-MD/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer--Mid_R0238489","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Lexington-Park-MD/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer--Mid_R0238489","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"abb8430a65f66428f09f2725fd224bdedcb627e370571c79eebcc1ab92375e00","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Model-Based Systems Engineer, Mid","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Lexington-Park-MD/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer--Mid_R0238489","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Lexington-Park-MD/Model-Based-Systems-Engineer--Mid_R0238489","locations":[{"label":"Lexington Park, MD"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0238489","internal_job_id":"69eae4eb544a1001a1a785edc5560000","first_published_at":"2026-07-16","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Model-Based Systems Engineer, Mid The Opportunity:\nAre you looking for an opportunity to combine your te chn ical skills with big-picture thi nk ing to make an impact in national defense? You understand your customer’s environment and how to develop the right systems for their mission. Your ability to translate real-world needs into te chn ical specifications makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused engineering solution.\n\nAs a Model-Based Systems Engineer ( MBSE ) on our team, you have the chance to create, integrate, and apply interdisciplinary digital models of products from concept throughout the product lifecycle. You will provide engineering te chn ical direction for problem definition, analysis, requirement development, and implementation for complex systems in the engineering discipline required to meet te chn ical objectives. You have the chance to design model-based systems and develop digital twin models and architectures in support of government defense systems. Your te chn ical expertise will be vital as you evaluate and modernize how our clients go about li nk ing digital tools and te chn iques with system engineering, fostering a new way of cybersecurity and product development. You’ll develop your skills in MBSE while gaining experience across a complex, integrated system. Grow your skills by merging your system and digital engineering skills to create new and innovative solutions for our clients. Join our team and help turn requirements into accomplishments that drive change.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have: \n- 3+ years of experience with systems engineering and integration, and MBSE\n\n- 3+ years of experience using digital engineering tools to design DoD systems\n\n- Experience with architecting solutions from user requirements and use cases to be applied across a systems engineering life cycle\n\n- Experience with modeling tools, including Magic Draw or Cameo, Sparx Enterprise Architect, or IBM Rhapsody, and with the practical application of Unified Modeling Language ( UML ) or Systems Modeling Language ( SysML )\n\n- Knowledge of modular open systems approach ( MOSA ) design principles and te chn ologies, DoD architecture standards and framework, and Agile systems engineering methods and tools\n\n- Ability to use MBSE tools and processes to create and manage tailored MBSE artifacts that capture analysis and the resulting engineering decisions and trades made during acquisition and development\n\n- Ability to work eﬀectively in a multi-disciplinary, dynamic team environment, including internal staff, external contractors, and government clients to increase the use of MBSE for client acquisition programs\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\n- Object Management Group ( OMG ) Certified System Modeling Language Professional ( OCSMP ) Model User or Builder Certification or INCOSE Systems Engineering Professional Certification, including ASEP, CSEP, or ESEP Certification\n\nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience with supporting acquisition programs and government clients\n\n- Experience with extending systems models into other tools for analysis, including MATLAB, Simuli nk , or STK, and model-based product support, including Teamcenter or Windchill\n\n- Experience with scripting languages, including the Velocity Template Language\n\n- Experience using system models during government engineering reviews and other system engineering disciplines, including configuration management, risk management, cybersecurity, and cyber certification processes\n\n- Knowledge of DoDD 5000.01, DoDI 5000.02, the System Development Life Cycle, and object-oriented programming languages, including C++, Java, or Python\n\n- Master's degree in Engineering, Science, or Mathematics\n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.\n\nID17-G","description_html":"Model-Based Systems Engineer, Mid<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>Are you looking for an opportunity to combine your te<span>chn</span>ical skills with big-picture thi<span>nk</span>ing to make an impact in national defense? You understand your customer’s environment and how to develop the right systems for their mission. Your ability to translate real-world needs into te<span>chn</span>ical specifications makes you an integral part of delivering a customer-focused engineering solution.</p><p></p><p>As a Model-Based Systems Engineer <span>(</span>MBSE<span>)</span> on our team, you have the chance to create, integrate, and apply interdisciplinary digital models of products from concept throughout the product lifecycle. You will provide engineering te<span>chn</span>ical direction for problem definition, analysis, requirement development, and implementation for complex systems in the engineering discipline required to meet te<span>chn</span>ical objectives. You have the chance to design model-based systems and develop digital twin models and architectures in support of government defense systems. Your te<span>chn</span>ical expertise will be vital as you evaluate and modernize how our clients go about li<span>nk</span>ing digital tools and te<span>chn</span>iques with system engineering, fostering a new way of cybersecurity and product development. You’ll develop your skills in MBSE while gaining experience across a complex, integrated system. Grow your skills by merging your system and digital engineering skills to create new and innovative solutions for our clients. Join our team and help turn requirements into accomplishments that drive change.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have: </b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of experience with systems engineering and integration, and MBSE</p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of experience using digital engineering tools to design DoD systems</p></li><li><p>Experience with architecting solutions from user requirements and use cases to be applied across a systems engineering life cycle</p></li><li><p>Experience with modeling tools, including Magic Draw or Cameo, Sparx Enterprise Architect, or IBM Rhapsody, and with the practical application of Unified Modeling Language <span>(</span>UML<span>)</span> or Systems Modeling Language <span>(</span>SysML<span>)</span></p></li><li><p>Knowledge of modular open systems approach <span>(</span>MOSA<span>)</span> design principles and te<span>chn</span>ologies, DoD architecture standards and framework, and Agile systems engineering methods and tools</p></li><li><p>Ability to use MBSE tools and processes to create and manage tailored MBSE artifacts that capture analysis and the resulting engineering decisions and trades made during acquisition and development</p></li><li><p>Ability to work eﬀectively in a multi-disciplinary, dynamic team environment, including internal staff, external contractors, and government clients to increase the use of MBSE for client acquisition programs</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance </span></p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree</p></li><li><p>Object Management Group <span>(</span>OMG<span>)</span> Certified System Modeling Language Professional <span>(</span>OCSMP<span>)</span> Model User or Builder Certification or INCOSE Systems Engineering Professional Certification, including ASEP, CSEP, or ESEP Certification</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b> </p><ul><li><p>Experience with supporting acquisition programs and government clients</p></li><li><p>Experience with extending systems models into other tools for analysis, including MATLAB, Simuli<span>nk</span>, or STK, and model-based product support, including Teamcenter or Windchill</p></li><li><p>Experience with scripting languages, including the Velocity Template Language</p></li><li><p>Experience using system models during government engineering reviews and other system engineering disciplines, including configuration management, risk management, cybersecurity, and cyber certification processes</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of DoDD 5000.01, DoDI 5000.02, the System Development Life Cycle, and object-oriented programming languages, including C&#43;&#43;, Java, or Python</p></li><li><p>Master&#39;s degree in Engineering, Science, or Mathematics</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b> </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>ID17-G","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Systems Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
