{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Springfield-VA/Multimedia-Forensics-Research-Scientist-and-Analyst_R0240912","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Springfield-VA/Multimedia-Forensics-Research-Scientist-and-Analyst_R0240912","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"622c872750f77c4e1c4ef29b8f163b06fe7b2daaa36ff6b2785f3f9967efdc12","fetched_at":"2026-08-24T14:15:46.938Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Multimedia Research Scientist and Analyst","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Springfield-VA/Multimedia-Forensics-Research-Scientist-and-Analyst_R0240912","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Springfield-VA/Multimedia-Forensics-Research-Scientist-and-Analyst_R0240912","locations":[{"label":"Springfield, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0240912","internal_job_id":"31e03fc9eb56100119d6fd9d46960000","first_published_at":"2026-07-03","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Multimedia Research Scientist and Analyst The Opportunity:  \nDo you find yourself constantly looking for more and better information? Do you want a job where you can use your knowledge and research skills to improve national security? Join a team of scientists and analysts who investigate and solve challenging multimedia forensic problems.  \n\nYour research and development expertise and advising mindset, coupled with an original approach to your work, will give clients and stakeholders insights into media analysis and encourage actionable results. You'll perform forensic analysis and exploitation by leveraging scientific expertise and media analysis tools to digital media. You'll research and develop novel techniques through algorithm and prototype development in topic areas such as biometric recognition, signal processing, image processing, computer vision, media geolocation, and media authentication. You will analyze scientific publications with a high degree of comprehension, build out concepts from academia into real world use, and analyze current technology to address specific client missions. You'll attend conferences and community meetings with multimedia forensics experts and present findings and recommendations to non-technical audiences with an emphasis on impacting mission outcomes.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n \nYou Have:  \n- 2+ years of experience with interdisciplinary research, including analysis of a variety of multimedia data sources, images, videos, and signal processing\n\n- 2+ years of experience with implementing technical prototypes in Python or MATLAB  \n\n- 2+ years of experience with multimedia analysis, signal and imaging processing, algorithm development, or computer vision  \n\n- Experience with technical writing, including thesis, publications, technical manuals, or reports\n\n- Secret clearance  \n\n- Master's degree in Computer Science, Mathematics, Physics, Digital Forensics, or Engineering  \n\n \nNice If You Have:  \n- 2+ years of experience presenting scientific findings and publishing scientific papers in peer-reviewed journals \n\n- Experience with imagery and media analysis from a forensic perspective \n\n- Experience with analytical image comparison, facial recognition, or facial identification  \n\n- Experience with integrating commercial or open-source software tools for custom application development  \n\n- Knowledge of photographic concepts and basic image science, including multi-media file specifications, formats, and processing  \n\n- Possession of excellent oral and written communication skills  \n\n- Possession of excellent entrepreneurial thinking, innovation, and real-world problem-solving skills  \n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- Doctorate degree  \n\nClearance: \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.  \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Multimedia Research Scientist and Analyst<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span><span> </span></b></p><p><span>Do you find yourself constantly looking for more and better information? Do you want a job where you can use your knowledge and research skills to improve national security? Join a team of scientists and analysts who investigate and solve challenging multimedia forensic problems.</span><span> </span></p><p></p><p><span>Your research and development expertise and advising mindset, coupled with an original approach to your work, will give clients and stakeholders insights into media analysis and encourage actionable results. You&#39;ll perform forensic analysis and exploitation by leveraging scientific expertise and media analysis tools to digital media. You&#39;ll research and develop novel techniques through algorithm and prototype development in topic areas such as biometric recognition, signal processing, image processing, computer vision, media geolocation, and media authentication. You will analyze scientific publications with a high degree of comprehension, build out concepts from academia into real world use, and analyze current technology to address specific client missions. You&#39;ll attend conferences and community meetings with multimedia forensics experts and present findings and recommendations to non-technical audiences with an emphasis on impacting mission outcomes. </span><span> </span></p><p></p><p><span>Join us. The world can’t wait.</span></p><p><span> </span></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span><span> </span></b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with interdisciplinary research, including analysis of a variety of multimedia data sources, images, videos, and signal processing</p></li><li><p><span>2&#43; years of experience with implementing technical prototypes in Python or MATLAB</span><span> </span></p></li><li><p><span>2&#43; years of experience with multimedia analysis, signal and imaging processing, algorithm development, or computer vision</span><span> </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with technical writing, including thesis, publications, technical manuals, or reports </span></p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span><span> </span></p></li><li><p><span>Master&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Mathematics, Physics, Digital Forensics, or Engineering </span><span> </span></p></li></ul><p><span> </span></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span><span> </span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>2&#43; years of experience presenting scientific findings and publishing scientific papers in peer-reviewed journals </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with imagery and media analysis from a forensic perspective </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with analytical image comparison, facial recognition, or facial identification</span><span> </span></p></li><li><p><span>Experience with integrating commercial or open-source</span><span> software tools for custom application development</span><span> </span></p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of photographic concepts and basic image science, including multi-media file specifications, formats, and processing</span><span> </span></p></li><li><p><span>Possession of excellent oral and written communication skills</span><span> </span></p></li><li><p><span>Possession of excellent entrepreneurial thinking, innovation, and real-world problem-solving skills</span><span> </span></p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Doctorate degree</span><span> </span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance: </b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.  </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"possibly_closed","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-24T14:15:46.938Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","missing_complete_scans":1,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":[],"role_matches":["Research Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Springfield-VA/Multimedia-Research-Scientist-and-Analyst_R0247290","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Springfield-VA/Multimedia-Research-Scientist-and-Analyst_R0247290","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"363b28adfca2ac0e1c34ca5fd22cb3f070a0c3a7593d0ac30153d0379c2f7cba","fetched_at":"2026-08-24T14:15:46.938Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Multimedia Research Scientist and Analyst","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Springfield-VA/Multimedia-Research-Scientist-and-Analyst_R0247290","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Springfield-VA/Multimedia-Research-Scientist-and-Analyst_R0247290","locations":[{"label":"Springfield, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247290","internal_job_id":"ce7800f7d14610010d29c55087e60000","first_published_at":"2026-08-18","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Multimedia Research Scientist and Analyst The Opportunity: \nDo you find yourself constantly looking for more and better information? Do you want a job where you can use your knowledge and research skills to improve national security? Join a team of scientists and analysts who investigate and solve challenging multimedia forensic problems. \n\nYour research and development expertise and advising mindset, coupled with an original approach to your work, will give clients and stakeholders insights into media analysis and encourage actionable results. You'll perform forensic analysis and exploitation by leveraging scientific expertise and media analysis tools to digital media. You'll research and develop novel techniques through algorithm and prototype development in topic areas such as bio met ric recognition, signal processing, image processing, computer vision, media geolocation, and media authentication. You will analyze scientific publications with a high degree of comprehension, build out concepts from academia into real world use, and analyze current technology to address specific client missions. You'll attend conferences and community meetings with multimedia forensics experts and present findings and recommendations to non-technical audiences with an emphasis on impacting mission outcomes.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have: \n- 2+ years of experience with interdisciplinary research or supporting project management activities for R & D projects\n\n- Experience with multimedia analysis, signal and imaging processing, algorithm development, or computer vision \n\n- Experience implementing technical prototypes\n\n- Experience with technical writing, including thesis, publications, technical manuals, or reports\n\n- Secret clearance\n\n- Master's degree in Computer Science, Mathematics, Physics, Digital Forensics, or Engineering  \n\nNice If You Have: \n- 2+ years of experience presenting scientific findings and publishing scientific papers in peer-reviewed journals \n\n- Experience with imagery and media analysis from a forensic perspective, including analysis of a variety of multimedia data sources, images, videos, and signal processing\n\n- Experience with analytical image comparison, fa cia l recognition, or fa cia l identification \n\n- Experience with integrating commer cia l or open-source sof tware tools for custom application development \n\n- Knowledge of photographic concepts and basic image science, including multi-media file specifications, formats, and processing \n\n- Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills \n\n- Possession of excellent entrepreneurial thinking, innovation, and real-world problem-solving skills \n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- Doctorate degree\n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $128,700.00 to $292,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Multimedia Research Scientist and Analyst<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>Do you find yourself constantly looking for more and better information? Do you want a job where you can use your knowledge and research skills to improve national security? Join a team of scientists and analysts who investigate and solve challenging multimedia forensic problems. </p><p></p><p>Your research and development expertise and advising mindset, coupled with an original approach to your work, will give clients and stakeholders insights into media analysis and encourage actionable results. You&#39;ll perform forensic analysis and exploitation by leveraging scientific expertise and media analysis tools to digital media. You&#39;ll research and develop novel techniques through algorithm and prototype development in topic areas such as bio<span>met</span>ric recognition, signal processing, image processing, computer vision, media geolocation, and media authentication. You will analyze scientific publications with a high degree of comprehension, build out concepts from academia into real world use, and analyze <span>current</span> technology to address specific client missions. You&#39;ll attend conferences and community meetings with multimedia forensics experts and present findings and recommendations to non-technical audiences with an emphasis on impacting mission outcomes.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with interdisciplinary research or supporting project management activities for R<span>&amp;</span>D projects</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with multimedia analysis, signal and imaging processing, algorithm development, or computer vision </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> implementing technical prototypes</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with technical writing, including thesis, publications, technical manuals, or reports</p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Master&#39;s degree</span> in Computer Science, Mathematics, Physics, Digital Forensics, or Engineering  </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> presenting scientific findings and publishing scientific papers in peer-reviewed journals </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with imagery and media analysis from a forensic perspective, including analysis of a variety of multimedia data sources, images, videos, and signal processing</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with analytical image comparison, fa<span>cia</span>l recognition, or fa<span>cia</span>l identification </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with integrating commer<span>cia</span>l or open-source <span>sof</span>tware tools for custom application development </p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> photographic concepts and basic image science, including multi-media file specifications, formats, and processing </p></li><li><p><span>Possession of</span> excellent verbal and written communication skills </p></li><li><p><span>Possession of</span> excellent entrepreneurial thinking, innovation, and real-world problem-solving skills </p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Doctorate degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b> </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $128,700.00 to $292,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 6 Days Ago"},"status":"possibly_closed","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-24T14:15:46.938Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","missing_complete_scans":1,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":[],"role_matches":["Research Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
