{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/San-Antonio-TX/Network-Systems-Engineer_R0246111","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/San-Antonio-TX/Network-Systems-Engineer_R0246111","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"6a826ea948c188d6cb6ed36ca2ff359e979d3519b8b45bd2511149e1f5a7587d","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Network Systems Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/San-Antonio-TX/Network-Systems-Engineer_R0246111","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/San-Antonio-TX/Network-Systems-Engineer_R0246111","locations":[{"label":"San Antonio, TX"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246111","internal_job_id":"6d3435a3a87a1001583ea33d02ba0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-12","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Network Systems Engineer The Opportunity: \nA well-designed network is critical to move data and enable the DoD to achieve their mission, but how can an organization make sure their network will fit their evolving needs? Crafting the right network, with the right equipment and sof tware, requires a combination of technical skill and careful planning. That’s why we need a network engineer like you who knows how to craft the exact network the DoD needs.\n\nAs a Network Engineer on our team, you’ll help the DoD deploy a reliable network to support national defense. You’ll work with customers to learn the strategic goals and operational needs that shape network requirements. You’ll then plan the acquisition, installation, configuration, and maintenance of network components. From resolving interoperability issues across platforms, to supporting the acquisition of hardware, you’ll put your hardware and sof tware talents to good use. This is your chance to grow your skills in network optimization and cloud technologies while continuing to grow your network engineering experience . Join us as we help the DoD to expand their enterprise service capabilities.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have: \n- 5+ years of experience with network security and the design of IT systems or networks for large commer cia l enterprises or government agencies\n- 3+ years of experience with firewall and enterprise security design, including device hardening, int rus ion detection and int rus ion prevention systems, SIEM, firewalls, internet protocol security, and vulnerability assessment\n- Experience with Palo Alto firewalls, Cisco, or Juniper firewalls\n- Experience with monitoring tools and log collectors to perform analysis of traffic\n- Experience with boundary protection\n- Knowledge of packet analysis tools, such as Wireshark\n- Ability to travel up to 25% of the time\n- TS/SCI clearance\n- HS diploma or GED\n- DoD 8140 baseline Level II Certification such as Security+, CySA+, CISSP, or DoD Cyber Workforce Framework Certification\n\nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience designing and implementing cloud-native and over-the-top networking in AWS, Azure, or GCP\n- Experience with SD-WAN\n- Experience with Ansible or Python\n- Knowledge of DoD IT and cloud security policies , including STIGs and DoD Cloud SRG, and how to apply them to the design and implementation of cloud solutions\n- Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills, including public speaking, prior publications, and speaking e nga gements in industry or vendor forums\n\nClearance:   \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Network Systems Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>A well-designed network is critical to move data and enable the DoD to achieve their mission, but how can an organization make sure their network will fit their evolving needs? Crafting the right network, with the right equipment and <span>sof</span>tware, requires a combination of technical skill and careful planning. That’s why we need a network engineer like you who knows how to craft the exact network the DoD needs.</p><p></p><p>As a Network Engineer on our team, you’ll help the DoD deploy a reliable network to support national defense. You’ll work with customers to learn the strategic goals and operational needs that shape network requirements. You’ll then plan the acquisition, installation, configuration, and maintenance of network components. From resolving interoperability issues across platforms, to supporting the acquisition of hardware, you’ll put your hardware and <span>sof</span>tware talents to good use. This is your chance to grow your skills in network optimization and cloud technologies while continuing to grow your network engineering <span>experience</span>. Join us as we help the DoD to expand their enterprise service capabilities.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with network security and the design of IT systems or networks for large commer<span>cia</span>l enterprises or government agencies</li><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with firewall and enterprise security design, including device hardening, int<span>rus</span>ion detection and int<span>rus</span>ion prevention systems, SIEM, firewalls, internet protocol security, and vulnerability assessment</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Palo Alto firewalls, Cisco, or Juniper firewalls</li><li><span>Experience</span> with monitoring tools and log collectors to perform analysis of traffic</li><li><span>Experience</span> with boundary protection</li><li>Knowledge of packet analysis tools, such as Wireshark</li><li><span>Ability to</span> travel up to 25% of the time</li><li><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></li><li><span>HS diploma or GED </span></li><li>DoD 8140 baseline Level II <span>Certification</span> such as Security&#43;, CySA&#43;, CISSP, or DoD Cyber Workforce Framework <span>Certification</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b> </p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> designing and implementing cloud-native and over-the-top networking in AWS, Azure, or GCP</li><li><span>Experience</span> with SD-WAN</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Ansible or Python</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> DoD IT and cloud security <span>policies</span>, including STIGs and DoD Cloud SRG, and how to apply them to the design and implementation of cloud solutions</li><li><span>Possession of</span> excellent verbal and written communication skills, including public speaking, prior publications, and speaking e<span>nga</span>gements in industry or vendor forums</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b>   </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 12 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Systems Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/San-Antonio-TX/Network-Systems-Engineer_R0247216-1","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/San-Antonio-TX/Network-Systems-Engineer_R0247216-1","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"16436aca92cb287f33a17b5be1c79a3dc572ff16c829189475f6f4a5f7567779","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Network Systems Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/San-Antonio-TX/Network-Systems-Engineer_R0247216-1","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/San-Antonio-TX/Network-Systems-Engineer_R0247216-1","locations":[{"label":"San Antonio, TX"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247216","internal_job_id":"26f0e5a9193a100106b722106b640000","first_published_at":"2026-08-18","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Network Systems Engineer The Opportunity: \nA well-designed network is critical to move data and enable the DoD to achieve their mission, but how can an organization make sure their network will fit their evolving needs? Crafting the right network, with the right equipment and sof tware, requires a combination of technical skill and careful planning. That’s why we need a network engineer like you who knows how to craft the exact network the DoD needs.\n\nAs a Network Engineer on our team, you’ll help the DoD deploy a reliable network to support national defense. You’ll work with customers to learn the strategic goals and operational needs that shape network requirements. You’ll then plan the acquisition, installation, configuration, and maintenance of network components. From resolving interoperability issues across platforms, to supporting the acquisition of hardware, you’ll put your hardware and sof tware talents to good use. This is your chance to grow your skills in network optimization and cloud technologies while continuing to grow your network engineering experience . Join us as we help the DoD to expand their enterprise service capabilities.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have: \n- 5+ years of experience with network security and the design of IT systems or networks for large commer cia l enterprises or government agencies\n\n- 3+ years of experience with firewall and enterprise security design, including device hardening, int rus ion detection and int rus ion prevention systems, SIEM, firewalls, internet protocol security, and vulnerability assessment\n\n- Experience with Palo Alto firewalls, Cisco, or Juniper firewalls\n\n- Experience with monitoring tools and log collectors to perform analysis of traffic\n\n- Experience with boundary protection\n\n- Knowledge of packet analysis tools, such as Wireshark\n\n- Ability to travel up to 25% of the time\n\n- TS/SCI clearance\n\n- HS diploma or GED\n\n- DoD 8140 baseline Level II Certification such as Security+, CySA+, CISSP, or DoD Cyber Workforce Framework Certification\n\nNice If You Have:  \n- Experience designing and implementing cloud-native and over-the-top networking in AWS, Azure, or GCP\n\n- Experience with SD-WAN\n\n- Experience with Ansible or Python\n\n- Knowledge of DoD IT and cloud security policies , including STIGs and DoD Cloud SRG, and how to apply them to the design and implementation of cloud solutions\n\n- Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills, including public speaking, prior publications, and speaking e nga gements in industry or vendor forums\n\nClearance:   \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Network Systems Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>A well-designed network is critical to move data and enable the DoD to achieve their mission, but how can an organization make sure their network will fit their evolving needs? Crafting the right network, with the right equipment and <span>sof</span>tware, requires a combination of technical skill and careful planning. That’s why we need a network engineer like you who knows how to craft the exact network the DoD needs.</p><p></p><p>As a Network Engineer on our team, you’ll help the DoD deploy a reliable network to support national defense. You’ll work with customers to learn the strategic goals and operational needs that shape network requirements. You’ll then plan the acquisition, installation, configuration, and maintenance of network components. From resolving interoperability issues across platforms, to supporting the acquisition of hardware, you’ll put your hardware and <span>sof</span>tware talents to good use. This is your chance to grow your skills in network optimization and cloud technologies while continuing to grow your network engineering <span>experience</span>. Join us as we help the DoD to expand their enterprise service capabilities.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with network security and the design of IT systems or networks for large commer<span>cia</span>l enterprises or government agencies</p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with firewall and enterprise security design, including device hardening, int<span>rus</span>ion detection and int<span>rus</span>ion prevention systems, SIEM, firewalls, internet protocol security, and vulnerability assessment</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Palo Alto firewalls, Cisco, or Juniper firewalls</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with monitoring tools and log collectors to perform analysis of traffic</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with boundary protection</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of packet analysis tools, such as Wireshark</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> travel up to 25% of the time</p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>HS diploma or GED </span></p></li><li><p>DoD 8140 baseline Level II <span>Certification</span> such as Security&#43;, CySA&#43;, CISSP, or DoD Cyber Workforce Framework <span>Certification</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b> </p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> designing and implementing cloud-native and over-the-top networking in AWS, Azure, or GCP</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with SD-WAN</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Ansible or Python</p></li><li><p><span>Knowledge of</span> DoD IT and cloud security <span>policies</span>, including STIGs and DoD Cloud SRG, and how to apply them to the design and implementation of cloud solutions</p></li><li><p><span>Possession of</span> excellent verbal and written communication skills, including public speaking, prior publications, and speaking e<span>nga</span>gements in industry or vendor forums</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b>   </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 6 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Systems Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/San-Diego-CA/Program-Management-Support-Specialist--Mid_R0244199","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/San-Diego-CA/Program-Management-Support-Specialist--Mid_R0244199","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"d43b5fad237273b2f801ac0b000d8b737862d06182edf6a4de6702ef31b953f7","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"New Ship Construction Program Management Specialist, Mid","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/San-Diego-CA/Program-Management-Support-Specialist--Mid_R0244199","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/San-Diego-CA/Program-Management-Support-Specialist--Mid_R0244199","locations":[{"label":"San Diego, CA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"unknown","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0244199","internal_job_id":null,"first_published_at":null,"source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":null,"description_html":null,"compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":null,"country":null,"posted_on":"Posted 17 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":false,"tier":"stretch","score":0,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":[],"role_matches":[],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Chantilly-VA/Nodejs-Developer-SME_R0246020","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Chantilly-VA/Nodejs-Developer-SME_R0246020","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"05845875721a301e52af7c1923d6073c8e69cf9f8a72aa09d50938b363bb79a2","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Node.js Developer SME","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Nodejs-Developer-SME_R0246020","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Nodejs-Developer-SME_R0246020","locations":[{"label":"Chantilly, VA"},{"label":"Herndon, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246020","internal_job_id":"cdcfc075bb40100111be97b511970000","first_published_at":"2026-08-04","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Node.js Developer SME The Opportunity:  \nAs an expert Node.js developer, you know that a good site or system needs the right combination of clean code, APIs, analytics, and infrastructure to develop a user-focused solution. We’re looking for an experienced back-end-focused developer with the software engineering skills it takes to identify potential risks, contribute to solution development, and create efficient and effective systems for our clients. \n\nAs a developer at Booz Allen, you’ll use the latest architectural approaches and open-source frameworks and tools to deliver solutions. Using your software engineering experience, you’ll work with the development team to create custom tools, systems, and sites with consistent performance and scalability. \n\nIn this role, you’ll make a mission-forward impact as you further your skillset and career. Work with us as we shape systems for the better.   \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have: \n- 5+ years of experience implementing, maintaining, and supporting agile software development\n\n- 5+ years of experience developing web applications\n\n- 2+ years of experience with Node.js software development\n\n- 2+ years of experience with TypeScript\n\n- Experience developing Linux-based systems in AWS\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- Bachelor's degree or 7+ years of experience in software engineering in lieu of a degree \n\n Nice If You Have:   \n- Experience with Angular\n\n- Experience with ElasticSearch\n\n- Experience with MongoDB\n\n- Experience with Redis\n\n- Experience with AWS\n\n- Experience with DevOps, CI/CD, and IaC\n\n- Experience with designing, implementing, and deploying microservices\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Node.js Developer SME<p><b>The Opportunity:  </b></p><p>As an expert Node.js developer, you know that a good site or system needs the right combination of clean code, APIs, analytics, and infrastructure to develop a user-focused solution. We’re looking for an experienced back-end-focused developer with the software engineering skills it takes to identify potential risks, contribute to solution development, and create efficient and effective systems for our clients. </p><p></p><p>As a developer at Booz Allen, you’ll use the latest architectural approaches and open-source frameworks and tools to deliver solutions. Using your software engineering experience, you’ll work with the development team to create custom tools, systems, and sites with consistent performance and scalability. </p><p></p><p>In this role, you’ll make a mission-forward impact as you further your skillset and career. Work with us as we shape systems for the better.   </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b>You Have: </b></p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of experience implementing, maintaining, and supporting agile software development</p></li><li><p>5&#43; years of experience developing web applications</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with Node.js software development</p></li><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with TypeScript</p></li><li><p>Experience developing Linux-based systems in AWS</p></li><li><p>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree or 7&#43; years of experience in software engineering in lieu of a degree </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b> Nice If You Have:</b>  </p><ul><li><p>Experience with Angular</p></li><li><p>Experience with ElasticSearch</p></li><li><p>Experience with MongoDB</p></li><li><p>Experience with Redis</p></li><li><p>Experience with AWS</p></li><li><p>Experience with DevOps, CI/CD, and IaC</p></li><li><p>Experience with designing, implementing, and deploying microservices</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 20 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
