{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Aberdeen-Proving-Ground-MD/Palantir-Data-Engineer_R0246475","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Aberdeen-Proving-Ground-MD/Palantir-Data-Engineer_R0246475","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"3e7a9ed43c513389078a999d82a82f4f8e5b0b33ebd3213edafa86722d31103d","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Palantir Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Aberdeen-Proving-Ground-MD/Palantir-Data-Engineer_R0246475","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Aberdeen-Proving-Ground-MD/Palantir-Data-Engineer_R0246475","locations":[{"label":"Aberdeen Proving Ground, MD"},{"label":"Norfolk, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246475","internal_job_id":"5fd54a09d5d0100111c1b650cf890000","first_published_at":"2026-08-11","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Palantir Data Engineer The Opportunity:\nAs an analytics professional, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi cia l intelligence. If you care about leading a mission forward as much as advancing the field of data science, this is the opportunity for you. Your deep analytics expertise, coupled with an original approach to your work, will guide clients and stakeholders as they make sense of their data and encourage actionable results. We’re looking for someone like you to support complex data exploration and analytics projects through your experience with Palantir for defense clients.\n\nAs an AI Solutions Architect on our defense technology team, you’ll introduce innovative met hodologies to make a real-world impact on protecting our military. You’ll share your skills in data engineering, data science modeling, and technology integration to shape the future of analytics through developing solutions to drive the mission forward.\n\nWe’ll keep you sharp and moving forward in your career, with access to the latest tools and met hods and opportunities to publish or present at conferences. Whether you’re improving government efficiency or providing better services to the public, you’ll lead a team that serves critical missions from end to end.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 3+ years of experience with Palantir Foundry AIP for application development\n- Experience with Python or TypeScript\n- Experience with data connections and Code Repositories or Pipeline Builder for data ingestion and transformation\n- Experience with Foundry application and workflow development in Workshop and Ontology Manager\n- Experience working with Agile sof tware teams, conducting code reviews, and implementing DevSecOps practices\n- Experience with Git repositories, CI / CD workflows, or infrastructure automation\n- Ability to e nga ge with stakeholders, define requirements, and translate them into technical solutions\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance\n- Bachelor’s degree and 5+ years of experience with Palantir Foundry, or Master’s degree and 3+ years of experience with Palantir Foundry\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with mission analytics or government-focused data solutions\n- Experience with AI or ML model integration within Foundry applications\n- Knowledge of Foundry security models, access control, and compliance frameworks\n- Master's degree in CS\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information .\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Palantir Data Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As an analytics professional, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence. If you care about leading a mission forward as much as advancing the field of data science, this is the opportunity for you. Your deep analytics expertise, coupled with an original approach to your work, will guide clients and stakeholders as they make sense of their data and encourage actionable results. We’re looking for someone like you to support complex data exploration and analytics projects through your <span>experience</span> with Palantir for defense clients.</p><p></p><p>As an AI Solutions Architect on our defense technology team, you’ll introduce innovative <span>met</span>hodologies to make a real-world impact on protecting our military. You’ll share your skills in data engineering, data science modeling, and technology integration to shape the future of analytics through developing solutions to drive the mission forward.</p><p></p><p>We’ll keep you sharp and moving forward in your career, with access to the latest tools and <span>met</span>hods and opportunities to publish or present at conferences. Whether you’re improving government efficiency or providing better services to the public, you’ll lead a team that serves critical missions from end to end.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with Palantir Foundry AIP for application development</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Python or TypeScript</li><li><span>Experience</span> with data connections and Code Repositories or Pipeline Builder for data ingestion and transformation</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Foundry application and workflow development in Workshop and Ontology Manager</li><li><span>Experience</span> working with Agile <span>sof</span>tware teams, conducting code reviews, and implementing DevSecOps practices</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Git repositories, CI<span>/</span>CD workflows, or infrastructure automation</li><li><span>Ability to</span> e<span>nga</span>ge with stakeholders, define requirements, and translate them into technical solutions</li><li><span>Ability to</span><span> obtain a Secret clearance</span></li><li><span>Bachelor’s degree</span> and 5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with Palantir Foundry, or <span>Master’s degree</span> and 3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with Palantir Foundry</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with mission analytics or government-focused data solutions</li><li><span>Experience</span> with AI or ML model integration within Foundry applications</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> Foundry security models, access control, and compliance frameworks</li><li><span>Master&#39;s degree</span> in CS</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span>.</p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 13 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
