ou’ll share your skills in data engineering, data science modeling and technology integration to shape the future of analytics through developing solutions to drive the mission forward.\n\nWe’ll keep you sharp and moving forward in your career, with access to the latest tools and methods and opportunities to publish or present at conferences. Whether you’re improving government efficiency or providing better services to the public, you’ll lead a team that serves critical missions from end to end.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 3+ years of experience with Palantir Foundry AIP for application development\n\n- Experience with Python or TypeScript\n\n- Experience with Data Connections and Code Repos or Pipeline Builder for data ingestion and transformation\n\n- Experience with Foundry application and workflow development in Workshop and Ontology Manager\n\n- Experience working with Agile software teams, conducting code reviews, and implementing DevSecOps practices\n\n- Experience with Git repositories, CI/CD workflows, or infrastructure automation\n\n- Ability to engage with stakeholders, define requirements, and translate them into technical solutions\n\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with mission analytics or government-focused data solutions\n\n- Experience with AI or ML model integration within Foundry applications\n\n- Knowledge of Foundry security models, access control, and compliance frameworks\n\n- Master's degree in Computer Science\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Palantir Data Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p>As an analytics professional, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence. If you care about leading a mission forward as much as advancing the field of data science, this is the opportunity for you. Your deep analytics expertise, coupled with an original approach to your work, will guide clients and stakeholders as they make sense of their data and encourage actionable results. We’re looking for someone like you to support complex data exploration and analytics projects through your experience with Palantir for Defense clients.</p><p></p><p>As an AI Solutions Architect on our Defense Technology team, you’ll introduce innovative methodologies to make a real-world impact on protecting our military. You’ll share your skills in data engineering, data science modeling and technology integration to shape the future of analytics through developing solutions to drive the mission forward.</p><p></p><p>We’ll keep you sharp and moving forward in your career, with access to the latest tools and methods and opportunities to publish or present at conferences. Whether you’re improving government efficiency or providing better services to the public, you’ll lead a team that serves critical missions from end to end.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b>You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of experience with Palantir Foundry AIP for application development</p></li><li><p>Experience with Python or TypeScript</p></li><li><p>Experience with Data Connections and Code Repos or Pipeline Builder for data ingestion and transformation</p></li><li><p>Experience with Foundry application and workflow development in Workshop and Ontology Manager</p></li><li><p>Experience working with Agile software teams, conducting code reviews, and implementing DevSecOps practices</p></li><li><p>Experience with Git repositories, CI/CD workflows, or infrastructure automation</p></li><li><p>Ability to engage with stakeholders, define requirements, and translate them into technical solutions</p></li><li><p>Ability to obtain a Secret clearance</p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>Experience with mission analytics or government-focused data solutions</p></li><li><p>Experience with AI or ML model integration within Foundry applications</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of Foundry security models, access control, and compliance frameworks</p></li><li><p>Master&#39;s degree in Computer Science</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Clearance:</b></p><p>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,600.00 to $176,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Norfolk-VA/Palantir-Data-Engineer_R0244009-1","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Norfolk-VA/Palantir-Data-Engineer_R0244009-1","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"7431b79b4c59da24c68d6c81c9bc77ac8760429106ee7added483f08423a25a0","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Palantir Data Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Norfolk-VA/Palantir-Data-Engineer_R0244009-1","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Norfolk-VA/Palantir-Data-Engineer_R0244009-1","locations":[{"label":"Norfolk, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0244009","internal_job_id":"5fd54a09d5d01000c5e063fabd700001","first_published_at":"2026-08-10","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Palantir Data Engineer The Opportunity:\nEver-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artifi cia l intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need a data professional like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions, from fraud detection to cancer research, to national intelligence. \n\nAs a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your skills and experience to help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll develop and deploy the pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful.\n\nHere, you’ll work with a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll sharpen your skills in analytical exploration and data examination while you support the assessment, design, development, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients.\n\nWork with us to use data for good.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have:\n- 3+ years of experience with data science, machine learning, data engineering, or data analytics\n- Experience with Palantir sof tware\n- Experience with data connections and code repos or pipeline builder for data ingestion and transformation\n- Experience working with Agile sof tware teams or conducting code reviews\n- Experience with infrastructure automation\n- Ability to e nga ge with stakeholders, define requirements, and translate them into technical solutions\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with Foundry application and workflow development in Workshop and Ontology Manager\n- Experience with mission analytics or government-focused data solutions\n- Experience with AI or ML model integration within Foundry applications\n- Knowledge of Foundry security models, access control, and compliance frameworks\n- Master's degree in CS\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information .\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Palantir Data Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>Ever-expanding technology like IoT, machine learning, and artifi<span>cia</span>l intelligence means that there’s more structured and unstructured data available today than ever before. As a data engineer, you know that organizing data can yield pivotal insights when it’s gathered from disparate sources. We need a data professional like you to help our clients find answers in their data to impact important missions, from fraud detection to cancer research, to national intelligence. </p><p></p><p>As a data engineer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your skills and <span>experience</span> to help build advanced technology solutions and implement data engineering activities on some of the most mission-driven projects in the industry. You’ll develop and deploy the pipelines and platforms that organize and make disparate data meaningful.</p><p></p><p>Here, you’ll work with a multi-disciplinary team of analysts, data engineers, developers, and data consumers in a fast-paced, agile environment. You’ll sharpen your skills in analytical exploration and data examination while you support the assessment, design, development, and maintenance of scalable platforms for your clients.</p><p></p><p>Work with us to use data for good.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with data science, machine learning, data engineering, or data analytics</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Palantir <span>sof</span>tware</li><li><span>Experience</span> with data connections and code repos or pipeline builder for data ingestion and transformation</li><li><span>Experience</span> working with Agile <span>sof</span>tware teams or conducting code reviews</li><li><span>Experience</span> with infrastructure automation</li><li><span>Ability to</span> e<span>nga</span>ge with stakeholders, define requirements, and translate them into technical solutions</li><li><span>Ability to</span><span> obtain a Secret clearance</span></li><li><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with Foundry application and workflow development in Workshop and Ontology Manager</li><li><span>Experience</span> with mission analytics or government-focused data solutions</li><li><span>Experience</span> with AI or ML model integration within Foundry applications</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> Foundry security models, access control, and compliance frameworks</li><li><span>Master&#39;s degree</span> in CS</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span>.</p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $61,900.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 14 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Springfield-VA/Palantir-Data-Scientist_R0247243","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Springfield-VA/Palantir-Data-Scientist_R0247243","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"9446e3df23dc66f134ff5e35c39a67273a22444e7f196c03866efc94ce6b8e11","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Palantir Data Scientist","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Springfield-VA/Palantir-Data-Scientist_R0247243","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Springfield-VA/Palantir-Data-Scientist_R0247243","locations":[{"label":"Springfield, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247243","internal_job_id":"ae74c1d5954e1001698341f88c960000","first_published_at":"2026-08-19","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Palantir Data Scientist The Opportunity:\nAs a Data Scientist, you're driven by curiosity and inspired by the challenge of uncovering insights from complex, messy data. You're passionate about solving real-world problems, and you're excited by the transformative potential of working with powerful tools like Palantir Foundry. In a world increasingly shaped by data, you see the opportunity to make a lasting impact from national security and defense to public health and critical infrastructure. \n\nAt Booz Allen, you'll be at the forefront of using Palantir’s advanced platforms to tackle high-impact, mission-critical problems. Working alongside engineers, analysts, and mission stakeholders, you’ll transform varied and often siloed data into actionable intelligence. Your work will help clients make informed, data-driven decisions that truly matter. \n\nAs a data scientist on our national security team, you’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. Not only will you provide a deep understanding of their data, but you’ll also advise your client on what the information means and how it can be used to make an impact on the tasking of national, commer cia l, and emerging assets.\n\nJoin us. The world can't wait. \n\nYou Have:  \n- 5+ years of experience with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining \n\n- 5+ years of experience with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis such as Python or R\n\n- 3+ years of experience analyzing structured and unstructured data sources\n\n- 1+ years of experience deploying data workflows and models within platforms such as Palantir Foundry or Gotham\n\n- Experience developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses, and visualization of targeted data sources\n\n- Experience leading the development of solutions to complex programs \n\n- Active TS/SCI clearance; willingness to take a polygraph exam\n\n- Bachelor’s degree\n\nNice If You Have:\n- 2+ years of experience with SQL\n\n- Experience with the design, production, and implementation of a federated approach to provide end-to-end GEOINT collection performance met rics that ensure continuity, consistency, agreement, transparency, and awareness\n\n- Experience working with structured and unstructured data in mission-critical environments\n\n- Experience building dashboards and visualizations using Foundry or Power BI\n\n- Experience in the development of algorithms leveraging SQL or NoSQL, R, or Python\n\n- Experience with distributed data or computing tools, including MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL  \n\n- Experience with visualization packages, including Plotly, Seaborn, or ggplot2 \n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph   \n\nClearance:  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; TS/SCI clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Palantir Data Scientist<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>As a Data Scientist, you&#39;re driven by curiosity and inspired by the challenge of uncovering insights from complex, messy data. You&#39;re passionate about solving real-world problems, and you&#39;re excited by the transformative potential of working with powerful tools like Palantir Foundry. In a world increasingly shaped by data, you see the opportunity to make a lasting impact from national security and defense to public health and critical infrastructure. </p><p></p><p>At Booz Allen, you&#39;ll be at the forefront of using Palantir’s advanced platforms to tackle high-impact, mission-critical problems. Working alongside engineers, analysts, and mission stakeholders, you’ll transform varied and often siloed data into actionable intelligence. Your work will help clients make informed, data-driven decisions that truly matter. </p><p></p><p>As a data scientist on our national security team, you’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs and then dig into their data-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. Not only will you provide a deep understanding of their data, but you’ll also advise your client on what the information means and how it can be used to make an impact on the tasking of national, commer<span>cia</span>l, and emerging assets.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b> </p><ul><li><p>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with data exploration, data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, or data mining </p></li><li><p>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with statistical and general-purpose programming languages for data analysis such as Python or R</p></li><li><p>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> analyzing structured and unstructured data sources</p></li><li><p>1&#43; years of <span>experience</span> deploying data workflows and models within platforms such as Palantir Foundry or Gotham</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses, and visualization of targeted data sources</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> leading the development of solutions to complex programs </p></li><li><p><span>Active TS/SCI clearance; willingness to take a polygraph exam</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor’s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with SQL</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with the design, production, and implementation of a federated approach to provide end-to-end GEOINT collection performance <span>met</span>rics that ensure continuity, consistency, agreement, transparency, and awareness</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> working with structured and unstructured data in mission-critical environments</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> building dashboards and visualizations using Foundry or Power BI</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> in the development of algorithms leveraging SQL or NoSQL, R, or Python</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with distributed data or computing tools, including MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL  </p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with visualization packages, including Plotly, Seaborn, or ggplot2 </p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</span>  </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b> </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>TS/SCI clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $99,000.00 to $225,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 5 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":2,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["data"],"role_matches":["Data Scientist"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":[],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
