nstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Power Platform Developer<p><b><span>The Opportunity</span></b><b>:</b></p><p>Design, develop, and implement Power Platform solutions by using out-of-the-box features to create custom pages, site templates, features, and Web parts. Write custom code to create and deploy Power Platform solutions, as needed. Customize and brand Sharepoint sites, configure workflows, and customize lists, pages, and forms using Power Platform. Support installation and configuration of Power Platform instances in cloud environments. Foster user adoption of Power Platform by demonstrating Power Platform features and technologies to clients and enabling the conversion of business requirements into solutions. Document system processes and procedures in a clear manner. Discuss requirements with clients and follow internal and client-specific protocols used to document and design Power Platform sites, templates, structure, and taxonomy development required to develop and implement solutions using Power Platform. Participate in all facets of the <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e development lifecycle, including requirements solicitation and documentation, system and acceptance testing, and training, as needed.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> developing custom PowerApps applications</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> working with Power Platform environmental data sourcing and management components, including connectors, gateways, and Office 365 integrations</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> integrating apps with SharePoint, Dataverse, and REST APIs</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> use Micro<span>sof</span>t Flow</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> design and implement Power BI dashboards, Power Automate Flows, Cloud flows, desktop flows, or business process flows</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> work with general web technologies, including AngularJS, SPFX, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and jQuery </p></li><li><p><span>Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> with database modeling and concepts, Performance Points, Reporting Services, Business Data Catalogs, and Business Connectivity Services</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Agile <span>Sof</span>t<span>war</span>e Development Life Cycle <span>met</span>hodology</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Object-Oriented Programming concepts</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> work in a team environment and offer or support ideas</p></li><li><p><span>Possession of</span> excellent verbal and written communication skills</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 7 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Platform","Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Arlington-VA/Power-Platform-Developer--Mid_R0245301","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Arlington-VA/Power-Platform-Developer--Mid_R0245301","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"f64fe8df2e29be31b854cf25b6eeec4d711712659519156bec3ff7529fc3f387","fetched_at":"2026-08-21T07:47:34.705Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Power Platform Developer, Mid","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Power-Platform-Developer--Mid_R0245301","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Arlington-VA/Power-Platform-Developer--Mid_R0245301","locations":[{"label":"Arlington, VA"},{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245301","internal_job_id":"ef696249f59b1001fcf39c726bc10000","first_published_at":"2026-07-24","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Power Platform Developer, Mid The Opportunity:\nSupports the design, development, and maintenance of   low code   and   no code   business applications and workflow automations using Microsoft Power Platform technologies. Applies foundational technical knowledge and growing advisory skills to contribute to solution delivery across the full development lifecycle. Works with guidance from senior developers and analysts while gaining experience engaging stakeholders, gathering requirements, and translating business needs into scalable technical solutions.\n \nAs a Power Platform Developer,   you’re   excited by the opportunity to solve real-world business challenges through intuitive applications and automated workflows.   You’ll   partner closely with stakeholders, business analysts, and senior developers to build and enhance solutions using Microsoft Power Apps, Power Automate, Power BI, and Microsoft 365 services.  \n\nIn this role,   you’ll   contribute to the full solution lifecycle, from understanding user needs and gathering requirements, through application development and workflow automation, to testing, deployment, and continuous improvement. Your ability to analyze problems, learn   new technologies , and collaborate across teams will help clients streamline operations and unlock the value of modern low-code platforms. Join us as we build innovative digital solutions that improve mission outcomes and empower users across our client environments.  \n\n \nJoin us. The world can't wait.\n\nYou Have:  \n\n- 1+ years of experience building low-code/no-code solutions using Microsoft Power Apps, Power Automate, or Power BI \n\n- Experience with core technical concepts such as Power Fx, JSON, REST APIs, Excel formulas, or basic scripting principles \n\n- Knowledge of data sources such as Microsoft Dataverse, SharePoint Online, Excel, or SQL databases \n\n- Ability to gather requirements and translate business needs into workflows, forms, dashboards, and automated processes \n\n- Ability to work independently and collaboratively within a team\n\n- Ability to obtain a Secret clearance  \n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\n \n\nNice If You Have:  \n\n- Experience developing solutions supporting federal government clients, particularly Department of War (DoW) organizations\n\n- Experience building Canvas Apps, Model-Driven Apps, Power Automate cloud flows, or Power BI reports and dashboards  \n\n- Experience with Power Platform Application Lifecycle Management (ALM), solution deployment, and environment management \n\n- Experience working with SharePoint Online, Microsoft Teams integrations, Microsoft Forms, or custom connectors  \n\n- Experience with Agile methodologies and tools such as Azure DevOps or Jira and Azure services such as Logic Apps, Azure Functions, API Management, or cloud computing fundamentals  \n\n- Experience working with relational data structures and basic SQL queries \n\n- Knowledge of user experience (UX) and user interface (UI) design principles  \n\n- Knowledge of Microsoft 365 administration concepts and security best practices  \n\n- Possession of strong analytical, problem-solving, troubleshooting, and clear and effective verbal and written communication skills \n\n- Microsoft Certifications such as Microsoft Certified: Power Platform Fundamentals (PL-900), Microsoft Certified: Power Platform App Maker Associate (PL-100), or Microsoft Certified: Power Platform Functional Consultant Associate (PL-200) Certification\n\n \n\nClearance:  \n\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.  \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Power Platform Developer, Mid<div><div><p><b>The Opportunity:</b></p><p><span><span>Supports the design, development, and maintenance of<span> </span></span><span>low</span><span>code</span><span><span> </span>and<span> </span></span><span>no</span><span>code</span><span><span> </span>business applications and workflow automations using Microsoft Power Platform technologies. Applies foundational technical knowledge and growing advisory skills to contribute to solution delivery across the full development lifecycle. Works with guidance from senior developers and analysts while gaining experience engaging stakeholders, gathering requirements, and translating business needs into scalable technical solutions. </span></span><br /><span><span> </span></span><br /><span><span>As a Power Platform Developer,<span> </span></span><span>you’re</span><span><span> </span>excited by the opportunity to solve real-world business challenges through intuitive applications and automated workflows.<span> </span></span><span>You’ll</span><span><span> </span>partner closely with stakeholders, business analysts, and senior developers to build and enhance solutions using Microsoft Power Apps, Power Automate, Power BI, and Microsoft 365 services.</span></span><span> </span></p></div><div><p></p></div><div><p><span><span>In this role,<span> </span></span><span>you’ll</span><span><span> </span>contribute to the full solution lifecycle, from understanding user needs and gathering requirements, through application development and workflow automation, to testing, deployment, and continuous improvement. Your ability to analyze problems, learn<span> </span></span><span>new technologies</span><span>, and collaborate across teams will help clients streamline operations and unlock the value of modern low-code platforms. </span></span><span><span>Join us as we build innovative digital solutions that improve mission outcomes and empower users across our client environments.</span></span><span> </span></p></div><div><p><span><span> </span></span></p><p>Join us. The world can&#39;t wait.</p><p><br /><b><span>You Have:</span></b><span> </span></p></div><div><ul><li><p>1&#43; years of experience building low-code/no-code solutions using Microsoft Power Apps, Power Automate, or Power BI </p></li><li><p>Experience with core technical concepts such as Power Fx, JSON, REST APIs, Excel formulas, or basic scripting principles </p></li><li><p>Knowledge of data sources such as Microsoft Dataverse, SharePoint Online, Excel, or SQL databases </p></li><li><p>Ability to gather requirements and translate business needs into workflows, forms, dashboards, and automated processes </p></li><li><p>Ability to work independently and collaboratively within a team</p></li><li><p>Ability to obtain a Secret clearance  </p></li><li><p>Bachelor&#39;s degree</p></li></ul></div></div><div><div><p><span> </span></p></div><div><p><b><span>Nice If You Have:</span></b><span> </span></p></div><div><ul><li><p>Experience developing solutions supporting federal government clients, particularly Department of War (DoW) organizations</p></li><li><p>Experience building Canvas Apps, Model-Driven Apps, Power Automate cloud flows, or Power BI reports and dashboards  </p></li><li><p>Experience with Power Platform Application Lifecycle Management (ALM), solution deployment, and environment management </p></li><li><p>Experience working with SharePoint Online, Microsoft Teams integrations, Microsoft Forms, or custom connectors  </p></li><li><p>Experience with Agile methodologies and tools such as Azure DevOps or Jira and Azure services such as Logic Apps, Azure Functions, API Management, or cloud computing fundamentals  </p></li><li><p>Experience working with relational data structures and basic SQL queries </p></li><li><p>Knowledge of user experience (UX) and user interface (UI) design principles  </p></li><li><p>Knowledge of Microsoft 365 administration concepts and security best practices  </p></li><li><p>Possession of strong analytical, problem-solving, troubleshooting, and clear and effective verbal and written communication skills </p></li><li><p>Microsoft Certifications such as Microsoft Certified: Power Platform Fundamentals (PL-900), Microsoft Certified: Power Platform App Maker Associate (PL-100), or Microsoft Certified: Power Platform Functional Consultant Associate (PL-200) Certification</p></li></ul></div><div><p><span> </span></p></div><div><p><b><span><span>Clearance:</span></span><span> </span></b></p></div><div><p><span><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.</span></span><span> </span></p></div></div><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 28 Days Ago"},"status":"closed","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-21T07:47:34.705Z","closed_at":"2026-08-24T14:15:46.938Z","possibly_closed_at":"2026-08-24T01:56:20.339Z","missing_complete_scans":2,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Platform","Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Rockville-MD/Power-Platform-Developer--Senior_R0240817","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Rockville-MD/Power-Platform-Developer--Senior_R0240817","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"8b3e27ef1ee95fe6fea5dcc78d42dba6e44df7dc01b1948eec1bfff35c49f1c0","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Power Platform Developer, Senior","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Rockville-MD/Power-Platform-Developer--Senior_R0240817","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Rockville-MD/Power-Platform-Developer--Senior_R0240817","locations":[{"label":"Rockville, MD"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"unknown","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0240817","internal_job_id":null,"first_published_at":null,"source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":null,"description_html":null,"compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":null,"country":null,"posted_on":"Posted 7 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":false,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"senior","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Platform","Developer"],"exclude_matches":["Senior"],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:R0245792","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"R0245792","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"782962fef989a90aba726e933d7d81f5d8fe85e0422b51ef855e7bcf39b8ef5a","fetched_at":"2026-08-20T07:20:48.759Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Power Platform Solution Developer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Power-Platform-Solution-Developer_R0245792-1","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Power-Platform-Solution-Developer_R0245792-1","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0245792","internal_job_id":"cdcfc075bb40100119ffe297a80f0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-11","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Power Platform Solution Developer The Opportunity:\nA solution developer on our team uses equal parts skill and vision to build a user experience that delivers functionality and efficiency. Our solution developers combine the analytical power of a data scientist with the ability to design intuitive visualizations that drive important business and client decisions. They are responsible for both developing new analytical tools and designing dashboard interfaces that enhance user experience and operational efficiency.\n\nWe need an experience d Dataverse developer who will use their passion to design, develop, and maintain Power Platform solutions while helping to ingest and visualize data to empower our client to make meaningful insights and informed decisions. This is an opportunity to solve problems both with external clients and our internal team by collaborating with a development team and functional experts to leverage Power Platform and Power BI to build user-centric solutions. You will coordinate with workforce spe cia lists, UI / UX designers, and Power BI development team members to create a seamless user experience using Power BI. You will ensure accessibility for all users by developing a solution that functions across browsers, platforms, and devices while meeting accessibility and security requirements. With opportunities to learn new tools and skills, mentoring, and positive code reviews, we focus on growing as a team to create the best solutions for our customers. Due to the nature of work performed within this facility, U.S. citizen ship is required .\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 3+ years of experience with Micro sof t Dataverse \n- 3+ years of experience with Python and JavaScript \n- 3+ years of experience with Micro sof t Power BI for development, data visualization, data analytics, and dashboards  \n- Experience with data storage and analysis, including SQL\n- Experience with APIs\n- Knowledge of ETL and data transformation \n- Knowledge of human capital and workforce analytics \n- Ability to provide communication to multiple levels of stakeholders and end-users \n- Ability to obtain and maintain a Public Trust or Suitability/Fitness determination based on client requirements\n- Bachelor’s degree in CS, Engineering, or Mathematics and 10+ years of experience in data, analytics, or development, or 18+ years of experience in data, analytics, or development in lieu of a degree\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience with APIs such as Placer.ai, REST, and SOAP \n- Experience in a sof tware developer or data science role \n- Experience with SharePoint \n- Knowledge of human capital and workforce analytics \n- Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills\n- Public Trust\n\nVetting:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a government investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements of the U.S. government client .\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Power Platform Solution Developer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>A solution developer on our team uses equal parts skill and vision to build a user <span>experience</span> that delivers functionality and efficiency. Our solution developers combine the analytical power of a data scientist with the <span>ability to</span> design intuitive visualizations that drive important business and client decisions. They are responsible for both developing new analytical tools and designing dashboard interfaces that enhance user <span>experience</span> and operational efficiency.</p><p><br />We need an <span>experience</span>d Dataverse developer who will use their passion to design, develop, and maintain Power Platform solutions while helping to ingest and visualize data to empower our client to make meaningful insights and informed decisions. This is an opportunity to solve problems both with external clients and our internal team by collaborating with a development team and functional experts to leverage Power Platform and Power BI to build user-centric solutions. You will coordinate with workforce spe<span>cia</span>lists, UI<span>/</span>UX designers, and Power BI development team members to create a seamless user <span>experience</span> using Power BI. You will ensure accessibility for all users by developing a solution that functions across browsers, platforms, and devices while meeting accessibility and security requirements. With opportunities to learn new tools and skills, mentoring, and positive code reviews, we focus on growing as a team to create the best solutions for our customers. <span>Due to the nature of work performed within this facility, U.S. </span><span>citizen</span><span>ship is required</span>.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with Micro<span>sof</span>t Dataverse </li><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with Python and JavaScript </li><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with Micro<span>sof</span>t Power BI for development, data visualization, data analytics, and dashboards  </li><li><span>Experience</span> with data storage and analysis, including SQL</li><li><span>Experience</span> with APIs</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> ETL and data transformation </li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> human capital and workforce analytics </li><li><span>Ability to</span> provide communication to multiple levels of stakeholders and end-users </li><li><span>Ability to</span><span> obtain and maintain a Public Trust or Suitability/Fitness determination based on client requirements </span></li><li><span>Bachelor’s degree</span> in CS, Engineering, or Mathematics and 10&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in data, analytics, or development, or 18&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in data, analytics, or development in lieu of a degree</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with APIs such as Placer.ai, REST, and SOAP </li><li><span>Experience</span> in a <span>sof</span>tware developer or data science role </li><li><span>Experience</span> with SharePoint </li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> human capital and workforce analytics </li><li><span>Possession of</span> excellent verbal and written communication skills</li><li><span>Public Trust </span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Vetting: </span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a government investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements of the U.S. government client</span>.</p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 9 Days Ago"},"status":"closed","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-20T07:20:48.759Z","closed_at":"2026-08-21T07:47:34.705Z","possibly_closed_at":"2026-08-20T19:35:50.646Z","missing_complete_scans":2,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":4,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Platform","Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
