{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/Salesforce-Developer--Mid_R0247567","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/Salesforce-Developer--Mid_R0247567","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"79d5ce7da8d133b53fba707b0cca9268f2463fee8500e71c3b455f0b67adba79","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Salesforce Developer, Mid","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Salesforce-Developer--Mid_R0247567","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Salesforce-Developer--Mid_R0247567","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0247567","internal_job_id":"ce7800f7d146100206a08d4720f30000","first_published_at":"2026-08-21","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Salesforce Developer, Mid The Opportunity:\nAs a Salesforce develop er, you will work closely with other develop ers, product owners, test engineers, and architects to ensure the timely and effective delivery of Salesforce requirements in a variety of industry contexts. You'll work in all aspects of the Salesforce develop ment lifecycle, including configuration, customization, and implementation of applications and 3rd party integrations. You’ll also serve as an advisor to our clients and provide guidance regarding how they might adopt new technologies or add new features to support the mission.\n\nIn this role, you’ll have an impact from day one. You'll apply extensive experience develop ing on the Salesforce platform following best practices and utilizing Salesforce declarative capabilities where appropriate. You'll build positive relationships with other team members, write clean, maintainable Apex code while keeping governor limits in mind. You'll be able to use web develop ment technologies such as Lightning Web Components, and the platform’s declarative capabilities. Most importantly, you’ll advise our government clients on the best ways to improve and modernize their existing systems.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have:\n- 3+ years of experience with Salesforce platform develop ment, including Apex, JavaScript, Visualforce pages, and Aura Components or Lightning Web Components\n- 3+ years of experience with sof tware engineering or sof tware develop ment\n- Experience with committing code and met adata to git repositories, and Salesforce DevOps technologies and tools, including GitHub, Copado, Salesforce DX, and Flosum\n- Experience integrating Salesforce with external systems and applications using REST and SOAP APIs, Batch, and Async processes\n- Knowledge of version control systems, including Git and Bitbucket\n- Knowledge of the Salesforce develop ment lifecycle\n- Knowledge of Agile met hodologies\n- Secret clearance\n- Bachelor’s degree\n- Salesforce Platform Develop er I Certification\n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience with Java, Python, C#, Kotlin, C / C++, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and SQL\n- Active TS/SCI clearance; willingness to take a polygraph exam\n- Bachelor’s degree in Computer Engineering or Computer Science\n- Salesforce Platform Develop er II Certification , JavaScript Develop er Certification , or Omnistudio Develop er Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Salesforce Developer, Mid<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As a Salesforce <span>develop</span>er, you will work closely with other <span>develop</span>ers, product owners, test engineers, and architects to ensure the timely and effective delivery of Salesforce requirements in a variety of industry contexts. You&#39;ll work in all aspects of the Salesforce <span>develop</span>ment lifecycle, including configuration, customization, and implementation of applications and 3rd party integrations. You’ll also serve as an advisor to our clients and provide guidance regarding how they might adopt new technologies or add new features to support the mission.</p><p></p><p>In this role, you’ll have an impact from day one. You&#39;ll apply extensive <span>experience</span> <span>develop</span>ing on the Salesforce platform following best practices and utilizing Salesforce declarative capabilities where appropriate. You&#39;ll build positive relationships with other team members, write clean, maintainable Apex code while keeping governor limits in mind. You&#39;ll be able to use web <span>develop</span>ment technologies such as Lightning Web Components, and the platform’s declarative capabilities. Most importantly, you’ll advise our government clients on the best ways to improve and modernize their existing systems.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have:</span></b></p><ul><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with Salesforce platform <span>develop</span>ment, including Apex, JavaScript, Visualforce pages, and Aura Components or Lightning Web Components</li><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with <span>sof</span>tware engineering or <span>sof</span>tware <span>develop</span>ment</li><li><span>Experience</span> with committing code and <span>met</span>adata to git repositories, and Salesforce DevOps technologies and tools, including GitHub, Copado, Salesforce DX, and Flosum</li><li><span>Experience</span> integrating Salesforce with external systems and applications using REST and SOAP APIs, Batch, and Async processes</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> version control systems, including Git and Bitbucket</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> the Salesforce <span>develop</span>ment lifecycle</li><li><span>Knowledge of</span> Agile <span>met</span>hodologies</li><li><span>Secret clearance</span></li><li><span>Bachelor’s degree</span></li><li>Salesforce Platform <span>Develop</span>er I <span>Certification</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with Java, Python, C#, Kotlin, C<span>/</span>C&#43;&#43;, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and SQL</li><li><span>Active TS/SCI clearance; willingness to take a polygraph exam</span></li><li><span>Bachelor’s degree</span> in Computer Engineering or Computer Science</li><li>Salesforce Platform <span>Develop</span>er II <span>Certification</span>, JavaScript <span>Develop</span>er <span>Certification</span>, or Omnistudio <span>Develop</span>er <span>Certification</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span>; Secret clearance is required.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $62,000.00 to $141,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 3 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-24T01:56:20.339Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Developer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Developer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/McLean-VA/Salesforce-Platform-Engineer_R0242944","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/McLean-VA/Salesforce-Platform-Engineer_R0242944","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"29aca8e608dbc7f9db03efa79e37a91035a28bb0de709539621f67eb668010d4","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Salesforce Platform Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Salesforce-Platform-Engineer_R0242944","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/McLean-VA/Salesforce-Platform-Engineer_R0242944","locations":[{"label":"McLean, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0242944","internal_job_id":"93ded21bf03e10015efdf7ea46230000","first_published_at":"2026-07-20","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Salesforce Platform Engineer The Opportunity:\nAs a full stack developer, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast, agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just develop sof tware, but to help create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for a developer like you with the skills needed to develop sof tware and systems from vision to production ready. \n\nThis role is more than just coding. As a full stack developer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to learn new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll help make sure the solution developed by the team considers the current architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements. Due to the nature of work performed within this facility, U.S. citizenship is required.\n\nWork with us as we shape systems for the better.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.  \n\nYou Have:   \n- 2+ years of experience with Salesforce platform delivery, including Flow, Apex, and Lightning Web Components \n\n- Experience committing code and metadata to Git repositories  \n\n- Experience with Salesforce DevOps tools and practices, including GitHub, or Salesforce DX \n\n- Knowledge of Agile methodologies \n\n- Knowledge of the Salesforce development lifecycle \n\n- Bachelors degree, or 5+ years of experience in software engineering in lieu of degree \n\nNice If You Have:\n- Experience supporting Sales Cloud and Agentforce implementations \n\n- Possession of strong verbal and written communication skills \n\n- Salesforce Administrator, Platform App Builder Certification, or Salesforce Platform Developer Certification \n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Salesforce Platform Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As a full stack developer, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast, agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just develop <span>sof</span>tware, but to help create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for a developer like you with the skills needed to develop <span>sof</span>tware and systems from vision to production ready. </p><p></p><p>This role is more than just coding. As a full stack developer at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to learn new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll help make sure the solution developed by the team considers the <span>current</span> architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements. Due to the nature of work performed within this facility, U.S. citizenship is required.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we shape systems for the better.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.  </p><p></p><p><b>You Have:   </b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of experience with Salesforce platform delivery, including Flow, Apex, and Lightning Web Components </p></li><li><p>Experience committing code and metadata to Git repositories  </p></li><li><p>Experience with Salesforce DevOps tools and practices, including GitHub, or Salesforce DX </p></li><li><p>Knowledge of Agile methodologies </p></li><li><p>Knowledge of the Salesforce development lifecycle </p></li><li><p>Bachelors degree, or 5&#43; years of experience in software engineering in lieu of degree </p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Nice If You Have:</b></p><ul><li><p>Experience supporting Sales Cloud and Agentforce implementations </p></li><li><p>Possession of strong verbal and written communication skills </p></li><li><p>Salesforce Administrator, Platform App Builder Certification, or Salesforce Platform Developer Certification </p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Platform Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Platform"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
