 eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,300.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Software Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As a full stack <span>develop</span>er, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast, agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just <span>develop</span> <span>sof</span>tware, but to help create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for a <span>develop</span>er like you with the <span>skills</span> needed to <span>develop</span> <span>sof</span>tware and systems from vision to production-ready. </p><p></p><p>This role is more than just coding. As a full stack <span>develop</span>er at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to learn new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll help make sure the solution <span>develop</span>ed by the team considers the <span>current</span> architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements.  </p><p></p><p>Work with us as we shape systems for the better.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> designing, modifying, <span>develop</span>ing, writing, and implementing <span>sof</span>tware programming applications  </li><li>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>tware <span>develop</span>ment with basic programming languages, technologies, tools, or web <span>develop</span>ment stacks  </li><li><span>Experience</span> writing source code for new applications or generating and enhancing code samples for existing applications </li><li><span>Experience</span> using back-end and front-end languages to <span>develop</span> complete solutions </li><li><span>Experience</span> creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative team environment </li><li><span>Secret clearance </span></li><li><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span> or 5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>tware engineering in lieu of a degree </li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with Agile <span>met</span>hodology, extreme programming, <span>sof</span>tware engineering, product management, and <span>sof</span>tware products </li><li><span>Experience</span> with Java, Python, C#, C, C&#43;&#43;, .NET, JavaScript, React, NodeJS, PHP, or Drupal </li><li><span>Ability to</span> acquire client requirements and resolve workflow problems through automation optimization </li><li><span>Ability to</span> work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance </li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,300.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Beavercreek-OH/Software-Engineer_R0243546","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Beavercreek-OH/Software-Engineer_R0243546","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"15f82d7094ec29851255103d4fd604d7a7fdf8420a9e1e29bf0795dccf41a7de","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Beavercreek-OH/Software-Engineer_R0243546","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Beavercreek-OH/Software-Engineer_R0243546","locations":[{"label":"Beavercreek, OH"},{"label":"Arlington, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0243546","internal_job_id":"8a40f76bf6d61001681b00882adc0000","first_published_at":"2026-07-01","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Software Engineer The Opportunity:\nAs a full stack develop er, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast, agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just develop sof tware, but to help create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for a develop er like you with the skills needed to develop sof tware and systems from vision to production-ready. \n\nThis role is more than just coding. As a full stack develop er at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to learn new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll help make sure the solution develop ed by the team considers the current architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements.  \n\nWork with us as we shape systems for the better.  \n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait. \n\nYou Have: \n- 2+ years of experience designing, modifying, develop ing, writing, and implementing sof tware programming applications  \n- 2+ years of experience in sof tware develop ment with basic programming languages, technologies, tools, or web develop ment stacks  \n- Experience writing source code for new applications or generating and enhancing code samples for existing applications \n- Experience using back-end and front-end languages to develop complete solutions \n- Experience creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative team environment \n- Secret clearance \n- Bachelor's degree or 5+ years of experience in sof tware engineering in lieu of a degree \n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience with Agile met hodology, extreme programming, sof tware engineering, product management, and sof tware products \n- Experience with Java, Python, C#, C, C++, .NET, JavaScript, React, NodeJS, PHP, or Drupal \n- Ability to acquire client requirements and resolve workflow problems through automation optimization \n- Ability to work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance \n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,300.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Software Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity:</span></b></p><p>As a full stack <span>develop</span>er, you can resolve a problem with a complete end-to-end solution in a fast, agile environment. If you’re looking for the chance to not just <span>develop</span> <span>sof</span>tware, but to help create a system that will make a difference, we need you on our team. We’re looking for a <span>develop</span>er like you with the <span>skills</span> needed to <span>develop</span> <span>sof</span>tware and systems from vision to production-ready. </p><p></p><p>This role is more than just coding. As a full stack <span>develop</span>er at Booz Allen, you’ll use your passion to learn new tools and techniques and identify needed system improvements. You’ll help clients overcome their most difficult challenges using the latest architectural approaches, tools, and technologies. You’ll help make sure the solution <span>develop</span>ed by the team considers the <span>current</span> architecture and operating environment, as well as future functionality and enhancements.  </p><p></p><p>Work with us as we shape systems for the better.  </p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait. </p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> designing, modifying, <span>develop</span>ing, writing, and implementing <span>sof</span>tware programming applications  </li><li>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>tware <span>develop</span>ment with basic programming languages, technologies, tools, or web <span>develop</span>ment stacks  </li><li><span>Experience</span> writing source code for new applications or generating and enhancing code samples for existing applications </li><li><span>Experience</span> using back-end and front-end languages to <span>develop</span> complete solutions </li><li><span>Experience</span> creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative team environment </li><li><span>Secret clearance </span></li><li><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span> or 5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>tware engineering in lieu of a degree </li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> with Agile <span>met</span>hodology, extreme programming, <span>sof</span>tware engineering, product management, and <span>sof</span>tware products </li><li><span>Experience</span> with Java, Python, C#, C, C&#43;&#43;, .NET, JavaScript, React, NodeJS, PHP, or Drupal </li><li><span>Ability to</span> acquire client requirements and resolve workflow problems through automation optimization </li><li><span>Ability to</span> work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance </li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,300.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0237844-1","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0237844-1","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"1e5d73b62d1886b7987dfe1f697a4d8bfb29e792af10f9ea3e0c2ca8317e9336","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0237844-1","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0237844-1","locations":[{"label":"Chantilly, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0237844","internal_job_id":"c219b70d827e100159157cde50970001","first_published_at":"2026-07-13","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Software Engineer The Opportunity: \nBooz Allen is looking for a Sof t war e Engineer who is driven by purpose and ready to build sof t war e that directly supports mission‑critical operations across the space domain. In this role, you’ll design, develop, and enhance the sof t war e developed for ground systems and the real‑time capabilities that space missions rely on.\n\nYou’ll take ownership of complex engineering challenges from modernizing legacy components to architecting new mission‑focused capabilities that improve performance, resilience, and operational speed. Your work will shape how data is processed, how systems communicate, and how mission teams execute with precision.\n\nThis role is built for someone who thrives on solving hard problems, emb race s innovation, and understands the responsibility of building sof t war e that must perform flawlessly. If you’re motivated by mission impact, energized by technical depth, and ready to engineer solutions that advance GEOINT and space operations, we want to meet you.\n\nWork with us as we shape systems for the better.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have: \n- 2+ years of experience in sof t war e development with programming languages, including Java, Python, Rus t, or GO\n- Experience transitioning legacy applications to a modernized microservice-based architecture\n- Experience writing source code for new applications or generating and enhancing code samples for existing applications\n- Experience creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative, cross-functional team\n- Top Secret clearance\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience operating within an Agile environment\n- Experience with Linux-based systems, containers, and orchestration tools, including Docker or Kubernetes\n- Experience designing, modifying, developing, writing, and implementing sof t war e programming applications\n- Experience acquiring client requirements and resolving workflow problems through automation optimization\n- Experience working within a Cloud Solution Provider ( CSP ) , including AWS, Azure, or Google\n- Experience with C#, C, C++, JavaScript, React, or Node.js\n- Ability to work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n- Master’s degree\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Top Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Software Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>Booz Allen is looking for a <span>Sof</span>t<span>war</span>e Engineer who is driven by purpose and ready to build <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e that directly supports mission‑critical operations across the space domain. In this role, you’ll design, develop, and enhance the <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e developed for ground systems and the real‑time capabilities that space missions rely on.</p><p></p><p>You’ll take ownership of complex engineering challenges from modernizing legacy components to architecting new mission‑focused capabilities that improve performance, resilience, and operational speed. Your work will shape how data is processed, how systems communicate, and how mission teams execute with precision.</p><p></p><p>This role is built for someone who thrives on solving hard problems, emb<span>race</span>s innovation, and understands the responsibility of building <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e that must perform flawlessly. If you’re motivated by mission impact, energized by technical depth, and ready to engineer solutions that advance GEOINT and space operations, we want to meet you.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we shape systems for the better.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e development with programming languages, including Java, Python, <span>Rus</span>t, or GO</li><li><span>Experience</span> transitioning legacy applications to a modernized microservice-based architecture</li><li><span>Experience</span> writing source code for new applications or generating and enhancing code samples for existing applications</li><li><span>Experience</span> creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative, cross-functional team</li><li><span>Top Secret clearance</span></li><li><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> operating within an Agile environment</li><li><span>Experience</span> with Linux-based systems, containers, and orchestration tools, including Docker or Kubernetes</li><li><span>Experience</span> designing, modifying, developing, writing, and implementing <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e programming applications</li><li><span>Experience</span> acquiring client requirements and resolving workflow problems through automation optimization</li><li><span>Experience</span> working within a Cloud Solution Provider <span>(</span>CSP<span>)</span>, including AWS, Azure, or Google</li><li><span>Experience</span> with C#, C, C&#43;&#43;, JavaScript, React, or Node.js</li><li><span>Ability to</span> work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance</li><li><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</span></li><li><span>Master’s degree</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Top Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 30+ Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0239081","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0239081","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"af1c47d1e75c6b5e65ec11ce596182cf49ff227771f70ec49c90b0e4a19295f5","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0239081","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0239081","locations":[{"label":"Chantilly, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0239081","internal_job_id":"300ac85b20c21001b2a0b423b41c0000","first_published_at":"2026-07-30","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Software Engineer The Opportunity: \nBooz Allen is looking for a Sof t war e Engineer who is driven by purpose and ready to build sof t war e that directly supports mission‑critical operations across the space domain. In this role, you’ll design, develop, and enhance the sof t war e developed for ground systems and the real‑time capabilities that space missions rely on.\n\nYou’ll take ownership of complex engineering challenges from modernizing legacy components to architecting new mission‑focused capabilities that improve performance, resilience, and operational speed. Your work will shape how data is processed, how systems communicate, and how mission teams execute with precision.\n\nThis role is built for someone who thrives on solving hard problems, emb race s innovation, and understands the responsibility of building sof t war e that must perform flawlessly. If you’re motivated by mission impact, energized by technical depth, and ready to engineer solutions that advance GEOINT and space operations, we want to meet you.\n\nWork with us as we shape systems for the better.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have: \n- 2+ years of experience in sof t war e development with programming languages, including Java, Python, Rus t, or GO\n\n- Experience transitioning legacy applications to a modernized microservice-based architecture\n\n- Experience writing source code for new applications or generating and enhancing code samples for existing applications\n\n- Experience creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative, cross-functional team\n\n- Top Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience operating within an Agile environment\n\n- Experience with Linux-based systems, containers, and orchestration tools, including Docker or Kubernetes\n\n- Experience designing, modifying, developing, writing, and implementing sof t war e programming applications\n\n- Experience acquiring client requirements and resolving workflow problems through automation optimization\n\n- Experience working within a Cloud Solution Provider ( CSP ) , including AWS, Azure, or Google\n\n- Experience with C#, C, C++, JavaScript, React, or Node.js\n\n- Ability to work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- Master’s degree\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Top Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Software Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>Booz Allen is looking for a <span>Sof</span>t<span>war</span>e Engineer who is driven by purpose and ready to build <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e that directly supports mission‑critical operations across the space domain. In this role, you’ll design, develop, and enhance the <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e developed for ground systems and the real‑time capabilities that space missions rely on.</p><p></p><p>You’ll take ownership of complex engineering challenges from modernizing legacy components to architecting new mission‑focused capabilities that improve performance, resilience, and operational speed. Your work will shape how data is processed, how systems communicate, and how mission teams execute with precision.</p><p></p><p>This role is built for someone who thrives on solving hard problems, emb<span>race</span>s innovation, and understands the responsibility of building <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e that must perform flawlessly. If you’re motivated by mission impact, energized by technical depth, and ready to engineer solutions that advance GEOINT and space operations, we want to meet you.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we shape systems for the better.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e development with programming languages, including Java, Python, <span>Rus</span>t, or GO</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> transitioning legacy applications to a modernized microservice-based architecture</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> writing source code for new applications or generating and enhancing code samples for existing applications</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative, cross-functional team</p></li><li><p><span>Top Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> operating within an Agile environment</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Linux-based systems, containers, and orchestration tools, including Docker or Kubernetes</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> designing, modifying, developing, writing, and implementing <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e programming applications</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> acquiring client requirements and resolving workflow problems through automation optimization</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> working within a Cloud Solution Provider <span>(</span>CSP<span>)</span>, including AWS, Azure, or Google</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with C#, C, C&#43;&#43;, JavaScript, React, or Node.js</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance</p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</span></p></li><li><p><span>Master’s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Top Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 25 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0241095","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0241095","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"30add4012979708f7253adfb2d4f2e743619b5618961fba4963ef07a15dfe9a7","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0241095","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0241095","locations":[{"label":"Chantilly, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0241095","internal_job_id":"31e03fc9eb56100166962c758e7c0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-24","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Software Engineer The Opportunity: \nBooz Allen is looking for a Sof tware Engineer who is driven by purpose and ready to build sof tware that directly supports mission‑critical operations across the space domain. In this role, you’ll design, develop, and enhance the sof tware developed for ground systems and the real‑time capabilities that space missions rely on.\n\nYou’ll take ownership of complex engineering challenges from modernizing legacy components to architecting new mission‑focused capabilities that improve performance, resilience, and operational speed. Your work will shape how data is processed, how systems communicate, and how mission teams execute with precision.\n\nThis role is built for someone who thrives on solving hard problems, emb race s innovation, and understands the responsibility of building sof tware that must perform flawlessly. If you’re motivated by mission impact, energized by technical depth, and ready to engineer solutions that advance GEOINT and space operations, we want to meet you.\n\nWork with us as we shape systems for the better.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have: \n- 5+ years of experience in sof tware development with programming languages such as Java, Python, Rus t, or GO\n- 3+ years of experience with Linux-based systems, containers, and orchestration tools such as Docker or Kubernetes\n- Experience transitioning legacy applications to a modernized microservice-based architecture\n- Experience working within a Cloud Service Provider ( CSP ) such as AWS, Azure, or Google\n- Experience using back-end and front-end languages to develop complete solutions\n- Experience creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative, cross-functional team\n- Top Secret clearance\n- Bachelor's degree and 5+ years of experience in sof tware engineering, or 10+ years of experience in sof tware engineering in lieu of a degree\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience in an Agile environment\n- Experience acquiring client requirements and resolving workflow problems through automation optimization\n- Experience with C#, C, C++, JavaScript, React, or Node.JS\n- Ability to work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n- Master’s degree\n\nClearance :  \nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Top Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Software Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>Booz Allen is looking for a <span>Sof</span>tware Engineer who is driven by purpose and ready to build <span>sof</span>tware that directly supports mission‑critical operations across the space domain. In this role, you’ll design, develop, and enhance the <span>sof</span>tware developed for ground systems and the real‑time capabilities that space missions rely on.</p><p><br />You’ll take ownership of complex engineering challenges from modernizing legacy components to architecting new mission‑focused capabilities that improve performance, resilience, and operational speed. Your work will shape how data is processed, how systems communicate, and how mission teams execute with precision.</p><p><br />This role is built for someone who thrives on solving hard problems, emb<span>race</span>s innovation, and understands the responsibility of building <span>sof</span>tware that must perform flawlessly. If you’re motivated by mission impact, energized by technical depth, and ready to engineer solutions that advance GEOINT and space operations, we want to meet you.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we shape systems for the better.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li>5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>tware development with programming languages such as Java, Python, <span>Rus</span>t, or GO</li><li>3&#43; years of <span>experience</span> with Linux-based systems, containers, and orchestration tools such as Docker or Kubernetes</li><li><span>Experience</span> transitioning legacy applications to a modernized microservice-based architecture</li><li><span>Experience</span> working within a Cloud <span>Service Provider</span> <span>(</span>CSP<span>)</span> such as AWS, Azure, or Google</li><li><span>Experience</span> using back-end and front-end languages to develop complete solutions</li><li><span>Experience</span> creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative, cross-functional team</li><li><span>Top Secret clearance</span></li><li><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span> and 5&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>tware engineering, or 10&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>tware engineering in lieu of a degree</li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><span>Experience</span> in an Agile environment</li><li><span>Experience</span> acquiring client requirements and resolving workflow problems through automation optimization</li><li><span>Experience</span> with C#, C, C&#43;&#43;, JavaScript, React, or Node.JS</li><li><span>Ability to</span> work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance</li><li><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</span></li><li><span>Master’s degree</span></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance</span></b><span>:</span> </p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Top Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted Today"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-20T06:16:39.881Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0244279","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0244279","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"1b66868b6a9d22ad13ff25c0f34e78c87cea2d762ea4762697cea039e6ac62d7","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0244279","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0244279","locations":[{"label":"Chantilly, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0244279","internal_job_id":"6c9b0fa821f61000c4e8c0c1251d0000","first_published_at":"2026-08-21","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Software Engineer The Opportunity: \nBooz Allen is looking for a Sof t war e Engineer who is driven by purpose and ready to build sof t war e that directly supports mission‑critical operations across the space domain. In this role, you’ll design, develop, and enhance the sof t war e developed for ground systems and the real‑time capabilities that space missions rely on.\n\nYou’ll take ownership of complex engineering challenges from modernizing legacy components to architecting new mission‑focused capabilities that improve performance, resilience, and operational speed. Your work will shape how data is processed, how systems communicate, and how mission teams execute with precision.\n\nThis role is built for someone who thrives on solving hard problems, emb race s innovation, and understands the responsibility of building sof t war e that must perform flawlessly. If you’re motivated by mission impact, energized by technical depth, and ready to engineer solutions that advance GEOINT and space operations, we want to meet you.\n\nWork with us as we shape systems for the better.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have: \n- 2+ years of experience in sof t war e development with programming languages, including Java, Python, Rus t, or GO\n\n- Experience transitioning legacy applications to a modernized microservice-based architecture\n\n- Experience writing source code for new applications or generating and enhancing code samples for existing applications\n\n- Experience creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative, cross-functional team\n\n- Top Secret clearance\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience operating within an Agile environment\n\n- Experience with Linux-based systems, containers, and orchestration tools, including Docker or Kubernetes\n\n- Experience designing, modifying, developing, writing, and implementing sof t war e programming applications\n\n- Experience acquiring client requirements and resolving workflow problems through automation optimization\n\n- Experience working within a Cloud Solution Provider ( CSP ) , including AWS, Azure, or Google\n\n- Experience with C#, C, C++, JavaScript, React, or Node.js\n\n- Ability to work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- Master’s degree\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information ; Top Secret clearance is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Software Engineer<p><b><span>The Opportunity: </span></b></p><p>Booz Allen is looking for a <span>Sof</span>t<span>war</span>e Engineer who is driven by purpose and ready to build <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e that directly supports mission‑critical operations across the space domain. In this role, you’ll design, develop, and enhance the <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e developed for ground systems and the real‑time capabilities that space missions rely on.</p><p></p><p>You’ll take ownership of complex engineering challenges from modernizing legacy components to architecting new mission‑focused capabilities that improve performance, resilience, and operational speed. Your work will shape how data is processed, how systems communicate, and how mission teams execute with precision.</p><p></p><p>This role is built for someone who thrives on solving hard problems, emb<span>race</span>s innovation, and understands the responsibility of building <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e that must perform flawlessly. If you’re motivated by mission impact, energized by technical depth, and ready to engineer solutions that advance GEOINT and space operations, we want to meet you.</p><p></p><p>Work with us as we shape systems for the better.</p><p></p><p>Join us. The world can’t wait.</p><p></p><p><b><span>You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p>2&#43; years of <span>experience</span> in <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e development with programming languages, including Java, Python, <span>Rus</span>t, or GO</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> transitioning legacy applications to a modernized microservice-based architecture</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> writing source code for new applications or generating and enhancing code samples for existing applications</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> creating solutions to complex problems within a collaborative, cross-functional team</p></li><li><p><span>Top Secret clearance</span></p></li><li><p><span>Bachelor&#39;s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Nice If You Have: </span></b></p><ul><li><p><span>Experience</span> operating within an Agile environment</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with Linux-based systems, containers, and orchestration tools, including Docker or Kubernetes</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> designing, modifying, developing, writing, and implementing <span>sof</span>t<span>war</span>e programming applications</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> acquiring client requirements and resolving workflow problems through automation optimization</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> working within a Cloud Solution Provider <span>(</span>CSP<span>)</span>, including AWS, Azure, or Google</p></li><li><p><span>Experience</span> with C#, C, C&#43;&#43;, JavaScript, React, or Node.js</p></li><li><p><span>Ability to</span> work with automated testing tools to perform testing and maintenance</p></li><li><p><span>TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph</span></p></li><li><p><span>Master’s degree</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><b><span>Clearance:</span></b></p><p><span>Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information</span><span>;</span> <span>Top Secret clearance is required.</span></p><p></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left\"><b>Compensation</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left\">At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $69,400.00 to $158,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.<p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Identity Statement</b></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\">As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.</p><p></p><p><b>Candidate AI Usage Policy</b></p><p>AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on <b>your </b>own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited <b>unless permission is explicitly provided</b>. </p><p style=\"text-align:inherit !important\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left !important\"><b>Work Model</b><br />Our people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Remote</b>: If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Hybrid</b>: If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.</p></li><li><p><b>Onsite</b>: If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Commitment to Non-Discrimination</b></p><p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.</p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p><p style=\"text-align:inherit\"></p>","compensation":[],"custom_fields":{"can_apply":true,"country":{"descriptor":"United States of America","id":"bc33aa3152ec42d4995f4791a106ed09"},"posted_on":"Posted 3 Days Ago"},"status":"open","first_seen_at":"2026-08-24T01:56:20.339Z","last_seen_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z","closed_at":null,"possibly_closed_at":null,"missing_complete_scans":0,"data_quality":null,"classification":{"included":true,"tier":"stretch","score":3,"level":"unspecified","term":null,"tracks":["software"],"role_matches":["Software Engineer"],"early_career_matches":[],"positive_matches":["Software Engineer"],"exclude_matches":[],"configured_tracks":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"]}}
{"schema_version":1,"job_key":"workday:bah-bah-jobs:/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0246016","source":{"type":"workday","board":"bah-BAH_Jobs","job_id":"/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0246016","source_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/bah/BAH_Jobs/jobs","response_hash":"840c25d796f478dfb5311f0d5b329f8270c407fa73099a1b3991bbfff8d39759","fetched_at":"2026-08-25T02:30:45.417Z"},"company":{"name":"Booz Allen","slug":"booz-allen","lists":["consulting-ai","enterprise-ai"],"target_role":null,"fit_tier":null},"title":"Software Engineer","canonical_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0246016","apply_url":"https://bah.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/BAH_Jobs/job/Chantilly-VA/Software-Engineer_R0246016","locations":[{"label":"Chantilly, VA"}],"workplace_type":"unknown","employment_type":"full_time","departments":[],"teams":[],"language":null,"requisition_id":"R0246016","internal_job_id":"adece80c64641001129b1291e4160000","first_published_at":"2026-08-04","source_updated_at":null,"application_deadline":null,"description_plain":"Software Engineer The Opportunity: \nBooz Allen is looking for a Software Engineer who is driven by purpose and ready to build software that directly supports mission‑critical operations across the space domain. In this role, you’ll design, develop, and enhance the software developed for ground systems and the real‑time capabilities that space missions rely on.\n\nYou’ll take ownership of complex engineering challenges from modernizing legacy components to architecting new mission‑focused capabilities that improve performance, resilience, and operational speed. Your work will shape how data is processed, how systems communicate, and how mission teams execute with precision.\n\nThis role is built for someone who thrives on solving hard problems, embraces innovation, and understands the responsibility of building software that must perform flawlessly. If you’re motivated by mission impact, energized by technical depth, and ready to engineer solutions that advance GEOINT and space operations, we want to meet you.\n\nWork with us as we shape systems for the better.\n\nJoin us. The world can’t wait.\n\nYou Have: \n- 8+ years of experience in DevSecOps with a major Cloud Service Provider, such as AWS, Azure, GCP, or Oracle, within the government\n\n- Experience building and supporting CI/CD pipelines using tools such as Jenkins, GitHub Actions, or GitLab CI\n\n- Experience with version control tools, including Git, including branching strategies and workflow management\n\n- Experience with container technologies such as Docker or ECS\n\n- Experience with RHEL\n\n- Experience with collaboration and project tracking tools such as Confluence and Jira\n\n- Experience programming in Java, Python, or Bash\n\n- Knowledge of aws-cli and azure-cli, secure software development practices, IAM, secrets management, and cloud security principles\n\n- TS/SCI clearance with a polygraph\n\n- Bachelor's degree\n\nNice If You Have: \n- Experience with Jenkins or GitLab administration, including developing and maintaining custom pipeline configurations on self‑hosted infrastructure\n\n- Knowledge of Microservice architectures, including Cloud Native stacks, such as Kubernetes or OpenShift, or Cloud centric design using AWS Lambda functions\n\n- Knowledge of developing an enterprise level CI/CD pipeline that delivers products from development to production\n\n- Master’s degree\n\n- AWS Solution Architecture Certification, Azure Architecture Certification or AWS Certified Developer Associate Certification\n\nClearance:\nApplicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; TS/SCI clearance with polygraph is required.\n\nCompensation\nAt Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full-time and part-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n\nSalary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $86,800.00 to $198,000.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\nIdentity Statement\nAs part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n\nCandidate AI Usage Policy\nAI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on your own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in-person or virtual) is prohibited unless permission is explicitly provided .\n\nWork Model\nOur people-first culture prioritizes the benefits of collaboration, whether it occurs in person or virtually. To support engagement and effective communication, employees working virtually are generally expected to have their cameras on during meetings.\n- Remote : If this position is listed as remote, there may still be occasions when you are required to work in person at a Booz Allen or customer facility.\n\n- Hybrid : If this position is listed as hybrid, you will be expected to work from a Booz Allen facility frequently, in alignment with leadership expectations and the needs of the role. You may also be required to work from or visit a customer facility.\n\n- Onsite : If this position is listed as onsite, work will primarily be performed at a Booz Allen office or customer facility, where employees will collaborate directly with colleagues and customers as required by the role.\n\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to disability, status as a protected veteran or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, local, or international law.","description_html":"Software Engineer<p><b>The Opportunity: </b></p><p>Booz Allen is looking for a Software Engineer who is driven by purpose and ready to build software that directly supports mission‑critical operations across the space domain. In this role, you’ll desi